VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, NEW LATERAL AND POSTERIOR MARGINS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, apocrine change\u000aand columnar cell change, foreign body giant cell reaction to\u000apolarizable material, and fat necrosis, consistent with prior\u000abiopsy site.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Shave margin off anterior-lateral side of cavity and extended into\u000afloor of cavity (posterior margin). Positive margins on 1st excision.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: As above.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast -new lateral and posterior margin, stitch- long lateral,\u000ashort superior, white stitch on new margin side.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Right breast new lateral and posterior margins, stitch\u000along lateral, short superior, whip stitch on new margin side", and consists of\u000aa shave margin around a prior excision cavity (7.0 cm from anterior to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral). The specimen is oriented with a long stitch designated lateral, a\u000ashort stitch designated superior, and a whipstitch designated new margin per\u000athe surgeon. According to the accompanying specimen sketch, the prosector\u000adesignated the excision cavity side medial and the new margin side\u000alateral/posterior. The specimen consists of yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue with a firm nodular excision cavity and an attached tan/white REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm skin ellipse bearing a well-healed REMOVED_DATE cm longitudinal scar. The specimen\u000ais oriented according to the surgeon's designations. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal 70%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30% white/tan, nodular, firm fibrous/scar\u000atissue. The fibrous tissue is extending to the inferior margin and is present\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margins. The cavity is lined by\u000awhite/tan firm tissue. The entire specimen is submitted. A metal clip is\u000afound REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen submitted from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE frags\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aAWE/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01, 2009 at 04:29:47PM\u000a[report_end]
