 = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Attached\u000ato the breast tissue is a tan-white skin ellipse (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) on the\u000aanterior margin. The specimen contains a hookwire. The specimen is\u000aaccompanyied by a radiograph, which demonstrates a hookwire, a clip and an\u000aill-defined opacity. The specimen is serially sectioned and radiograph. The\u000aclip is identified within an area of firm white fibrous tissue that contains\u000athe prior core biopsy site. This fibrous tissue comprises approximately 30% of\u000athe specimen. Representative sections are submitted. All fibrous tissue is\u000aentirely submitted. Approximately 50% of the entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1,2: section anterior to clip area, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3,4: section with clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections posterior to clip, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral and posterior margins, perpendicular, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin including skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast tissue, deep, short/superior,\u000along/lateral", consists of a piece of breast tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000atwo (2) orienting sutures. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon. The\u000asuperior surface is red, the inferior green, the lateral yellow, and no inked\u000a(orange) is seen for medial. There is an uninked surface anteriorly, which\u000alikely represents the old margin. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen\u000ais greater than 99% yellow-tan grossly unremarkable adipose tissue.\u000aApproximately 50% of the specimen is submitted. This specimen is submitted\u000aserially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000ahph\u000aReports 