DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, irregular, fibrofatty breast\u000atissue which has a short suture designating superior and a long suture\u000adesignating lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal a predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with\u000ascant thin white fibrous tissue in which a discrete lesion is not appreciated.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro 1: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: lateral margin to include posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: lateral margin to include anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: inferior anterior margin, micro 1, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: inferior medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "#2 left breast core biopsy cavity, suture marks long lateral, short\u000asuperior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, fibrofatty breast tissue with a\u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral to reveal a yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with scant thin white\u000afibrous tissue in which a discrete mass is not appreciated. Representative\u000asections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro 8: anterior lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin to include superior and inferior margins, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: lateral margin to include superior and inferior margin, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 12: lateral margin to include inferior margin\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin to include lateral and medial aspects, 3 frags\u000atotal, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: posterior margin to include superior and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart three, "#3 left breast mass, short superior, long lateral", consists of\u000athree fibrofatty breast tissues in which the largest (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) has\u000abeen previously incised along the midline, bisecting the anterior, inferior,\u000aposterior aspects and has a short suture designating superior and a long suture\u000adesignating lateral. The larger tissue has been inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning the\u000alarger fragment reveals a predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed\u000awith scant thin white fibrous tissue in which a discrete lesion is not\u000aappreciated. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to\u000alateral. The additional breast tissues (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) are black-inked and serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable yellow\u000alobulated fatty tissue surface admixed with scant thin white fibrous tissue.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire smallest breast tissue, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mid size breast tissue, 6 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro 21: largest breast tissue, lateral margin to include inferior margin,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 22: superior anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 23: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 24: inferior margin to include the lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 25: medial anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000alm\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
