st wall margin --> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1 - No clip present/wire intact. Discussed with Dr. Rhei by Dr.\u000aRitner.\u000aSpecimen #2 - No clip. DGS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a wire localized breast excision\u000aspecimen (3.4 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture\u000adesignating superior, a long suture designating lateral, and a whipstitch\u000adesignating the chest wall margin/posterior. There is a wire entering on the\u000amedial aspect inferiorly and exiting on the medial aspect superiorly. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates an intact wire with no\u000aclip present. There is a firm white fibrotic area (2.6 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm AP) that abuts the superior, inferior, medial, lateral, and anterior\u000amargins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. It contains the core biopsy\u000asite. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serially sectioned specimen anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE frags per\u000ablock, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Superior shave margin", consists of a breast shave excision (3.5 x\u000a2.7 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm SI) that is oriented with a whipstitch on a new superior margin\u000a(inked blue). The old margin is inked black. An accompanying radiograph shows\u000ano clip, and the case has been discussed with Dr. Rhei. There is a firm white\u000afibrotic area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the old margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the new margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entirely submitted specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aTA/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/21/2008\u000a[report_end]
