VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: AMNON WACHMAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and micropapillary types (low\u000anuclear grade), is present associated with calcifications and necrosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor,\u000aprogesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 71 year old female with heterogeneous grouped coarse calc in LUOQ,\u000aasymptomatic. DDx: Fibrocystic changes, r/o cancer.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 3 mm, Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 8G Stereotactic . Blue cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "Left breast, blue", and consists of multiple tan/yellow to\u000atan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). Portion of the breast tissue cores were received in a blue\u000acassette marked "A. Ca++", and the remainder of the breast tissue cores were\u000areceived in a blue cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/8/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (11/13/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
