with radiation CA Rt Brst.\u000aOperation: SNB Rt bilat mastex.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA Rt Brst.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast, short - superior, long - lateral 279 gm.\u000aB/2) Left breast, short - superior, long - lateral, 272 gm.\u000aC/3) Right sentinel lymph node - F.S.\u000aD/4) Right breast skin.\u000aE/5) Left breast skin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE RIGHT" (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: HEJIN P. HAHN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: Agoston T. Agoston, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimens are received fresh in five parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast, short-superior, long-lateral", consists of a\u000aright mastectomy specimen (270.0 g, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm deep) with skin ellipse (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and everted\u000anipple (0.7 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in height) with areola (2.3 cm in\u000adiameter). The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. On the skin ellipse\u000aare two sutures with short designating superior and long designating lateral.\u000aOn the skin, there is a scar (1.4 cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to nipple and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the nearest skin edge. No muscle is grossly identified. The deep margin\u000ais inked blue. Sectioning the specimen reveals an ill-defined fibrous area\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located in the lower outer aspect of the specimen, deep to\u000athe skin scar. The fibrous area comes to REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. No\u000aother mass lesions are grossly identified. No lymph nodes are grossly\u000aidentified. The breast tissue is approximately 5% fibrous and 95% adipose\u000atissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin scar, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous area deep to scar, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Axillary tail, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast, short-superior, long-lateral", consists of a\u000aleft mastectomy specimen (234.0 g, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm deep) with skin ellipse (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and everted\u000anipple (0.8 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in height) with areola (1.8 cm in\u000adiameter). The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No muscle is\u000agrossly identified. The deep margin is inked blue. Sectioning the specimen\u000areveals no mass lesions. The breast parenchyma is approximately 5% fibrous and\u000a95% adipose tissue. In the same container is a separate fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No lymph nodes are grossly\u000aidentified in either the mastectomy specimen or separate fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Axillary tail, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Separate fragment of fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Sentinel lymph node right", consists of a fragment of\u000apink/yellow soft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is bisected and\u000aentirely submitted for frozen section as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Frozen section remnant A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right breast skin", consists of a skin ellipse (23.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm x REMOVED_DATE cm deep with two fresh incisions measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000a6.5 cm incision is surrounded by blue dye and comes to REMOVED_DATE cm to the nearest\u000askin edge. The REMOVED_DATE cm incision comes to REMOVED_DATE cm to nearest skin edge. Deep\u000aaspect of the specimen is inked blue. Representative sections are submitted\u000afor histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE cm incision with dye, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE cm incision, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Left breast skin", consists of a skin ellipse (11.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which has the center portion excised in another elliptical shape (8.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) such that the inner aspect of the ellipse has been excised. The specimen\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm deep. The skin portion varies in width from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. On one\u000aaspect of the ellipse, there is a fresh incision (5.0 cm in length) on the\u000aportion of skin that measures REMOVED_DATE cm in width. The incision comes to REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000anearest skin edge. Representative sections are submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Incision site, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Portion of skin ellipse opposite portion with incision, 7 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aGL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
