VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread.\u000aIntraductal papilloma (up to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, DEEP MARGIN OF NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal (block #12).\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aNOTE:\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast pathology service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Patient with nipple discharge, left breast ductagram, dilated duct\u000awith filling defect.\u000aOperation: Left breast needle localized breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Tissue left breast, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000a2. Left breast tissue, deep margin - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aRadiology:\u000aHookwire and nodule in specimen. DIR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, tissue left breast, short=superior, long = lateral,\u000aposterior to nipple edge at duct", consists of a piece of breast tissue (4.2 x\u000a3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that has two (2) orienting sutures. The specimen was inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green. No orange or yellow\u000aink is identified. The lateral edge as indicated by the long suture is inked\u000ayellow by the pathology resident. The medial surface is inked orange by the\u000apathology resident. A hook wire is received in the container, but it is no\u000alonger within the specimen. The specimen is accompanyied by a radiograph which\u000ademonstrates a hookwire and an ill-defined mass. Serial sectioning reveals an\u000aill-defined, firm, white area (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains a possible\u000aduct (0.3 cm in diameter) that contains tan-orange material within its lumen.\u000aThe firm white area grossly abuts the inferior margin, is abutting the\u000aposterior margin, is abutting the anterior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, abuts the lateral margin, and is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. The entire specimen is submitted serially from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast tissue, deep margin - short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of a piece of breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two\u000a(2) orienting sutures. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked red for superior, yellow for lateral, green for inferior, and\u000ablack for posterior. No orange ink or blue ink is present. One surface\u000aof the specimen is uninked, and may represent the old margin. Serial sectioning\u000areveals that the specimen is 5% white fibrous tissue. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional deep margin of left breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
