VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, squamous metaplasia\u000aof ducts, benign calcification, sclerosing adenosis, and cystic change.\u000aNo DCIS or LCIS.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59 year old female whose REMOVED_DATE  mammograms demonstrate two clusters\u000aof clacifications at the 9 + 10 o'clock axes for which wire loc + excision is\u000arecommended (S/P REMOVED_DATE core and excision revealing right breast ADH bordering\u000aon DCIS and LCIS).\u000aOperation: L breast double wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - L breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin --> mammo.\u000aRadiograph report: Calcifications in speicmen - 2 areas of calcs.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"L breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on chest wall\u000amargin", is an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to white/tan breast parenchyma (10\u000agrams, REMOVED_DATE (m/l) x REMOVED_DATE (s/i) x REMOVED_DATE (a/p) cm), which per the surgeon is oriented\u000aas indicated. The specimen is inked per the surgeon per the pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one needle\u000alocalization wire in place entering the medial/superior aspect of the specimen,\u000aand exiting the medial/posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed (per radiologist, "calcifications in specimen - two\u000aareas of calcs"). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to\u000aexhibit an ill-defined area of very dense, white/tan to pink/tan fibrous stroma\u000a(approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), involving approximately 90% of the\u000aspecimen. In slice two, the wire traverses the most-medial aspect of the\u000aaforementioned ill-defined dense stroma. No clip is identified. The dense\u000astroma abuts each of the inked margins in multiple areas. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen is composed of a small amount of unremarkable yellow/tan, lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral, as\u000afollows:\u000aMicro #1: slice one (most medial), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: slice two (traversed by wire), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3: slice three with dense fibrous stroma, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #4-5: slice four, bisected, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro #6: slice five, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #7: slice six, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #8: slice seven (most lateral), 1 frag, ESS.\u000almb/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
