VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: James L Connolly, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 12:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED REMOVED_DATE 7 CM MASS\u000aFragments of cyst wall with associated foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE NEEDLE\u000aBIOPSIESF FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present associated with calcifications, (see\u000anote).\u000aNOTE: Atypical ductal hyperplasia is best evaluated after excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 53 y o with "nodule" by US, left breast; S/P US core bx this morning -\u000aprob. cyst.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: Circumscribed mass; size of lesion - REMOVED_DATE mm.\u000a2. Left: Calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: 12:00\u000a2. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000a2. 11G Stereotactic, vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. 3 cores; Diff Dx - Probable complicated cyst, R/O DCIS - Blue cassette.\u000aB/2. Diff. Dx - Prob FCC, R/O DCIS. - Pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Blue, left breast", consists of multiple yellow/white irregular\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in an\u000aunlabeled blue cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Pink, left breast ", consists of multiple yellow/white focally\u000ahemorrhagic irregular fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich are received in two pink cassettes labeled "A. Ca2+" and "B". The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca2+", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
