VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia and calcifications\u000aassociated with benign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with:\u000aUsual epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated calcifications.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aCore biopsy site changes, present at the medial, inferior and anterior\u000amargins.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Recent bx of calcs, Lt breast --> ADH for resection.\u000aOperation: Resection, abnorm. area, Lt breast.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH, Lt.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Tissue, left breast - anterior/inferior.\u000aB/2) Tissue, left breast - posterior/superior (ADH); long suture = lateral;\u000ashort suture = superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1) Specimen: Wire & Ca++ in specimen. OR called/SR.\u000a2) Specimen: Clip & wire present. OR called/SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Tissue-left breast-anterior-inferior", consists of a\u000asingle breast lumpectomy specimen (3.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior). The specimen is marked with sutures\u000aas follows: Short equals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalizing wire enters in the lateral margin to mark calcifications as\u000ademonstrated on the accompanying radiograph. The specimen is sequentially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a white, irregularly-defined area\u000a(1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This white area appears to grossly abut the inferior,\u000aposterior, and anterior margins. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin,\u000aand greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins. The lateral most\u000aarea of this white area appears to correspond with the location of\u000acalcifications as demonstrated in the accompanying radiograph. The remainder\u000aof the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable adipose tissue with no other\u000alesions or masses grossly noted. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; calcifications\u000acorresponding to sections in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Tissue-left breast, posterior-inferior (ADH)", consists of\u000aa breast lumpectomy specimen (3.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is marked by sutures as\u000afollows: Short equals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aPlease note that separately conceived in the container is a localization wire.\u000aThe accompanying radiograph demonstrates a lumpectomy specimen containing a\u000aclip in the anterior portion with a separate wire. The specimen is\u000asequentially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a white, firm,\u000aill-defined area (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This white area appears to grossly abut\u000athe superior, anterior, and posterior margins. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins.\u000aWithin this white fibrotic area is a black, circular area (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat is grossly consistent with core biopsy site. The clip is identified in\u000athis area. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable\u000aadipose tissue with no other grossly noted lesions or masses. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White, ill-defined area (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID); 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aEM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/20/2008\u000a[report_end]
