VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA present as a single focus (block 2; best seen\u000ain the third level of the original levels, or in the deeper levels).\u000aSmall calcifications are present.\u000aMultiple large calcifications associated with apocrine cysts (block 1;\u000aadditional levels examined).\u000aNOTE: The atypical hyperplasia consists of a monomorphic population of\u000acells with low grade nuclei forming cribriform spaces in a small cluster\u000aof ductal spaces. The entire area measures less than REMOVED_DATE cm. Although\u000athis area borders on a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ, given the\u000asmall size, final classification should be based on findings after\u000aexcision.\u000aThe majority of the calcifications appear to be associated with cysts in\u000ablock 1, which was the location of the mammographic calcifications in the\u000acore biopsies.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51 year old woman with calcifications in left breast.\u000aOperation: 11 gauge core biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Benign.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Specimen in white cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHU,GERALD CHEN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fixed in formalin, in one (1) part, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number, "left breast," and consists of two (2) white\u000acassettes. The first cassette is labeled "A - left ca ++," and consists of\u000amultiple fragments of tan/red soft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The second\u000awhite cassette is labeled "B- left," and consists of multiple fragments of\u000ared/tan soft tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro #1 : "A" multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #2 : "B" multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: LOPKIN, CARL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
