VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Joseph Woodward Carlson, M.D., Ph.D.; Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 2:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR\u000aMASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade), is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells around the invasive carcinoma. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is negative in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 y o female with 9-mm mass 2:00 left breast. Hx lt Bx 1998 with\u000asevere ADH.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: irregular\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Cores obtained - lesion decreased in size.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspected carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aCores in white cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aPart A, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"Left breast", is a one (1), unlabeled, white cassette which contains multiple,\u000ayellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (2.3 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette contents, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/22/05): DR. DEBORAH DILLON\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
