etermined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS, right breast. Anterior, posterior and lateral close margins\u000afor re-excision.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Tissue from right breast (stitch markings = long/\u000alateral, short/superior).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to\u000amedial x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. There is a tan-pink skin ellipse\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A long black suture has been placed by the surgeon to\u000adenote the lateral margin and a short black suture is placed by the surgeon to\u000adenote the superior margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen has been\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior and entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation. The breast tissue is approximately 70% adipose and 30%\u000afibrous tissue with no discrete nodules or other lesions grossly visible.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000adk\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
