VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTIONS (2\u000aSPECIMENS):\u000aINVASVIE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE(S).\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II(Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Low\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present (extensive)\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - Negative (>0.3 cm) Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: Positive (see note)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 5 (see note)\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 11\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS Atypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: Metastatic carcinoma is not identified on H&E stains, which show nodes\u000awith fibrosis and lymphoid depletion consistent with chemotherapy effect.\u000aKeratin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) immunostains highlight isolated tumor cells in 5 of the 11\u000anodes.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma carcinoma and lymphovascular invasion\u000a(block 4):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aThe patient is s/p chemotherapy. Therefore, these negative results should be\u000ainterpreted with caution.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43 year old female with locally advanced right breast cancer, S/P\u000aneo-adjuvant chemo.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 - right breast and axillary contents, short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral, bow tie on axilla.\u000a#2 - right axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000athe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 - right breast and axillary contents, short\u000astitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, bow tie on axilla", consists of a 299\u000agram modified right radical mastectomy specimen, with axillary tail (18 cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, 15 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior), and a brown/tan skin ellipse (12.5 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm), with areola (3.0\u000acm in diameter), and nipple (1.2 cm). The brown skin ellipse and nipple are\u000aunremarkable with no evidence of inversion of the nipple. The deep fascial\u000amargin is inked black, and the breast serially sectioned to reveal a poorly\u000acircumscribed firm white fibrous area (5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 cm), 1 cm deep to the\u000anipple, and coming to within 1 cm of the deep margin. Within the fibrous area\u000athere is a firm white nodule (0.8 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm deep to\u000athe nipple and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Suspicious nodules tethering the\u000aadipose tissue in the upper/outer quadrant are identified, and may be lymph\u000anodes.\u000aMicro #1: Retro-areolar nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #2: Deep margin to this nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #3+4: Firm fibrous tissue in relation to skin and nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #5-7: Upper/outer quadrant suspicious firm tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #8+9: Lower/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #11+12: Upper/inner quadrant to include edge of fibrous area and deep\u000amargin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #13-16: Axillary lymph node, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 - right axillary contents", consists of fragments of\u000ayellow/tan fibrous adipose tissue (10 cm x 4 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate),\u000acontaining ten candidate lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm to 2 cm in\u000agreatest dimension.\u000aMicro #17: Four candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #18: Five candidate lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #19: Largest lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajeb/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
