g to protocol: black = posterior,\u000ablue = anterior, orange = medial, yellow = lateral, red = superior, green -\u000ainferior. There are three sutures marking the lateral, superior, and chest\u000awall margins.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm elongated hemorrhagic needle track in the central\u000aportion of the specimen in the area of the clip. The remainder of the tissue\u000aconsists of adipose tissue with very little fibrous tissue. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aCass 1,2: Inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 3,4: Superior margin, including portion of core track, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 4,6: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 7,8: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen including core track and anterior and\u000aposterior margins, medial to lateral, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/24/2007\u000a[report_end]
