VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - superior, medial, lateral, posterior,\u000aanterior.\u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - inferior, focal (micro 8)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 4:8 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - inferior, posterior, superior, lateral,\u000amedial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - anterior (3)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS - core biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) positive (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast, core biopsy REMOVED_MONTH 30th; tumor is ER positive\u000aPR positive, Her-2 neu positive.\u000aOperation: Left mammographical directed biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (short stitch = superior margin,\u000along stitch = lateral margin).\u000aRadiology: Mass in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by IAFRATE,ANTHONY JOHN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "left breast tissue, short stitch = superior, long\u000astitch = lateral", and consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a single localization wire in place, and two\u000a(2) orienting sutures, a short suture designating superior, and a long suture\u000adesignating lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A firm, white fibrotic\u000amass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. It is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the green\u000ainked margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the red inked margin, 2 cm from the yellow and\u000aorange inked margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the black inked margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ablue inked margin. The remainder of the tissue consists of approximately 10%\u000awhite fibrous tissue, and 90% unremarkable adipose tissue. Adjacent to the\u000amass is an approximate REMOVED_DATE cm area of hemorrhage, consistent with recent needle\u000abiopsy.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and closest green and red margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3 : tumor and black margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4 : lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5 : medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6 : anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7 : lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8 : uninvolved breast tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
