VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aIncidental TUBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I/III) (0.1 cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin (block #5; see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen (EIC-negative).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aSeparate foci of calcifications associated with benign epithelium and\u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypia.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe area of invasive carcinoma is no longer present on deeper levels and\u000aadditional studies cannot be performed. This case was reviewed by Dr. Andrea\u000aRichardson and Dr. Susan Lester who concur with this diagnosis.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa Nx Mx.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcs, rt breast.\u000aOperation: Rt breast wire direct biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Rt breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ are in specimen. cd\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "right breast\u000atissue", is a single ragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.1 cm from medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior). The specimen is received with a hookwire in the specimen and is\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is accompanied by radiograph which\u000ademonstrates a hook wire near an area of calcifications in the specimen,\u000acorresponding to the inferior portion of the specimen. The specimen is\u000acomposed of approximately 50% firm, white, fibrous tissue, predominantly\u000alocated at the inferior portion. The specimen is entirely submitted from\u000ainferior to superior.\u000aMicro 1: inferior margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 10&11: superior margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000apsc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
