VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST 2:00, 7 CM FROM THE NIPPPLE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A\u000aHYPOECHOIC AREA:\u000aCore site changes are present associated with dense fibrous breast tissue (see\u000aNOTE).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications in normal breast epithelium and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change (0.8 cm focus; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked an evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: All of the fibrous tissue has been submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aRadiologic correlation is advised to ensure the excision is representative of\u000athe radiologic lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56-year-old post-menopausal women S/P L breast WL Exc REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing ALH and L breast shave margin revealing fibroadenoma & sclerosing\u000aadenosis with calcifications and U/S REMOVED_DATE showing architectural distortion at\u000aclip - hypoechoic vague area 2:00 - 7-cm FN may represent incomplete excision\u000aof lesions.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx (2 wires), U/S-guided + mammo-guided.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue; short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral; whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin - mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, mass & wire in specimen. OR called. - LBS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number and "#1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whipstitch on chest wall margin", and consists of a wire localized\u000aexcisional breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with three stitches\u000adesignating the superior, lateral, and chest wall margins. A wire is present\u000ain the specimen. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates an area of\u000acentral hyperlucency adjacent to the wire and associated with a clip. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The lateral and medial aspects of the specimen were removed and\u000arepresentatively submitted as perpendicular sections. The remaining tissue is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial such that the lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen is represented in slice #1 and that the final medial margin is\u000arepresented in slice #11. Sectioning demonstrates a predominantly tan/white\u000afirm cut surface likely representing fibrosis or fibroadenoma which appears to\u000aabut the inferior margin, superior margin, and anterior margin. A clip is\u000aidentified in the specimen in slices #9 and #10 contain an area of tan/pink\u000afirm tissue, focal area of hemorrhage present in slice #9 and potentially\u000arepresents prior biopsy sites. All of the fibrous breast tissue is submitted\u000afor histological evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of slice #4 to include area of tan/white\u000afibrous nodule to green ink, blue ink, and red ink, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, trisected to include green, red, blue, black inks, 1\u000afrag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, trisected, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 partially sectioned to include an area of focal hemorrhage,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, partially fragmented tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Portion of slice #6 to include anterior/posterior/inferior margins,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional section of slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aSRK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/30/2008\u000a[report_end]
