VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Sebastien de Feraudy, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST LATERAL MARGIN RE-EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical micropapillary hyperplasia and prior excision\u000asite changes, negative for carcinoma.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST INFERIOR MARGIN RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia and prior excision site\u000achanges, negative for carcinoma.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 81 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE  R W L lumpectomy demonstrating DCIS with a\u000aclear inferior and positive lateral margin. ER/PR(+) Her-2 (-).\u000aOperation: R breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast lateral margin; whip stitch - new margin with scar.\u000aB/2) Rt breast inferior margin; whip stitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast lateral margin, whip-stitch new margin with\u000ascar", consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000awhip-stitch on one surface designating "new margin with scar" per the surgeon.\u000aThe whip-stitch surface is inked blue and the opposing focally cauterized\u000asurface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned, exhibiting\u000apredominantly yellow lobulated adipose tissue with scant fibrous soft tissue.\u000aNo gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Rt breast inferior margin, whip-stitch new margin",\u000aconsists of a concave portion of yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm) with a whip-stitch along one surface designating "new margin" per the\u000asurgeon. The surface marked by the whip-stitch is inked blue and the opposing\u000aconcave, focally fibrotic/hemorrhagic surface (non-true margin) is inked black.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned, exhibiting predominantly fibrotic/focally\u000anecrotic, hemorrhagic tissue abutting the non-true margin and focally extending\u000ato the new margin. There is scant yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue. No\u000aother gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 21, 2009 at 06:16:59PM\u000a[report_end]
