VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 10:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aPALPABLE IRREGULAR SHADOWING WITH ASSOCIATED DILATED DUCTS (0.4 CM):\u000aFocus of dense stromal fibrosis (up to REMOVED_DATE cm) with focal chronic inflammation\u000aand cysts, (See, Note).\u000aNOTE: The pathological correlate with an irregular palpable lesion is poor and\u000aradiologic correlation is advised.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 67 year old female with history of bloody nipple d/c on the left.\u000aIrregular and hypoechoic mass seen on US for which biopsy was recommended.\u000aAlso extensive dilated ducts in upper/inner quadrant. Patient on Coumadin.\u000aUnable to biopsy largest area of suspected invasion. Biopsy performed on small\u000asuperficial superior palpable mass 10:00, 1 cm from nipple. Time in formalin\u000a9:07 am.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: Palpable, lesion biopsied 4 mm size - area of disease entire LUIQ, and\u000airregular mass shadowing with associated dilated ducts.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper/inner 10:00.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy in one blue cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of a blue cassette, which contains\u000amultiple irregular tan/yellow focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues received in blue cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000almc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday August 18, 2009 at 03:31:23PM\u000a[report_end]
