VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE DIRECTED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, extensive.\u000aFlorid duct hyperplasia (focally involved by LCIS in block #12).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aPapilloma.\u000a(Levels examined).\u000aMargins examined microscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Rt. needle directed.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt. breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Rt. breast mass\u000aRADIOLOGY: A few cysts in specimen. No definite mass...\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LAZAR,ALEXANDER J FAULKNER,M.D.,PH.D\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right\u000abreast mass" is a right breast excision specimen (5 cm anterior to posterior,\u000a5 cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior). Sutures are left by\u000athe surgeon for orientation (long = lateral, short = superior). The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. In addition, there are three small fragments of unoriented\u000abreast tissue, the largest measuring 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. These unoriented\u000afragments of breast tissue are inked in black, however, it is not known which\u000amargin they are associated with. There is no needle associated with the right\u000abreast excision specimen, however, by report the needle came out and is not\u000apresent with the specimen. Coming off of the lateral portion of the right\u000abreast excision specimen is a section of tissue (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is\u000aentirely inked in orange given its location. Cysts measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension are identified but no definitive mass is located. The\u000atissue is entirely submitted.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  main body of mass, multi margins, ESS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  medial arm coming off main specimen, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  3 frags of unoriented tissue, black demarks unknown margin,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aafl\u000aReports to: JACOBSEN, DAVID M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
