VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUBAREOLAR WIRE LOCALISED EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aTwo slides are received for review (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, (low nuclear grade) is present as a\u000a0.15cm focus (8 duct profiles) in one slide (by report of nine total).\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with DCIS. No necrosis is present.\u000aDCIS is present at the inferior (green inked) margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000a(black inked) margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left nipple discharge REMOVED_DATE cm area of abnormality in left\u000asubareolar area\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, LCIS and ADH\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are two (2) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding\u000ato a left breast, subareolar, wire guided excision (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/18/2006\u000a[report_end]
