VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marian H Harris, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aFocal apocrine metaplasia.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "RETROAREOLAR SHAVE MARGIN", RIGHT BREAST:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (<0.1 cm from black-inked old margin).\u000aColumnar hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aBiopsy site present at new margin.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 y.o. female with abnl mammo REMOVED_DATE -> indeterminate microcalcs in\u000adeep central portion of R breast -> core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  showed atypia/LCIS for\u000aexcision\u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Rt needle directed breast biopsy, short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral, whip stitch on deep margin, to mammography\u000a2. Retro areolar lateral shave margin, whip stitch in new margin, to mammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe case is received fresh in two parts labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, "right needle directed breast biopsy," consists of one portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen has been inked\u000aby the surgeon as follows: red/superior, green/inferior, yellow/lateral,\u000aorange/medial, blue/anterior and black/posterior. There are three orienting\u000asutures, designated by the surgeon to be short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhip-stitch/deep. There is a localization wire in the specimen, passing\u000athrough its lateral-most edge. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates no clip in the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: right breast biopsy, 9 frags, ESS\u000aPart B, "retroareolar shave margin," consists of one portion of cylindrical\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is one orienting whip\u000astitch designated by the surgeon to be the new margin. The new margin is inked\u000ablue and the old margin is inked black. The specimen in serially sectioned to\u000areveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: retroareolar shave margin, 9 frags, ESS\u000aMAH/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
