VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS\u000aAND A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSmall cysts with calcifications.\u000aCalcifications associated with lobules.\u000aCore needle biopsy site.\u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for calcifications\u000athat revealed lobular carcinoma in situ, atypical lobular hyperplasia, and\u000acolumnar cell change associated with calcifications (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The entire\u000aspecimen is examined microscopically, including margins. No atypical\u000ahyperplasia or carcinoma is present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 year old postmenopausal woman s/p right upper outer quadrant core\u000abiopsy on REMOVED_DATE  revealing LCIS and ALH with calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: LCIS\u000aSPECIMEN RADIOGRAPH:\u000aClip, calcifications, and wire in specimen. Dr. Esther Rhei in the O.R. phoned\u000aby Dr. C. Denison.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight breast tissue: short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip stitch\u000adeep margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived fresh labeled with the patient's name and unit number and "Right\u000abreast tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior)\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior to posterior) biopsy with an inserted wire and sutures\u000amarking the superior, lateral, and deep margins. The specimen radiograph shows\u000aa clip next to the wire (closest to the superior margin) and an adjacent area\u000aof numerous calcifications throughout the midportion of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon according to protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: black = posterior, blue = anterior, medial = orange, lateral =\u000ayellow, superior = red, inferior = green. There is a clip in a 1 x 1 cm\u000aill-defined firm area of tissue that abuts the superior margin. The remainder\u000aof the specimen consists of predominantly fatty tissue with interspersed\u000astrands of fibrous tissue. No other gross lesions are present. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic examination sequentially from the lateral\u000amargin to the medial margin.\u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 3: Area of clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Sequential sections from lateral to medial, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/7/2008\u000a[report_end]
