VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread and associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU focally involves an intraductal papilloma.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE  right breast mammogram - "Increasing upper outer quadrant\u000acalcifications" - not able to complete core biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - sort stitch superior, long lateral, whip stitch on\u000achest wall margin - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcifications present in specimen. Hookwire in specimen.\u000aPhoned to Operating Room. [No signature]\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Right breast tissue - sort stitch superior, long lateral, whip stitch\u000aon chest wall margin", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.9 x\u000a3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting sutures ("short stitch - superior, long\u000astitch - lateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin"), two accompanying\u000aradiographs, and a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is received\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The needle localization wire enters at the anteromedial aspect\u000aand exits superiorly. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to\u000amedial, revealing approximately 75% tan/white dense focally nodular fibrous\u000astroma admixed with 25% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. As confirmed by the\u000aaccompanying radiograph, two foci of calcification are present within the\u000aspecimen as well as the presence of a hookwire within the specimen. No other\u000agross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aNote: Foci of calcification predominantly within REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID as well as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000athrough REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aDFI/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/30/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aImmunoperoxidase stains for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/p63 show the presence of basal cells.\u000aThe diagnosis remains UNCHANGED.\u000aAddendum #1 by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/31/2006\u000a[report_end]
