VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia associated with calcifications, sclerosing\u000aadenosis, and pagetoid spread.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications.\u000aStromal calcifications are present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 56-year-old postmenopausal female with abnormal right mammo status\u000apost right breast WL excision Bx on REMOVED_DATE  from upper outer quadrant\u000acalcifications revealing LCIS, ALH - REMOVED_DATE  mammo showed increased bilateral\u000acalcs that are suspicious on right side at 90 axis, new cluster of\u000acalcifications; wire-localized excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Not given.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. R breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whipstitch\u000achest wall margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMultiple groups of calcifications in specimen and intact hookwire.\u000aReviewed with Dr. Gombos and Dr. Rhei.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "R breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whipstitch\u000achest wall", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (3.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). There is a short stitch\u000adesignating the superior margin, long stitch designating the lateral margin,\u000aand a whipstitch designating the posterior margin. There is a needle\u000alocalization wire in place entering through the superior lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen and extends through the medial inferior aspect of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen has been previously inked per pathology protocol by the surgeon\u000a(superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial orange, anterior blue,\u000aand posterior black). The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior. The cut surface has tan/yellow homogenous focal areas and dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue adjacent to the needle localization wire at the inferior\u000amedial aspect of the specimen. The fibrous tissue constitutes approximately\u000a80% of the breast parenchyma. No definitive lesions or areas of disruption are\u000agrossly identified. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS. Blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include radiographed areas of\u000acalcification.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a4/2/2007\u000a[report_end]
