ED_DATE cm).\u000aAdjacent to this area on the inferior portion is a foci of hemorrhage (0.3 x\u000a0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The area of nodularity is about the lateral superior portion of\u000athe specimen. The areas of interest approach the lateral, inferior, posterior,\u000asuperior margins within less than REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is composed of 90%\u000aadipose tissue, 10% fibrous tissue. The entire (100%) specimen is submitted\u000afor microcscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, perpendicular, may appear green, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  rest of the specimen submitted from anterior to posterior,\u000aincluding areas of interest, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000adwu\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
