VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B TWOHIG MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a1 CM PALPABLE IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, well differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade I/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade), is present and\u000ais not associated with calcifications or necrosis.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Palpable 10 mm mass UIQ right breast. History of surgical biopsy for\u000acalcifications in 1998 showing ALH right breast (Faulkner) (reviewed as\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. 10 mm, palpable irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Upper inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue in yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of multiple yellow-white irregular\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000ayellow cassette. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/7/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/11/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
