VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (3 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S).\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive):\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - anterior, superior, inferior, medial\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - posterior (0.2 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), lateral (0.1 cm,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - posterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLobular carcinoma in situ is absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes ? Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: Perineural invasion is identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 year old female with right breast cancer, invasive carcinoma with\u000aductal and lobular features. Patient with history of previous ALH in 1998.\u000aOperation: #1. Right axilla sentinel node biopsy.\u000a#2. Right breast wire located lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right axilla sentinel lymph node #1.\u000aB/2. Right axilla sentinel lymph node #2.\u000aC/3. Right breast wire localized lumpectomy *Short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and clip in specimen - wire intact. Report called to Dr.\u000aGolshan by Dr. Ritner REMOVED_DATE  at 5:00 PM.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in parts, each labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Rt axilla sentinel lymph node #1", consists of an irregular\u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed pink/tan smooth rubbery\u000anodule consistent with lymph node (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible lymph node serially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Rt axilla sentinel lymph node #2", consists of an irregular\u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed pink/tan smooth rubbery\u000anodule consistent with lymph node (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000atrisected, and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "right breast wire localized lumpectomy short suture superior\u000along suture lateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (3.8 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). There is a short suture\u000adesignating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral\u000amargin. There is a needle localization wire entering through the lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting through the medial posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior\u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and\u000athe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior. The cut surface\u000ais tan/yellow and homogeneous with a focal area of dense white ill-defined\u000afibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly abuts the lateral and\u000aposterior margins and comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin. Within the dense white fibrous tissue is a metallic clip. No\u000aadditional lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections superior to inferior, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude fibrous area, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include radiographed area with metallic clip,\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
