VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aNo residual carcinoma present.\u000aFocal microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aSkeletal muscle, negative for tumor.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (residual)\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 2 points\u000aLVI - Present\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- As focus of lymphovascular invasion\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) to new inferior margin\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aEstimated overall size - <0.1 cm (single minute focus, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - New inferior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity changes\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 year old woman s/p REMOVED_DATE  left breast re-excision of multiple\u000amargins revealing 1. Medial margin - poorly differentiated grade III/III IDC,\u000ano LVI; intermediate nuclear grade DCIS with close margin; 2. Inferior margin\u000arevealing poorly differentiated grade III/III IDC with LVI + margin;\u000aintermediate nuclear grade DCIS with close margin.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left medial shave margin, whip stitch new margin plus scar.\u000aB/2. Inferior shaved margin, whip stitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "left medial shaved margin, whipstitch new margin plus scar". The\u000aspecimen consists of two fragments of tissue, the first, a pink/white skin\u000aellipse (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) has no gross abnormalities. The second part is a\u000ayellow/red fatty breast tissue fragment (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is oriented\u000aper surgeon with a whipstitch on the new margin (inked black). The old\u000aresection margin was inked blue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal no gross\u000aabnormalities. The entire specimen is submitted for review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin ellipse, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "inferior shaved margin, whipstitch new margin". The specimen consists\u000aof one fragment of yellow/red fatty adipose tissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), that\u000ais partially disrupted. The specimen is oriented per surgeon with a whipstitch\u000aon the new margin (inked black). The old resection margin was inked blue. The\u000aspecimen is uninked on the disrupted internal aspect of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Marginal tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aKG/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
