VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLODA, MASSIMO, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aSevere atypical ductal hyperplasia (0.3 cm focu), with\u000aassociated microcalcifications.\u000aADH is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior/lateral margins.\u000aRadial scar.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aLevels examined.\u000aSpecimen radiograph is reviewed.\u000aCase reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson of Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with left breast calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core\u000abiopsy showed ADH, intraductal papillomas.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left needle directed breast biopsy, inking per path\u000aprotocol (short suture/superior; long suture/lateral; whipstitch/deep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and wire in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GREISMAN,HARVEY A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left needle directed breast biopsy - short=superior,\u000along=lateral, whipstitch=deep margin, inking per path", and consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm marked\u000awith a short suture designated superior, long suture designated lateral, and a\u000awhipstitch designated deep by the surgeon. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. A needle localization wire is in place. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a specimen radiograph. Sections reveal unremarkable tan/pink\u000afibrofatty tissue. The specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast biopsy, mult frags, ESS\u000ahg\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
