VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BG-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Kenneth R Lee, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST AND WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND\u000aCALCIFICATION, MEDIAL":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications, apocrine metaplasia and\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.2 cm).\u000aNote: There is no malignancy.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST AND WIRE LOCALIZATION EXCISINO FOR A CLIP\u000aLATERAL":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications, apocrine metaplasia and\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aNote: There is no malignancy.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester of Breast Pathology.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast masses x 2.\u000aOperation: Needle-localized excision right breast masses x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1) Medial wire localization - right (FS) to mammo, path\u000a#2) Lateral wire localization right to mammo and path\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1) Ca++ clip in specimen. JM\u000a#2) Clip in specimen. JM/JMS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. right medial wire localization (FS) mammo, path", consists\u000aof one unoriented breast excision specimen (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle\u000alocalization wire in place. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a\u000aclip and calcifications near the tip of the wire. The specimen is composed of\u000a90% adipose tissue and 10% fibrous tissue, and contains approximately seven\u000asmall white gel foam fragments near the tip of the wire in a cavitated area\u000a(0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No masses or lesions are identified grossly, however,\u000are-radiographing of the specimen demonstrates the clip in section number two\u000a(near tip of wire with gel foam) of ten, and calcifications in section number\u000afive. The clip is on the margin of the specimen, and the calcifications are in\u000athe center of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest resection margin. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted in ten levels (approximately REMOVED_DATE cm in thickness\u000aeach).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 1, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 2 with clip, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 2, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 3 with gel foam in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 4 with gel foam, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 4, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 5 with calcifications, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue level 6, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: levels 6 and 7, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue level 7, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue level 8, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: levels 8 and 9, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 9, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 10, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. lateral right wire localization to mammo and path",\u000aconsists of an unoriented breast excision specimen (6.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000aneedle wire localization in place as well as multiple gel foam pieces at the\u000atip of the wire. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a clip\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the tip of the localization wire as well as a dense\u000aregion surrounding the clip with no calcifications. The specimen consists of\u000aapproximately 95% adipose tissue and 5% fibrous tissue, and contains a\u000ahemorrhagic biopsy cavity (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with multiple gel beads. The\u000abiopsy site is located near the tip of the localization wire, and is touching\u000athe nearest inked margin. The specimen is re-radiographed, but no clip is\u000aidentified. There are no calcifications on the re-radiograph, but the area\u000anear the gel foam appears radiodense. The specimen is entirely submitted in\u000atwelve levels with level one starting at the end nearest the biopsy cavity.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 1, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 2 with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 3 with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 3, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 4 with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 4, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 5 with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 5, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 6 with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 6, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 7, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 8, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 9, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 10, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 11, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: level 12, 1 frag, ESS\u000aaf/jl\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kenneth R Lee M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
