VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (including FSA):\u000aOne (1) Lymph node negative for tumor\u000a(3 H&E levels examined).\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aAND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODE\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Cribriform, Papillary, Micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Present-multiple foci (Blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE (including part A)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aSkin negative for tumor\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmic REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aC. ADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST SKIN:\u000aSkin with scar; negative for tumor\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Extensive DCIS, Lt breast.\u000aOperation: SNB; total mastex/Lt\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Extensive DCIS, Lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left sentinel lymph node (FS).\u000aB/2) Left breast, short stitch - superior, long - lateral.\u000aC/3) Additional lt breast skin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node(s), negative for tumor.\u000aArrival time: 8:43\u000aReport time: 9:05\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aThe specimen, Part A, "Left sentinel lymph node", consists of one tan/yellow\u000afragment of adipose tissue (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one lymph node (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was sectioned inked and entirely submitted frozen\u000asection review and designated as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fat, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast, short stitch equals superior, long equals lateral", the\u000aspecimen consists of one radical mastectomy (1400 grams; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat is oriented with sutures; short equals superior, long equals lateral.\u000aThere is an unremarkable skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In addition,\u000athere is an unremarkable nipple (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep fascial margin\u000ais without skeletal muscle and is inked black. The specimen was radiographed\u000ato reveal a clip in the central upper breast. The clip was identified in a\u000afirm mass (designated as mass #1) that is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe deep margin. Approximately 90% of this area was submitted. Approximately\u000a9 cm away in the lower outer quadrant is another firm mass (mass #2) that\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. 75% of this\u000aarea was submitted. In the upper inner quadrant, approximately 10 cm away from\u000amass #2 (7.5 cm from mass #1), there is another firm white mass (mass #3) that\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Approximately\u000a75% of this area was submitted. In addition, there is a hemorrhagic area (2.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) located in the central upper breast and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is approximately 80% adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral to mass #1, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #1, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep to mass #1, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin of mass #1, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial to mass #1, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #2, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin to mass #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral to mass #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial to mass #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hemorrhagic area, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue between mass #1 and #3, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #3, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin of mass #3, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral to mass #3, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Candidate lymph nodes, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial to mass #1, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aThe specimen, Part C, "Additional left breast skin", consists of four fragments\u000aof white/tan skin measuring in range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aOverlying skin is unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted for\u000areview.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aKG/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/13/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCAL) (2+)\u000aNote: The areas of microinvasion are very small and are no longer present on\u000athe deeper levels used for the immunoperoxidase studies or deeper levels\u000a(blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
