VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST", TOTAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia and gynecomastoid hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aPseudoangiomatoid stromal hyperplasia.\u000aTwo 92) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST", TOTAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia and gynecomastoid hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aCalcificationos noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aPseudoangiomatoid stromal hyperplasia.\u000aThree (3) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Strong family history for breast cancer - mother and two sisters.\u000aPatient has had bilateral breast biopsies, most recently PASH at BID.\u000aOperation: Bilateral total mastectomy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast (suture/tail of breast)\u000a2) Right breast (suture/tail)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "left breast (suture/tail of breast)", consists of a mastectomy\u000aspecimen consisting of breast (26.5 x 25 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin ellipse (25.4 x\u000a12.4 cm), nipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), and axillary tail (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe deep surface of the specimen is bordered by a smooth fascial plane with no\u000amuscle. The deep surface is inked in black, and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed mass (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with little\u000astromal reaction, lying REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Representative sections\u000afrom this mass, the deep margin underlying the mass, and all four quadrants are\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis. Dissection of the presumed axillary tail\u000areveals only two definite lymph nodes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro 3: deep margin underlying mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: 2 lymph nodes, 2 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, "right breast (suture/tail)", consists of a right breast (26.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin (27.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), nipple (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), and small\u000aaxillary tail (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep surface is a smooth fascial\u000aplane. This plane is inked in black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a cystic breast, but no gross mass lesions. Representative sections of\u000athe breast are submitted for histologic analysis. The axillary tail is\u000adissected for lymph nodes, and these are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  outer upper quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro 22: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 23: 3 potential lymph nodes from small axillary tail, 3 frag, RSS\u000adwa\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
