VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION, RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE, FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU, present in blocks #5 and #10.\u000aEXTENSIVE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA present in nine of thirteen (9:13)\u000ablocks.\u000aCalcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAll margins are negative (>0.3 cm) for severely atypical foci.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "CEPHALAD MARGIN":\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia in one of four (1:4) blocks (block 15).\u000aApocrine metaplasia, cysts, and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: Case reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57-year-old black female with DCIS right breast.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision, right breast mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue.\u000a2. Cephalad margin, right breast mass.\u000aCa++ in specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue and skin measuring 9 cm from medial to lateral, 6 cm from\u000ainferior to superior and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The skin measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and contains an area consistent with\u000ascar measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. This appears well-healed. There is an accompanying\u000aradiograph showing calcifications in the specimen. The radiograph also shows\u000aa needle. When the specimen was received, the needle was not present in the\u000aspecimen. A radiograph is taken to identify any calcifications. These are\u000aidentified in the sample and coincide with the areas of fibrous tissue. The\u000aspecimen is approximately 80% fat and 20% fibrous tissue. There are no masses.\u000aThere is a single area of possible prior biopsy site. This is located adjacent\u000ato the medial and superior aspects of the specimen and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. This is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin,\u000a7.0 cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The entire\u000abiopsy cavity, with closest margins as well as possible areas of calcification\u000awith closest margins, is submitted. Representative sections of the remainder\u000aof the specimen are also submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  potential biopsy cavity, with closest margins, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aThis corresponds also to the first area of calcifications.\u000aMicro 6: lateral margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  second area of calcification with closest margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  third area of calcification with closest margins, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: additional posterior and anterior margins closest to the second and\u000athird area of calcification, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: anterior margin (skin), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, cephalad margin, right breast mass", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon with red surface indicating superior, black\u000aposterior and orange medial. The side not inked corresponds to the area\u000aabutting the previous specimen as per surgeon. This area is inked blue, there\u000aare no masses in this specimen. The specimen is approximately 90% fat and 10%\u000afibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections, 6 frags, RSS.\u000amir\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
