e, unit number, and "right breast site B", and consists of two (2) brown\u000acassettes. One cassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.7 x\u000a1.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 3: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: DENISON, CHRISTINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
