VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE", NEEDLE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving a focus of epithelial hyperplasia\u000a(slide 4).\u000aAtypical apocrine adenosis associated with calcifications.\u000aCysts, intraductal papilloma.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, BWH Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast LCIS, microcalcifications in left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue - stitch short/superior; long/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcification in specimen. CG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a\u000asingle piece of breast lumpectomy tissue with a wire localized to the area of\u000acalcification. There is one long stitch which designates the lateral and one\u000ashort stitch designating the superior margin. The specimen measures 4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm, and is 70% fibrous with no masses palpated. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals the localization wire and a cluster of\u000acalcifications.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area corresponding to the wire localized calcification, 2 frags,\u000aESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, 3 frags, ESS\u000arfi\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
