VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aSUMMARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, MIXED DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - moderate\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - n/a\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - n/a\u000aSkin invasion - n/a\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - n/a\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm): - superior, inferior, anterior, lateral, medial\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm): - posterior (0.2 cm; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present, in association with invasive\u000acarcinoma\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia,\u000aM?nckeberg's arteriosclerosis\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aB) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY - NEW POSTERIOR AND MEDIAL MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy, after needle localization.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast mass - long lateral, short superior - FS\u000aB/2) Left breast biopsy - new posterior and medial margin - stitch on margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass in specimen.\u000aRadiologic interpretation by: C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, sublabeled "#1 Left Breast Mass", consists a yellow/pink fragment of\u000afibrofatty soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented by the surgeon\u000aby two sutures designating the superior and lateral aspects. The specimen is\u000ainked in the Pathology Department per the pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The inferior aspect of the specimen is white and\u000afirm, without discrete nodules. In the same container is a needle localization\u000awire, which is not piercing the specimen at the time it is received in the\u000aPathology Department. Accompanying this specimen is a radiograph with the\u000apatient's name and unit number, documenting a soft tissue mass with a needle\u000alocalization wire, and a rim of calcifications and a stellate opacification,\u000awhich is encircled by the Radiologist. The specimen is entirely and serially\u000asubmitted from medial to lateral for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial to lateral left breast mass, 14 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, sublabeled "#2 Left Breast Biopsy", consists of one fragment of\u000ared/yellow fibrofatty soft tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented by\u000athe surgeon with a stitch on one surface, designating the "new posterior and\u000amedial margin", according to the Form 86 Requisition. The old margin is inked\u000ain blue, the new margin (indicated by suture) is inked in black. The specimen\u000ais entirely, serially submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New posterior and medial margins, serially submitted, 5 frags in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 4 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000apab/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Lucian Chirieac M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFIRST ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. DEBORAH DILLON\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
