VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JUDY E GARBER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, THREE EXCISIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aWIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aApocrine metaplasia in cysts.\u000aBy report, epithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aFocal core biopsy site changes are present, transected at the inferomedial\u000amargin.\u000aNote: The patient has a REMOVED_DATE cm irregular mass at 1:00. A core needle biopsy\u000aperformed at BWH showed atypical lobular hyperplasia and cysts, but no definite\u000acorrelate for a mass (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). This site was marked with a clip.\u000aBy report, the specimen radiograph did not show the clip in this specimen or in\u000athe specimen below designated "posterior lateral margin". In this specimen,\u000athe core biopsy site is transected at the inferomedial margin. An additional\u000aportion of the core needle site is present in the specimen reported below.\u000aNEW MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aNOTE: The patient has nipple discharge. A ductogram is reported to show a\u000afilling defect and a cytology specimen showed "abundant papillary clusters of\u000aatypical ductal cells" (Faulkner Hospital REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAccording to the operative report, this specimen was intended to resect the\u000aarea of the filling defect. A correlate for an intraductal lesion is not\u000areported.\u000aPOSTERIOR LATERAL MARGIN:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aCore biopsy site changes are present and the site is transected at the new\u000amargin (green inked).\u000aA complex sclerosing lesion (0.4 cm) is adjacent to the core needle biopsy\u000asite.\u000aNote: By report, the clip was not present in this specimen. The core site is\u000apresent. It is unclear how the core site in this specimen is related to the\u000acore site present in the main specimen.\u000aThe complex sclerosing lesion is a possible correlate for the irregular mass.\u000aClinical and radiologic correlation is suggested to ensure that the targeted\u000alesion has been removed.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left nipple spontaneous discharge. Prior core with ALH.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: LCIS and ALH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are nine (9) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"\u000athrough "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) left breast wire guided localized excision\u000a(4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) left breast, medial margin, excision (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report\u000abearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/18/2007\u000a[report_end]
