VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:00 MID OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade),\u000awith focal necrosis and calcifications, is present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000aDCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu EQUIVOCAL (2+)\u000aNote: The patient has a prior history of DCIS, ER and PR positive and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu 2+, presenting as calcifications in the lower outer quadrant in 2005\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The histologic appearance and immunoprofile of the DCIS in\u000athe current core needle biopsy are consistent with a recurrence of the prior\u000aDCIS. Clinical and radiologic correlation is suggested to determine if the\u000acurrent DCIS is in the area of the prior excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: History of right breast DCIS in REMOVED_DATE year old woman with cluster\u000aof pleomorphic calcifications in the 9:00 position of the right breast.\u000aDifferential diagnosis: indeterminate.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 2 mm, nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 9:00 mid outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted; submitted in formalin at 12:20 p.m. -\u000aWhite cassettes. Cassette A (with Ca++) - 2 samples; cassette B (without Ca++)\u000a- 2 samples.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue, received in\u000atwo white cassettes, each with a white lid, A CA++ (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and B.\u000a(2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast white cassette, A cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast white cassette, B cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 9911\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 06:44:44PM\u000a[report_end]
