VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA with cribriform architecture (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000amicropapillary architecture.\u000aNo residual DCIS is seen.\u000aOther findings:\u000aCore biopsy site changes\u000aExtensive calcifications associated with cysts and columnar cell change with\u000aatypia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. CHEST WALL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, intermediate nuclear grade, with\u000anecrosis and without calcifications is present in one of seven (1:7) blocks as\u000aa single focus (0.4 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, intermediate nuclear grade, with lobular morphology and\u000afocal necrosis is present (approximately REMOVED_DATE cm focus) adjacent to an area of\u000amore classic low nuclear grade LCIS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). This focus of CIS with necrosis shows\u000aabsent membranous staining for E-Cadherin and is strongly positive for ER and\u000aPR and negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (O).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, classic type\u000aE-cadherin negative CARCINOMA IN SITU with necrosis is present <0.1 cm from\u000aboth the black-inked and blue-inked margins (unoriented shave; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is <0.1 cm from the blue-inked margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the black-inked\u000amargin (unoriented shave; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 84 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE R lumpectomy for treatment of ER/PR(+)\u000aHer2/Neu (+), DCIS, declined XRT. REMOVED_DATE  R mammogram revealed calcifications\u000awith REMOVED_DATE  stereotactic core biopsy, diagnosed recurrent DCIS.\u000aOperation: R breast wire-localized lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Recurrent R DCIS.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Entire wire and clip in the specimen. Results called to Dr. Rhei @\u000a12:30 PM on the date of the study. (ILLEGIBLE physician)\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast mass with wire (F.S.); long ? lateral; short ? superior; whip\u000astitch ? deep margin, scar ? anterior.\u000aB/2) Chest wall shave margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast mass", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE \u000a(anterior to posterior) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) cm breast biopsy with a\u000alocalization wire in place, a short suture marking the superior margin, a long\u000asuture marking the lateral margin and a whipstitch marking the deep margin. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a clip adjacent to localization\u000awire on a side aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The medial and\u000alateral margins are removed and the remainder of the specimen is sectioned into\u000anine sections from medial to lateral. The previous biopsy site measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm and is located less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross-sections medial to lateral. Biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (clip\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, REMOVED_DATE frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fragments of breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Chest wall shave margin", consists of an unoriented shave of\u000afibroadipose tissue (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is differentially inked blue on\u000aone surface and black on the other and submitted in its entirety for\u000ahistological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Shave margin (sequential sections), REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aCEL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 06:31:56PM\u000a[report_end]
