re no orienting sutures, but it is presumed that the\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins\u000a(posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange). The anterior and inferior surfaces are partially covered by a\u000ared-pink, scabrous, focally smooth surface (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with prior\u000abiopsy cavity. The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral revealing focal\u000achalky yellow discoloration surrounding the prior biopsy site, consistent with\u000afat necrosis. No definite residual tumor is identified. Specimen is otherwise\u000aapproximately 30% tan-white fibrous tissue and 70% golden yellow fatty tissue.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted serially, from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS\u000aRLR/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/31/2005\u000a[report_end]
