VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCIBAS, EDMUND, SAULIUS, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CIBAS,EDMUND SAULIUS,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST BIOPSY:\u000aMultifocal HIGHLY ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA. See note.\u000aFibrocystic changes with florid ductal hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia,\u000amicrocysts, sclerosing adenosis, micropapillomas, and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aNOTE: All of the available tissue has been processed for histological\u000aexamination. An atypical lobular hyperplasia is identified, characterized\u000aby a proliferation of uniform cells within multiple lobules and ducts,\u000aclosely approaching but not quite forming a pattern recognizable as\u000alobular carcinoma-in-situ. This places the patient at an increased risk\u000a(4-5 times that of the general population) for the subsequent development\u000aof invasive carcinoma. Annual mammography and periodic clinical\u000are-examination every four months is generally recommended.\u000aREF.: Cancer 55:2698, 1985.\u000aO. R. CONSULTATION REPORT:\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
