VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDILLON, DEBORAH, A, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 6:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium and stroma.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aSlides from this case were reviewed at the request of Dr. E. Gombos, who notes\u000athat the tissue in block C represents a separate focus (Area #2). Cores from\u000aArea #1 (blocks A and B) show benign fibrous breast tissue with ductal\u000aepithelial hyperplasia. Calcification in A is associated with benign\u000aepithelium and calcification in B is associated with stroma. Tissue cores\u000afrom Area #2 (block C) show benign fibrous breast tissue with epithelial\u000ahyperplasia. No calcifications are seen in tissue from Area #2.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 72-year-old with left upper outer quadrant ADH and complex sclerosing\u000alesion - status post excision of these lesions. Now with cluster of\u000afaint, amorphous, indistinct calcifications in left 6:00 position.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic.\u000aOperative findings: Calcifications.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Calcifications x 2.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast - calcifications - "faint, amorphous" in A -\u000a"coarse" in B - 3 blue cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTEN,ADAM,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left Breast", and consists of three (3) blue cassettes. The first\u000ablue cassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented,\u000ayellow/tan fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000asecond blue cassette is labeled "B ca++" and contains mutliple\u000ayellow/tan fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000athird blue cassette labeled "C" contains multiple yellow/tan, focally\u000ahemorrhagic, fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: "C", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: BABAGBEMI, T.KEMI M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
