VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions, and atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypia.\u000aCysts.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions with atypia and atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aNOTE: Dr. Andrea Richardson, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed this case\u000aand concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 54 yo postmenopausal female s/p REMOVED_DATE  bilateral core biopsies for\u000aevaluation of calcifications, L lower inner quadrant revealing severely\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on DCIS and R upper outer quadrant\u000arevealing ADH. Excision recommended for each.\u000aOperation: Bilateral WL excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral abnormal mammograms.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. R breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whip stitch deep margin.\u000a2. L breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whip stitch deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aLEFT BREAST: Clip in specimen. BT/jms\u000aRIGHT BREAST: Clip is seen in right specimen. S. Raza, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one is labeled "#1 right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whip\u000astitch deep margin". The specimen consists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(4.8 cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior). Three sutures placed in the specimen by the surgeon denote in the\u000asuperior, lateral, and deep orientations to the specimen. In addition, the\u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon, presumably per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A wire is present in the\u000aspecimen which is removed. A specimen radiograph is taken and the clips as\u000awell as multiple areas of calcification are located. No tumor mass is grossly\u000aevident. Representative sections are submitted, including all areas of\u000acalcification identified on radiography.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of calcification, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: area of clip, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional areas of calcification, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional fibrous areas of breast, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two is labeled "#2 left breast tissue, long lateral, short superior, whip\u000astitch deep margin". It consists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 cm\u000aanterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior).\u000aThree sutures are present in the specimen designating superior, lateral and\u000adeep margins of the specimen. A wire is also present in the specimen which is\u000aremoved. In addition, the specimen has been inked previously by the surgeon,\u000apresumably per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. A specimen radiograph is taken and the clip is identified and\u000aremoved. No discrete mass is present in the specimen which is serially\u000asectioned and entirely submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS. The area of the clip is in micros 17&18.\u000adl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
