VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Marisa R Nucci, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCysts with associated calcium oxalate.\u000aColumnar cell change with focal associated microcalcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated microcalcifications.\u000aThere are benign glands in a perineural location (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNOTE: Evaluation of the large duct profiles at the specimen edges is limited by\u000acautery artifact.\u000aCase was also reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old female screening mammo calcs L breast LOQ; 6 months f/u\u000amammo - calcs slightly increased; posterior location not amenable to core\u000abiopsy. Wire loc excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire directed excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abn L mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1. Left breast tissue (short superior; long lateral; whip deep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications and wire within the specimen.\u000a[signature illegible}\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. left breast tissue", and consists of one breast excisional biopsy (3.2\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with orienting suture in place and a localizing wire entering\u000athrough the inferolateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is received\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A radiograph is received. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal an area of firm, vaguely nodular tan/white fibrous tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) that comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the lateral margin, and is distant from the superior margin. An area of\u000ahemorrhage corresponding with the localizing wire tract abuts the fibrous\u000alesion at its medial aspect. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000aapproximately 50% unremarkable adipose tissue and 50% firm white fibrous\u000atissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast excisional biopsy submitted from inferior to superior,\u000amult frags, ESS\u000alys/jl\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Marisa R Nucci M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
