VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (single focus), columnar alteration of lobules\u000awith prominent snouts and secretions, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPapilloma with hyalinized stromal cores.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (including examination of margins).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51 year old female, microcalcifications left breast. No diagnosis\u000ayet.\u000aOperation: L breast biopsy with needle placement.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast microcalcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast biopsy after needle localization\u000a(long/lateral, short/superior).\u000aRadiology report: Calcifications seen in specimen radiograph. AJ.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber, and "#1 - left breast biopsy after needle localization (long/lateral\u000aand short/superior)", and consists of one yellow/tan lumpectomy specimen (5.0 x\u000a2.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a short stitch indicating superior, and a long stitch\u000aindicating lateral. The specimen is inked by the pathologist per the pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is\u000aa wire protruding from the lateral aspect of the specimen, and the specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph and a pink form signed by the radiologist\u000aindicating that the calcifications are in the specimen. There is an area of\u000ahemorrhage (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen is composed of predominantly white/tan\u000afibrous tissue which grossly extends to all margins. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro #1: Lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: Inferior, superior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3: Inferior, anterior, posterior, superior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #4: Anterior, superior, posterior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5: Superior, inferior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #6: Anterior, posterior, superior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #7: Superior, inferior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #8: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajdr/\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
