VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aCore biopsy site changes present.\u000aCalcifications associated with normal epithelium.\u000aFocal columnar cell change with atypia and papillary hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aNo residual atypical proliferation seen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID slides reviewed).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 65-year-old post-menopausal woman A/P REMOVED_DATE  L breast core Bx's\u000arevealing ADH.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast WL bx; short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral; whip\u000astitch on deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Hookwire and clip in specimen. Called to OR 11:30 A.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. Left breast WL", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (anterior to\u000aposterior) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) cm breast\u000abiopsy with a localization wire in place. A short stitch designates the\u000asuperior margin, a long stitch designating lateral, and a whipstitch designates\u000athe deep margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a clip in the central portion of the specimen adjacent\u000ato the localization wire. The specimen is sectioned into eight slices from\u000aanterior to posterior. A REMOVED_DATE cubic centimeter region consistent with the\u000aprevious biopsy site and containing the clip (slice #4) is identified REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and\u000a1.6 cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists 90% of\u000aunremarkable adipose tissue and 10% dense white fibrous tissue. Gross\u000aphotographs are taken. The specimen is submitted in its entirety for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCEL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 21, 2009 at 12:03:58PM\u000a[report_end]
