VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES RECEIVED FROM MORTON HOSPITAL, TAUNTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY (96:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: According to the original report, the specimen radiograph did not\u000ashow any abnormalities.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES RECEIVED FROM STURDY MEMORIAL HOSPITAL, ATTLEBORO, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aMultifocal lactational changes (blocks A to C; see NOTE).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block D).\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aNumerous benign calcifications.\u000aA prior biopsy site is present.\u000aNOTE: The areas of lactational changes are somewhat unusual in that in\u000asome areas the lactational changes involve areas of epithelial\u000ahyperplasia. Of note, the changes are restricted to the lobular units and\u000ado not involve the terminal ducts.\u000aThe cytologic and architectural features are felt to be insufficient for a\u000adiagnosis of DCIS.\u000aLactational changes can be seen in response to pregnancy or hormone use\u000abut are also seen as an incidental finding.\u000aThis case was also reviewed at the BWH staff conference.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aApocrine adenosis with numerous calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aLobules with calcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 47-year-old female with history of multiple bilateral breast\u000abiopsies: left breast biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  at BWH (benign); right breast wire\u000alocalized biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  (Morton Hospital) for inner lower quadrant\u000acalcifications showing fibrocystic changes; right breast excision for\u000acalcifications on REMOVED_DATE  (Sturdy Memorial Hospital) with initial pathology\u000aread as fibrocystic changes, but review of slides on REMOVED_DATE  interpreted as\u000amultifocal high nuclear grade DCIS with positive margins (Sturdy Memorial\u000aHospital REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). After change in reading patient subsequently had right\u000abreast core biopsy of calcifications in UOQ and UIQ (read as benign and\u000areviewed by Dr. Schnitt as having "florid ductal hyperplasia"). Also,\u000apatient recently underwent left breast core biopsy (upper) for calcifications,\u000aand pathology showed fibrocystic changes. Please review all her pathology\u000aslides, especially the REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (6/12/96). Slides to Dr. Lester.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aPlease call patient (508-824-4843) after the slides are reviewed so that she\u000acan pick up the slides herself. Do not send slides back to original hospitals.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CAI,YUN-CAI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCall patient for pickup of slides at REMOVED_DATE \u000aReceived from Morton Hospital are three glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "Re", corresponding to right\u000abreast tissue collected on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name. Also received is a consultation report from\u000aSturdy Memorial HOspital numbered "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  concerning these\u000aslides.\u000aReceived from Sturdy Memorial Hospital are sixteen glass slides.\u000aFour slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A", "B", "C" and "D",\u000acorresponding to right breast tissue collected on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aFour slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" and\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2", corresponding to left breast core biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aSix slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a2", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE " and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE ", corresponding to right breast core biopsies\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name. Also received is a consultation report from Beth Israel\u000aDeaconess Medical Center numbered "99-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  concerning\u000athese slides.\u000aReports to: HARRIS, JAY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000a[report_end]
