ce,\u000awhich enters the superolateral aspect of the specimen and exits the\u000ainferolateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed\u000a(per radiologist "distortion present in specimen". The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit approximately 45% diffusely dense\u000alumpy white/tan fibrous stroma extending to all surgical margins, and\u000aapproximately 55% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are grossly identified. The needle localization wire traverses a focus\u000aof dense stroma towards the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is\u000aentirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: specimen sequentially submitted from medial to lateral (dense\u000astroma traversed by needle localization wire in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Travis J Hollmann M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
