e specimen, long suture marks the lateral aspect, and a\u000awhipstitch marks the deep (posterior) margin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior. There is a single wire present in the specimen, which\u000aenters anteriorly. A radiograph shows the wire passing through an area of\u000acalcifications in an area of density and a clip adjacent to the wire. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior into six slices, such\u000athat slice #1 includes the superior margin and slice #6 includes the inferior\u000amargin. There is a firm, well-circumscribed, pink/white mass, which measures\u000a1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This grossly abuts the anterior and inferior margins, is\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. Re-radiography\u000aof the serially sectioned specimen indicates the presence of the clip. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 (superior margin), 9 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, anterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, posterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, anterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, posterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, anterior including main mass, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, central tissue between mass and ill-defined nodularity, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, posterior including area of ill-defined nodularity, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, anterior including mass and clip site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, central, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, posterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 (inferior margin), perpendicular sections, 4 frags\u000aper cassette, ESS.\u000aSBL/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/27/2008\u000a[report_end]
