VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (focal), epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine\u000acysts, and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast tissue - taken by mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ & 2 wires in specimen. epf\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BRINSTER,NOOSHIN K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "1 right breast tissue", and consists of a breast excision specimen (red\u000ato green margin REMOVED_DATE cm, orange to yellow margin REMOVED_DATE cm, and black to blue\u000amargin REMOVED_DATE cm) without any orienting sutures. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon with red, green, black, blue, yellow, and\u000aorange colors. The colors are undesignated and there are no orienting sutures\u000ain the specimen. There are two localizing wires in the specimen which is\u000aaccompanied by a radiologic plain film. The wires will be designated as wire\u000aA and wire B and correspond to following margins: wire A (simple radiologic\u000amass, one calcification - corresponding to margins inked yellow, black and\u000agreen) and wire B (complex radiologic mass, mulitple calcifications -\u000acorresponding to margins inked red, orange and blue). The specimen consists\u000aof yellow/white adipose tissue. There is a discrete white/gray nodule (0.5 x\u000a0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) toward the green margin. There are ill-defined fibrotic areas\u000athroughout the remainder of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, adjacent to wire A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 6, wire A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, wire A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 8, wire A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: portion of slice 9, wire A, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: portion of slice 9, wire A, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 10, adjacent to wire A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 14, adjacent to wire B, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 15, wire B, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 16, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: portion of slice 4 containing cyst, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 20: portion of slice 4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 11, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 12, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 13, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 27: slices 1&2, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 28: slice 3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 29: slice 17, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
