VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU present as a microscopic focus in\u000aone of five blocks (block 1).\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative, with duct dilatation,\u000ainterlobular fibrosis, sclerosing adenosis, and microcalcifications\u000ain association with benign ducts.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT NEEDLE DIRECTED BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA present as a single microscopic focus,\u000atoo small to grade, and present within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inked margin\u000a(block 8).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid type, intermediate grade nuclei,\u000apresent multifocally and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inked margin in\u000afour of five blocks (blocks REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SCALP LESION":\u000aSkin with cicatrix and foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aNo residual carcinoma seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast biopsy\u000a2. Left needle directed breast biopsy\u000a3. Scalp lesion (short superior long anterior)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aLEFT NEEDLE DIRECTED BREAST BIOPSY:\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aGross only.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "right breast biopsy", consists of one fragment of\u000awhite/yellow fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast biopsy, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of one\u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue with a needle localization wire in place and\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "scalp lesion short stitch superior, long anterior",\u000aconsists of a tan/pink skin ellipse, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm (depth), with\u000aa long stitch designating anterior and a short stitch designating superior.\u000aThe long stitch is now designated 12 o'clock. The 3 o'clock half of the\u000aspecimen is inked in black and the 9 o'clock half is inked in blue.\u000aMicro 11: 12 o'clock tip, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: 6 o'clock tip, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of ellipse, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
