VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LUMPECTOMY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBUSAM, KLAUS, JOHANNES, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BUSAM,KLAUS JOHANNES,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RE-EXCISION MASS, LEFT BREAST":\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribiform and clinging type, high\u000anuclear grade, focally present in the lateral en-face margin and near the\u000aprevious biopsy site.\u000aNo invasive component is identified.\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative.\u000aGranulation tissue with foreign body giant cell reaction and fat necrosis,\u000aconsistent with old biopsy site.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEVEL ONE LYMPH NODE":\u000aSix lymph nodes with no carcinoma present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Re-excision left breast mass-short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral.\u000a2. Level 1 lymph node.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SAMPSON,BARBARA ALEXANDRA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fresh in two parts, each labelled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe first part, labelled "re-excision mass left breast" and consists of an\u000aorienting mass of yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3 cm. At\u000aone aspect of the mass of soft tissue is a tan skin ellipse, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain length x 2 cm in diameter. In the middle of the tan skin ellipse is a\u000awell-healed REMOVED_DATE cm in length surgical scar. 2 cm deep to the skin surface is a\u000ayellow/tan hemorrhagic biopsy cavity that measures 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Grossly there is no tumor present.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow adipose tissue with focal\u000aareas that are fibrous.\u000aMicro #1: Lateral margin, en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #2: Medial margin, en face, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #3: Superior margin, en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #4: Inferior margin, en face, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #5: Deep margin, en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #6: Biopsy cavity with respect to superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #7: Biopsy cavity with respect to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicros #8-9: Biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe second part is labelled "level 1 lymh node" and consists of a tan/yellow\u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Eight lymph nodes\u000aare identified, the greatest REMOVED_DATE cm in dimension.\u000aMicros #11-12: One lymph node per cass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #13: Four lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicros #14-15: One lymph node per cass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LUMPECTOMY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: AXILLARY NODES\u000a[report_end]
