VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (#1, ONE SPECIMEN):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, and\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU WITH MICROINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes: - Solid\u000aNuclear grade: - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS: - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS: - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm): - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS):\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) Anterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) Medial, focal (block 5)\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) Posterior, focal (block 3)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present, single-focus (block 4)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Calcifications in benign epithelium, core biopsy site.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2): - Pending\u000aNOTE: There is a single of invasive lobular carcinoma measuring less than\u000a0.1 cm (block 4) which is separate from the area of DCIS and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin.\u000a#2. RIGHT BREAST RE-EXCISION NEW POSTERIOR MARGIN (#2, ONE SPECMIEN):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA 3 FOCI, and\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, and\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA:\u000aSize: - REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - Yes\u000aHistologic Type: - Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR): - I(Well)\u000aNuclear Grade: - Low\u000aEIC: - N/A\u000aLymphovascular invasion: - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion: - N/A\u000aSkin invasion: - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion: - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive): - Positive (ink on tumor) new posterior\u000amargin, focal (block 18)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes: - Solid\u000aNuclear grade: - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS: - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS: - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm): - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS): Negative (>0.3 cm) new posterior margin\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium, core biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION: REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa(multifocal)pNxMX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2): - Pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (blocks 4 and 18):\u000aEstrogen receptor Positive.\u000aProgesterone receptor Negative.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Negative (0).\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right needle directed breast biopsy, inked per path\u000aprotocol.\u000a2. Right breast biopsy, stitch at new posterior margin.\u000aRadiology: Calcifications are seen in specimen.... C. Dennison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by IAFRATE,ANTHONY JOHN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right needle directed breast biopsy", and consists of a\u000asingle fragment of pink-tan fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is received inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a single localization wire in\u000aplace. Along the medial edge of the specimen there is an irregular firm tan\u000aarea (1.5 cm in greatest dimension) with focal areas of hemorrhage and\u000anecrosis. The mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and inferior margins.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable fibroadipose\u000atissue.\u000aMicro 1: mass and closest medial and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of mass, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: closest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: closest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: closest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: closest anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast biopsy, stitch at new posterior margin",\u000aand consists of a single fragment of pink-yellow fibroadipose tissue (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a single orienting suture designating the new posterior\u000amargin, and the new posterior margin is inked black and the anterior surface\u000ais inked blue. There is an irregular firm tan-pink area (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich contains a REMOVED_DATE cm cavity and focal areas of hemorrhage and necrosis. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
