VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aHyalinized fibroadenoma.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aOld biopsy cavity.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aTraumatic neuroma (1.0 cm).\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aSUMMARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (Well)\u000aNuclear Grade - Low\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, papillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes:\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 8\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCysts.\u000aOld biopsy cavity with foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Report pending\u000aNOTE: The invasive carcinoma was present adjacent to (along the inferior\u000aaspect of) the prior biopsy site.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 26):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: The absence of hormone receptors is unusual for a well differentiated\u000alobular carcinoma. Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive\u000afor estrogen and progesterone receptors indicating that the tissue\u000aimmunogenicity is intact.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Bilateral mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left invasive ductal carcinoma with DCIS, s/p lumpectomy\u000awith axillary lymph node dissection; right DCIS and LCIS with minimal lobular\u000ainvasive carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast\u000a#2) Right breast\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LAZAR,ALEXANDER J FAULKNER,M.D.,PH.D\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast", consists of a 1250g left mastectomy\u000aspecimen (22.5 cm superior to inferior, 24 cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with a white/tan skin ellipse (19 cm lateral to medial x\u000a8.5 cm) containing an inferiorly located areola (5 cm in diameter) with\u000aretracted nipple (1 cm in diameter). Stitches are left by the surgeon for\u000aorientation (short = superior, long = lateral). Along the medial inferior\u000aaspect of the skin ellipse is a 5 cm well-healed surgical scar. Deep to the\u000ascar is a firm white area (4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) that is consistent with an old\u000abiopsy site. The deep margin of the specimen is a smooth fascial plane with\u000ano skeletal muscle present. The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly\u000awhite and firm, and surrounded by yellow adipose tissue. The deep margin of\u000athe specimen is inked black. This patient has had a previous axillary node\u000adissection on this side however the tissue at the lateral edge is extensively\u000asearched for lymph nodes and a potential lymph node is identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: nipple, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue surrounding old biopsy site, 5 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 7: inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10; outer lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: potential node from axillary region, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast", consists of a 1445g right mastectomy\u000aspecimen (22 cm superior to inferior, 23 cm lateral to medial, and 5 cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with overlying skin ellipse (14.5 cm lateral to medial x\u000a8.5 cm). Stitches are left by the surgeon for orientation (short = superior,\u000along = lateral). The skin ellipse contains a puckered scar (1.5 cm) at the\u000alateral aspect and an areola (7 cm in diameter) with nipple (1.2 cm) in the\u000amedial/inferior portion. Beneath the puckered scar is a fibrotic stellate\u000alesion (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm) consistent with prior biopsy site that extends to\u000athe deep margin and contains a REMOVED_DATE cm cyst. Inferior to the biopsy site is a\u000a2 cm firm suspicious area. The remaining breast parenchyma contains cysts\u000ameasuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter including a blue domed cyst (0.5 cm). The\u000adeep margin of the specimen is a smooth fascial plane with no skeletal muscle\u000aattached. This deep margin is inked black. No axillary section is designated\u000abut the specimen however, the lateral aspect of the specimen is searched for\u000alymph nodes and eight lymph nodes are revealed measuring up to 2 cm in\u000agreatest dimension. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 13: puckered scar leading to old biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  old biopsy site, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 18: inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 20: outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 21: outer lower quadrant inferior to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 22: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 23: 2 lymph nodes, bisected, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 24: 2 lymph nodes, bisected, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 cm mass inferior to biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 27: area superior to biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 28: biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aafl\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
