en is incompletely inked and will be touched up by the prosector\u000aaccording to the orientation designated by the surgeon. The wire enters the\u000aspecimen at the inferolateral aspect, and there is no exit point. The specimen\u000ais somewhat distorted, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm overall (5.1 medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE anterior to posterior). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral into 14 slices, and the tip of the\u000awire is found between slices #8 and #9 at the inferoposterior aspect. The clip\u000ais not grossly identified.\u000aThere is a firm white mass (? fibrosis versus tumor) (5.2 cm x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThis white region extends to margins. Approximately, 40% of the total specimen\u000ais yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The entirety of the white firm tissue will\u000abe submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #1 (margins include M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #2 (margins include M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #3 (S, M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #4 (S, M, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #5 (S, M, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #6 (S, M, A, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 white tissue (S, P, A, I), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #8 (S, A, P, ?I), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 white tissue including region of wire tip (S, A, I, ?P), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 fatty portion inferior to wire tip, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #10 bisected (S, L, I, P, A), 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11 white tissue bisected 