VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Alison Z Young, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY:\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (three HE levels examined).\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, is present adjacent to the prior core needle biopsy site (see\u000anote).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen (EIC negative).\u000aThe margins are free of invasive carcinoma. The closest margin is superior\u000a(0.2 cm).\u000aSkin is present and is not involved by carcinoma.\u000aNote: The radiologic size of the carcinoma prior to core needle biopsy was REMOVED_DATE \u000acm and this is likely the best size for T classification. This carcinoma was\u000apreviously shown to be positive for ER and PR and negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu.\u000aC. RIGHT AXILLA, SKIN EXCISIONS:\u000aFibroepithelial polyps.\u000aD. RIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), REMOVED_DATE cm (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is present (EIC negative).\u000aThe invasive carcinoma is present at the new superior margin.\u000aNote: This carcinoma appears to be a separate focus of invasive carcinoma.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThe patient's carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX with multiple foci of invasion.\u000aE. RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNote: No tumor is seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Carcinoma of right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized exc. Biopsy, sentinel node\u000abiopsy/mapping. Skin tag removal - right axilla.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Sentinal lymph node (FS).\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue (Mammo).\u000aC/3. Skin tags.\u000aD/4. Superior shave margin (R) breast tissue.\u000aE/5. Inferior shave margin (R) breast tissue. (Suture superior).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass, clip and wire are in the center of the specimen.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" (FSA):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: MARISA ROSE NUCCI, M.D.\u000aResident: LYNETTE MARIE SHOLL, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, received fresh in the frozen section lab, labeled "#1. Sentinel lymph\u000anode", consists of a single tan/pink soft tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), within\u000awhich a single lymph node candidate (1.1 cm in greatest dimension) is\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely frozen as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue", consists of a portion of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) partially surfaced by a tan skin ellipse\u000a(5.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and accompanied by a radiograph. The specimen is received\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange, which corresponds to the orienting sutures (long\u000a- lateral; short - superior). A needle localization wire is in place (enters\u000afrom the superoanterior aspect). A definitive scar is not identified. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial, revealing a\u000atan/white/pink, firm fibrotic area with fat necrosis (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is grossly at the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior soft tissue\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin,\u000a2.6 cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. There is\u000ahemorrhage associated with the mass (consistent with previous biopsy site) and\u000athe needle localization wire traverses the mass, and the clip is identified\u000awithin the mass. The accompanying radiograph confirms the presence of a needle\u000alocalization wire, clip, and mass as confirmed by radiology. The remaining\u000abreast tissue consists of approximately 80% yellow/tan lobulated fat and 20%\u000atan/white unremarkable fibrous stroma. No other lesions are grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass, sequentially from lateral to medial, including relationship\u000ato superior, inferior, and anterior margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000a(Note clip present in Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin nearest mass, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin nearest mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin nearest mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Skin tags", consists of multiple tan, wrinkled cauterized\u000apapules (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Papules, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#3. Superior shave margin (R) breast tissue (suture\u000asuperior)", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast tissue (5.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with an orienting suture (suture designates superior) on one surface (inked\u000ablue by the surgeon). The opposing surface is inked black and the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned. There is a white/tan, firm, ill defined mass (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm), which is at the blue inked suture margin (superior margin) and comes\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the opposing inferior margin. The remaining breast tissue\u000aconsists of approximately 80% yellow/tan lobulated fat and 20% tan/white\u000afibrous stroma. No other gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast mass at margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue adjacent to mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous tissue away from mass, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Inferior shave margin (R) breast tissue, suture superior",\u000aconsists of a portion of fibrofatty breast tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.2 cm) with a suture designating "superior" on the uninked surface and\u000aopposing blue inked surface (inferior). The non inked surface is inked black\u000aby the prosector and the specimen is serially sectioned revealing focal\u000atan/white dense fibrous tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), extending to the blue\u000ainked inferior margin. A definitive lesion or mass is not identified. The\u000abreast tissue consists predominately of yellow tan lobulated fat with scant\u000afibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous tissue and adjacent breast stroma, multi frags, RSS.\u000aDfi/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/12/2005\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for the invasive carcinoma in the specimen from the superior\u000ashave margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
