VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA: SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST RE-EXCISION (LONG LATERAL, SHORT/SUPERIOR):\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy site changes including fat necrosis, hemorrhage\u000afibrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction to polarizable material and chronic\u000ainflammation.\u000aCalcifications in vessel wall.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer of right breast - superior margin with cancer at previous\u000aoperation.\u000aOperation: Re-excision of sup margin.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Ca R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right breast re-excision (long/lateral, short/superior).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - R breast tissue re-excision", and consists of an irregular fragment\u000aof yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (10.1 m-l x REMOVED_DATE s-i x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aa-p), which is oriented per surgeon with two sutures (short/superior,\u000along/lateral) and with an adherent tan/white wrinkled skin ellipse (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) on the anterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen was partially inked\u000aper surgeon (blue=anterior, red=superior), and the remainder of the specimen is\u000ainked per pro-sector as follows: black=posterior, orange=medial,\u000ayellow=lateral, and green=inferior. The central inferior aspect of the\u000aspecimen exhibits a smooth-walled, tan/white focally hemorrhagic fibrous biopsy\u000acavity (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) as consistent with prior procedure. The cavity is\u000aexposed and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aanterior soft tissue/skin margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial. The tissue adjacent to the aforementioned\u000abiopsy cavity (which abuts the green-inked inferior margin) is firm tan/white,\u000agritty, with multiple punctate areas of yellow/tan fat necrosis and red/brown\u000ahemorrhage. This dense tissue comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin,\u000a0.5 cm of the blue-inked anterior/skin margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin,\u000a2.7 from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. A discrete\u000amass is not grossly identified. The remainder of the specimen is composed of\u000aapproximately 99% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with approximately 1%\u000aintervening bands of delicate white/tan fibrous stroma. Representative\u000asections to include the biopsy cavity and adjacent dense, gritty fibrous tissue\u000ain relation to inferior margin, are submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity with adjacent green-inked inferior margin,\u000adense fibrous tissue with fat necrosis and hemorrhage, from\u000alateral to medial, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: skin/anterior margin with closest dense fibrous tissue/fat\u000anecrosis/hemorrhage, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin closest to cavity (no cavity grossly\u000apresent), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin closest to cavity (no cavity grossly\u000apresent),\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior margin closest to cavity (no cavity grossly\u000apresent), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior margin closest to cavity (no cavity grossly\u000apresent), 2 frags, RSS.\u000almb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/2/2005\u000a[report_end]
