VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AFTER CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks 25 and 12, level 3).\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma identified, including inked margins.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aFibrocystic change with cysts, apocrine metaplasia and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 44 year old female with abnormal mammo, REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy showed\u000aseverely atypical ductal hyperplasia with apocrine features, associated\u000awith calcifications. Two adjacent areas of calcifications noted to be\u000aexcised as well.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization biopsy x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue (short suture/superior; long\u000asuture/lateral; whipstitch/deep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcifications in specimen......Dr. D.Smith/KP\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GREISMAN,HARVEY A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast tissue (short suture/superior; long\u000asuture/lateral; whipstitch/deep margin)", and consists of one fragment of\u000atan/yellow fibrofatty tissue (8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a long suture designated\u000alateral and a short suture designated superior by the surgeon. There are two\u000aneedle localization wires are in place and the specimen is received inked in\u000asix colors by the surgeon as follows: anterior=blue, posterior=black,\u000amedial=orange, lateral=yellow, superior=red and inferior=green. Also received\u000ain the same container is a separate fragment of unoriented tan/yellow\u000afibrofatty tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is partially inked and may\u000arepresent a fragment of the main specimen. Also received with the specimen is\u000aa specimen radiographed from the radiology department. The specimen is\u000asectioned and radiograph in the pathology department and is entirely\u000asubmitted. The area of the clip along with several clustered calcifications\u000ais in cassette #12.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  main specimen, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000ahg\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
