VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP, AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (including FSA) (three specimens):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform, papillary\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1 cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - inferior, anterior, lateral\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - superior (0.2 cm, focal, in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amedial (0.3 cm, focal, in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close (< REMOVED_DATE cm) - posterior (focal)\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 HE levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for DCIS\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: The DCIS is present as a predominant REMOVED_DATE cm intracystic mass. However,\u000aDCIS is also present in adjacent breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69 year-old female s/p right breast core needle biopsy REMOVED_DATE \u000aperformed at BWH; pathology demonstrated papillary Ca. History of left breast\u000abiopsy 1994 - atypical ductal and atypical lobular hyperplasia. BS 05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000abreast; BC 05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, thyroid.\u000aOperation: (R) breast wire loc lumpectomy, SNM, SLNB; possible ALND\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (R) breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Sentinel node (R) hot x 2 - FS.\u000aB/2. (R) breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip stitch\u000achest wall - FS - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: The mass and wire are within the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT HOT SENTINEL NODE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" (FSA):\u000aTwo lymph nodes; negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: PAULA C. ABREU-E-LIMA, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Sentinel node (R) hot sentinel node x 2", consists of one\u000ayellow/tan piece of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing two\u000alymph nodes (1.2 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest diameter). The larger lymph node is\u000ainked blue and bisected, and the smaller lymph node is inked orange. Both\u000alymph nodes are submitted in their entirely as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue", consists of a breast excision\u000aspecimen measuring REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and\u000a2.0 cm anterior to posterior. The specimen has one long suture marking the\u000alateral margin and one short suture marking the superior margin. In addition,\u000athere is a localizing wire through the lateral area of the specimen. There is\u000aa REMOVED_DATE cm in length disruption of the tissue in the lateral area that has been\u000apreviously sewn up. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying radiograph\u000ashows the localizing wire through a fairly well circumscribed mass. There is a\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm pink soft papillary well-circumscribed mass near the lateral\u000amargin of the specimen corresponding to the mammographic density. The mass is\u000a0.9 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of the specimen is\u000aapproximately 50% fatty and 50% fibrous tissue. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.6 cm cystic dilation in the medial margin. Approximately 60% of the specimen\u000ais submitted, including all fibrous tissue. Gross photographs were taken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to closest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue and superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cyst at medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibrous tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aAf/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/18/2005\u000a[report_end]
