ing demonstrates a nodular, circumscribed, tan/white, firm\u000amass abutting the superior, inferior, lateral and medial margins and within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the anterior, and posterior margins (mass) is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Mass\u000ademonstrates multifocal hemorrhage (15% of nodule). Specimen is received with\u000aan accompanying radiograph, which demonstrates the localizing wire in place\u000awithin the specimen, in addition a REMOVED_DATE cm, metallic, radiologic clip within the\u000amass. The entire specimen is submitted\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross-sections from anterior to posterior\u000a(Slice with radiologic clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 12 frags, ESS.\u000adb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by David Wu M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
