VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, extensive (blocks 5, 7, REMOVED_DATE  18, and 22;\u000alevels examined) (see note).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, extensive\u000a(e.g. blocks 3, 9, REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications. Apocrine metaplasia involves\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications.\u000aNote: The ADH consists of cells with small hyperchromatic nuclei and\u000ascant cytoplasm. Well formed cribriform spaces are present. Each\u000aindividual focus measures < REMOVED_DATE cm and the foci appear to partially\u000ainvolve terminal lobules but not larger ducts. Although some of the foci\u000aapproach a diagnosis of low grade DCIS (best seen in the original slide of\u000ablock 14), a diagnosis of ADH is favored.\u000aThe calcifications do not appear to be specifically associated with\u000aatypical ductal or lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThe entire specimen is examined histologically, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Has known atypical lobular hyperplasia. Has developed 3 new\u000acalcification clusters in left upper inner quadrant.\u000aOperation: Breast resection - wire directed\u000aOperative findings: 2 wires\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Fibrocystic change, rule out neoplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue, stitch superior short - lateral long\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Calcifications in specimen. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC\u000aThe specimen, fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left\u000abreast tissue", is received with a specimen mammogram showing wire\u000alocalization needle and two areas of calcifications circled. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Cut sections of the specimen show fibrofatty surface. The specimen is\u000asampled to include all of the tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - sampling around proximal portion of wire localization needle,\u000a3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - sampling from remaining tissue, 13 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
