VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA RUSSELL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.; Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS WITH CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aIntraductal papilloma with calcifications and prior biopsy site changes,\u000a1.3 cm, correlating with the radiologic lesion.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (e.g. blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle localization right breast excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue. Short stitch-superior, long stitch-lateral, whip\u000astitch-posterior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass + hookwire in specimen. Jack E. Meyer, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part (designated Part A), labeled,\u000a"#1. Right breast tissue," with an accompanying radiograph that demonstrates a\u000amass. There is a metal wire extending through the mass. There are three\u000aattached sutures with short indicating superior, long indicating lateral and a\u000awhip stitch indicating posterior. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aMeasurements are anterior to posterior REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000asuperior to inferior REMOVED_DATE cm. On sectioning, located closest to the superior\u000asurgical margin, there is a firm well-defined gray/white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The edges of the lesion are ill-defined with a slight scalloped\u000aappearance. The closet superior margin is grossly within 1 mm. The remaining\u000amargins distances are as follows: inferior margin 1 cm, lateral margin REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000amedial margin 4 cm, posterior margin REMOVED_DATE cm, and anterior margin REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aremaining breast tissue is soft red/yellow fibroadipose tissue. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The entire tumor and closest superior and inferior margin,\u000a3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining superior margin, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of breast excision specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aSF/mmm/PES\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/5/2006\u000a[report_end]
