VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: AYODALE S ODULATE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE \u000aCM CIRCUMSCRIBED MASS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, with a solid and cribriform\u000apattern, involving an area of adenosis (at least REMOVED_DATE cm) (see note). An\u000aimmunoperoxidase study for cytokeratin and p63 confirms the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells. No necrosis or calcifications are seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000aADH (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: The atypical cell proliferation may be carcinoma in situ involving\u000aan area of sclerosing adenosis. Final classification should be made after\u000aexcision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 63 year old woman with a new mammographic mass in left breast at\u000a12:00, 3 cm from nipple. Macrolobulated hypoechoic mass on ultrasound, r/o\u000amalignancy.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 8 mm, Nonpalpable circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound - Blue cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast, blue", and consists of multiple tan/yellow to\u000atan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). The breast tissue cores are received in a blue cassette and are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/1/2008\u000a[report_end]
