VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR DENSITIES:\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with atypical features, is present in\u000a7 of 11 blocks (see note). Rare calcifications are associated with the\u000aLCIS. Rare small foci of necrosis are associated with the LCIS.\u000aLCIS involves fibroadenomas.\u000aA core needle biopsy site involves a fibroadenoma. Epithelial\u000adisplacement is present.\u000aLCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, medial, inferior, and anterior margins.\u000aCauterized cells are close to the superior margin that may represent LCIS.\u000aLCIS is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aNote: The excision was performed for a mammographic density which\u000acorrelates with a REMOVED_DATE cm fibroadenoma. The LCIS is incidental to the\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aThe overall architectural appearance is of LCIS. Atypical features are\u000aoccasional cells of high nuclear grade, focal cohesive appearing areas,\u000aand rare small foci of necrosis (best seen in blocks 5 and 6). The\u000aclinical behavior of LCIS with atypical features is not known.\u000aDr. Stuart Schnitt reviewed this case and favors a diagnosis of LCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female with right breast abnormal mammogram. Core\u000abiopsy showed FA and ADH.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy - inking\u000aper protocol\u000aRADIOLOGY: Multiple masses in specimen. OR called 10:45. CG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast wire localization excisional biospy", and\u000ais received together with a specimen radiograph showing multiple masses in\u000aspecimen and a wire localization needle. The specimen consists of fibrofatty\u000atissue (4.5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior and shows focal cystic\u000achange, fibrosis and ill-defined white mass (approximately REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm),\u000alying REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral and anterior margins, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aall other margins. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast excision, 15 frags, ESS\u000amab\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
