VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, CENTRAL, SLIGHTLY MEDIAL, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, consisting of a cribriform proliferation of cells\u000awith low grade nuclei in two duct profiles (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note).\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aNote: The area of ADH closely approaches a diagnosis of DCIS. Very small\u000acalcifications are associated with DCIS. No necrosis is present. This area\u000awould be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: New calcifications right breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: Central slightly medial\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. 11 G Stereotactic 12 cores taken. Biopsy clip placed - Green cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast green", and contains two green cassettes. The first\u000agreen cassette labeled "A CA++", contains multiple yellow/red fibroadipose soft\u000atissue cores (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second green cassette\u000alabeled "B", contains multiple yellow/tan, focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose\u000atissue cores (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/10/2007\u000a[report_end]
