VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Alison Z Young, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, DOUBLE WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR TWO MASSES:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, LOW GRADE, REMOVED_DATE cm, adjacent to the prior core\u000aneedle biopsy site (0.5 cm); see NOTE.\u000aThe stroma is mildly cellular.\u000aNo mitoses are seen.\u000aNo stromal invasion is present.\u000aNo heterologous areas are present.\u000aPhyllodes tumor is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aand grossly, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin; by gross\u000areport, the tumor is >1.0 cm from all other margins.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with florid hyperplasia (1.6 cm) associated\u000awith core needle biopsy sites.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe prior core needle biopsy of the phyllodes tumor showed mild stromal\u000aovergrowth and occasional mitoses, classified as a phyllodes tumor.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester of the Breast Pathology Service,\u000awho concurs with the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 y/o female with history of multiple breast biopsies dating back to\u000a1994. Mammogram REMOVED_DATE  demonstrated 2 cm lower inner breast mass and\u000alobular mass lower/inner quadrant, S/P core needle biopsies @ BWH REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire loc biopsy REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast phyllodes tumor and papilloma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - left breast tissue -- short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch/deep\u000amargin (mammo).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aPart A is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, and\u000a"left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE \u000a(medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast biopsy with two\u000alocalization wires, one entering the specimen at the superior margin, and the\u000aother entering the specimen at the inferior margin, and a short suture marking\u000athe superior margin, and a long suture marking the lateral margin. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the presence of two localization\u000awires, one entering the specimen at the superior margin, and the other entering\u000athe specimen at the inferior margin. There are two masses on the radiograph,\u000aone is close to the superior margin, and the other is close to the inferior\u000amargin. Within the two masses are two clips, respectively. The specimen\u000aconsists of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awhite/tan mass with focal hemorrhage abutting the superior margin. This lesion\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, 2 cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. There is a second tan/white mass with focal hemorrhage abutting the\u000aanterior margin, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. It is 1 cm from the lateral\u000amargin, 3 cm from the medial margin, 3 cm from the superior margin, 2 cm from\u000athe inferior margin, and 1 cm from the posterior margin. The two tumors are 1\u000acm from each other. Representative sections of intervening breast tissue\u000abetween the two tumors and the entire two tumors are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: sections submitted from superior to inferior margin, 13\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aASO/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Alison Z Young M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
