e second pink\u000acassette is labeled "B", contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on Wednesday August 19, 2009 at\u000a02:06:24PM\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on Wednesday August 19, 2009 at\u000a02:08:48PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aAugust 19, 2009 at 02:11:57PM\u000a[report_end]
