VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.; Elizabeth M. Manion, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD; Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP, A BIOPSY SITE AND\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is focally present in two duct profiles adjacent to\u000aa biopsy site, < REMOVED_DATE cm in size (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined) (see NOTE).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined).\u000aA biopsy site is present and extends to the inferior and lateral margins.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with columnar cell change and normal breast\u000atissue.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes, intraductal papillomas, epithelial hyperplasia, a\u000asclerosing lesion, and apocrine cysts are present.\u000aNOTE: The focus of ADH is cytologically similar to the focus of ADH in the\u000apatient's previous core biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSlides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reviewed by Dr. Tan Ince who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE  bilateral mammogram with mammogram and\u000aultrasound demonstrating, right central/medial calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core\u000abiopsy revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia for which excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mmg.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue with short stitch superior; long lateral whip stitch\u000adeep margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aMR number, and "#1. Right breast tissue with short stitch superior, long\u000alateral, whip-stitch deep margin", and consists of a lumpectomy specimen (5.0\u000acm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior). A wire enters the specimen from the medial to lateral side. A\u000ashort stitch designates superior aspect, long designates lateral, and\u000awhip-stitch designates deep margin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a fibrotic area abutting the\u000ainferior margin consistent with a core biopsy site (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A\u000aclip is identified within the area of fibrosis immediately adjacent to the\u000ainferior margin. The entire specimen is submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lumpectomy, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain the area of fibrosis described above.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain area marked by the clip.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000akst/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 08, 2009 at 05:44:11PM\u000a[report_end]
