he majority of the specimen is composed\u000aof white fibrous material. There is no necrosis.\u000aMicro #1-4: breast excision specimen, serially sectioned, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aPart two is labeled "#2 - breast mass right axillary tail", and consists of a\u000abreast excision specimen that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is\u000ainked by the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000afibrous tissue that comprises the majority of the excision specimen.\u000aMicro #5-7: breast excision, serially sectioned, 3, 2, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000apes/\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
