VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aRESIDUAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Micropapillary with intermediate nuclear\u000agrade in one (1) block (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aRESIDUAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - With mixed ductal and lobular features\u000apresent adjacent to the biopsy cavity\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in CIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in CIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of CIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 4:31 blocks (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMargins (CIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity changes extending to the deep margin.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis Nx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SKIN":\u000aSkin with scar and foreign body giant cell reaction\u000ato polarizable suture material.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right total mastectomy short stitch - superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast skin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimens are received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right total mastectomy - short stitch, superior and long\u000astitch, lateral", consists of a mastectomy specimen (915.0 grams, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior)\u000awith skin ellipse (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and with everted\u000anipple (1.0 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in height). There are two orienting\u000asutures with short superior and long lateral per surgeon. The deep aspect of\u000athe specimen is inked black. There is a cavity, which is opened to both the\u000adeep/posterior and anterior aspect of the specimen with an opening measuring\u000a3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm with the anterior-posterior dimension measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000acavity is located in the central outer aspect of the specimen and is lateral to\u000athe lateral aspect of the skin ellipse. Sectioning the specimen reveals no\u000aother lesions. The specimen is approximately 10% fibrous and 90% adipose\u000atissue. In addition, there are separately received attached fragments of\u000afibroadipose tissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). No lymph nodes or\u000askeletal muscle are grossly identified. The cavity is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior aspect of cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast skin", consists of an ovoid donut-shaped\u000afragment of skin (outer ovoid dimension REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and inner ovoid dimension\u000a9.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, with width range, REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm, and depth up to REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais a well-healed linear scar (2.5 cm) that extends to skin edge. The deep\u000aaspect of the specimen is inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Scar, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional representative sections of skin, 3 frag, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aGL/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday February 25, 2009 at 08:21:50PM\u000a[report_end]
