o further orient the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is sectioned from superior to lateral (due to tissue\u000adistortion the lateral margin is now opposite the superior margin) in twelve\u000aslices. Sectioning reveals the breast parenchyma to be composed of greater\u000athan 95% dense white fibrous tissue with less than 5% fatty tissue. The wire\u000aends in slice four. There are no grossly apparent masses or calcifications.\u000aThe specimen is radiographed, showing calcifications in slice four and possible\u000acalcifications in slices one, two and eight. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one (superior margin, en face), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice two (superior and anterior margins), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice three (superior, inferior, posterior margins), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice four (inferior, superior, medial margins), 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice five (inferior, medial, superior margins), 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice six (inferior, medial, superior margins), 4 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice seven (inferior, superior, medial margins), 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eight (inferior, superior, medial margins), 4 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice nine (superior, medial, lateral margins), 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice ten (medial, inferior, deep, lateral margins), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eleven (medial, lateral, inferior, deep margins), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice twelve (lateral and deep margins, en face), 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aJUB/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/11/2005\u000a[report_end]
