VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma present, including examination of the deep\u000amargin.\u000aFocal stronal hyalinization with dystrophic calcifications.\u000aCalcification in benign breast tissue.\u000aBiopsy cavity present.\u000aSKIN, LEFT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aSkin with subcutaneous hyalinization, chronic perivascular inflammation\u000aand fat necrosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69 year old female with hx of stage I left breast Ca 1981, rx'd with\u000abreast preservation. Recent US core bx of REMOVED_DATE cm core bx left breast -->\u000ainvasive cancer with ductal and lobular features. ER/PR positive, Her2Neu\u000anegative.\u000aOperation: Lt simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt breast Ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - lt breast - short/sup, long/lateral.\u000a#2 - skin lt breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BRUNKER,PATRICIA A. R.,M.D.,D.PHIL.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aThe first part, sublabeled "#1 - left breast, short/superior, long/lateral",\u000aconsists of an 848 gram simple mastectomy specimen (22.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aa peri-areolar skin circle (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with no evident scars. The nipple\u000a(1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is everted without crusting. The deep margin consists of a\u000asmooth, fascial plane with sparse adherent skeletal muscle, and is inked in\u000ablack. In the upper/outer quadrant, there is a defect (5.5 cm in length),\u000aimmediately lateral to the skin ellipse that exposes the interior of a previous\u000abiopsy cavity (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Subjacent to this cavity, there is a very\u000afirm, white, stellate, poorly circumscribed mass (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000agrossly abuts the presumed biopsy cavity and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin.\u000aAlso in the upper/outer quadrant, there is a second, firm, white,\u000awell-circumscribed nodule (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the\u000alarge mass and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The remainder of breast tissue is\u000aapproximately 80% fat and 20% fibrous tissue. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1: Biopsy cavity candidate site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #2: Firm area at probable biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #3: Medial biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #4: Margin deep to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #5: Extremely firm mass subjacent to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #6: More lateral section of extremely firm mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #7: Deep margin to nodule, to include small, well-circumscribed nodule,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Nipple with subjacent breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #11: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #12: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe second part, sublabeled "#2 - skin left breast", consists of four fragments\u000aof unoriented skin, the largest of which is a circle (13.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a central, punched-out concentric circle (5 cm in diameter), with a\u000acut-out radial projection (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The other three skin fragments are\u000atriangles (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to a depth of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). The largest fragment is inked by\u000aassigning the radial projection to 12 o'clock and inking from 12 to 3 to 6\u000ao'clock in black, and from 6 to 9 to 12 o'clock in blue. In the largest\u000afragment, the radial defect is firm, fibrous, and consistent with a scar site,\u000aand it is possible to overlay the segment on the mastectomy specimen (Part\u000a#1), such that it overlies the exposed biopsy site. There are no gross\u000alesions identified. Representative sections are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro #13: En face black margin at 12 o'clock with perpendicular blue margin\u000aat 12 o'clock, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #14: Perpendicular, black, 2 o'clock firm area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000apab/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
