VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. RIGHT BREAST, MRI WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN ILL-DEFINED REMOVED_DATE CM AREA\u000aOF ENHANCEMENT:\u000aBenign breast tissue with extensive sclerosing adenosis and\u000acalcifications.\u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen upon complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB/2. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION OF A NODULE:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 y o woman with history of LCIS, now with abnormal right breast\u000aMRI, without mammographic or ultrasound correlate.\u000aOperation: Right breast MRI-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right breast MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast MRI-localized excision - short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral - mammo.\u000aB/2. Right breast nodule - posterior lateral cavity.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Wire in specimen with no mammogram or ultrasound findings to\u000acorrelate with MRI area of interest. - S. Nielson REMOVED_DATE  350 p.m.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "1. Right breast MRI-localized excision - short stitch\u000asuperior, long stitch lateral", consists of one (1) breast excision specimen\u000a(1.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior) with a needle-localization wire in place as well as two (2)\u000aorienting sutures (short stitch = superior, long stitch = lateral). The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aPosterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the wire\u000awithin the specimen, but no calcifications or masses are identified. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned into nine (9) slices from lateral to medial. It consists\u000aof grossly normal-appearing fibroadipose tissue (approximately 40% fibrous\u000atissue and 60% adipose tissue). The specimen is entirely submitted from\u000alateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Level 1 perpendicular sections of lateral margin, 5 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Levels 2 and 3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Levels 4 and 5, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Levels 6 and 7, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Level 8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Level 9, perpendicular sections of medial margin, 5 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Right breast nodule, posterolateral cavity", consists of\u000aone (1) unoriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aentire specimen is inked black. The specimen contains a small white\u000apoorly-circumscribed nodule (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly abuts the inked\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast nodule, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aAF/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/14/2006\u000a[report_end]
