VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE NEEDLE LOC FOR FS":\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aBenign papilloma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass.\u000aOperation: Needle loc right breast excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue needle loc for fs.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aOne group of Ca++ in specimen and other additional calcifications.\u000aE.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire-localized excision", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.9 cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). Two localizing wires enter the anterior surface, one\u000aenters the superior/central aspect of the anterior surface, and the other\u000aenters the medial/anterior surface. Per the accompanying radiograph, the more\u000acentral localizing wire marks a few small clusters of calcifications. There is\u000aan additional small focus of calcifications in the intervening tissue between\u000athe two wires. The calcifications appear posterolateral, per radiograph.\u000aSectioning demonstrates tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue (at least 85%),\u000aadmixed with unremarkable, granular, tan/white, fibrodense tissue,\u000apredominantly posterolaterally. There are no obvious masses, lesions or other\u000aabnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000alateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular\u000amedial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the area of interest per localizing wires in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to\u000amedial, with perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular medial margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the area of interest per localizing wires in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
