VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 9 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES:\u000aUPPER OUTER, REMOVED_DATE CM AREA OF SLIGHTLY IRREGULAR ENHANCEMENT:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aNote: The LCIS has a slightly higher nuclear grade than is typical and\u000athere is single cell necrosis.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aLOWER OUTER, 1 CM AREA OF NON-MASS FORMING ENHANCEMENT:\u000aColumnar cell change with apocrine metaplasia and calcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 54 year old female with history of ADH and LCIS on prior biopsies,\u000awith 2 focally enhancing areas in left breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Site #1, upper outer: REMOVED_DATE cm, focal enhancement, slightly spiculated.\u000a2. Site #2, lower outer: 1 cm, focal and non-mass forming.\u000aThe two sites are 4 cm apart.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000a2. Left: lower outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted\u000a2. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a2. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted A/1. - Green top/white bottom\u000aB/2. - Blue top, white bottom\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast site #1", consists of three white cassettes with\u000agreen lids containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty focally hemorrhagic soft\u000atissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of white cassettes with green lids, multi frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast site #2", contains four white cassettes with blue\u000alids with multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (3.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of white cassettes with blue lid, multi frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aJC/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aFebruary 13, 2009 at 12:17:27PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (2/19/09):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for\u000aprogesterone receptors.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aFebruary 19, 2009 at 07:44:28PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for e-cadherin is performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Although\u000athe invasive carcinoma has lobular morphology, the carcinoma is moderately\u000aimmunoreactive. Therefore, this is an unusual lobular carcinoma with\u000ae-cadherin expression. Some of the in situ carcinoma is also e-cadherin\u000apositive. Other cells have weak or absent expression. Final classification of\u000aboth components should be made on the excisional specimen.\u000aAddendum #2 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 07:24:18PM\u000a[report_end]
