VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY #1":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic change with ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY #2":\u000aBiopsy site with fibrosis.\u000aFibrocystic change with ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 61 year old female with left breast calcification x 2.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy x 2\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast biopsy #1\u000a2. Left breast biopsy #2\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 2 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "#1", consists of a single fragment of pink/yellow fibroadipose tissue\u000a(3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph,\u000awhich shows a localization wire and clip in place, adjacent to an area of\u000amicrocalcifications. The specimen consists of 80% pink/white firm fibrous\u000atissue and 20% yellow adipose tissue. No discrete lesions are identified.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - breast biopsy #1 (clip between sections in micro 2 and\u000amicrocalcifications in micro 3), 10 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "#2", consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is accompanied by a full specimen\u000aradiograph, which shows a micro clip in place, centrally located in the\u000aspecimen, and adjacent to an area of microcalfications. The specimen consists\u000aof approximately 40% pink/white firm fibrous tissue, and 60% yellow adipose\u000atissue, with the fibrous tissue primarily present at one aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Sectioning reveals a hemorrhagic biopsy site (0.6 cm in greatest\u000adimension), centrally located in the specimen. There are also areas of\u000aintervening hemorrhage in the parenchyma. No other masses or lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - breast biopsy #2 (biopsy cavity in micros REMOVED_DATE  clip in micro X)\u000a12 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
