VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (2.4 cm), well differentiated, modified Bloom\u000aRichardson grade I (of III).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion present.\u000aNo in situ component is present.\u000aTumor extends to the surgical resection margins.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aNote: The tumor involves the specimen extensively and extends diffusely to the\u000asurgical resection margins.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Excision of left breast mass\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"left breast mass", is an unoriented tan/pink soft tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe external surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a lobulated pink/yellow color on cut surface. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - serial sections with ends taken perpendicularly, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
