nstrates the localization wire within the specimen, adjacent to\u000athe clip. In addition, an area is circled away from the clip site showing\u000afaint calcifications. The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral, and a\u000aclip is localized to Slice 7. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 1 through 3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slide 6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 12, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aDM/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/27/2006\u000a[report_end]
