VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Andrew M. Quinn, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND A MASS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, focal, see NOTE.\u000aOther findings:\u000aPrevious core biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications present in microcysts and benign epithelium.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia with micropapillary and papillary architecture\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: Two areas show an intraductal proliferation of low nuclear grade with\u000ajust sufficient architectural atypia for a diagnosis of ADH (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000alevels examined). Neither are associated with calcifications.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69 year old woman with abnormal mammogram - core biopsy --> atypical\u000aepithelial proliferation.\u000aOperation: Left breast needle loc excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: History of left breast atypical epithelial proliferation.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left needle loc breast biopsy - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left needle localized breast biopsy - short/superior, long/lateral", and\u000aconsists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast\u000atissue (5.0 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with a short suture designating the superior margin, and\u000along suture designating the lateral margin. The specimen radiograph is\u000areviewed in centricity and shows a wire clip and mass in the specimen. There is\u000aa needle localization wire in place within the specimen, which enters through\u000athe anterior-inferior aspect of the specimen and exits through the\u000aposterior-lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow,\u000aanterior/blue, and posterior/black) and is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior. The cut surface is tan and homogeneous with an irregular dense white\u000afibrous hemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and\u000a3.8 cm from the superior margin. Within this area is a silver metallic biopsy\u000aclip. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous\u000awith a scant amount of fibrous soft tissue constituting less than 5% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID include fibrous area/previous\u000abiopsy cavity; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID include area of clip), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the specimen radiograph as interpreted via Centricity\u000ademonstrates a wire localizing a clip within a mass.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 27, 2009 at 08:10:16PM\u000a[report_end]
