VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCONNOLLY, JAMES, L., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CONNOLLY,JAMES L.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 6:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, comedo type, (high nuclear grade) is present\u000aWith microcalcifications and necrosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54-year-old female on tamoxifen, history of ADH with new\u000acalcifications (suspicious) in the 6 o'clock axis of the left breast.\u000aOperation: 11G stereotactic.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rule out DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 11G tissue samples of left breast calcifications at\u000a6:00, + ca++ in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAI,HONGWEI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "#1, left breast", and consists of two (2) light blue cassettes.\u000aOne cassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented,\u000ayellow to white tissue cores (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other\u000acassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A" ca++, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: DURFEE, SARA, MANNARELLI M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
