VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE" (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (high nuclear grade),with central\u000anecrosis and calcifications.\u000aTumor is present in three of twelve (3:12) blocks.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is NOT present.\u000aResection margin, negative for tumor.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aBiopsy cavity is identified.\u000aBenign changes include microfibroadenomata, cysts, and\u000amicrocalcifications in benign lobules.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: R breast DCIS.\u000aOperation: R simple mastectomy sentinel node bx, reconstruction.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) r axillary sentinel node (fs) - 5100.\u000aB/2) right breast, stitch - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - R AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: HEJIN P. HAHN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: QINGHONG YANG, MD, PHD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. R axillary sentinel node", consists of a tan rubbery lymph node\u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is bisected and submitted in its entirety for\u000afrozen section as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, stitch short superior, long lateral", consists of a\u000aright simple mastectomy (220 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is an\u000aoverlying unremarkable tan skin ellipse (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with an unremarkable\u000anipple areolar complex (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with an everted nipple (1.5 cm in\u000adiameter). The posterior margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located\u000abetween the upper inner and lower inner quadrants. The cavity contains a\u000asurgical clip, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest black-inked posterior margin, and\u000ais located directly posterior to the nipple, REMOVED_DATE cm. The remaining cut surface\u000adisplays 50% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and 50% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. No\u000alymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity, sequentially from lateral to medial, with the clip\u000aidentified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, to include the posterior\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include the posterior\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, to include the\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include the\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
