VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy cavity site, fat necrosis, giant cell\u000areaction to foreign material, and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aVessel with obstruction of the lumen with granulation tissue, seen by\u000aJones stain.\u000aNo residual tumor present.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43 year-old female status post right upper outer quadrant breast\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE  revealing REMOVED_DATE cm low grade phyllodes tumor with close margins.\u000aADH presents as well.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision partial mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue, short suture - superior, long stitch -\u000alateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin, and skin - interior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. re-excison right breast mass", and consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue with three orienting sutures, which is received inked by\u000athe surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen measures (9.2 cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior\u000ato posterior). No discrete nodules are grossly identified, however, there is\u000aan area of yellowish/tan discoloration, consistent with fat necrosis, located\u000a0.2 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The yellowish/tan area measures\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the specimen is composed of\u000aapproximately 30% firm white fibrous tissue, primarily located near the\u000asuperior and medial margins. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy site and closest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity and closest anterior/posterior margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity and closest lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous tissue in superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Inferior margin perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000apsc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
