VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with\u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent apocrine snouts\u000awith atypia (blocks #1 and #10), atypical lobular hyperplasia (blocks\u000a#2 and #9), and apocrine metaplasia (block #21).\u000aAdenosis, cysts, and calcifications associated wtih benign breast tissue\u000a(blocks #10, #12, #16, #19, #22).\u000aThere is extensive granulation tissue, fat necrosis, and giant cell\u000areaction consistent with the previous biopsy site (block #12).\u000aThere is no carcinoma seen in the specimen, including the margins.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was embedded.\u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. T. Ince who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass, status post BWH core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  showing atypical\u000alobular hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left needle localized breast biopsy, left breast tissue\u000ashort superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FACTOR,RACHEL E.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical\u000arecord number, and "Left breast tissue, long lateral, short superior", and\u000aconsists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere is a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch\u000adesignating the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Two needles are\u000apresent in the specimen. A radiograph accompanies the specimen showing two\u000aneedles, a clip, fibrocystic breast, and microcalcifications. The specimen is\u000abivalved between the needles revealing the breast tissue is 60% fibrous with\u000apunctate areas of hemorrhage and some nodular tan densities (0.1 cm in\u000adiameter) which likely represents the core biopsy site. The clip could not be\u000aidentified after sectioning, and the tissue was radiographed revealing the\u000aclip in block #12 and calcifications in blocks #15 and #16. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Tissue close to the first needle, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Tissue adjancent to the second needle, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of breast specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aref\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
