VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION with single cell necrosis (see\u000aNOTE).\u000aCalcifications are present in ducts with denuded epithelial lining and a dense\u000aperi-ductal fibrosis and inflammatory infiltrate.\u000aApocrine cysts with associated microcalcifications.\u000aNOTE: Two duct profiles are present containing atypical cells with single cell\u000anecrosis, surrounded by a dense peri-ductal inflammatory infiltrate which are\u000asuspicious but not diagnostic of DCIS. Although the calcifications are seen in\u000adenuded ducts with periductal inflammation, they likely are associated with the\u000aatypical ductal proliferation. The ducts of interest are not present on\u000aadditional levels used for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu\u000aand p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. This lesion would be best evaluated by excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 64 y o female with Ca++, left UOQ; hx bilateral ADH.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 6 mm ? and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: Upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic - Yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of two yellow cassettes. First yellow\u000acassette "A. Ca++" contains multiple pink/tan tissues (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). Second yellow cassette "B" contains multiple pink/tan soft tissues\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Yellow cassette A contents (CA++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Yellow cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/3/2008\u000a[report_end]
