VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE ANN RITNER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A LOBULATED\u000a0.8 CM MASS:\u000aFragments of cyst wall lined by a papillary proliferation with focal mucin\u000aproduction and focal architectural and cytological atypia, (See Note).\u000aSclerosing adenosis with apocrine metaplasia and calcifications.\u000aNOTE: Although atypical features sufficient for a diagnosis of atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia are not seen, complete excision is recommended to exclude a more\u000asignificant lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Complicated cyst that aspirated mucin material and core biopsy\u000aperformed. DDx: Cyst vs mucinous IDC. Time in formalin - 3:45 pm.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 8-mm lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 9 o'clock.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Ultrasound and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast core biopsy in one yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast", and consists of a yellow cassette\u000acontaining multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues\u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of yellow cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 05, 2009 at 03:25:35PM\u000a[report_end]
