VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A\u000aCLIP":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multifocal, in radial scars.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, multifocal.\u000aSclerosing adenosis, multifocal.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Palpable mass left breast abnormal L ultrasound.\u000aOperation: Left breast ultrasound guided excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast palpable mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue with palpable mass with wire (clip on mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called to Dr. Lesnikoski, clip density and wire on radiograph. Dr.\u000aOdulate.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of an irregular portion\u000aof fibrofatty tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is received previously inked\u000aper pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red,\u000ainferior green, lateral yellow, and medial orange. There is an inserted\u000aneedle-localization wire, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph which\u000aenters along the superior/lateral margin, and exits at the inferior margin.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (0.5 x\u000a0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a surgical clip, as identified on the accompanying\u000aradiograph. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aThe remaining cut surface displays 60% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and\u000a40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, from posterior to anterior, with the\u000abiopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the surgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
