VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MITRA NOROOZIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, POSTERIOR, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications and possible architectural atypia (see\u000anote).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (seen only on level REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: There are micropapillae associated with the columnar cell changes.\u000aAlthough some features suggest these are "pseudo" micropapillae, due to lifting\u000aof the epithelium off the basement membrane, true architectural atypia cannot\u000abe completely excluded. This lesion would be evaluated best by excision.\u000aSelected slides were also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: New group of punctate/amorphous calcifications - with milk of calcium\u000aincluded and other indeterminate calcifications approximately 10 mm in right\u000aUOQ posteriorly.\u000aOperation: 11-G stereotactic.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Benign ? CA++ and micro cysts. R/o DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Calcifications in cassette "A", rest in cassette "B" (both orange right\u000abreast)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", consists of two orange cassettes. First cassette\u000alabeled "A CA++" consisting of multiple irregular tan/yellow to tan/white\u000afibrofatty cylindrical soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Second\u000acassette labeled "B" contains multiple tan/white to tan/yellow fibrofatty cores\u000aof breast tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDRD/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2006\u000a[report_end]
