VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Reduction mamoplasty\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DENNIS P ORGILL M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST" (695g):\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications in association\u000awith benign epithelium, sclerosing adenosis, and\u000afibrosis with hemosiderin-laden macrophages.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST" (790g):\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined).\u000aAn immunohistochemical study for e-cadherin is positive in the\u000aarea of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aBreast tissue with usual ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000acalcifications in association with benign epithelium, and columnar\u000acell change.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MASS":\u000aBreast tissue with fat necrosis, chronic inflammation,\u000aand hemosiderin-laden macrophages.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast hypertrophy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast, REMOVED_DATE kg.\u000aB/2. Left breast REMOVED_DATE kg.\u000aC/3. Right breast mass, ? fat necrosis.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast", and consists of a 695-gram specimen consisting of\u000amultiple fragments of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibroadipose tissue admixed with\u000atan wrinkled skin (20.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The fragments are\u000asectioned to exhibit approximately 20% focally dense white tan fibrous tissue\u000aand 80% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are\u000agrossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and fibrous tissue, multi frags in each, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast", and consists of a 790-gram specimen consisting of\u000amultiple fragments of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibroadipose tissue admixed with\u000atan skin (18.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The fragments are sectioned to\u000aexhibit approximately 20% focally dense white tan fibrous tissue and 80%\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. (After examination of the original sections, the specimen is\u000are-examined and no gross lesions are seen. Four (4) additional representative\u000asections of tissue are submitted.)\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and fibrous tissue, multi frags in each, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast mass ? fat necrosis", and consists of three irregular\u000afragments of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). Due to the disrupted nature of the specimen, surgical margins are\u000anot grossly apparent. The fragments are sectioned to exhibit dense focally\u000acystic fibrous tissue and yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000almb/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
