VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aJONES, DANIEL, MORGAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by JONES,DANIEL MORGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFibrocystic change, with apocrine metaplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block 7).\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules (with snouts and secretions; best seen on\u000ablock #7).\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old premenopausal female not on hormones whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram demonstrates a new cluster of microcalcifications in the\u000aright medial breast. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed columnar\u000aalteration of lobules with associated calcifications, and focal\u000aatypia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast microcalcification.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue\u000a(short suture = superior, long suture = lateral).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT MEDIAL BREAST CALCIFICATIONS, BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aRadiology: Calcifications in speicmen ----D. Smith, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DEBNATH,JAYANTA,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast tissue," and consists of a single fragment\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a needle localization wire in\u000aplace. There is a short suture designated as superior, and a long suture\u000adesignated as lateral. The specimen is inked in six colors: blue = anterior,\u000aorange = medial, green = superior, red = inferior, black = posterior, yellow =\u000alateral. There is a firm gritty tan/yellow soft tissue which is grossly away\u000afrom all margins. There are no areas grossly consistent with invasive\u000acarcinoma. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
