re\u000alocated.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 frags each, 22 probable lymph nodes, ESS (differentially inked,\u000aorange, black).\u000aThe second specimen consists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm thick). One margin is indicated by the surgeon as the new margin with a\u000astitch. The new margin is inked blue and the old, black. There is no lesion\u000ain the interior which is suspicious for carcinoma. A second fragment is found\u000awithin the same container; it is not attached to the oriented specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  oriented margin, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: unattached specimen, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aThe third container is labeled "#3 lateral shaved margin of right breast\u000atissue, stitch on new margin". Received fresh is a mass of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm deep). It is oriented by the surgeon with a suture. The\u000anew margin is inked blue and the old, black. There is no lesion in the\u000ainterior margin that is suggestive of malignancy.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral shaved margin, right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000ahdh\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
