VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Edmund S Cibas, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS MARKED BY A CLIP:\u000aFibroadenoma and core needle biopsy site (0.8 cm; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note). The\u000alesion is not present at the margin (0.3 cm).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread (e.g. block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: A prior core needle biopsy of a 1 cm mass showed a fibroepithelial\u000alesion with some features suggestive of a low grade phyllodes tumor (see\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). In this excision, there is only a small portion of residual\u000alesion adjacent to the biopsy site. Diagnostic features of a phyllodes tumor\u000aare not seen.\u000aThe entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 2:00, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aFibroadenoma with cellular stroma (0.9 cm) (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aA core needle biopsy site is present, but is not adjacent to the fibroadenoma.\u000aNote: A prior core needle biopsy for a REMOVED_DATE cm lesion was performed, but only\u000ashowed normal breast tissue (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). In this specimen, a fibroadenoma\u000ais present in tissue separate from the core needle biopsy site.\u000aThe entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aCOMMENT: This case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass - core biopsy reveals fibroepithelial lesion,\u000afibroadenoma versus phyllodes. Left breast mass with core biopsy with\u000adiscordant findings to breast imaging.\u000aOperation: 1. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy for\u000afibroepithelial lesion. 2. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy for\u000amass.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: 1. Left breast fibroepithelial lesion. 2. Left\u000abreast mass. Postop: Same.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire localized excisional fibroepithelial lesion, short\u000asuture equals superior, long suture equals lateral to mammo.\u000aB/2. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy mass - short suture equals\u000asuperior, long lateral to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. Mass in specimen. C. Denison, MD\u000aClip in specimen. Mass confirmed present with ultrasound.\u000aDr. C. Denison. MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast wire localized excisional fibroepithelial lesion",\u000aconsists of a breast excisional specimen (A-P REMOVED_DATE cm, S-I REMOVED_DATE cm, and M-L REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with two orienting sutures (short superior, long lateral) and a localizing\u000awire. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a mass containing a clip and a\u000awire. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The cut parenchyma demonstrates a firm,\u000awhite/tan nodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral\u000amargin). The specimen is entirely submitted (medial to lateral) for\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin (perpendicular sections), REMOVED_DATE frags per cassette,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8 (wire), 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin (perpendicular sections), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#1. Left breast wire excisional biopsy mass, long lateral, short\u000asuperior", consists of an excisional breast specimen (A-P REMOVED_DATE cm, S-I REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aand M-L REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked according to protocol. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe accompanying radiograph demonstrates a clip marked by a wire. No masses\u000aare seen. The cut parenchyma demonstrates a cavity (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000acontains the clip, wire, and foreign material. The parenchyma is otherwise\u000aunremarkable. The specimen is entirely submitted inferiorly to superiorly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin (perpendicular sections), 3 frags per cassette,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8 (wire and clip), 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin (perpendicular sections), 4 frags per cassette,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000awcf/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Edmund S Cibas M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
