VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MITRA NOROOZIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 6:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS AND AN IRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade), with\u000aassociated calcifications, is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Irregular 13 mm mass with pleomorphic calcifications at 6:30 in the\u000aleft breast (remote from previous surgical site excision for ADH (left upper\u000ainner quadrant)).\u000aOperation: 14-G ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Positive calcs in REMOVED_DATE cores on specimen radiograph.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ID CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Calcs left breast in green cassette "A". Remainder in green cassette B.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast green", and consists of two green cassettes. The\u000afirst green cassette labeled "A. CA ++", contains two tan/pink fibroadipose\u000atissue cores (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second green cassette,\u000alabeled "B", consists of multiple tan/white fibroadipose tissue cores (0.9 x\u000a0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: A, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: B, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/19/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (10/20/06):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
