000awhich is oriented per surgeon with three sutures: short = superior, long =\u000alateral, whip stitch = chest wall margin. The specimen is inked per prosector\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000aneedle localization wire is received free-floating in the specimen container.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit\u000aapproximately 30% focally dense, tan/white fibrostroma extending to the\u000aanterior, posterior, superior and medial margin, and approximately 70%\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from superior to\u000ainferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially submitted from superior to inferior,\u000amultiple frags total, ESS.\u000aLMB/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
