VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WITH WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade) is\u000apresent in one of 17 slides (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE cm focus) and is associated with\u000abiopsy site changes. No necrosis or calcifications are seen.\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63 and cytokeratin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) confirm the\u000apresence of myoepithelial cells in the area of the DCIS.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin in the single slide with DCIS.\u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSkin is present.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Known DCIS with close margin and microcalcifications (right breast).\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue (stitch at long lateral and short superior) (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aDistal wire with hook in specimen.\u000aMicrocalcifications in specimen radiograph.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Right breast tissue (stitch at long lateral and short superior)", and\u000aconsists of a previously-inked breast surgical specimen (containing two sutures\u000a- short designates superior, long designates lateral). The specimen (5.0 cm\u000afrom medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior) is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The anterior margin contains a REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000atan/white skin ellipse. Within the specimen is a single localization wire. The\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph shows the wire and scattered\u000amicrocalcifications. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to\u000aposterior to reveal a white, firm, fibrous area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000agrossly abuts the superior and inferior margins, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral,\u000a0.7 cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior (skin), and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from lateral to medial, fibrous area in cassettes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags, ESS.\u000apal/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/5/2005\u000a[report_end]
