teral) is safe inked by the surgeon and has a wire\u000aembedded through the specimen from antral inferior to posterior superior. The\u000asecond fragment is unoriented (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an area of firm\u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue throughout. The first fragment is serially sectioned\u000afrom lateral to medial and entirely submitted. A section of fragment #1,\u000areveals a white/tan fibrous tissue abutting the inferior and posterior margins.\u000aThe entire surface of the second fragment has been inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1st fragment, lateral most and fibrous area, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Next slice and fibrous area, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Third slice, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4th slice, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5th slice, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial most, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second fragment, 6 frags, ESS\u000aSpecimen B is labeled "#2. Tissue from left breast, clusters of level of\u000anipple", and consists of two unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with the smaller fragment having an\u000aembedded wire. Each fragment has diffuse areas of firm fibrous tissue. The\u000asurface of each fragment have been entirely inked blue. Each fragment has been\u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1st fragment, 8 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2nd fragment, 5 frags, ESS\u000aEUB/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Edilberto G Bauza M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/29/2005\u000a[report_end]
