VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia (block #2).\u000aJuvenile papillomatosis (1.8 cm).\u000aThe inked inferior surgical margin of resection is involved by\u000ajuvenile papillomatosis.\u000aAll other inked surgical margins of resection are greater than\u000a0.1 cm from the papillomatosis.\u000aNOTE: This lesion is characterized by a circumscribed area of cysts with\u000aflorid epithelial hyperplasia, intraductal histiocytes, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, papillomas, and fibroadenomatoid change. These findings\u000aare consistent with juvenile papillomatosis. While the margins are\u000afocally microscopically involved, the gross lesion appears to be\u000aexcised.\u000aDr. Andrea Richardson of the Breast Pathology Service has reviewed\u000athis case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Density seen by U/S at 8 o'clock. (See previous core biopsy).\u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue at 8 o'clock.\u000aShort stitch = superior margin.\u000aLong stitch = lateral margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1, left breast tissue at 8 o'clock", is a nodular fragment\u000aof fatty breast tissue (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; deep\u000amargin = blue; superior = black; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a somewhat cystic,\u000airregular shaped mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Areas of the mass are yellow and\u000aresemble fat necrosis grossly. Grossly, the mass lies at the deep and inferior\u000amargins. It lies REMOVED_DATE cm from the superficial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superficial margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass in its entirety with margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  normal appearing breast tissue, 2 frags each cass., RSS.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
