VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROBERT T OSTEEN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm) with associated microcalcifications\u000aand with atypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: The atypical ductal hyperplasia is focal and is limited to the\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Mammographic abnormality.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mammographic abnormality.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcs and hookwire in specimen. DIR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - needle loc R breast", and consists of a yellow/tan, unoriented\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization wire in place. The\u000aspecimen is inked black and serially sectioned, revealing a firm, white,\u000aill-defined lesion (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest margin, and\u000atraversed by the needle localization wire. As confirmed by the accompanying\u000aradiograph and radiology, the calcifications and hookwire are present within\u000athis area. Adjacent to the firm lesion is a unilocular, smooth-lined cyst (0.7\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The remaining breast tissue consists predominantly of\u000awhite/tan, cystic, dense fibrous stroma (approximately 80%) and scant yellow,\u000alobulated adipose tissue. No other lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000a[NOTE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain tan/white firm lesion; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains cyst.]\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
