VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED WIRE EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (present in 1 of 22 blocks) with associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aSingle lobular unit with squamous metaplasia, nuclear pleomorphism and\u000amitoses. Surrounding stromal reaction (see note).\u000aBenign epithelium with associated microcalcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts, multifocal.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen on microscopic examination, incluing margins.\u000aNOTE: Despite atypical nuclei and a peculiar architecture of squamous\u000ametaplasia, it is probable that this focus represents a vigorous reaction to\u000athe previous core biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), rather than atypical hyperplasia or DCIS.\u000aIn any event, this lobule is completely excised with negative margins\u000a(greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to nearest margin).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast hyperplasia\u000aOperation: Right needle-localized wire breast excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast, tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications and clip in specimen. OR called.\u000a[signature illegible]\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "1) right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (7 x 6 x 3 cm). The specimen is received inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aWithin the specimen, there are two (2) wires. The specimen is received with a\u000amammogram. The specimen radiograph was examined. On the mammogram, multiple\u000afoci of calcifications are seen, as well as the clip. On sectioning, an area\u000aof biopsy cavity (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) is identified. The clip is identified, and\u000atissue surrounding the clip is placed in microcassettes one and two. On\u000asectioning, no discrete masses are identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around clip, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of tissue around wire close to clip,\u000amulti frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around second wire, multi frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue away from wires, multi frag, RSS\u000aafn\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
