VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY, AXILLARY LYMPH NODES AND ADDITIONAL DEEP, LATERAL AND\u000aINFERIOR MARGINS (FIVE SPECIMENS):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (low to intermediate\u000anuclear grade), is present in at least 7 of 36 blocks, adjacent to and away\u000afrom excision site changes.\u000aNecrosis is associated with DCIS. No calcifications are associated with DCIS.\u000aNo definite residual invasive carcinoma is present in breast tissue (see note).\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is seen in breast tissue.\u000aDCIS is present <0.1 cm from the deep margin in the mastectomy specimen (0.5 cm\u000afront; block 31). Separately submitted additional deep, lateral and inferior\u000amargins with no carcinoma seen (specimens C, D, E).\u000aSkin with scar and underlying biopsy site changes; no carcinoma seen.\u000aNipple with no carcinoma seen.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium and stroma.\u000aMETASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA is present in at least one (1) of six (6) axillary\u000alymph nodes. The largest deposit measures REMOVED_DATE cm, with at least REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aassociated extracapsular extension. Carcinoma is also present within axillary\u000alymphatics.\u000aNOTE: The patient has a history of right breast invasive ductal carcinoma\u000astatus post excision and axillary node dissection in 1993 and a recently\u000aexcised right breast invasive lobular carcinoma (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMetastatic carcinoma is seen in lymph node tissue with extensive involvement of\u000aadjacent extranodal tissue in the current specimen labeled "mid axillary\u000acontents ?fibrosis". No breast epithelium is seen in axillary tissue.\u000aMorphologic and immunophenotypic features of the metastatic carcinoma are\u000adistinct from the recently excised invasive lobular carcinoma. The mastectomy\u000aspecimen has been extensively searched and additional tissue submitted for\u000ahistologic examination. No additional foci of invasive lobular or invasive\u000aductal carcinoma are seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for metastatic carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (2+)\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in the metastatic carcinoma, consistent with ductal phenotype.\u000aOf note, immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in the invasive lobular carcinoma (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aFISH analysis for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu might be helpful if clinically warranted.\u000aInterpretation of immunoperoxidase studies:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Past history carcinoma right breast 1993 (invasive ductal, well\u000adifferentiated, with DCIS)-> lumpectomy + radiation, 15 negative nodes ->\u000arecent mammogram plus lumpectomy (invasive lobular carcinoma and DCIS).\u000aOperation: Right total mastectomy plus axillary dissection.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: PreOp: Carcinoma right breast (recurrent). PostOp: Same.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast with lower axillary contents (short stitch superior, long\u000astitch axilla).\u000aB/2. Right mid axillary contents - ? fibrosis.\u000aC/3. Right breast tissue from pectoralis majoris.\u000aD/4. Serous fascia lower lateral breast right.\u000aE/5. Right inferior breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aSpecimen #1, labeled "#1. Right breast with lower axillary contents", consists\u000aof a 196 gram right mastectomy specimen (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan\u000askin ellipse (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a well healed scar in the lower outer\u000aquadrant (3.6 cm) and a completely retracted nipple (0.6 cm). A short stitch\u000aat the skin ellipse designates superior, a long stitch is attached to the\u000aaxillary fat. The deep surface of the specimen is covered by a focally\u000adisrupted (1.3 cm) fascial plane. This area is inked in blue, the remaining\u000afascia is inked in black. The lateral aspect of the specimen contains a short\u000aaxillary tail (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). An area of white/yellow/brown fat necrosis\u000awith focal hemorrhage (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present, extending from the\u000acentral portion of the breast to the lower outer quadrant. No discrete masses\u000aare identified. The remaining breast tissue is composed of yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue with fibrous septae (approximately 10% of specimen).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma around fat necrosis, consecutively from\u000alateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous area of central deep breast, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Axillary adipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional lateral tissue, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional medial tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aSpecimen #2, labeled "#2. Right mid axillary contents, ? fibrosis", consists of\u000atwo pieces of tan/yellow adipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) with\u000atwo ill-defined white firm masses (1.0 and REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Larger mass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second mass, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node and fibroadipose tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining adipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aSpecimen #3, labeled "#3. Right breast tissue from pectoralis major", consists\u000aof two pieces of fibroadipose tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which\u000aare not further oriented.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aSpecimen #4, labeled "#4. Right serous fascia lower lateral breast", consists\u000aof one fragment of tan/brown fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), entirely\u000asubmitted in one micro cassette.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags, ESS.\u000aSpecimen #5, labeled "#5. Right inferior breast tissue", consists of three\u000afragments of tan/yellow adipose tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are not\u000afurther oriented. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSTS:jjk\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
