VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (levels examined; blocks 7 and 8).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies for e-cadherin reveal absent to markedly reduced\u000aimmunoreactivity, consistent with this diagnosis (see note).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (e.g. block 22).\u000aComplex sclerosing lesions.\u000aColumnar hyperplasia.\u000aNumerous calcifications are present associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNote: Slides 7 and 8 have been reviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt, Dr. Susan\u000aLester, and Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concur with the diagnosis of LCIS.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma or DCIS is seen after complete microscopic\u000aexamination of the specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mammographic lesion.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast mass, short superior, long lateral\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Calcifications in specimen. Dr. Babagemi.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABREU-E-LIMA,PAULA C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Right breast mass", and consists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE (s-i) x REMOVED_DATE (m-l) x REMOVED_DATE (a-p) cm. The specimen is disrupted,\u000ahaving been partially transected in one plane, and reapproximated with surgical\u000asutures. The specimen is oriented with two sutures designating short (superior)\u000aand long (lateral).\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aContained within the specimen is a single localization wire corresponding to an\u000aarea of calcifications on the accompanying specimen radiograph.\u000aThe specimen is composed predominantly of fibrous tissue with focal cystic\u000achanges. The entire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breast tissue in serial sections from inferior to superior,\u000alikely calcifications in Micro REMOVED_DATE  multiple frags, ESS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
