aPart one, labeled "#1, lesion at 2:30" and is accompanied by a mammogram\u000ademonstrating a wire in breast tissue and a circumscribed breast mass. No\u000acalcifications or clip are identified. The specimen is marked with sutures:\u000ashort/superior and long/lateral, and is inked by the pathologist per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of firm\u000afibrous tissue. All of the fibrous tissue is examined histologically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, entire area of fibrous tissue is submitted,\u000a1-2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Wire #2, wire localization at 12 o'clock", and is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph dated REMOVED_DATE  which reveals one wire in specimen;\u000ano clip or microcalcifications are identified. The radiograph shows an\u000airregular density. The specimen is inked by the pathologist per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen consists of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Serial\u000asectioning of the specimen reveals an area of fibrous hard stellate breast\u000atissue (0.8 cm) that is within the center of the specimen. The entire fibrous\u000atissue is submitted.\u000aMicro 17: fibrous breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: fibrous breast tissue with area of stellate hard mass, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of fibrous tissue within specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000amrk\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
