VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. Calcifications are not associated with\u000aatypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aBenign dilated ducts with mucinous differentiation and associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 6-mm cluster punctate microcalcifications RIGHT breast on mammograms\u000a2/15/06 (850 Boylston, Chestnut Hills).\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Microcalcifications\u000aOperation: 11 G Stereotactic.\u000aOperative Findings: Multiple Ca+ seen in core samples.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS vs benign.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1_ 11-gauge core biopsy; right breast upper outer quadrant.\u000aOrange cassette:\u000aCa+ - Cassette A.\u000aNon-Ca+ - Cassette B.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Right\u000abreast", are two (2) orange cassettes (A. Ca++, B).\u000aCassette A is labeled "A. Ca++" and contains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty\u000asoft tissue cores (1.3 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aCassette B is labeled "b" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.3 X REMOVED_DATE X\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette A cores, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette B cores, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aAdditionally received, freely floating in the specimen container, is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of tan/yellow adipose tissue, entirely embedded in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Mingjian J You M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/6/2006\u000a[report_end]
