VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR ARCHITECTURAL\u000aDISTORTION":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), extensive sclerosing adenosis, apocrine\u000acysts, columnar cell changes, and calcification associated with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, ADDITIONAL POSTERIOR TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was also viewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast architectural distortion on mammography.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire-localized excision, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral (mammo).\u000aB/2) right breast additional posterior tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Targeted area is within the specimen. Conveyed to Dr. J. Jones\u000ain the OR. P. Burns (pb53).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast wire localized excision, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral", consists of an ovoid white/tan breast excision specimen (3.3 A\u000a- P x REMOVED_DATE S - I x REMOVED_DATE M - L cm) oriented per surgeon with two sutures: short =\u000asuperior, long = lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one\u000aneedle-localization wire in place, entering the anterolateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exiting the posterior medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen\u000awas previously radiographed, confirming the target area within the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to exhibit\u000aapproximately 75% dense focally cystic tan/pink fibrous stroma and\u000aapproximately 25% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The fibrous stroma\u000aextends to all six inked margins. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from anterior to posterior, multi frags total,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast additional posterior tissue", consists of an\u000aunoriented yellow/tan tissue (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one ragged/cauterized\u000asurface (inked blue per prosector) and an opposite smooth surface (inked\u000ablack). Please note that the new true margin surface is not designated per\u000asurgeon. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit greater than 90% dense\u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue and less than 10% yellow/tan adipose tissue. No\u000adiscrete masses are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
