VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ERICA L MAYER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM JORDAN HOSPITAL, PLYMOUTH, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST CORE BIOPSY FOR A NODULE (06:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade I/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen.\u000aNo definitive lymphovascular invasion identified in this limited specimen.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU NEGATIVE\u000aRIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSIES (06:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), two foci, REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm by report.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion identified.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aPagetoid spread of the LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU involves a major lactiferous\u000aduct (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDeep margin is negative for invasive and in situ carcinoma.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults (not reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE (90%)\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE (70%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU 1+/NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (FISH) REMOVED_DATE (NOT AMPLIFIED)\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA present in one (1) of five (5) lymph nodes, measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, with focal extranodal extension.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn)\u000aLEFT BREAST, STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS (08:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA with lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in\u000athis limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion identified in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type, (low nuclear grade), without necrosis or\u000acalcifications.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE (95%)\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE (95%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU 0/NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (FISH) REMOVED_DATE EQUIVOCAL (by report)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: LCIS in the right breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right Br ILC and LCIS; left Br IDLC\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Jordan Hospital, Pathology Department, 275 Sandwich Street,\u000aPlymouth, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are thirty-two (32) glass slides.\u000aNine (9) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1", "3", "(+)ctrl/ER",\u000a"(+)ctrl/PR", "(+)ctrl/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID HercepTest", "(+)ctrl/Ki-67", "(+)ctrlp53" and "Neg\u000aControl"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), corresponding to a right breast core biopsy (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aSeventeen (17) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) sentinel node #1, hot, excision\u000a(2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) sentinel node #2, hot, excision (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) C)\u000asentinel node #3, hot, excision (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) D) sentinel node #4, very\u000ahot, excision (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) E) right breast simple mastectomy (26.7 x\u000a23.2 x 3 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name.\u000aSeven (7) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "A (+)ctrl/ER", "A\u000a(+)ctrl/PR"," A (+)ctrl/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID HercepTest", "A Neg Control", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000acorresponding to a left breast core needle biopsies A) with microcalcifications\u000a(1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) remaining tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on\u000a9/24/08, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25, 2008 at 06:23:31PM\u000a[report_end]
