VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. TISSUE FROM RIGHT BREAST (ABNORMAL AREA) - FS RM - MAMMO LONG\u000aSTITCH/LATERAL, SHORT STITCH/SUPERIOR:\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium, apocrine metaplasia, atypical\u000alobular hyperplasia, Columnar alteration of lobules with prominent\u000aapocrine snouts, adenosis, sclerosing adenosis, and dense\u000ainterlobular fibrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aB/2. LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN RIGHT BREAST - SUTURE IS LATERAL:\u000aBreast tissue (2.3 x 2 x 1 cm) with no significant pathologic change.\u000aC/3. TISSUE FROM LEFT BREAST:\u000aBreast tissue with fibroadenomatous change, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, atypical lobular hyperplasia,\u000aadenosis and dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Micro calcs rt breast, perceived mass in lt @ 500.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo R (micro-calcs), possible mass L breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - tissue from right breast (abnormal area) --> fs rm --> mammo, long\u000astitch/lateral, short stitch/superior (while inking huge drop of red dye\u000adropped on ant blue).\u000aB/2 - lateral shave margin right breast - suture is lateral.\u000aC/3 - tissue from left breast.\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Ca++ wire in specimen. Reviewed with Dr. Christian/SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - tissue from right breast", consists of a single 32 gram\u000abreast excision specimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(anterior to posterior) x REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior). The specimen is\u000areceived already inked by the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a wire that enters the\u000alateral aspect of the specimen and the tip is visible on the anterior face of\u000athe specimen. Examination of the radiograph accompanying the specimen reveals\u000athe wire to pass through an area of calcifications. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from inferior to superior, such that the inferior-most slice is\u000adesignated at slice one. The wire passes between slices two and three. The\u000aspecimen consists of mostly firm, dense, white fibrous tissue. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one, 7 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice two, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice three, 4 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice four, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice five, 4 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice six, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice seven, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - lateral shave margin right breast", consists of a single\u000abreast excision shave specimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000asingle suture marking the lateral surface per surgeon, and this surface is\u000aalready inked yellow by the surgeon. The opposite surface is inked black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned, and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral shave margin of right breast, 6 frags total, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - tissue from left breast", consists of four unoriented\u000abreast tissue fragments, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. The entire\u000aouter surface of each fragment is inked black. Serial sectioning of fragments\u000aone, two and three reveal predominantly white, firm, fibrous tissue and serial\u000asectioning of fragment four reveals mostly soft, tan/yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fragment one, 4 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fragment two, 3 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fragment three, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fragment four, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aROH/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
