VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aUsual ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcificiations in benign epithelium.\u000aCysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (approxmately REMOVED_DATE cm) with epithelial\u000ahyperplasia and features of intraductal papilloma with associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aMedial arterial calcifications.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, breast pathology service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications, left breast.\u000aOperation: Excision of mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Specimen labeled "#1. Tissue from LIQ (lt) breast".\u000aSpecimen labeled "#2. Tissue from UOQ (lt) breast".\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000a#1. Tissue from LIQ, Lt breast:\u000aCa++ in specimen.\u000aSigned: S. Durfee, MD.\u000a#2. Tissue from UOQ, Lt breast:\u000aThe distortion is in the specimen.\u000aSigned: D.N. Smith, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and two accompanying radiographs.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Tissue from lower inner quadrant left breast", consists\u000aof a previously inked specimen that is in accordance with the pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange and\u000aconsists of a single fragment of unremarkable fibroadipose breast tissue\u000a(superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm; medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen radiograph reveals a loose cluster of\u000acalcifications and localization wire. The blocks are radiographed and the\u000acluster is identified in Block 4. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Posterior margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Body of lesion with respect to medial, lateral, superior, and\u000ainferior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. Tissue from upper outer quadrant left breast", received\u000afresh is a fragment of fibroadipose breast tissue (medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm;\u000ainferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains no focal nodules are lesions,\u000ahowever, it appears to be diffusely involved by dilated fibrous firm white\u000adilated tubes, which do not express necrotic material upon gentle palpation.\u000aThese abnormal structures cover an area of approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aand appear to abut medial and anterior margins, and come within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm of superior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior. The\u000aspecimen radiograph reveals a central core of architectural distortion near the\u000alocalization wire and scattered clacifications in the specimen. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior and lateral margins, 8 frags, ESS.\u000ahdh\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
