VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPALSIA (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm).\u000aCysts with apocrine metaplasia and microcalcifications.\u000aRadial sclerosing lesions.\u000aNOTE: No carcinoma is seen after complete histologic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: (L) micro-Ca++ on screening mammo, increased risk breast cancer.\u000aOperation: (L) wire localization biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications (L) breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(L) breast tissue with wire REMOVED_DATE \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Wire and calcs contained in specimen. ? Dr. Elman\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue with wire in", and consists of a portion of breast\u000atissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0.6 cm. The specimen does not have sutures, and\u000ait is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol. A wire is present in the\u000aspecimen. A radiograph accompanies the specimen, showing a wire and\u000amicrocalcifications close to the wire tip. The specimen is bisected along the\u000awire. The wire tip is present along the medial and posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is 99% fibrous tissue with some cystic areas. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. The area at the wire tip is submitted in\u000ablocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags, ESS.\u000aref/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Rachel E Factor M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/17/2005\u000a[report_end]
