posterior/black,\u000aanterior/blue, superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is bisected along the localization wire and a gross lesion at the\u000asite of the clip is not seen. The specimen consists of 90% yellow adipose\u000atissue and 10% dense white tissue. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from inferior to superior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Inferior lesion right breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (superior\u000ato inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000abiopsy with a localization wire in place and short suture marking the superior\u000aand the long suture marking lateral margins. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a clip close to the superior and medial margin. The\u000aspecimen is inked for the evaluation of margins posterior/black, anterior/blue,\u000asuperior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, and medial/equals orange. The\u000aspecimen is bisected along the localization wire and a clip was found close to\u000athe superior and lateral margin. No gross lesion at the site of clip is seen.\u000aThe specimen consists of 90% yellow/white adipose tissue and less than 10%\u000adense fibrous tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior and 95% of the specimen is submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from superior to inferior with the clip site and\u000aadjacent tissue in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aLC/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
