VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy site changes, cysts, and apocrine\u000achange.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: A 62-year-old woman with abnormal mammo, left atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia and stereotactic core for microcalcifications.\u000aOperation: Left breast wide excision with wire localization.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Left abnormal mammo, left atypical breast ductal\u000ahyperplasia. Postop: Left abnormal mammo, left atypical breast ductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue with wire, clip in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, in a container labeled with the\u000apatient's name, medical record number, and "left breast tissue with wire", and\u000aconsists of a wire localized breast excision (2.8 cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is inked\u000aprior to receipt in pathology by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. No sutures are present to\u000aconfirm the orientation of the specimen. A localization wire traverses the\u000aspecimen from inferior to superior. Due to the orientation of the specimen,\u000athe specimen is sectioned from posterior to lateral in seven slices. The\u000alocalization wire is present in slice #3. The clip is identified in slice #3.\u000aAdjacent to the clip is a well-circumscribed white nodule (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin and approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. No other\u000agross abnormalities are identified. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000acomposed of less than 10% fibrous tissue and over 90% adipose tissue. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted. A radiograph is received with the specimen\u000ademonstrating a localization and a clip within the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 (posterior margin), perpendicular sections, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 with nodule and superior, medial, inferior, posterior\u000amargin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 with nodule and clip site with inferior, superior,\u000aposterior, medial margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 with inferior, superior, medial, posterior margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 with posterior, anterior, inferior, superior margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 with inferior, superior, anterior margins, 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 (lateral margin), perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000ajub/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/26/2007\u000a[report_end]
