VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (levels examined; not associated with\u000acalcifications).\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNumerous calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNumerous calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 73-year-old female with mammogram REMOVED_DATE  left breast with increasing\u000apunctate calcifications at 3 o'clock. Right breast with grouped punctate and\u000around calcifications in UOQ.\u000aOperation: Bilateral needle directed breast biopsies.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whip-\u000astitch and deep margin and colors as per path.\u000a2. Left needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aRadiology: Specimens #1 and #2 have calcifications in both specimens.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue", consists of a right breast wire\u000alocalized biopsy specimen (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains a short stitch\u000adenoting the superior and long stitch denoting lateral margin. The specimen\u000aalso contains a wire localization needle. No whipstitch is identified. The\u000aspecimen has been previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph shows the specimen with the wire localization needle\u000anear a site of a small group of microcalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from a lateral to medial, revealing\u000apredominantly white-yellow adipose tissue with very minimal amount of fibrous\u000atissue, with no masses or lesions suggestive of malignancy, which are grossly\u000aidentified. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: lateral perpendicular margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right wire localized breast biopsy from lateral to medial,\u000a1-2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: medial perpendicular margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of a\u000afragmented, unoriented left wire localized breast biopsy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate; two (2) fragments are connected by a very small\u000aportion of tissue and contain a needle localization wire. This larger fragment\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The smaller detached fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph shows the specimen to be intact, with a wire\u000alocalization needle at the site of a small cluster of microcalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is inked in black and serially sectioned to reveal predominantly\u000ayellow adipose tissue with a very small amount of white fibrous tissue, with no\u000amasses or lesions suggestive of malignancy grossly identified. The specimen is\u000aradiographed and the slices containing microcalcifications are entirely\u000asubmitted; representative sections of the detached fragment are also submitted.\u000aApproximately 30% of the entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast wire localized biopsy, containing calcifications,\u000amulti frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 20: detached fragment, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aNOTE: Slices containing the microcalcifications are submitted in micro 17\u000athrough 19.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
