VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aBreast tissue with fat necrosis, hemorrhage, hemosiderin deposition,\u000afibrosis, and focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "MEDIAL SPECIMEN, RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with prior biopsy site with associated hemorrhage,\u000afibrosis, hemosiderin deposition, multinucleated giant cells, and\u000afat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: MRI for breast discomfort --> abnormal area; MRI core bx --> ADH.\u000aOperation: Wire=directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast discomfort --> abnormal area.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Specimen with wire, right breast tissue.\u000aB/2) Medial specimen, Right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1. Tissue with wire.\u000a2. Tissue marker present (MRI tissue marker). C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Specimen with wire", consists of a yellow/tan unoriented breast\u000aexcision (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a radiographic localization wire. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a wire running through the\u000aspecimen with the prior biopsy site changes. The section of breast tissue\u000aclosest to the curled wire edge is inked yellow and closest to the bent wire\u000aedge is inked blue. The remainder of the specimen is inked black. The main\u000aspecimen has a central friable dark brown area closest to the blue-inked margin\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Additionally, separate fragments of fibroadipose tissue\u000aaccompany the main specimen (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Wire localized specimen, serially sectioned from blue to yellow\u000amargin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Unoriented separate fibroadipose tissue frags, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Medial specimen", consists of a firm yellow/tan/red fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates the tissue fragment with a centrally located MRI clip. No other\u000acalcifications are identified. The specimen is inked black and is serially\u000asectioned.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen serially sectioned, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aKRI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/31/2008\u000a[report_end]
