breast", consists of two (2) light green cassettes.\u000aOne cassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains multiple tan to\u000ared fibrofatty cores of breast tissue. They range up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter x\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm in maximum length, and demonstrate hemorrhagic areas. The\u000aother cassette is labeled "B" and contains multiple tan to red fibrofatty\u000acores of breast tissue. They range up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter x approximately\u000a1.5 cm in maximum length, and demonstrate hemorrhagic areas.\u000aMicro 3: "A" multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: "B" multi frags, ESS.\u000adf\u000aReports to: LORANS, ROXANNE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
