VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (levels examined).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign breast epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51 year old female with history of right abnormal mammogram.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast biopsy.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aArea of concern on specimen radiograph identified.\u000aBest evaluated on permanent sections.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Localized area is on specimen. C. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by VARGAS,SARA OAKES,M.D.\u000aReceived in one part, designated "right breast biopsy", is a single fragment of\u000ayellow/white fibrofatty tissue (5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm) with a localization wire in\u000aplace. An area of calcification corresponding to the mammographic lesion is\u000aidentified and considered too small (less than REMOVED_DATE cm) to freeze.\u000aMICRO #1: Area with calcification, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #2-11: 15 fragments, 11 cass, ESS.\u000aReports to: SINGER, SAMUEL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
