VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "NON-SENTINEL NODE":\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "SENTINEL NODE #1" (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1) (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE WITH PALPABLE MASS, EXCISION":\u000aBreast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, calcifications associated\u000awith benign epithelium, and interlobular fibrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: No core biopsy site or clip was identified after radiographic and\u000amicroscopic examination of the entire specimen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Rt breast Ca.\u000aOperation: Rt partial mastectomy; sentinel node bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Non-sentinel node.\u000aB/2) Sentinel node #1 (FS).\u000aC/3) Rt breast tissue with palpable mass (Tissue Banking)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. SENTINEL NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aNegative for metastatic carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: SHAKTI RAMKISSOON, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Nonsentinel node", consists of one fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing one pink/tan lymph node\u000acandidate (1.7 cm in greatest dimension) which is bisected.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, received fresh in the frozen section room, "#2. Sentinel node #1, FS",\u000aconsists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing\u000aone lymph node candidate (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph node candidate was\u000apreviously entirely frozen as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. RT breast tissue with palpable mass, tissue banking" received\u000afresh in a frozen section room for tissue allocation, and consists of a\u000ayellow/tan breast excision specimen (7.5 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm). The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was previously serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral into a total ten slices (slice #1 equals medial, slice\u000a#10 equals lateral). The cut surface is composed of approximately 65%\u000adiffusely dense/nodular white/tan fibrous stroma extending to all six inked\u000amargins, and approximately 35% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000adiscrete masses grossly identified. In slices #3 through #7, there is an\u000aill-defined dense white/tan indurated area (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which extends\u000ato the superior and posterior margins, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin and\u000a1.5 cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin. The sectioned specimen was radiographed upon received in\u000apathology. A clip was not identified. In slice #5, within the possible mass,\u000athere is a probable calcification identified. No tissue was allocated to the\u000abreast tissue bank per Dr. Andrea Richardson. The specimen was entirely\u000asubmitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, ? mass with superior and anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, ? mass with superior, anterior and posterior\u000amargins, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, ? mass with superior and posterior margins and\u000apossible calcification, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, ? mass with anterior, superior, and posterior margins, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, ? mass with superior, and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #3 and #4, inferior margin, closest to ? mass, 1\u000afrag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #4 and #5, additional posterior margin, closest\u000ato ? mass with dense fibrous stroma, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, medial margin, closest to ? mass, with dense\u000afibrous stroma, perpendicular sections, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, lateral margin closest to ? mass,\u000aperpendicular section, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000alm/mmm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/8/2008\u000a[report_end]
