VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFERO-MEDIAL MARGIN, RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED\u000aPARTIAL MASTECTOMY FOR A MASS, CALCIFICATIONS, AND A CLIP":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior, superior, anterior, medial,\u000ainferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral (0.2 cm; focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, posterior, medial, inferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral (0.1 cm; focal)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Anterior (focal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb NX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy site changes, negative for tumor.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue, negative for tumor.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN (DEEP SUBAREOLAR)":\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy site changes, negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast cancer s/p excision for palpable mass. Thought to\u000acorrespond with core biopsy proven right breast cancer seen on imaging. Prior\u000aexcision showed benign mass forming changes but no cancer.\u000aOperation: Right wire localized partial mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Specimen mammo + clip, ca++ and density; mass not palpable.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, calcification and spiculated mass are included in specimen.\u000aCalled to OR 7 @ 16:13 Hesham Malik\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Inferior medial margin with 2 wires - mammo.\u000aB/2. Additional deep margin - blue prior resection black = chest wall.\u000aC/3. Additional inferior margin - black = new true inferior margin.\u000aD/4. Addition al deep margin - black new true medial margin (deep subareolar).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right inferomedial margin with two wires", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by inked per surgeon\u000aaccording to pathology breast inking protocol. (The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.)\u000aThere are two localizing wires in place within the specimen, one entering\u000aanterolaterally and exiting anteromedially, and a second entering\u000aposterolaterally and exiting posteromedially, through the central aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wires in\u000aplace within the specimen, adjacent to a spiculated lesion marked by a metallic\u000asurgical clip in the central aspect of the specimen. The specimen is sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral, revealing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white lobulated\u000aill-defined lesion centrally, within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior margin,\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest posterior\u000amargin, and remote (at least REMOVED_DATE cm) from the medial margin. Please note:\u000aMetallic surgical clip is identified in this area. Additionally, marked by a\u000asecond, more linear clip (1.4 cm) superior to the previously mentioned lesion\u000ais an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE cm from fibrous area abutting the superior/lateral\u000amargin. There are no additional lesions grossly. Remainder of the specimen is\u000acomprised of at least 10% lobulated fibrous tissue, without additional masses\u000anoted grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from medial to\u000alateral, with perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, central lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and peripheral superior lesion\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "additional deep margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue, previously inked by the surgeon as follows: Blue equals\u000aprior resection, black equals chest wall. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand entirely sequentially submitted. Cut surfaces demonstrate a predominantly\u000asoft, lobulated, tan/yellow adipose tissue, with occasional scant fibrous\u000aseptae. There is no palpable or visible tumor or other abnormality grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Additional inferior margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue, previously partially inked black on one broad\u000asurface by the surgeon, designating "new true inferior margin". The opposing\u000asurface (likely not true margin) is inked in blue by the prosector, the\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely sequentially submitted. Cut\u000asurfaces demonstrate predominantly soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue\u000a(at least 90%), with occasional tan/white fibrous septae. There are no\u000apalpable or visible abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Additional medial margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue, previously partially inked black on one broad\u000asurface by the surgeon, designating "new true medial margin". The opposing\u000a(not true margin) surface is inked blue by the prosector, the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and entirely sequentially submitted. Cut surfaces\u000ademonstrate focal fibrosis and fat necrosis along the blue-inked surface.\u000aThere are no obvious masses grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
