VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aRadial scar.\u000aFibroadenoma (1.0 cm).\u000aFibrocystic change with cysts, apocrine metaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications present in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass not palpable. Mammogram reveals nodule deep in\u000abreast, probably benign. Past history of fibroadenoma left breast\u000ain 1990.\u000aOperation: Right breast resection (wire localization)\u000aOperative findings: Palpable nodule near wire\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Nodule right breast\u000a?Fibroadenoma, rule out cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast mass - mammo, suture on lesion\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS":\u000aGrossly benign firm mass, possibly a fibroadenoma.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications and small mass with fragment of wire.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHAN,JENNIFER A.,M.D.,C.M.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "right breast\u000amass", are three unoriented fragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (1.7 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The REMOVED_DATE cm fragment\u000ahas a needle localization wire in place. The REMOVED_DATE cm fragment has a suture.\u000aThe REMOVED_DATE cm (sutured) fragment has a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm round, lobulated,\u000arubbery, well circumscribed mass which bulges from the cut surface. The mass\u000ais located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked edge. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - largest frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - medium size fragment with nodule, 2 f, ESS.\u000aMicro 5 - smallest fragment, 1 f, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
