VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFocal epithelial hyperplasia with ATYPIA (best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, level 1; see\u000anote).\u000aApocrine cysts with associated microcalcifications.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications.\u000aNOTE: No evidence of amyloid deposition is seen. Atypia is evaluated best\u000afollowing excision. Slides seen also by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications and flat epithelial ATYPIA\u000a(see note).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: No evidence of amyloid deposition is seen. Atypia is evaluated best\u000afollowing excision. Slides seen also by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 45 y/o patient with family h/o amyloidosis and few elements of disease\u000ain her; wanted a Congo red stain but, per Dr. Lester, H&E is sufficient.\u000aPresently, stereotactic biopsy for new calcifications, L breast UOQ.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 3 mm, Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000a2. Right: 4 mm, Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000a2. Right: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8G Stereotactic\u000a2. 8G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. A - with calcs; B - no calcs - Blue cassette.\u000aB/2. A - with calcs; B - no calcs - Pink cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast blue", consists of two blue cassettes. First blue\u000acassette labeled "A. Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical tan/pink tissues (2.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Second blue cassette labeled "B", contains\u000amultiple cylindrical pink/tan tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Blue cassette A contents (A. CA++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Blue cassette B contents (B), multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast pink", consists of two pink cassettes. First\u000apink cassette labeled "A. Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical tan/pink tissues\u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Second pink cassette labeled "B", contains\u000amultiple cylindrical yellow/tan tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Pink cassette A contents (A. Ca++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Pink cassette B contents (B), multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
