VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: HOPE E PETERS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES:\u000a9:00, REMOVED_DATE CM, IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH).\u000aGynecomastoid hyperplasia.\u000a10:00, REMOVED_DATE CM, INDISTINCT MASS:\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH).\u000aGynecomastoid hyperplasia.\u000aNote: The findings in both biopsies are identical. PASH can be\u000aassociated with circumscribed or ill-defined masses. Radiologic\u000acorrelation is suggested to ensure the biopsies are representative of the\u000aradiologic lesions.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: History of right breast biopsy with ADH in 1992 (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). History\u000aof prior reduction mammoplasty with mammographic mass (left), shown to be 2\u000amasses possibly connected by a tubular duct on ultrasound. REMOVED_DATE cm apart.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: Nonpalpable irregular mass, hypoechoic with echogenic borders,\u000apartially obscured margins. REMOVED_DATE cm. ? fat necrosis.\u000a2. Left: Nonpalpable, hypoechoic, partially indistinct margins, echogenic\u000aborders. REMOVED_DATE cm. Similar to mass at 9:00.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: 9:00\u000a2. Left: 10:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000a2. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. 5 samples - Blue cassette\u000aB/2. 4 samples - Pink cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast, 9 o'clock, blue", consists of multiple cylindrical\u000atan/yellow tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Blue cassette contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast, 10 o'clock, pink", consists of multiple cylindrical\u000apink/tan tissues (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Pink cassette contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/21/2007\u000a[report_end]
