VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLEE, KENNETH, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LEE,KENNETH ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with polarizable crystalline material consistent with\u000acalcium oxalate in association with apocrine metaplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aInterlobular fibrosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalfications right breast. No palpable mass.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed excision breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalfications right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aOne or two calcifications in specimen.\u000aThe specimen, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast tissue", consists of four fragments of tissue (4.5 x\u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). A specimen radiograph is also received. The\u000alargest fragment (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) contains a localization wire and is\u000acomprised primarily of fibrous tissue with surrounding adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is otherwise unoriented. The other three fragments of tissue were\u000areceived unattached from the main specimen and it is unclear how they relate\u000ato the main specimen from the radiograph which only shows the largest fragment\u000aof tissue with wire and they are primarily comprised of adipose tissue. The\u000asurface of all fragments is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - largest fragment with wire, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - remaining fragments of tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aNote: The area of calcifications is primarily in micros 2 through 5.\u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
