VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aMarkedly atypical epithelial cells involving a lobular unit, present <0.1\u000acm from the nearest inked margin (see note).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aNOTE: Some of the acini in this lobular unit also show small foci of necrosis.\u000aWhile it is difficult to determine the nature of this process with certainty,\u000athe possibility that this represents DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU involving a\u000alobule cannot be excluded. Given the severity of the atypia and the proximity\u000aof this lesion to the inked margin, a re-excision should be performed if\u000aclinically feasible. (Dr. Stuart Schnitt, Breast pathologist, has reviewed\u000aselected slides of this case.)\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with adenosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications right breast. Past history of right breast\u000aresection (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aOperation: Right breast resection (wire)\u000aOperative findings: No suspicious lesion\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue to mammo\u000a2. Right breast tissue - to mammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT (Right breast tissue #2):\u000aCalcifications not definitely seen.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 2 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "right breast tissue", consists of three fragments of fibroadipose\u000atissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). A wire is present in the specimen\u000abag, but it is not associated with any part of the specimen. The specimens\u000aare inked, sectioned and entirely submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - right breast tissue, each fragment bisected, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "right breast tissue", consists of a lump of fibroadipose tissue (1.0 x\u000a0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is inked, bisected and entirely submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro 3 - right breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
