VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - no residual invasive tumor present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm)\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 2:10 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: CA of rt breast, 3 resections, still close margin; hence, mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Total mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer of rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast, short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a 501-gram\u000amastectomy specimen (19 x 15 x 4 cm) with a tan/white skin ellipse (17 x 10 cm)\u000awhich contains areola (3.4 x 4 cm) and unremarkable nipple (1.1 cm diameter).\u000aTwo linear, well-healed surgical scars are identified, the first one measures 4\u000acm and is located REMOVED_DATE cm superiorly and laterally to the nipple; the second\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm and is located REMOVED_DATE cm inferiorly to the nipple. The deep\u000aexcision margin is partially covered by fascia and partially covered by\u000awhite/tan, glistening surface (9 x 3 cm) which is grossly consistent with the\u000aprevious biopsy site. This area extends to an adjacent cavity (3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). Surrounding area of fibrosis is present in this area. This large biopsy\u000asite is located underneath the skin scar, partially becoming part of deep\u000aexcisional margin. The deep margin is inked. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted. No lymph nodes are identified within the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity with closest margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: inner outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000ajis\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
