VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aINCE, TAN, A., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by INCE,TAN A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aAdenosis with associated microcalcifications.\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma.\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by INCE,TAN A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe adenosis associated with calcifications has some columnar cell change and\u000athere is a small area of cribriforming (additional levels examined).\u000aThis lesion is difficult to classify due to its small size. The case was shown\u000ato other breast pathologists without consensus as to whether the findings are\u000asufficient for classification as atypical ductal hyperplasia. Thus, this\u000alesion is best classified as "hyperplasia with atypia" but not sufficient for a\u000astrict diagnosis of ADH.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Dr. Stuart Schnitt, Dr. Andrea\u000aRichardson, and Dr. James Connolly.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left upper inner calcifications 4 mm cluster.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast core samples (pink cassettes - ca++ in A)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of two (2) pink cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow\u000ato white tissue cores (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette\u000ais labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: MEYER, JACK, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
