VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, CENTRAL DUCT, EXCISION:\u000aDuct ectasia with periductal chronic inflammation, florid epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aSmall intraductal papilloma (0.2 cm).\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks #6 and #7; levels examined).\u000aFocal columnar hyperplasia with severe nuclear atypa (block #8).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, involving lactiferous ducts.\u000aPeriductal chronic inflammation.\u000aCysts.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal right breast nipple discharge.\u000aOperation: Right central duct excision.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast central duct excision, short superior, long\u000alateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARLSON,JOSEPH WOODWARD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast central duct excision long lateral short\u000asuperior", and consists of a single fragment of fibrofatty tissue (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.3 cm) with two orienting sutures placed by the surgeon. The long suture\u000aindicates the lateral edge and the short suture indicates the superior edge.\u000aThe specimen is inked in the Pathology Department per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned\u000afrom superior to inferior in eight sections and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, medial to lateral, 8 frags, ESS.\u000ajoc\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
