VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM WINCHESTER HOSPITAL, WINCHESTER, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 6:00, SUBAREOLAR, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A MASS (02:SU REMOVED_CASE_ID;\u000a11/13/02):\u000aConsistent with fragments of a fibroadenoma.\u000aNote: The specimen is highly fragmented making evaluation difficult.\u000aRadiologic correlation is suggested to ensure the findings are consistent\u000awith the radiologic lesion.\u000aLEFT BREAST, STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A MASS (02:SU REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma with epithelial hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aNote: Epithelial hyperplasia is difficult to evaluate within a\u000afibroadenoma due to the distorted ductal architecture and frequent\u000atangential sectioning and artifactual disruption of epithelium. In this\u000acase, there does appear to be atypical hyperplasia within the fibroadenoma.\u000aThe significance of atypical ductal hyperplasia confined to a fibroadenoma,\u000ais currently not clearly defined.\u000aExcision would be helpful to completely evaluate this lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aReceived from Winchester Hospital, Pathology Department, 41 Highland Avenue,\u000aWinchester, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are thirteen (13) slides.\u000aOne (1) slide is labeled "02-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a\u000aleft breast core needle biopsy at 6 o'clock (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE cmf) performed on\u000a11/13/02, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aTwelve (12) slides are labeled "02-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "1\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "3 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "3 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "4 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "4 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"\u000athrough "4 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast stereotactic core needle biopsy\u000a(0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
