VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aFIRM TISSUE, EXCISION, LEFT BREAST:\u000aFlorid usual-type hyperplasia.\u000aIntraductal papillomata.\u000aTISSUE AT PERIPHERY OF OPERATIVE SITE:\u000aFlorid usual-type hyperplasia.\u000aIntraductal papillomata.\u000aThis case was also seen by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Strong F H breast cancer: dense breasts, MRI --> enlarged duct, Lt\u000abreast.\u000aOperation: MRI wire-directed excision of abnormal area (L) breast.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal MRI (L) breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(1) Tissue firm (L) breast - sent to mammography.\u000a(2) Bit of tissue @ periph of op site; stitch marks additional piece of\u000adilated duct (with probable mass within).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aWire and calcifications within the specimen\u000a- E. G., MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "1. Tissue from left breast", consists of one (1) fragment of\u000atan/pink, fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localizing wire,\u000apresent within the tissue. A radiograph is received with the specimen, which\u000ashows a wire and calcifications within the specimen. The external surface is\u000ainked entirely in black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000aapproximately 90% dense, white, fibrous tissue, through which the needle tract\u000apasses. There is approximately 10% interspersed, yellow, adipose tissue. No\u000amasses are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue from left breast, 1 frag each cassette.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Tissue, left breast", consists of one fragment of\u000awhite/pink soft tissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A stitch is present at one aspect\u000aof the specimen, designated by the surgeon as additional piece of dilated duct.\u000aThe area around the suture is inked in blue, and the remainder of the specimen\u000ais inked in black. The specimen is bisected to reveal a yellow/tan\u000afluid-filled cyst (0.3 cm in diameter). The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000alys/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
