VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES:\u000a14 G, UPPER INNER (9:30), REMOVED_DATE CM IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is seen in this limited specimen.\u000a11 G, 12:00, PALPABLE 2 CM MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade III/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types (high nuclear\u000agrade), without necrosis or calcifications, is present.\u000aNote: The two carcinomas are morphologically similar.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed for both invasive carcinomas and\u000areported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 56 year old woman with two masses. History of thyroid cancer.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 12 mm non-palpable irregular mass.\u000a2. Left: ~2 cm, palpable irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper inner 9:30\u000a2. Left: 12:00, approximately 2 cm above nipple\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000a2. 11 G Ultrasound Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left - 2 orange cassettes.\u000aB/2. Left - 8 passes - 2 yellow cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast #1", and consists of two orange cassettes\u000acontaining cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassettes, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast #2", and consists of two yellow cassettes\u000acontaining multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues\u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of yellow cassettes, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aJC/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 13, 2009 at 04:17:45PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (3/17/09):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) EQUIVOCAL (2+)\u000aNOTE: Normal epithelium shows appropriate immunoreactivity for estrogen and\u000aprogesterone receptors.\u000aFISH analysis for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed; results will be reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000ainvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: Normal epithelium shows appropriate immunoreactivity for estrogen and\u000aprogesterone receptors.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH\u000a17, 2009 at 04:54:32PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (3/24/09)\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24, 