VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. See note.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications are present in association with the epithelial\u000ahyperplasia and atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aCicatrix.\u000aThree lymph nodes; no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: The atypical ductal hyperplasia arises in the context of a florid\u000aproliferative epithelial changes; the atypia does not quite satisfy\u000acriteria for DCIS (levels examined).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS in two quadrants, right upper and right medial\u000alower quadrant.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast (stitch marks axillary tail).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DEBNATH,JAYANTA,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast," and consists of a right simple\u000amastectomy specimen weighing 895 grams and measuring 26 x 18 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is\u000aa white/tan skin ellipse (19 x 13 cm) with two (2) well-healed surgical\u000ascars.The first scar is in the lower inner quadrant (4.5 cm in length), and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from an unremarkable nipple. The second is in the lower outer quadrant\u000a(4.5 cm), and is located 5 cm from an unremarkable 1 cm nipple. There is a\u000astitch that marks a short axillary tail and corresponds to level 1 lymph nodes\u000a(3 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep margin is inked in black, and consists of smooth\u000afascia, except for a surgical tear measuring 4 x 2 cm, which opens into a\u000ahollow cavity. Sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals a large biopsy\u000acavity, red/pink in color, and measuring 12 x 4 x 4 cm. The biopsy cavity is\u000agrossly REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm in its closest approach to\u000athe skin. The biopsy cavity is located 7 cm from the inferior aspect, 9 cm\u000afrom the lateral aspect, 7 cm from the superior aspect, and 4 cm from the\u000amedial aspect of the breast. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000aunremarkable with no evidence of any masses, and consists of 90% yellow/white\u000aadipose tissue and 10% grey/tan fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, including with respect to deep margin, multiple\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7 : upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8 : upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9 : lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10 : lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11 : scar in lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12 : scar in lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13 : nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14 : 1 lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15 : 2 lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
