VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MRI-DETECTED FOCAL AREA OF RAPID\u000aENHANCEMENT:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread into ducts.\u000aColumnar cell change with hyperplasia, calcifications, and flat epithelial\u000aatypia.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia with involvement by lobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aThere is no invasive malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female with R breast MRI on REMOVED_DATE  revealing REMOVED_DATE cm focal\u000aarea of rapid enhancement (posterior UIQ) - 7 cm from the nipple at 12:30 -\u000asurgical exc bx recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast MRI-guided WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, whip\u000astitch/chest wall margin -- FS to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMRI localization: specimen shows tissue and a few scattered calcifications.\u000aRB --> ER.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhipstitch chest wall margin", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting sutures ("short stitch equals\u000asuperior; long stitch equals lateral; whipstitch chest wall margin") and a\u000aneedle localization wire in placed (entering at the superolateral aspect and\u000aexiting at the superior aspect). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, which exhibit a few scattered\u000acalcifications and a hookwire in placed. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom superior to inferior, exhibiting approximately 75% tan/white dense,\u000afocally cystic fibrous stroma and 25% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000aother gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from superior to inferior (probable\u000acalcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000adl/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a8/15/2007\u000a[report_end]
