m of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin and greater\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins. A clip is identified in the\u000aspecimen adjacent to the mass. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000acomposed of approximately 60% fibrous tissue and 40% adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue with multiple margins, serially submitted\u000afrom lateral to medial, mult frags, ESS\u000aNOTE: The section with the clip is cut transversely and entirely submitted in\u000acassettes 11 and 12.\u000amsh\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
