VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident\u000aBRIANA CLAIRE GLEASON, M.D.\u000aPathologist\u000aGILBERT BRODSKY, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, comedo type, high nuclear grade, single focus\u000a(0.1 cm) involving a large duct, present <0.1 cm from the unoriented\u000aresection margin, with associated microcalcifications.\u000aCalcifications also seen in association with benign atrophic duct.\u000aHormone receptor studies pending.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications, left breast, in site near cancer. Treated 1989.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-directed excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA) Tissue from left breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications and hookwire in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand ?Tissue from left breast?, and consists of an unoriented breast excision\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localizing wire in place. The specimen is\u000aaccompanies by a radiograph that demonstrates a cluster of microcalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is inked black. The gross parenchyma is approximately 50% fibrous\u000atissue and 50% adipose tissue, and no discrete lesions are identified. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast, 7 frags, ESS.\u000abgl/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: Only a single duct involved by DICS is present on the\u000aimmunohistochemistry stained slide.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/20/2005\u000a[report_end]
