ior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000aand entirely submitted. No focal abnormalities are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, 10 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x d2.5 cm\u000ayellow/tan breast specimen which has two orienting sutures indicating 12\u000ao'clock and lateral. Two wires are present within the specimen. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted\u000afrom lateral to medial. No clip was identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast, 15 frags, ESS\u000absc\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
