VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aJONES, DANIEL, MORGAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by JONES,DANIEL MORGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, NEEDLE DIRECTED BIOPSY:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU, present in three of thirty one blocks\u000awith pagetoid spread.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibrocystic change including cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and numerous\u000amicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 42 year old female with abnormal mammogram with increased\u000acalcifications in upper outer aspect of right breast, s/p left needle\u000alocalization in 1995 of fibroadenoma.\u000aOperation: Right needle direct breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue - marker on wire labeled anterior\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (GROSS EXAM ONLY):\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GINEVAN,KIM MICHELE,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimensions with two\u000aneedle localization wires in place. The specimen is oriented by Dr. Shoji such\u000athat the microcalcifications are near the medial margin on mammography. Cut\u000asectioning reveals dense, white/tan fibroadipose tissue without areas grossly\u000aconsistent with invasive carcinoma. The specimen is inked as follows:\u000adeep=black, superficial=blue, medial=red, lateral=green, superior=yellow, and\u000ainferior=orange. Approximately ninety five per cent of the specimen is\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis (including all fibrous tissue).\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral inked perpendicular margin, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative breast tissue, multi frags, RSS\u000akmg\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
