VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY OF A MASS:\u000aCore biopsy site with adjacent pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia and\u000adense fibrous tissue forming a REMOVED_DATE cm mass.\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia, cysts and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia,\u000acysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55 year old postmenopausal female on estrogen patch, s/p REMOVED_DATE \u000aoutside hospital core biopsy of a mammographic density, left breast,\u000arevealing ADH and PASH.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ADH and PASH on core biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast tissue - palpable nodule in medial tail\u000a(short/superior; long/lateral; whip/deep margin)\u000a#2) Left superior shave margin (whip new margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. D.N. Smith,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast tissue long/lateral, whip/deep,\u000ashort/superior", consists of a piece of fibrofatty tissue white measures 9 x 6\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm which is irregular and outlined. The specimen has been marked by the\u000asurgeon with sutures and inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is an irregular white fibrous mass\u000aat the medial margin of the specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000amass is focally hemorrhagic and focally extends to the posterior margin of the\u000aspecimen. The mass extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin. The mass\u000aappears to be focally cystic. Of the remainder of the specimen, approximately\u000a5% consists of white fibrous tissue which extends to involve the medial margin\u000aof the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted from medial\u000ato lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass with medial posterior and inferior margins, 7 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 8: inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial and superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 13: inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left superior shaved margin whip new margin", consists\u000aof a portion of fibrofatty tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aspecimen has been marked on one surface by the surgeon with a suture. The\u000asurface is inked blue. The opposite surface is inked black. Approximately 5%\u000aof the specimen consists of white fibrous tissue which does not grossly appear\u000ato involve the margins. No other focal lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  8 frags, ESS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
