VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LUMPECTOMY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCIBAS, EDMUND, SAULIUS, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CIBAS,EDMUND SAULIUS,M.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aHealing biopsy site.\u000aNo residual tumor seen.\u000aFibrocystic change, focally proliferative.\u000a#2. ADDITIONAL DEEP LATERAL TISSUE:\u000aFibrocystic change, focally proliferative.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.2 cm).\u000a#3. ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS:\u000aSingle lymph node with diathermy artefact.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000a#4. LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS:\u000aNo tumor seen in twelve lymph nodes.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Infiltrating ductal carcinoma, left breast biopsy outside hospital.\u000aReceptors already done.\u000aOperation: Left lumpectomy and axillary dissection.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast partial mastectomy-short stitch medial-long\u000astitch superior.\u000a#2. Additional deep lateral tissue.\u000a#3. Left axillary contents.\u000a#4. Additional left axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RESNICK,MURRAY BERLE,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe first specimen, received fresh, labelled "left breast partial\u000amastectomy-short stitch medial and long stitch superior", consists of a skin\u000aellipse and underlying fibrous fatty tissue, measuring 9 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000askin ellipse is 3 cm in length with a central healed scar. Underlying the skin\u000aellipse is an elongated biopsy cavity, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension\u000aand surrounded by fat necrosis. The lateral aspect of the biopsy consists\u000aof fibrofatty tissue severely involved by fibrocystic disease.\u000aMicros #1-2: Deep medial margin, RSS, 2 frags, 2 cass.\u000aMicros #3-4: Deep mid portion, RSS, 2 frags, 2 cass.\u000aMicros #5-8: Deep lateral portion, RSS, 4 frags, 4 cass.\u000aMicros #9-10: Mid skin ellipse and biopsy cavity, RSS, 2 frags, 2 cass.\u000aThe second specimen, received fresh, labelled "additional deep lateral tissue",\u000aconsists of a 4 x 2 x 2 cm fragment of fibrous fatty tissue.\u000aMicros #11-15: Deep lateral tissue, ESS, 6 frags, 5 cass.\u000aThe fourth specimen, received fresh, labelled "additional left axillary\u000acontents", consists of a single fragment of fatty tissue, containing one\u000apossible lymph node.\u000aMicro #16: Additional left axillary contents, ESS, 1 frag, 1 cass.\u000aThe third specimen, received fresh, labelled "#3. left axillary contents",\u000aconsists of an 8 x 6 x 4 cm mass of fatty tissue. Throughout the axillary\u000amass, twelve lymph nodes are identified, the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain its greatest dimension.\u000aMicros #17-22: Axillary lymph nodes, RSS, 12 frags, 6 cass.\u000aReports to: SMITH, BARBARA, LYNN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LUMPECTOMY\u000a[report_end]
