VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Samuel G Katz, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low grade, multiple nodules (largest REMOVED_DATE cm as measured on\u000aglass slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see NOTE).\u000aMitoses number REMOVED_DATE hpfs\u000aThe stroma is mildly hypercellular with minimal nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aNo stromal overgrowth is seen.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aAll margins are negative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) for tumor.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNOTE: The patient has a history of a REMOVED_DATE cm fibroepithelial lesion in the\u000aupper outer quadrant of the left breast (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The current lesion is\u000aalso located in the upper outer quadrant and has a multinodular appearance. The\u000afindings are most consistent with the prior lesion being a low grade phyllodes\u000atumor that has now recurred at the excisional site.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Fibroepithelial lesion removed from left breast, January/02. Now\u000awith recurrence.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 (L) breast tumor site (short - superior, long - lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Left breast tumor site", and consists of a 44-gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aportion of fibrofatty breast tissue, partially surfaced by a tan/pink skin\u000aellipse (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two, orienting sutures (short - superior; long -\u000alateral). The breast is received previously inked by the surgeon per the\u000abreast inking protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior, revealing a\u000awhite/pink, homogeneous, rubbery, partially encapsulated mass (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which extends to the posterior, medial and inferior margins, comes to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the anterior margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of pale yellow,\u000afocally hemorrhagic, lobulated fat with scant, fibrous stroma. No other\u000alesions are identified grossly. Photographs were taken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass sequentially submitted from superior to inferior with\u000arelationship to posterior, medial, lateral and inferior\u000amargins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin and skin nearest mass, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, nearest mass, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000adfi/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Samuel G Katz M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/13/2005\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aTumor is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin.\u000aThe remaining margins are >1 cm away from the tumor.\u000aThe diagnosis remains UNCHANGED.\u000aAddendum #1 by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/16/2005\u000a[report_end]
