VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin bx cyst, tag, or debridement\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Briana Gleason, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SKIN TAG:\u000aCompound nevus.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with hemorrhage, fat necrosis, and\u000aforeign body giant cell reaction consistent with prior\u000abiopsy site.\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNo residual phyllodes tumor identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Phyllodes tumor, left breast -- 5 mm lateral margin for re-excision.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Skin tag.\u000a2. Left breast tissue, long stitch lateral, short stitch superior (blue dye\u000aused for new lateral margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 Skin tag", consists of one nodular fragment of gray/tan, wrinkled\u000askin (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The surgical margin is inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 Left breast tissue long stitch lateral, short stitch superior",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibrofatty tissue (14\u000agrams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per surgeon, there is a short suture designating\u000athe superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch designating the new\u000alateral margin (previously inked blue by the surgeon). The surface opposite to\u000athe previously blue-inked surface exhibits focally hemorrhagic, pink/tan,\u000afocally scabrous fibrous tissue (as consistent with prior biopsy procedure),\u000aand this surface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior into a total 10 slices (slice 1 = most superior, slice 10\u000a= most inferior). In slice 9, there is a well-delineated pink/white, firm,\u000abulging fibrous area (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the blue-inked\u000anew true lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the black-inked biopsy cavity surface.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of greater than 95% focally\u000ahemorrhagic, yellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue with a minimal amount of\u000adelicate band of white/tan fibrous stroma. Approximately 40% of the specimen,\u000ato include the entire fibrous areas, is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, to include entire fibrous area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000almb/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/7/2005\u000a[report_end]
