VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINA ZABICKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (low-grade) with marked epithelial proliferation and\u000ainvolvement by LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (see note).\u000aPhyllodes tumor is present <0.1 cm from medial and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aNOTE: The stroma shows focal moderate cellularity with occasional mitoses\u000a(<1/10 HPF). Marked epithelial proliferation is present, with focal morphologic\u000afeatures of lobular carcinoma in situ. Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin\u000ademonstrates absence of membrane immunoreactivity in these foci (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for p63 and SMMHC demonstrate intact myoepithelium.\u000aSlides also seen by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle local breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aIntact wire, clip and lesion in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue", consists of an irregular tan/pink to tan/yellow\u000afibrofatty breast tissue (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is previously radiographed\u000a(per radiologist, intact wire, clip, and lesion in specimen). The prosector is\u000apresent outside the wire, lobulated lesion and clip are located within the\u000aspecimen. Upon opening the container is noted that the wire is not located\u000awithin the specimen. The specimen is inked (the specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange).\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. The cut surface\u000ashows a tan/pink to tan/yellow lobulated, focally friable soft tissue (1.5 x\u000a0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm), that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, abuts the posterior\u000amargin, abuts the inferior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The clip is\u000afound.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multi frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDRD/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/18/2006\u000a[report_end]
