VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBreast tissue with focus of columnar cell alteration with atypia\u000aand hyperplasia with associated calcifications; the focus is not\u000aat or near the surgical margins.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: This case has been reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service),\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female with history of Hodgkin's disease. Right breast\u000amicrocalcifications not amenable to image guide biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short = superior, long =\u000alateral (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aRight specimen - contains Ca++. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "one equals right breast wire localized, long = lateral, short = superior",\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented\u000aby sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture)\u000amargins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). A localizing wire enters\u000athe inferolateral aspect of the specimen and exits medially. It is received\u000awith a radiograph demonstrating a localizing wire in place within the specimen,\u000awithin an area of faint calcifications. Cut surfaces demonstrates mostly soft,\u000alobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (at least 80%), with occasional intervening\u000atan/white fibrous septae. There are no discrete masses noted grossly. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with\u000aperpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aand area of interest (per localizing wire) likely in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially submitted, multiple frags, ESS (please\u000anote:\u000athe specimen will be held for further fixation prior to processing).\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
