ssue, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments, some of which are partially\u000asurfaced by a tan unremarkable skin. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal an 80% tan/yellow lobulated fatty to 20% dense white fibrous tissue, in\u000awhich definitive fibrocystic disease is not appreciated. Representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro #3-4: Left breast tissue, to include overlying skin, 2 frags in each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro #9-12: Additional fibrous breast tissue, mult frags, RSS.\u000alm/\u000aReports to: BREUING, KARL, HEINZ M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
