VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: HOPE E PETERS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL MID BREAST 3:00, 9 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a1 CM ENHANCING MASS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia within an area of fibroadenomatoid changes\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined). An immunoperoxidase study confirms the absence\u000aof e-cadherin in the area of ALH.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: S/p mantle/para-aortic radiation therapy in 1990 for Hodgkins\u000adisease. Now with new area of enhancement, right breast on MRI, not seen by\u000amammo/US.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 10 mm x 3 mm x 3 mm right medial mid breast (3:00) oval mass and\u000airregular-border mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 9 G MRI Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 9 G MRI Vacuum-assisted - White cassette with green top --> 10 samples\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "R breast, first R breast core biopsy", and consists of two white\u000acassettes with green tops, each containing multiple tan-white fibrofatty cores\u000aof soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of white cassettes with green tops, multi frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/22/2008\u000a[report_end]
