VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block #9, multiple levels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread, present in multiple\u000afoci.\u000aBreast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, apocrine metaplasia, cysts,\u000aand microcalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThe inked surgical margins of resection were examined microscopically.\u000aNOTE: Dr. A. Richardson of the BWH Breast Pathology Service has reviewed\u000athis case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast microcalcifications.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue. Short = superior, long = lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "left breast tissue", and consists of a tan/yellow, needle\u000alocalized breast biopsy specimen (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which bears a needle\u000alocalization wire and a short suture to designate superior and long suture to\u000adesignate lateral margins. An accompanying radiograph shows the specimen with\u000aa needle localization wire at the site of an irregular, radiopaque area\u000acontaining microcalcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial revealing approximately 90%\u000aunremarkable yellow adipose tissue and 10% rubbery white fibrous tissue. No\u000amasses or lesions suspicious for malignancy are identified. The area roughly\u000acorresponding to the site of microcalcifications is identified and all fibrous\u000atissue from this area is submitted. The area roughly corresponding to the area\u000aof microcalcifications is located in the superolateral quadrant. The specimen\u000ais subsequently radiographed; additional fibrous tissue with calcifications and\u000airregular densities are also submitted. Total tissue submitted is\u000aapproximately 70%.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margins, 1 or 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area corresponding to microcalcifications, 1 or 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  white fibrous tissue away from mass, 1 or 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: medial perpendicular margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
