VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRENSHAW, ANDREW, ALEXANDER, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RENSHAW,ANDREW ALEXANDER,M.D.\u000aRIGHT WIRE DIRECTED PARTIAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (INCLUDING\u000aFSA):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm. (SEE NOTE).\u000aThe carcinoma is moderately differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade II/III).\u000aNo lymphatic or vascular invasion seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is focally present at the margin (block 9; see NOTE).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present as multiple foci.\u000aFibrocystic changes are present including cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aNOTE:\u000aTumor is sent for ER/PR and flow cytometry. The positive margin is not\u000aprecisely known, but most likely represents the lateral margin.\u000aRIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aFive (5) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Right wire directed partial mastectomy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 Right breast tissue and wire (short suture = cephalad,\u000along suture = caudad).\u000a#2 Right axillary contents.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aINVASIVE poorly differentiated carcinoma, consistent with\u000alobular carcinoma (see note).\u000aLCIS.\u000aNote: Tumor is grossly near lateral and medial margins. (One frozen\u000asection, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, was technically inadequate).\u000aRadiology:\u000aMass is in specimen.\u000aT. Frenna, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MCCUSKER,MARGARET ELIZABETH,M.D.\u000aThe specimen consists of a right partial mastectomy specimen including a tan\u000askin ellipse (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm) and yellow/tan,\u000afibrofatty tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented and a needle\u000alocalization wire is in place. The chest wall margin is inked in blue and the\u000aremaining margin is inked in black. A short suture marks the cephalad\u000a(superior) margin and a long suture marks the caudad (inferior) margin. There\u000ais a tan, firm mass (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior (skin) margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and 4 cm\u000afrom the inferior margin. Representative sections of the tumor are submitted\u000aas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and representative section of the medial margin is submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: Chest wall margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: Superior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Tumor with lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: Tumor with medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: Inferior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: Deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Anterior margin, skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Representative sections of tumor, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Additional fibrous soft tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: FSAR, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "right axillary contents" consists of one fragment of yellow,\u000afibroadipose tissue (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Five lymph nodes (1.3 cm in greatest\u000adiameter) are identified in the axillary fat.\u000aMicro 11: One lymph node, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: One lymph node, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: One lymph node, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: One lymph node, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: One lymph node, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
