VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aWIRE LOCALIZED RIGHT BREAST EXCISION FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU and atypical lobular hyperplasia involving\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell change and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aDiffuse microcalcifications associated with atypical lobular hyperplasia,\u000abenign epithelium and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aThe case was reviewed by the Breast Service, Drs. Andrea Richardson and\u000aSusan Lester, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of calcifications in right breast too faint for core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right mammography, directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000a"#1. Right needle localized breast tissue", and consists of a wire localized\u000abreast lumpectomy specimen (4.5 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior), with two orienting\u000asutures. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is received with a\u000aradiograph which demonstrates a wire and two faint microcalcifications.\u000aSectioning reveals the specimen consists of 95% yellow lobulated adipose tissue\u000awith strands of fibrous tissue mostly located in the center of the specimen.\u000aPalpation of the central fibrous tissue reveals one slice to have a gritty\u000atexture. The slices are radiographed to identify the location of the\u000amicrocalcifications, and this coincides with the slice with gritty texture.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Lateral margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Area most suspicious for microcalcifications, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: Tissue with one possible calcification, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: 1, frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: Tissue with suspicious possible microcalcification, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, 7 frags, ESS.\u000ajeb\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
