VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS"\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aB) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT ADDITIONAL BREAST TISSUE"\u000aINTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA (0.7 cm), with focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: No clip was present in either specimen. The hypoechoic area was confirmed\u000aby ultrasound to be present in specimen 2. Immunohistochemical studies for\u000aE-cadherin show membrane immunoreactivity in areas of sclerosis and hyperplasia\u000ain specimens A and B, confirming ductal phenotype.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass. Abnormal mammography.\u000aOperation: Excision left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast mass\u000a2. Additional breast tissue (left)\u000aSpecimen #1 - No clip or mass in specimen.\u000aSpecimen #2 - Clip not in specimen. Hypoechoic area in specimen (spec US).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aTwo specimens were received fresh, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, "left breast mass", consists of one piece of breast tissue (5.9 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm) with a localization wire in place. The specimen is unoriented. The\u000aspecimen radiograph shows a localization wire in place. A clip is not\u000aidentified. Sections through the specimen show an area of hemorrhage (up to\u000a0.7 cm) in the area of the localization wire. One end of the specimen contains\u000awhite fibrous tissue. The specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections to breast tissue, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left additional breast tissue", consists of one piece of breast tissue\u000a(3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen contains three short tan sutures at\u000aopposing ends of the specimen, which all have the same length and are not\u000afurther designated. Sections through the specimen show yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, intermixed with white fibrous areas. There is also a small\u000ahemorrhagic cyst (0.2 cm). The specimen also contains areas of hemorrhage (up\u000ato REMOVED_DATE cm). The accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates two small\u000aill-defined radiodense lesions. The entire specimen is inked in black and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections through the specimen, 2 frags each (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSs:lc\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
