VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with micropapillary pattern (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000aassociated with biopsy site and microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirmed with loss of E-cadherin\u000astaining).\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium, sclerosing\u000aadenosis, extensive columnar change, and changes consistent with core\u000abiopsy site.\u000aMultiple levels examined.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe case was reviewed with Dr. J. Brock, Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47 year old premenopausal woman s/p REMOVED_DATE  right breast core\u000abiopsies, revealing epithelial hyperplasia with micropapillary pattern. EXL\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wl biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip short\u000achest wall margin (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, wire and calcifications are in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue short stitch superior long lateral whip stitch\u000achest wall margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose\u000atissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture), lateral (long\u000asuture) and chest wall (whipstitch) margins. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by surgeon). Localizing wire enters the anterior aspect of the specimen\u000aand traverses posteriorly. Specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating localizing wire in place with in a focus of calcifications marked\u000aby a metallic surgical clip at one edge of the specimen. Sectioning in the\u000aarea of interest demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm cavity containing the metallic surgical\u000aclip, abutting the superior edge of the specimen. The tissue in this area is\u000awithout palpable or visible definitive abnormalities grossly. The entire\u000aspecimen is comprised of vaguely nodular cystic-appearing fibrous tissue (at\u000aleast 90%), but is without a discrete identifiable mass lesion. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially following further fixation. Perpendicular\u000amedial margins in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and area of\u000ainterest (per metallic clip, localizing wire) in micro cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 26, 2009 at 07:14:25PM\u000a[report_end]
