 circumscribed area with focal hemorrhage and a focal cyst-like\u000aspace (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying\u000askin. This area is associated with chalky yellow discoloration grossly\u000aconsistent with fat necrosis. The specimen is otherwise approximately 60%\u000atan/white fibrous tissue and 40% yellow fatty tissue. Approximately 95% of the\u000aspecimen including all margins and the stellate area are submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue from superior to inferior, multi frags, RSS.\u000arlr\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
