ly\u000ahemorrhagic, ill-defined fibrous lesion (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000atraversed by the needle localization wire, and grossly extends to all surgical\u000amargins. The accompanying radiograph confirms the presence of a wire-hook\u000awithin the specimen (confirmed by Dr. Iglehart via phone). No clip is present\u000awithin the specimen. NOTE: a fragment of tan irregular, synthetic elastic\u000amaterial (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present loosely embedded within the breast\u000atissue. The remaining tissue consists of scant yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue sequentially from medial to lateral, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/29/2005\u000a[report_end]
