VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000a1. LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER POSTERIOR, 11 G STEREOTACTIC VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE\u000aNEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (KNOT-SHAPED CLIP):\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present with calcifications (see note).\u000aNOTE: Atypical ductal hyperplasia is evaluated best after excision.\u000a2. LEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE NEEDLE\u000aBIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (U-SHAPED CLIP):\u000aPAPILLOMA with associated calcifications.\u000aNOTE: Multiple additional levels examined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Area #1 Left\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: < 1 cm, Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000a2. Left: REMOVED_DATE cm and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper inner.\u000a2. Left: lower inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted (12 cores).\u000a2. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted (7 cores).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left upper inner posterior (knot-shaped clip) - Pink cassette.\u000aB/2. Left lower inner (U-shaped-clip) - Green cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast site #1 upper medial", consists of multiple\u000airregular tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm in aggregate). A portion of the breast tissue cores are received in a\u000apink cassette marked "A CA+2" and remainder of the breast tissue cores are\u000areceived in a pink cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A CA+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast site #2 lower medial", consists of multiple\u000airregular tan/yellow to tan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). A portion of the breast tissue cores are\u000areceived in a green cassette marked "A CA+2" and remainder of the breast tissue\u000acores are received in a green cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted\u000ain toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A CA+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
