000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/\u000ablack; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/\u000aorange. The parenchyma of the specimen consists of grossly unremarkable\u000aadipose tissue. No gross lesions are identified. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen from lateral to medial:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral-most slice,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 2,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 3,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 4,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 5,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 6,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 7,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Slice 8.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Right breast nodule", consists of one (1) unoriented\u000abreast biopsy specimen (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is unoriented and\u000aentirely inked blue. No gross lesions are identified. The specimen is\u000abisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast nodule, 2 frags, ESS.\u000amah/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
