VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aExtensive Intraductal Component - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, lateral, anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior, inferior.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 5:13 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral, superior, inferior, posterior\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Anterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Medial (near the anteromedial junction\u000aBlocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID?seen primarily on\u000alevels for immunohistochemical studies.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa NX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aA p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID immunostain showed absence of the myoepithelial layer in areas of\u000aDCIS.\u000aAn E-Cadherin stain is positive in the area of invasive carcinoma and negative\u000ain the areas of ALH and LCIS. Levels examined.\u000aSelect slides were also reviewed by Dr. Jane Brock, breast pathology service,\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 83 year old female with a history of right breast lobular carcinoma in\u000asitu, new right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aOperation: #1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right excisional biopsy - long, lateral, short superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Targeted 5 mm mass and intact wire are seen within the specimen. Dr.\u000aGumbos\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Right excisional breast, long lateral, short superior",\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram breast excision specimen with orienting sutures\u000adesignating superior and lateral positions. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior\u000aand is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a localization\u000awire entering the specimen and associated with an ill-defined increased density\u000aarea. The wire enters the specimen inferolaterally and exits superomedially\u000aand is associated with an area of soft fibrous breast parenchyma (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm), which is less than REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior,\u000a0.1 cm to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000ainferior margins. The remaining breast tissue comprises 90% adipose tissue and\u000a10% fibrous tissue. No additional gross lesions are identified. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and closest medial, lateral and superior margins, 1 frig, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and deep margin, 2 frogs, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and anterior margin, 1 frig each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and superior margin, 2 frogs, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frogs, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 1 frig, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, perpendicular margins, multi frogs,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLDO/age\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(se)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Thursday February 26, 2009 at 03:56:28PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (2/27/09)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday February 27, 2009 at 04:48:43PM\u000a[report_end]
