VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST ANTERIOR MARGIN":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with granulation tissue, chronic\u000ainflammation, foreign body giant cell reaction to polarizable material\u000aand fat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST MEDIAL MARGIN":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with granulation tissue, chronic inflammation,\u000aforeign body giant cell reaction, and fat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 84 year old female with right breast cancer, s/p wire localized\u000aexcisional biopsy, DCIS close to margins.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast anterior margin.\u000aB/2. Right breast medial margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimens are received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast anterior margin - stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of a fragment of skin with subcutaneous tissue (3.3 cm in length x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in width extending REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). There is a stitch on one long edge of\u000athe skin fragment designating new margin per surgeon. This aspect is inked\u000ablue with the other aspect inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, en face, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast medial margin - stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000astitch on the specimen designating new margin per surgeon, which is inked blue\u000aand opposite aspect inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aGL/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 02:10:41PM\u000a[report_end]
