VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 62 year old female with a left breast mass seen on imaging,\u000awire-localized excision revealed a papillary carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE cm close to a\u000amargin.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast papillary carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast re-excision lumpectomy, short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast re-excision, lumpectomy; short suture - superior, long\u000asuture - lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue with sutures designating superior (short suture) and\u000alateral (long suture). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). Please\u000anote: The posteromedial aspect of the specimen is diffusely ragged. The\u000aanterior surface of the specimen exhibits a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse with\u000aa linear well-healed scar along its length. Sectioning demonstrates an\u000aill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of fibrosis and fat necrosis, abutting the\u000asuperior, inferior, medial, and lateral margins, and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aclosest posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest anterior margin. There is\u000ano obvious residual tumor identified grossly. The remaining specimen is\u000acomprised of unremarkable-appearing fibrous tissue (40% of the specimen),\u000aadmixed with lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted, sequentially from anterior to posterior, with perpendicular anterior\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections from anterior to posterior, multiple frags,\u000aESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a5/22/2007\u000a[report_end]
