VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - OTHER\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FRANKLIN MEDICAL CENTER, GREENFIELD, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION BIOPSY (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia involving a single duct in the slide labeled\u000a"A" (levels examined; see note).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes including cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aNote: The area of atypia consists of a single space filled with cells\u000awhich appear heterogeneous in appearance. Although there is some\u000asuggestion of cribriform spaces, overall the spaces present are irregular\u000ain shape. A few macrophages are present in the center of the space and\u000apossibly a few degenerating cells, but these may represent degenerating\u000amacrophages and not epithelial necrosis. The area has been completely\u000asectioned in four levels. Diagnostic features of carcinoma in situ are\u000anot met cytologically, architecturally, or in the extent of the lesion.\u000aTherefore, this lesion is best designated atypical hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old woman with atypical finding on ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Franklin Medical Center, Greenfield, MA are eleven H&E glass\u000aslides labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and sublabeled "A" (four slides), "B" (four slides),\u000a"C", "D", and "E" which are described in an accompanying surgical pathology\u000areport as sections from a left breast wire localized biopsy from a procedure on\u000a11/14/95. The grossly apparent rubbery nodule was submitted in "A" though "C".\u000aAlso received is a consultation report on this case from Yale University\u000a(numbered REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and dated REMOVED_DATE ) from Dr. Darryl Carter (his diagnosis:\u000a"atypical ductal hyperplasia in a single duct").\u000aReports to:\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - OTHER\u000a[report_end]
