VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FRANKLIN MEDICAL CENTER, GREENFIELD, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aATYPIA and associated calcifications.\u000aCysts and calcifications.\u000aDuctal hyperplasia, moderate.\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade) with\u000anecrosis and calcifications, present as a minor component within the\u000ainvasive tumor.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia and associated calcifications.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is extensively present at inked margins.\u000aBy report, receptor studies are pending.\u000aLEFT BREAST CORE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypia, best evaluated on surgical excision.\u000aApocrine metaplasia and cysts.\u000aRadial scar.\u000aCalcifications present in atypical columnar epithelium and in benign\u000aducts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHAH,RAJSHRI N.,M.D.\u000aReceived from Franklin Medical Center, 164 High Street, Greenfield, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID,\u000aare thirty-six (36) glass slides.\u000aTwelve (12) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 1" through "1 3",\u000a"1 3 (2)" through "1 3 (6)", "1 4", "1 5", "1 5 (2)" and "1 6", corresponding\u000ato right breast needle localization biopsy (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on\u000a7/37/97, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aNine (9) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 1" through "1 9",\u000acorresponding to right breast needle localization biopsy (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aFifteen (15) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 1" "LEV #3 REMOVED_DATE ",\u000a"1 2", "LEV #2 REMOVED_DATE ", "LEV #2 REMOVED_DATE ", "LEV #3 REMOVED_DATE ", "2 1", "LEV #2 REMOVED_DATE ", "LEV #3 2\u000a1", "2 2", "LEV #2 REMOVED_DATE ", "LEV #3 REMOVED_DATE ", "2 3", "LEV #2 REMOVED_DATE " and "LEV #3 REMOVED_DATE ",\u000acorresponding to 1) left breast core needle biopsies with calcifications 2)\u000aleft breast core needle biopsies without calcifications performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: SHULMAN, LAWRENCE, NATHAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
