VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia (atypical columnar\u000aalteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions) and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aNOTE: Because of preoperative clinical or radiologic concern regarding the\u000apossibility of tumor, the margins of this specimen were inked, sampled, and\u000aexamined microscopically.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine metaplasia and a fibroadenoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 52 y/o premenopausal female, not on hormones, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate a L breast 12:00 axis cluster of calcifications.\u000a5/14/02 core biopsy revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast mass. Stitch markings: short = superior, long\u000a= lateral, whipstitch = deep margin.\u000a2. Superior medial shave margin (whipstitch in margin), L breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and ca++s in specimen #1. C. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number\u000ain two parts.\u000aPart one is labeled "left breast mass". The specimen consists of a single\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue that is oriented by the surgeon with short\u000astitch superior, long stitch lateral and whip stitch deep. The specimen is\u000aalso inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen measures 4 cm from\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior\u000ato posterior. There is a wire in the specimen and an accompanying radiograph\u000ashowing a clip and calcifications in relation to the wire. The specimen is\u000aapproximately 60% fibrous tissue and 40% fat. The area of the clip corresponds\u000ato an area of fibrous tissue. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE contain the tissue adjacent to the clip.\u000aPart two is labeled "superior medial shave margin". The specimen consists of a\u000asingle fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. One surface\u000acontains a whip stitch which indicates the margin as per the surgeon. This\u000aarea is inked blue. The opposite side is inked black. The specimen is\u000aapproximately 40% fibrous tissue and 60% fat. No definite masses are seen.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000amir\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
