VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT NIPPLE AND AREOLA":\u000aSkin with squamous metaplasia/cyst formation.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT NIPPLE AND AREOLA":\u000aSkin with squamous metaplasia/cyst formation.\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aFibrocystic change with apocrine metaplasia and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSquamous metaplasia/cyst formation.\u000aFocal foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000a#4. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000a#5. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST IMPLANT":\u000aBreast prosthesis (gross only).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43-year-old premenopausal female status post bilateral prophylactic\u000amastectomies in REMOVED_MONTH 99 for right LCIS resultant right breast\u000asubcutaneous skin flap necrosis requiring debridement for nipple\u000a(areola excision bilaterally. Had upper outer quadrant residual\u000aleft breast tissue for excision.\u000aOperation: Excision of left breast tissue and bilateral nipple areolar\u000aexcision. Implant exchange of left breast.\u000aOperative findings:\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left nipple and areola.\u000a2. Right nipple and areola.\u000a3. Right breast tissue.\u000a4. Left breast tissue.\u000a5. Left breast implant.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in five parts, all labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "Right nipple and areolar" and consists of a tan/pink\u000afragment of skin, consistent with a nipple and areolar (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe specimen has a centrally located nipple (1.0 cm that is grossly\u000aunremarkable). The base of the skin is inked in black and a representative\u000asection is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: left nipple and areolar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Right nipple and areolar", consists of a single fragment\u000aof pink/tan skin, consists of a nipple and areolar. The skin measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The base of the skin is\u000ainked in black and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 2: right nipple and areolar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Right breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of\u000awhite/yellow fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate.\u000aThe specimen is fragmented and no margin is evident. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "Left breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of\u000apink/yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate.\u000aThe specimen is fragmented and the no margin is evident. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart five, labeled "Left breast implant", consists of a clear breast implant\u000a(12.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with no tears or leaks. The external surface is smooth\u000aand there is no tissue attached. Gross exam only.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST IMPLANT\u000a[report_end]
