VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLODA, MASSIMO, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIDE LOCALIZED, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aALH with pagetoid spread.\u000aColumnar hyperplasia with atypia mucin production, calcification and\u000amucocele-like lesion.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester and Dr. S. Schnitt who agree with\u000athe above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle-directed excisional breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - right breast excisional biopsy, suture short/superior,\u000along/lateral (to fs/to mammo).\u000aRadiograph report: Calcifications and hook-wire in specimen. PIR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - rt breast excisional biopsy", and consists of a breast excisional\u000abiopsy specimen (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an embedded localization wire. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a localization wire passing\u000athrough an area of dense tissue adjacent to focal cluster of calcifications.\u000aTwo orienting sutures are present, designated by the surgeon as long/lateral\u000aand short/superior. The specimen is inked according to the pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000acomposed primarily of tan/white rubbery tissue (approximately 80%) and yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue (approximately 20%). No discrete lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is serially submitted in its entirety from superior\u000ato inferior for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1-9: Right breast excisional biopsy (area of calcification likely in\u000amicros REMOVED_DATE ), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000ajfs/\u000aReports to: WHANG, EDWARD, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
