e tissue\u000a(at least 80% of the specimen), admixed with unremarkable-appearing soft,\u000alobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (less than 20%). There are no obvious\u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted, sequentially from medial to lateral, with perpendicular medial\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/17/2007\u000a[report_end]
