VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES,D.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions is\u000apresent associated with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, focus of intraductal papillomatosis, prior\u000abiopsy site, and calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThe margins of the specimen were inked, submitted and examined\u000ahistologically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old female with history of ADH associated with left breast\u000acalcifications. See previous core biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue at REMOVED_DATE o'clock (short stitch/superior;\u000along stitch/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcifications in specimen. L. Frost, MD/LP\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast lump", and consists of a left breast wire\u000alocalized biopsy specimen (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short stitch to denote\u000athe superior, and long stitch to denote lateral margins. The specimen also\u000acontains a wire localization needle. An accompanying radiograph shows the\u000aspecimen with a clip, wire localization needle, and two discrete groups of\u000amicrocalcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral, revealing predominantly yellow adipose tissue\u000a(90%); there are focal areas of hemorrhage. The specimen is radiographed, and\u000athe slice containing the clip is identified and submitted in cassettes #8 and\u000a9. No discrete lesions or masses are identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margin, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast wire localized biopsy, from lateral to medial, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, 2 or 3 frags each, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
