VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.; Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with calcifications and a prior biopsy\u000asite.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERLASIA with pagetoid spread.\u000aCalcifications also present in columnar cell change.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: Case also reviewed by Dr. Jane Brock who concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 62 year old female with right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia, S/P\u000acore biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire localized excisional biopsy - short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short\u000asuture superior/long suture lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral\u000ax REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast biopsy\u000awith a localization wire in place and a short suture marking the superior\u000amargin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. Per radiograph obtained\u000afrom Centricity as well as radiology report, the radiograph demonstrates a\u000acluster of calcification near the anterior superior portion of the specimen,\u000aadjacent to the localization wire, which not only marks this cluster of\u000acalcification but also a biopsy clip previously done for a 3 mm cluster of fine\u000apleomorphic calcification located in the subareolar region of the right breast.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A biopsy cavity with clip is identified in the area of\u000aradiologic calcification. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to\u000aposterior to reveal the biopsy cavity mentioned before. The biopsy cavity is\u000alocated at the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through the anterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through the anterior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from anterior to posterior, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from anterior to posterior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sectioning from anterior to posterior, bisected with\u000asuperior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and inferior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sectioning anterior to posterior slice is bisected with\u000asuperior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and inferior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior to posterior, bisected with superior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000ainferior in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through posterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through posterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aNote: Clip and biopsy cavity located in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aERV/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 21, 2010 at 01:58:44PM\u000a[report_end]
