VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Adam Rosendorff, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell changes.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: NO invasive carcinoma or DCIS are seen after complete microscopic\u000aexamination of the specimen, including margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old female with right breast microcalcifications. Core biopsy\u000arevealed columnar cell change with atypia, residual calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right breast, wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) rt breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture = superior, long\u000asuture = lateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen image includes biopsy clip, calcification and hookwire.\u000aA MacLean/S Raza.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Rt breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture equals\u000asuperior, long suture equals lateral", and consists of a portion of yellow\u000alobulated fibroadipose tissue (4.1 (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to\u000ainferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm) with two orienting sutures "short\u000asuture equals superior; long suture equals lateral" and a needle localization\u000awire in place (entering anteriorly and exiting posteroinferiorly). The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph which exhibits a\u000ahook wire and clip within an area of calcification which grossly comes to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior and medial margins (approximately). The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from medial to lateral, exhibiting a firm tan/white\u000afairly well circumscribed nodule (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), adjacent to the clip,\u000aextending to the anterior margin, coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. The remaining breast\u000atissue consists of approximately 70% tan/white, dense, focally lumpy fibrous\u000astroma and 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No other gross lesion is\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissues sequentially from lateral to medial (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amulti frags, ESS [Please note nodule in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000adl/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/1/2007\u000a[report_end]
