VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative, with florid epithelial hyperplasia and\u000afocal Atypical Ductal Hyperplasia (block 7); there is no atypia at the\u000amargin.\u000aFibroadenoma(s) (0.5 cm).\u000aDuct ectasia and inspissation.\u000aMicrocalcifications are present in association with ducts.\u000a(Levels examined).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Atypical ductal cells on FNA. Biopsy requested by pathology\u000adepartment.\u000aOperation: Left breast mass resection.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE" (GROSS):\u000aFat necrosis (consistent with prior FNA site).\u000aGrossly nodular breast tissue with comedone-like material\u000afocally.\u000aRule out in situ neoplasia on permanents.\u000aNo gross evidence of invasive tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HEDVAT,CYRUS V.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "left breast\u000atissue", is a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.3 cm). On cut section there are multiple yellow nodular areas (up to REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension), and the remainder of the tissue consists of\u000aapproximately 30% dense white fibrous tissue, and the remainder of unremarkable\u000ayellow adipose tissue. The specimen is oriented with two sutures, a single\u000asuture designating the ventral portion and a double suture indicating the\u000acephalad portion of the specimen. The left side of specimen is inked in blue\u000aand the right side in black. There are no areas grossly suspicious for\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro 1: dorsal margin en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: ventral margin en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: lateral margin en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: medial margin en face, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: caudal margin en face,, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: cephalad margin en face, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, 10 frags, 6 cass, ESS.\u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
