VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLONGTINE, JANINA, A., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LONGTINE,JANINA A.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, INFERIOR:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (see note).\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE: There is severely atypical ductal hyperplasia involving a portion\u000aof the REMOVED_DATE cm fibroadenoma and immediately adjacent breast tissue. The\u000aproliferation in some of the ducts is sufficient for a diagnosis of\u000aINTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA. NO INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS SEEN. A re-excision is\u000arecommended.\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, SUPERIOR:\u000aFibroadenoma, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE (INFERIOR) (FSA):\u000aSuspicious (not confirmatory) for malignancy.\u000aComplete exam to follow.\u000aFS remnant taken for ER/PR studies.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen #1. M. Sonnenfeld, MD\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE (SUPERIOR):\u000aFibroadenoma (FSB).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen #2. M. Sonnenfeld, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FREEMAN,JONATHAN KEEN,M.D.\u000aReceived fresh, in two parts each labeled with the patient's name.\u000aPart one, labeled "right breast tissue inferior lesion", consists of fibrofatty\u000atissue (4 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a well circumscribed dense mass (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). An area within the circumscribed mass is suspicious for tumor and a\u000aportion of this area is frozen as A. The remainder of this suspicious area is\u000asubmitted as micro #1.\u000aMICRO #1: Non frozen portion of suspicious area, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #2-7: Remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "right breast tissue", consists of fibrofatty tissue (6 x 4 x\u000a2 cm). Within the specimen is a well circumscribed dense pearly white mass REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension grossly consistent with a fibroadenoma. The remainder\u000aof the breast tissue is largely fatty with no areas grossly suspicious for\u000ainvasive tumor. A portion of the dense lesion is frozen as FSB. Fatty areas\u000aare trimmed from the specimen and the remainder is entirely submitted.\u000aMICRO #8: FSR B, 1 frag, ESS, 1 cass.\u000aMICRO #9-15: 6 frags, RSS, 6 cas.\u000aMICRO #16: FSRA, retrieved from reproductive endocrinology lab, ESS, 1 frag, 1\u000acass.\u000aNote: The frozen section remnant A was submitted to the reproductive\u000aendocrinology lab for potential ERICA studies. This block was retrieved and\u000aprocessed for histologic examination. No ERICA was perfomed.\u000aReports to: SMITH, BARBARA, LYNN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
