VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Reduction mamoplasty\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELOF ERIKSSON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Andrew G. Evans, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE (370g):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, see NOTE.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.4 cm).\u000aSkin, no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: Immunostain for E-cadherin shows loss of E-cadherin\u000aexpression in the lesional ducts, supporting the above diagnosis. The\u000aspecimen was extensively sampled and multiple levels were examined.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, TISSUE (380g):\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change and\u000afocal sclerosing adenosis.\u000aSkin, no significant pathologic change.\u000aC. LIPOSUCTION FROM RIGHT AND LEFT BREASTS (100+ ml):\u000aFibroadipose tissue, no significant pathologic change.\u000a******\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None provided.\u000aOperation: Bilateral reduction mammoplasty.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Macromastia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue 370 gms.\u000aB/2) Left breast tissue 380 gms.\u000aC/3) Liposuction from R and L breast = 100+ ml's.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "right breast tissue", consists of REMOVED_DATE grams of tan-yellow\u000alobulated fibroadipose breast tissue (16.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with overlying\u000atan-white wrinkled skin (14.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cut surface is tan-yellow and\u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 20% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted, including >80% of fibrous\u000abreast tissue..\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous breast tissue, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of REMOVED_DATE grams of tan-yellow\u000alobulated fibroadipose breast tissue (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) with\u000aoverlying tan-white wrinkled skin (15.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cut surface is\u000atan-yellow and homogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue\u000aconstituting approximately 30% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions\u000aare grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "lateral section from right and left breasts", consists of\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE mL of tan-yellow partially liquified fibroadipose tissue\u000a(7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, RSS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009 at 09:17:06AM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (December 22, 2009)\u000aAt the request of Dr. E Eriksson, this case was re-reviewed in consultation\u000awith Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology Service). Upon re-review, the lesion in\u000aspecimen A is best classified as ?Atypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid\u000aspread?. This interpretation was communicated to Dr. Eriksson via phone by Dr.\u000aQian on REMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 2:30 PM.\u000aAddendum #1 by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 02:47:52PM\u000a[report_end]
