VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUTTER, GEORGE, LUTHER, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUTTER,GEORGE LUTHER,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, extensive, micropapillary type. See comment.\u000aFibrocystic changes, proliferative.\u000aCOMMENT: Criteria for a diagnosis of carcinoma in situ are not met in any of\u000athe slides examined, although the degree of atypia is extreme.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ENDOCERVICAL CURETTINGS":\u000aNegative endocervix with squamous metaplasia.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ENDOMETRIAL CURETTINGS":\u000aProliferative endometrium.\u000aNegative endocervix.\u000aLower uterine segment.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by MUTTER,GEORGE LUTHER,M.D.\u000aThe right breast biopsy was reveiwed at the request of Dr. Christine Denison,\u000aand the following addendum prepared in consultation with Dr. Susan Lester.\u000aAs stated in the original report, there is an extensive micropapillary lesion\u000awith severe atypia. Focal areas of epithelial cell necrosis and calcification\u000aare present within the lesion and likely correspond to the fine calcifications\u000apresent mammographically. This is an unsual lesion and difficult to classify.\u000aSome observors favor a diagnosis of ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH SEVERE\u000aATYPIA (i.e. bordening on carcinoma in situ) for the entire lesion whereas\u000aothers would classify some areas as DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aClinical correlation is advised.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Calcification right breast, bleeding polymenorrhea.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy needle directed, D+C.\u000aOperative findings: Calification right breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Calficiation right breast, polymenorrhea.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast mass\u000a#2. Endocervical curettings\u000a#3. Endometrial curettings\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS:"\u000aNo gross evidence of infiltrating malignancy.\u000aAwait permanents.\u000aRADIOLOGY: The Ca# are in the specimen. E. Waitzlein, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by POTEAT,HARRY TOWSLEY,M.D.,D.SC.\u000aThe specimen, "right breast mass", 6 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. piece of fibrofatty\u000atissue with no suspicious areas present on cut surface.\u000aSection code:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE fibrofatty tissue, multiple fragments, ESS. (75%)\u000aThe specimen, "endocervical curettings", consists of bloody red, slightly\u000amucinous tissue approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate.\u000aMicro 12, endocervical curettings, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aThe specimen, "endometrial curettings", consists of copious red fibrous,\u000ahemorrhagic tissue fragments approximately 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate.\u000aMicro 13, endometrial curettings, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aReports to: SAFON, LEONARD, ELIOTT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: CURETTINGS (C & M)\u000a[report_end]
