VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LIKE,A.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, (see note).\u000aPagetoid spread into small ducts is present.\u000aSclerosing adenosis and fibrocystic change, non-proliferative.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with lobular carcinoma in situ\u000aand benign fibrocystic change.\u000aOne intra-mammary lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: The neoplastic process is multifocal. The tumor cells are\u000asomewhat unusual in that they are larger than usual in lobular\u000acarcinoma in situ and show focal apocrine\u000achange. The dishesiveness of the cells and the presence of\u000aintracytoplasmic mucin vacuoles, however, supports the diagnosis\u000aof LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. The case was reviewed by Dr. J. Connelly\u000aat the Beth Israel Hospital who agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy - needle directed.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QUADE,BRADLEY JOSEPH,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived in a container of formalin, labeled with the patient's name and "right\u000abreast tissue", is a single fragment of fibrofatty tissue (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a localization needle in place. No areas of woody or sclerotic tissue are\u000agrossly identified. There are, however, areas of rubbery nodularity present.\u000aA specimen x-ray bearing the patient's name accompanies the specimen; no report\u000ais included.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  ESS, mult. frag., 11 cass.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
