 breast stroma, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: breast stroma to include cyst, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast tissue", and consists of a 509 gram, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a9.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of hemorrhagic fibrofatty breast tissue and multiple\u000afragments of unremarkable tan skin (ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). Serial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals approximately 50%\u000ayellow-tan lobulated fat and 50% tan-white, diffusely cystic fibrous stroma to\u000ainclude blue-gray fluid filled cyst (measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension). No masses or suspicious lesions are identified.\u000aMicro 3: skin and breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: ERIKSSON, ELOF M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
