VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Andrew M. Quinn, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, POSTERIOR UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL\u000aBIOPSY FOR A MASS AND A CLIP (14.85g):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined).\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia is present.\u000aA biopsy site is present and extends to the lateral margin.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE:\u000aDr. A. Ly, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed the case and agrees with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57-year-old nulliparous postmenopausal woman with a family history of\u000abreast cancer(mgm 60's; M cousin 51). REMOVED_DATE  mammogram and additional news\u000ademonstrate a right UOQ posterior asymmetry, oval mass by ultrasound. REMOVED_DATE \u000aultrasound guided core biopsy revealed PASH ; excision is recommended as it was\u000anot thought to be concordant with imaging findings (history of reduction 2006\u000awith bilateral ADH).\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral; Whip stitch on deep\u000amargin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short/superior,\u000along/lateral, whip stitch on deep margin", and consists of a right breast\u000alumpectomy (14.85-g) oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch superiorly,\u000along stitch laterally and a whipstitch on the deep margin. The specimen is\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol (superior equals red, inferior\u000aequals green, anterior equals blue, posterior equals black, medial equals\u000aorange, yellow equals lateral), and measures REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. A needle-localization\u000awire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen but does not exit. A radiograph\u000aon centricity shows a wire which localizes both a clip and a mass. The\u000aspecimen is fixed overnight and serially sectioned to reveal 90% fatty tissue\u000aand 10% fibrous tissue. A well-circumscribed, tan mass (0.6 cm in greatest\u000adimension) is present in the lateral aspect of the specimen, just distal to the\u000alocalization wire tip. The specimen has been entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Complete coronal section, including mass and tip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Complete coronal section, anterior to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular, multi\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Complete coronal section, posterior to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular, multi\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aAQU/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21, 2009 