VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BG-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm on glass slide.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade), with\u000anecrosis and calcifications, is present associated with the invasive carcinoma\u000ain two of two blocks.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is <0.1 cm from the unoriented black inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is REMOVED_DATE cm from the unoriented black inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in foci of atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThis carcinoma could be classified as AJCC (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb NX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast mass excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast biopsy\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast biopsy", and consists of an unoriented piece of tan/pink\u000afibroadipose soft tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is inked black on the outer\u000asurface and serially sectioned to reveal yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue with a\u000asmall focus of hemorrhage but no other lesion. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of the specimen, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aCA:lc\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/10/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
