VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUTTER, GEORGE, LUTHER, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUTTER,GEORGE LUTHER,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT NEEDLE DIRECTED BREAST BIOPSY, UPPER WIRE":\u000aMicroscopic focus of DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (block 1), present\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm. of the inked margin.\u000aMultiple foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic change with florid hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in the specimen (Micro #1 and 2), in\u000aassociation with benign epithelium.\u000aIntraductal papilloma, sclerosed (Micro #2).\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT NEEDLE DIRECTED BREAST BIOPSY, LOWER WIRE ":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, microscopic focus within REMOVED_DATE mm of surgical\u000amargin.\u000aFibrocystic change with florid hyperplasia, focally atypical.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium.\u000a(Levels examined).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications increased in UOQ left breast (2 spots),\u000amammography done at BWH, biopsy sampling recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast resection (2 areas) upper outer quadrant.\u000aOperative findings: Fibrocystic disease, firm breast tissue, no obvious\u000amalignancy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Pre-op: microcalcification left breast\u000aPost-op: probable fibrocystic disease\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left needle directed breast biopsy, upper wire\u000a#2. Left needle directed breast biopsy, lower wire\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1 LEFT BREAST BIOPSY-UPPER WIRE:"\u000aNo areas suspicious for invasive cancer.\u000aGross only.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY-LOWER WIRE:"\u000aNo areas suspicious for invasive cancer.\u000aGross only.\u000aRadiology: calcificatins seen in both #1 and #2 specimen. xxx\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KENDLER,ADY,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aThe first specimen labeled "1 left directed breast biopsy-upper wire", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/yellow, fibrous fatty tissue with a wire in place. There\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE cm area of firmness consistent with calcifications seen on mammogram.\u000aSection code:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left needle directed breast biopsy-upper wire, ESS, multiple\u000afragments, 3 cassettes.\u000aThe second specimen labeled "2 left needle directed breast biopsy-lower wire",\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/yellow fibrous fatty tissue with a wire in place.\u000aA REMOVED_DATE cm area of punctate firmness consists of a calcifications as seen on the\u000amammogram.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left needle directed breast biopsy-lower wire, ESS, multiple\u000afragments, 4 cassettes.\u000aNote: No micro #6 submitted.\u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
