uperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a2.0 cm from the medial margin. The cavity contains a surgical clip, as\u000adisplayed on the accompanying radiograph. The remaining cut surface displays\u000a98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 2% white fibrous tissue, with no\u000aadditional masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, with the cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, with the cavity containing the\u000asurgical clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, containing the cavity, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, containing the cavity, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, containing the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, containing the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, displaying the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
