VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JILL E. SAUNDERS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 12:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aILL-DEFINED/PALPABLE REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, (high nuclear grade) is present and\u000ainvolves fibroadenomatous change.\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 1:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR AN ILL-DEFINED/PALPABLE REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, (high nuclear grade) is present.\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Site #1: 71 y. o. with prior R lumpectomy for breast cancer. Now\u000apresents with new palpable finding, R breast 12:30 - 1:00 and ultrasound\u000afindings of two adjacent hypoechoic masses. This represents biopsy of the more\u000alateral 8-mm lesion at 12:30 = Site #1.\u000aSite 2: 71 y. o. with prior R lumpectomy and new R palpable mass. U/S shows\u000atwo adjacent hypoechoic ill-defined masses at palpable site. This represents\u000abiopsy of the more medial 11-mm lesion at 1:00 = Site 2.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 8 mm, palpable and ill-defined mass.\u000a2. Right: 11 mm, palpable and ill-defined mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 12:30\u000a2. Right: upper inner 1:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000a2. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. - Blue cassette\u000aB/2. - Pink cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "1230 position right breast", consists of multiple yellow-white\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000ablue cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast site #2 pink cassette", consists of multiple\u000ayellow-white fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are\u000areceived in a pink cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/7/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for the DCIS, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for the DCIS, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Positive (3+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/11/2008\u000a[report_end]
