VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION WITH WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia and ductal involvement by cells of atypical\u000alobular hyperplasia, and extensive involvement of a large well-developed\u000aarea of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aFocal expansion of lobules by lobular neoplasia meeting minimal criteria\u000afor LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aCalcifications are associated with the epithelium in the area of\u000asclerosing adenosis (both in areas involved and uninvolved by lobular\u000aneoplasia).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LAZAR,ALEXANDER J FAULKNER,M.D.,PH.D\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications present in specimen.\u000aThe specimen, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast mass", is a breast excision specimen (3.5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) consistent with primarily fat and breast glandular tissue. The specimen is\u000ainked black and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast mass, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
