tocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. On section, the specimen is friable and is composed predominately of\u000aadipose tissue with a firm fibrous area abutting the deep margin (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.7 cm). The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Smaller fragment (inked black), 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: Larger fragment, fibrous area to lateral/inferior margin, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 5: Fibrous area -posterior, inferior, lateral margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional fibrous area to margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, multiple frags, ESS.\u000assa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
