VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM SOUTH SHORE HOSPITAL, SOUTH WEYMOUTH, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (04-5222; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present as one focus (< REMOVED_DATE cm) in one of\u000a26 blocks (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note). This area is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin.\u000aThe ADH is associated with calcifications, but the majority of\u000acalcifications are present in association with sclerosing adenosis,\u000aapocrine cysts, and benign breast lobules.\u000aReactive stroma with focal giant cell reaction and hemosiderin laden\u000amacrophages are present. These changes may be indicative of a prior\u000abiopsy site or cyst rupture. Clinical correlation is suggested.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aRadial sclerosing lesions.\u000aNOTE: There is a relatively homogeneous population of cells forming\u000acribriform spaces in one duct profile. This case was reviewed by\u000aDr. Frederick Koerner (Massachusetts General Hospital), who favored a\u000adiagnosis of "severely atypical ductal hyperplasia, single microscopic\u000afocus" for this area (MGH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID).\u000aA subsequent re-excision revealed only columnar alteration with flat\u000aatypia (reviewed as BWH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTEN,ADAM,M.D.\u000aReceived from South shore Hospital, Pathology Department, 55 Fogg Road, South\u000aWeymouth, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are twenty-six (26) slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000acorresponding to a right breast needle localized biopsy (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm;\u000athe specimen was entirely submitted) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aIncluded is a consultation report from Tufts-New England Medical Center,\u000aBoston, MA; numbered "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to the case listed\u000aabove, bearing the patient's name.\u000aAlso included is a consultation report from Massachusetts General Hospital,\u000aBoston, MA; numbered "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to the case\u000alisted above, bearing the patient's name.\u000aIncluded is a letter from Dr. Frederick Koerner at Massachusetts General\u000aHospital, Boston, MA; to Dr. Ludmila Epshteyn at South Shore Hospital, South\u000aWeymouth, MA; referring to the case listed above and bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aReports to: CHEN, WENDY, YVONNE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
