tocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior\u000ato reveal a hemorrhagic cavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is grossly located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from anterior to posterior, 2 frags\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDCP:jjk\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher P Crum M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/7/2007\u000a[report_end]
