argins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localization wire enters at\u000athe junction of the superior and lateral margin, and marks off an area of\u000acalcification at the superior margin with a surgical clip. The specimen is cut\u000ainto eight slices in a medial to lateral direction. The clip is seen in slice\u000a#3. The specimen consists of approximately 95% white fibrous tissue with 5%\u000ayellow adipose tissue. No focal lesions are noted. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 (medial aspect), 4 perpendicular frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 (with clip removed), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 (lateral margin), 3 perpendicular frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCJD/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Sunday February 22, 2009 at 12:28:00PM\u000a[report_end]
