VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Sebastien de Feraudy, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION INCLUDING SKIN AND CICATRIX:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aSkin with cicatrix is present.\u000aA portion of the prior core needle biopsy site is present at the medial\u000amargin (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: The patient was found to have an area of thickening at 5:00. Ultrasound\u000ashowed a REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined mass in this area. There were no findings\u000aon mammography. A core needle biopsy showed dense breast stroma with\u000apseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aIn this excisional specimen the clip was not present. The core biopsy\u000asite is present at the edge of the specimen. Biopsy sites are also\u000apresent at the corresponding specimen edge in the additional excision\u000a(see below). Therefore, the core biopsy site appears to have been\u000atransected and removed in the two specimens.\u000aA specific histologic lesion corresponding to the ill-defined mass is\u000anot seen. There are areas of dense breast stroma adjacent to the\u000abiopsy site.\u000aRadiologic correlation is suggested.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVED MARGIN:\u000aBiopsy site changes are present at the edge of the tissue correlating\u000awith the main specimen (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBreast tissue with dense stroma is present.\u000aDr. Susan Lester has reviewed this case and concurs with the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47 year old nulliparous premenopausal female with an area of L lateral\u000anodularity - REMOVED_DATE  mammogram was unrevealing. U/S demonstrated a simple cyst\u000aand an adjacent area of asymmetric tissue. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed dense\u000afibrous stroma with focal PASH - not considered concordant for which biopsy was\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue and anterior scar, stitches - short/superior margin,\u000along/lateral margin, whip/deep margin (to mammo).\u000aB/2) L breast tissue medial shaved margin - whipstitch/new margin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Specimen x-rays show dense tissue, no clip.\u000aSpecimen #1 and Specimen #2: Ultrasounds of both specimens show areas of\u000ashadowing in #1, consistent with mass. Eva Gombos, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue and anterior scar, stitch - short/superior,\u000along/lateral, whip/deep margin", consists of a lumpectomy specimen measuring\u000a5.3 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior. A wire enters the specimen from medium to lateral. A portion of\u000askin is present at the anterior margin. No lesions are identified. The\u000aspecimen is inked by surgeon according to the pathology protocol (black =\u000aposterior; blue = anterior; orange = medial; yellow = lateral; red = superior;\u000agreen = inferior). The specimen is sectioned medial to lateral and entirely\u000asubmitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire specimen, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Breast tissue, medial shaved margin, whipstitch/new margin",\u000aconsists of one soft tissue fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a\u000awhipstitch indicating the new margin, inked blue. The specimen is sectioned\u000aperpendicular to the new margin and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire specimen, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aDEF/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 12:24:25PM\u000a[report_end]
