VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.; Priscilla S Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with severe\u000aatypia.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aComplex sclerosing lesions and florid adenosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast calcification, right breast core biopsy revealed atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral (to frozen section room for mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and single Ca++ in specimen. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to\u000atan/pink fibroadipose tissue (4.6 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE S-I cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon with two sutures: Short equals superior, long equals\u000alateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one needle localization wire in place,\u000awhich enters the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits the medial aspect of\u000athe specimen. The pink sheet received with the specimen says "clip and single\u000acalcification in specimen"; however, a radiograph is not received with the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit\u000aapproximately 60% diffusely dense focally cystic white/pink fibrous stroma\u000aextending to all inked margins, and approximately 40% yellow/tan lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. The needle localization wire traverses the dense fibrous\u000astroma, and a metal clip is identified within the fibrous stroma towards the\u000amedial aspect of the specimen. No discrete masses are grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially submitted from lateral to medial (clip\u000aidentified within fibrous stroma in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multiple frags total,\u000aESS.\u000almb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/11/2006\u000a[report_end]
