 to the posteroinferior aspect\u000aof the specimen (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, and grossly abuts the medial, superior, inferior, anterior, and\u000aposterior margins. The specimen is sectioned into ten slices with the area of\u000aclip being in slice #5.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from medial to lateral, 1 frag each,\u000aESS (micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID represents area of clip).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aDCP/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
