VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST":\u000aDuctal hyperplasia, multifocal, moderate-florid.\u000aFibrocystic change including cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000aadenosis.\u000aClip is radiographically present in block 1.\u000aExtensive microcalcifications, in association with fibrocystic change\u000aand otherwise normal lobules.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypia in this sample.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aAdditional levels have been obtained on the block with the clip\u000aradiologicallyy (#1).\u000aThese reveal a minute (0.1 cm) focus of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia,\u000awith associated microcalcifications, adjacent to the healed core biopsy\u000atract. This focus is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. It is\u000ahistologically similar to the lesion in the prior core biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000a(Case reviewed at Staff Conference and with Dr. Susan Lester.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 68 year old nulliparous postmenopausal woman not on hormones,\u000awhoses REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrated a right breast upper inner\u000aquadrant 5 mm cluster of microcalcification. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy\u000arevealed atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: right breast wire localization breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue\u000a(short suture = superior, long suture = lateral).\u000aRadiology: Clip is within the specimen-----Dr. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MCCUSKER,MARGARET ELIZABETH,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast tissue," and consists of a tan/yellow\u000aoriented fragment of fibradipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a short\u000asuture marking superior, and a long suture marking lateral. A needle\u000alocalization wire is in place. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Representative sections of margins\u000aare submitted for microscopic examination. The area contain the clip is grossly\u000aidentifiable, but the clip is not seen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area with clip, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, multiple frags,ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
