VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aPapilloma.\u000aFibrocystic changes including cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBreast parenchyma with focal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFocal dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm).\u000aMedial calcific sclerosis of arteries.\u000aNo malignancy seen.\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. Richardson, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: An 83 year old female with L breast bloody nipple discharge. L breast\u000aMRI supplemented by ultrasound demonstrates a retroareolar complex solid\u000alesion; solid nodules at 3:00 and 5:00 axis, all recommended for excisional\u000abiopsy.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision x2. L retroareolar mass\u000aexcision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass x3.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast tissue. Stitches: short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch/deep margin, blue bowtie on divided duct.\u000a2. 3:00 lesion - lateral shave margin, whipstitch on new margin.\u000a3. Inferior shave margin, 5:00 lesion, whipstitch on new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: masses in specimens. J.Meyer, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DINH,QUINN QUEYEN-BAO,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch deep margin, blue bowties on divided duct", consists of one\u000aoriented left breast excision (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented\u000aand inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cross section reveals an\u000aill-defined, white, firm fibrotic lesion (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), adjacent to the\u000aarea with the blue bowtie. The following are the nearest margins of this\u000alesion: less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, greater than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior and posterior margins. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: breast parenchyma around the area of the blue bowtie, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lesion, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining breast parenchyma, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two is labeled "#2 3 o'clock lesion, lateral shave margin, whipstich on\u000anew margin". The whipstitch on new margin is inked black and the old margin is\u000ainked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned and representative section is\u000asubmitted. Section reveals yellow adipose tissue without any evidence of\u000alesions.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of 3 o'clock shave margins, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 inferior shave margin, 5 o'clock lesion, whipstitch at\u000anew margin", consists of one fragment of yellow adipose tissue with whipstitch\u000a= new margin (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The new margin is inked black and the old\u000amargin is inked blue. Cross sections reveals diffuse, yellow adipose tissue.\u000aRepresentative section is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior shave margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aqqd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
