VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM CARITAS NORWOOD HOSPITAL, NORWOOD, MA:\u000aBILATERAL BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aRIGHT BREAST, ULTRASOUND GUIDED:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III) at least REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo definitive carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results (not\u000areviewed):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu EQUIVOCAL (2+)\u000aNote: The carcinoma has a lobular appearance, but would be classified\u000abest after excision.\u000aBy report, the block was sent for FISH analysis.\u000aLEFT BREAST STEREOTACTIC GUIDED, FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with cysts, columnar cell changes and normal\u000alobules.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of ADH of right breast in 1999. Invasive carcinoma right\u000abreast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Caritas Norwood Hospital, 800 Washington Street, Norwood, MA\u000aREMOVED_CASE_ID, are twenty five (25) slides.\u000aTwenty five (25) stained slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1/A",\u000a"1/A LEVEL 2" through "1/A LEVEL 5", "2/A", "2/A LEVEL 2" through "2/A LEVEL\u000a5", "2/B", "2/B LEVEL 2" through "2/B LEVEL 5", "2/C", "2/C LEVEL 2" through\u000a"2/C LEVEL 5", "2/D", "2/D LEVEL 2" through "2D LEVEL 5" which correspond to 1)\u000aright breast ultrasound guided core biopsies (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm);\u000aand 2) left breast stereotactic core biopsies (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aobtained on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe name Linda M. Panek with a date of birth of REMOVED_DATE  According to\u000aclinical information, this is the same person as Linda Quigley.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 09, 2009 at 04:42:30PM\u000a[report_end]
