VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ARPITA R. SWAMI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, MIDDLE DEPTH, 11 G STEREOTACTIC GUIDED CORE NEEDLE\u000aBIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this\u000alimited specimen.\u000aCalcifications are associated with invasive carcinoma and with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 54 year old female with new dx of right breast ILC. Has 2 groups of\u000aamorphous ca++ in UOQ approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from each other. Only one group\u000aamenable to core biopsy.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper outer middle depth\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted A: with ca++, B: without ca++ - Blue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of two blue cassettes, one labeled "A\u000aCA++" which contains multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm in aggregate). The second blue cassette is labeled "B" contains\u000amultiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate). The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-09-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aJC/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday February 06, 2009 at 05:07:24PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors. Given the differing morphologies and\u000aimmunophenotypes of the two right breast carcinomas biopsied (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000athere appear to be two separate primaries.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday February 11, 2009 at 05:20:58PM\u000a[report_end]
