VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY ANS SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (parts A and\u000aB including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and FSB):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES, TWO\u000aFOCI, LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND MESTASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm and > 5cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note)\u000aHistologic type - Lobular and Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - 10 to 75% (2 points) to < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Low (1 point) to Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Present\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent. Invasive carcinoma extends into\u000anipple and is present in stroma around lactiferous ducts.\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Present\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Medial, deep, anterior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU -Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU -Present\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aALH\u000aCore biopsy site (x2)\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE: Tumor is present as two distinct foci. There is an invasive lobular\u000acarcinoma present throughout the REMOVED_DATE cm mass in the medial part of the specimen\u000ain the upper inner quadrant (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). This tumor extensively infiltrates skeletal\u000amuscle extending to margins. The other focus has mixed ductal and lobular\u000afeatures and involves two grossly identified REMOVED_DATE cm nodules in the mid-upper\u000aouter quadrant as well as all tissue between the two nodules (2\u000acm).Additionally, all the tissue submitted between the larger REMOVED_DATE cm gross mass\u000a(invasive lobular carcinoma) and the two smaller gross masses (cumulatively 5\u000acm) are also involved by invasive carcinoma with mixed features. The overall\u000aexact size of the carcinoma with mixed features is difficult to determine, but\u000aexceeds 5 cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe micrometastasis [REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmi(sn)] is seen on deeper levels in the sentinel node\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, level 2) and is not present in the original frozen section slides.\u000aMorphologically, it is favored that the metastasis is from the tumor with mixed\u000aductal and lobular features.\u000aDr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology, has reviewed selected slides and concurs.\u000aC. CORE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aD. MEDIAL PECTORAL MUSCLE:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, invading skeletal muscle.\u000aCarcinoma is focally present at medial, anterior, and posterior margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 year old post menopausal woman s/p REMOVED_DATE  right breast, core\u000abiopsy, UIQ revealing moderately differentiated grade II/III ILC; no LVI, no\u000aCIS.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, SNM, SLNB, ? ALND, RECON.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right sentinel node hot and blue.\u000aB/2. Right breast short superior, long lateral bow tie firm medial margin.\u000aC/3. Core biopsy site.\u000aD/4. Medial pectoral muscle short medial long superior.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2, 3, 4):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT BREAST" (FSB):\u000aInvasive carcinoma involves the medial and deep margins.\u000aCarcinoma shows extensive infiltration of skeletal muscle.\u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: GEORGE LIN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right sentinel node, hot and blue", consists of one fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing one large fatty lymph node\u000a(3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), sliced in four sections and submitted in the frozen\u000asection room as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnants, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, short superior, long lateral, bowtie, firm medial\u000amargin", consists of a radical mastectomy specimen (900-g, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior). A patch of muscle is located on the deep margin at the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen (10.5 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior), which is inked orange and\u000amarked with a bowtie per the surgeon. The deep margin is inked black, the\u000aanterior margin is inked blue. Sectioning of the specimen reveals\u000aapproximately 90% lobulated yellow adipose tissue and 10% white, firm fibrous\u000atissue. The anterior surface displays a white/tan skin ellipse (11.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple-areolar complex, including an everted nipple (1.0 cm in\u000adiameter).\u000aAt the medial aspect of the specimen, located at the interface of fibroadipose\u000atissue and skeletal muscle, there is a white, firm, ill-defined, spiculated\u000amass (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, ill-defined) present. A\u000arepresentative section of this mass is submitted in the frozen section room as\u000aFSB. This mass (#1), located in the upper inner quadrant, is grossly present\u000aat the deep skeletal muscle margin and the medial margin, 5 cm from the\u000aanterior margin and approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple-areolar complex. Mass\u000a#1, including surrounding firm fibrous tissue and skeletal muscle, is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aAdditional ill-defined, firm, white areas (? additional masses, both measuring\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, found REMOVED_DATE cm apart from each other)\u000aare found in the mid to upper outer quadrant, located approximately 5 cm from\u000amass #1, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior/deep, > REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin\u000a(mass #2) as well as REMOVED_DATE cm from the NA complex, and in the mid to lower outer\u000aquadrant, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep and at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin as well as 4 cm from the NA complex (mass #3).\u000aNo other lesions or masses are identified. Approximately REMOVED_DATE % of the firm,\u000awhite fibrous tissue are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #1, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #2, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areolar complex, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue between mass #1 and mass #2, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue between mass #2 and mass#3, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Core needle biopsy site", consists of a fragment of tan/white firm\u000atissue (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Core biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Medial pectoral muscle, short medial, long superior", consists of\u000aa fragment of skeletal muscle (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked as\u000afollows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, and medial - orange. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from medial to lateral and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aAWE/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 01:47:29PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (4/7/09):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin is negative, supporting lobular\u000aphenotype.\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) EQUIVOCAL (1+ to 2+)\u000aNote: FISH analysis will be performed; results will be reported as an\u000aaddendum.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH\u000a07, 2009 at 02:11:42PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following results for the carcinoma with ductal and lobular features (block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 11:47:30AM\u000a[report_end]
