VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aSCHNITT, STUART, J., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by SCHNITT,STUART J.,M.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications present in association with ADH and lobules.\u000aLEFT BREAST AND RIGHT BREAST, WIRE GUIDED EXCISIONS AND LEFT BREAST INFERIOR\u000aMARGIN, SUPERIOR/ANTERIOR MARGIN EXCISIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION (PART A):\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypical hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with lobules.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION (PART B):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications present in association with ADH, sclerosing adenosis;\u000acysts and lobules.\u000aLEFT BREAST, INFERIOR/ANTERIOR MARGIN (PART C):\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypical hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR/ANTERIOR MAGIN (PART D):\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypical hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Ca++ medial (L) breast; (L) breast ADH and (R) breast\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are nineteen (19) slides.\u000aOne (1) slide is labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (3)", corresponding to\u000aleft breast stereotactically guided core biopsy (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aEighteen (18) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(4)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (6)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (5)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (5)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (6)",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (6)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (3)" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) left breast\u000awire guided excision (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) right breast wire guided excision\u000a(6.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) C) left breast inferior margin excision (4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) D) left breast superior/anterior margin excision (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
