VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM LAHEY CLINIC, BURLINGTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aA single stromal calcification is present.\u000aNote: Only a rare calcification is present. Radiologic correlation would be\u000anecessary to determine if the biopsies sampled the targeted lesion.\u000aLEFT BREAST, PARTIAL DUCTECTOMY FOR NIPPLE DISCHARGE (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present involving a lobular unit\u000a(0.4 cm), in 1 of 20 blocks (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note). No calcifications or\u000anecrosis are seen.\u000aADH is present at the anterior margin.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults for ADH (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aNote: The area of ADH was originally classified as DCIS. However, given the\u000asmall size and the partial involvement of spaces, classification as ADH is\u000afavored. Due to the presence of the lesion at the margin, a re-excision\u000awould be helpful to exclude an adjacent area of DCIS, if residual tissue\u000ais present at the anterior margin.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, not associated with calcifications (see note).\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults for ADH (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aNote: The ADH consists of low grade nuclei forming a cribriform pattern in a\u000a0.1 cm area and was originally classified as DCIS. Given the small size of the\u000alesion, classification as ADH is favored. However, excision would be helpful\u000ato exclude an adjacent area of DCIS.\u000aThe type of lesion biopsied is not stated. Radiologic correlation is necessary\u000ato ensure the biopsies are representative of the targeted lesion.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concurs wit this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aPapilloma.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aBenign epithelium with associated calcifications.\u000aNote: The type of lesion biopsied is not stated. Radiologic correlation is\u000anecessary to ensure the biopsies are representative of the targeted lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Lahey Clinic, Pathology Department, 41 Mall Road, Burlington, MA\u000aREMOVED_CASE_ID, are fifty-one (51) glass slides.\u000aFifteen (15) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a3", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3", corresponding to a left breast core biopsies A) well #12\u000awith calcifications (1.5 x 1 cm) B) well #3 with (1.58 x 1 cm) C) well #6 with\u000acalcifications (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) D) well #9 with calcifications (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) E)\u000acenter well with calcifications (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm)1.58 x 1 cm) C) well #6 with\u000acalcifications (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) D) well #9 with calcifications (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) E)\u000acenter well with calcifications (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according\u000ato the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aTwenty-three (23) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ER", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PR", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID UNC-Ms" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding\u000ato a left breast excision (5 x 4 x 3 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aSeven (7) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE ", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE ", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aER", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PR", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID UNC-Ms", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE " and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE ", corresponding to a right\u000abreast core biopsy (2.5 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying\u000apathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aSix (6) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE " through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE "\u000aand "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE " through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE ", corresponding to a left breast core biopsy (2.5\u000acm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report\u000abearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u0