en measures REMOVED_DATE x 28 x 2 cm and\u000aweighs 560 grams. The skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and has a nipple and\u000aareola present; the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and the areola, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aA 4 cm, well healed scar is present on the lateral border of the areola.\u000aThe axillary tail measures 8 x 8 x 1 cm. On incision, no gross residual tumor\u000awas present. The previous biopsy cavity was identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm, extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Muscle tissue is\u000apresent on the posterior surface of the breast, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Cavity, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Nipple and cavity, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: Right upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: Right lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right axillary lymph nodes, 12 frag, RSS.\u000aSpecimen's part two, labeled "left breast/axillary node (short=supeior;\u000along=lateral)", is received fresh in the frozen section room and weighs 535\u000agrams and measures, grossly, 28 x 19 x 3 cm. The specimen consists of a left\u000abreast, complete with axillary tail and skin ellipse. The skin ellipse\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and has a central nipple with a diameter of REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asurrounded by a REMOVED_DATE cm diameter areola. On the medial border of the areola,\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE cm well healed scar. The axillary tail measures 9 x 6 x 2 cm. On\u000aincision, no tumor was grossly present; however, a biopsy cavity was found\u000asurrounded by fat necrosis. The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000ais situated REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aMicro 13: Left breast biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: Left biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: Left breast scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: Left nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: Medial superior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: Medial inferior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: Left lateral superior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left lower outer quadrant, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left axillary lymph nodes, 10 frag, RSS.\u000arjb\u000aReports to: EBERLEIN, TIMOTHY, JOSEPH M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
