VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST UPPER INNER QUADRANT 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA with associated microcalcifications (see NOTE).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with microcalcifications.\u000aNOTE: The focus of ADH is present within a columnar cell lesion. Dr. Deborah\u000aDillon has also reviewed the slides and agrees with the diagnosis. Atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia is evaluated best after excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 52 year old with 3 mm group coarse heterogeneous Ca++ LUIQ\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 3 mm, non-palpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper/inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast - A/tissue with Ca++; B/remainder of tissues in two green\u000acassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left stereo-green", and consists of two green cassettes, one\u000alabeled A-CA++, the other received without designation. The main cassette is\u000alabeled "A Ca++", and contains multiple pink/tan tissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The undesignated green cassette contains multiple tan/yellow\u000atissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Green cassette labeled "A Ca++" contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Undesignated green cassette contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000apf/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/21/2008\u000a[report_end]
