men is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000abisected with the anterior portion containing the wire. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned lateral to medial and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior half of the specimen containing the wire, serial\u000asections from lateral to medial with microcalcifications contained potentially\u000ain micros REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro 19: lateral-most slice, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from lateral to medial, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 27: medial-most slice, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior half of the specimen, serial sections from lateral to\u000amedial:\u000aMicro 28: lateral-most slice, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from lateral to medial, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 35: medial-most slides, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
