D_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is unoriented and the soft tissue resection margin is inked black.\u000aThere is a slightly raised area of pink/tan skin (0.6 cm), similar in to color\u000ato surrounding skin, which extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the skin edge. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: tips, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, 6 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. re-excision left breast DCIS site short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of an oriented left breast lumpectomy specimen (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 cm) with attached pink/tan skin ellipse (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with a\u000ashort stitch marking the superior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral\u000asurface. The specimen is inked orange and green by the surgeon at the medial\u000aand inferior margins, respectively, and the remaining surfaces are inked per\u000athe histologic evaluation margins (skin is at the anterior surface, and biopsy\u000acavity located at the superior surface): posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; lateral = yellow. The skin contains a well-healed linear scar\u000a(3.0 cm). The specimen is serially sectioned from posterior to anterior\u000arevealing approximately 70% white/tan/pink lobular tissue which extends to all\u000aof the soft tissue resection margins. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posteriormost section, perpendicular, 14 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from posterior to anterior, 17 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anteriormost section, perpendicular, including skin with scar, 18\u000afrags, ESS\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
