VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CELINA G. MANKEY M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MID OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with columnar cell change,\u000asecretory features, and calcifications is present (see note).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 54 year old with history of LCIS on surgical biopsy right breast in\u000a1996 with suspicious Ca++ in the right mid outer breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: mid outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast in two orange cassettes - A/with Ca++ and B/no Ca++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "right breast", and consists of two orange cassettes. The first\u000aorange cassette, labeled "A Ca++" contains multiple cores of fibroadipose\u000atissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second orange cassette, labeled\u000a"B", contains multiple cores of fibroadipose tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Orange cassette A contents (Ca++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Orange cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/2/2008\u000a[report_end]
