VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, intermediate grade, cribriform-type with\u000asecretory features, preset as a single REMOVED_DATE cm focus.\u000aDCIS is close (0.15 cm) to the lateral and inferior margins.\u000aThe superior, medial, anterior, and posterior margins are negative\u000a(>0.3 cm).\u000aCalcifications are associated with DCIS.\u000aNo necrosis is present in DCIS.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aNOTE: Selected slides were also reviewed by Dr. Jane Brock (Breast Pathology\u000aService), who concurs.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aDr. Rhei was notified of the results on REMOVED_DATE  at 9:55 a.m. by Dr. Ricci.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54-year-old premenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast core Bx's,\u000arevealing ADH, ALH with Pagetoid spread - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast tissue; short stitch - superior, long stitch - lateral;\u000awhip - deep margin; to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Spoke to OR (Dr. Rhei) at 10:45 AM. Calcifications contained in\u000aspecimen. Wire is intact. (ILLEGIBLE signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Rt breast tissue, short stitch equal superior, long\u000astitch equals lateral, whipstitch equals deep margin", and consists of a single\u000alumpectomy specimen (3.9 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000a4.4 cm medial to lateral). The specimen has been oriented by the surgeon as\u000afollows: Short suture equals superior, long suture equals lateral, whipstitch\u000aequals posterior (deep). The specimen has been previously inked by the\u000asurgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a localizing wire entering the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen and marking a clip and calcifications as\u000ademonstrated on the accompanying radiograph. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial into eleven slices to reveal an ill-defined,\u000afirm, white area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which measures REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral and medial\u000amargins. This firm area is adjacent to the clip and is in association with\u000afibrosis, which spands REMOVED_DATE cm. The fibrosis encompasses approximately 30% of\u000athe specimen; the remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue. All of\u000athe fibrotic areas (85% of the specimen) are submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation. No other masses or lesions are noted. Gross photographs are\u000ataken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 (including clip and firm area), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aEM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/2/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/09/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCAL) (2+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
