rgin, blue bow-tie and divided margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture), lateral (long suture), and chest wall (whipstitch) margins. A\u000alocalizing wire is loosely associated with the superior aspect of the specimen.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wire in placed within an\u000aencircled area of possible abnormality within the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Sectioning demonstrates 60% to 70% unremarkable tan/white dense\u000afibrous tissue without palpable or visible nodules, lesions, or other\u000aabnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000aanterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Duct margin, en face section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior resection margin, perpendicular section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections anterior to posterior, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area near localizing wire, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections anterior to posterior, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior resection margin, perpendicular section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Tissue behind left nipple", consists of fragments of cauterized\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The\u000aspecimen is submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/19/2008\u000a[report_end]
