edial = orange. There is a localizing wire protruding from the specimen.\u000aSerial sectioning reveals multiple small firm areas (0.1 cm in greatest\u000adimension) but no large or discrete masses or suspicious areas. A mammogram\u000aaccompanying the specimen reveals the presence of a localizing wire and an\u000airregular density. This specimen is submitted in its entirety for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro 1: anterior, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: posterior, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, anterior to posterior, multi frags, ESS.\u000afsd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
