VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATION AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focally severe, multiple scattered foci\u000a(levels examined).\u000aColumnar alteration with flat atypia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aMicroscopic fibroadenomas.\u000aChanges consistent with prior core biopsy site.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCase reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson, breast pathology service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal left mammmogram on core biopsy showed ADH vs. DCIS.\u000aOperation: Needle localized left breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen includes clip and califications. BH\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. left breast tissue", and consists of a yellow/tan lumpectomy specimen\u000a(6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached grossly unremarkable white/tan triangular\u000afragment of skin (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been inked by the surgeon\u000aprior to receipt in pathology per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There are two wires protruding from the\u000aposterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph\u000adepicting the wires localized to an area of calcifications and a clip. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal an ill-defined white/tan to focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrous area (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in which the two wires are\u000alocalized and in which the clip is identified. The fibrous area grossly extends\u000ato the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, to the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior/skin margin, to the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow/tan\u000agrossly unremarkable adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMICRO #1 and 2: Medial margin, 3 frags in each cass, ESS.\u000aMICRO #3-5: Lateral and inferior margins, 3 frags in micro #3, 2 frags in\u000amicros #4 and 5, ESS.\u000aMICRO #6: Area containing clip with inferior and superior margins, 1 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMICRO #8: Superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #9: Superior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #10: Anterior/skin, superior, inferior margins, 1 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #11: Anterior, medial, inferior margins, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #12: Superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #13: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #14: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #15: Anterior and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #16: Inferior and posterior margins, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #17: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #18: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #19: Posterior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #20: Posterior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #21: Posterior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #22: Posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO #23: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
