VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP:\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCalcification sin benign epithelium.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aScar consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH, Lt.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH, lt.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) tissue lt breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. E.P. Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient?s name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast tissue", and consists of a wire localized excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue. The specimen is received with a radiograph which shows a\u000aclip and a wire within the specimen. The specimen is unoriented, and has\u000adimensions of REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm. The localization wire is protruding\u000afrom one end of the specimen and terminates in the specimen. There are no\u000apalpable lesions noted. Sectioning reveals focal areas of hemorrhage where the\u000awire terminated in the specimen. Sectioning also reveals a REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x\u000a0.5 cm firm white, fibrous area of tissue. The specimen is entirely inked blue\u000aand submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with focal hemorrhagic area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with fibrous lesion, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with fibrous lesion, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with fibrous lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with fibrous lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCJD/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/8/2008\u000a[report_end]
