perior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe superior and inferior margins are removed and the remainder of the specimen\u000ais sectioned into seven sections to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy site extending\u000afrom slices #3 through #7 and into the inferior section (clip site) of the\u000aspecimen. The biopsy site is located REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular sections, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-09-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acel\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 23, 2009 at 01:16:16PM\u000a[report_end]
