VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Reduction mamoplasty\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIAN J PRIBAZ M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, BREAST REDUCTION (655g):\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibroadenoma (3.2 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, BREAST REDUCTION (535g):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None specified.\u000aOperation: Bilateral breast reduction.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral macromastia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast tissue (655).\u000aB/2) Lt breast tissue (535).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue 655", consists of a 655-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a5.5 cm aggregate of multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue, partially\u000asurfaced by unremarkable tan skin. Sectioning demonstrates an ill-defined\u000alobulated firm tan/white mass (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with friable lobulated to\u000apapillary surfaces. Remaining specimen is comprised of 30% to 40% tan/white\u000afibrous tissue with multifocal occasional additional firm areas. Please note:\u000aDistance to surgical margins cannot be assessed due to the disrupted,\u000afragmented nature of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Relatively unremarkable fibrous tissue and skin, multi frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm lesional tissue (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID from largest mass, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID from scattered\u000aadditional site), multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue 535", consists of a 535-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm aggregate of multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue and attached\u000aunremarkable tan skin. Sectioning demonstrates focally firm tan/white\u000afiber-dense tissue (30% to 40%), with occasional dilated duct exuding a thick,\u000ayellow fluid. There are no discrete masses noted grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/30/2008\u000a[report_end]
