VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, ONE FOCUS\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - at least REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - mucinous\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - multiple broad fronts at unoriented\u000amargins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) -\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 1:3 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - focal at unoriented margin\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 39 year old female with left breast mass - 11 weeks post partum.\u000aOperation: Excision\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "left breast mass", and consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/pink soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is unoriented\u000aand inked black at the surface. There is a single nodular area of firmness\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and extending to the surface of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  6 frags, ESS\u000amir\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
