"#1. R breast tissue with needle wire tags long equals lateral, short\u000aequals superior, whip equals chest wall", consists of an irregular portion of\u000afibrofatty tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral,\u000aa short suture designating superior, and a whipstitch designating chest wall\u000amargin (posterior). The specimen is received previously inked per pathology\u000aprotocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green,\u000amedial orange and lateral yellow. There is an inserted needle localization\u000awire, which enters along the anterior-lateral margin, and does not exit the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic biopsy\u000acavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000abiopsy cavity is surrounded by dense white fibrous tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000apredominantly at the inferior-posterior aspect, coming to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The remaining cut surface displays\u000a98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 2% white fibrous tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the biopsy cavity in REMOVED