hology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black (deep margin), superior\u000ared, inferior green, lateral yellow, and medial orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a potential hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm), less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin,\u000a1.0 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin. A surgical clip is identified within the potential\u000ahemorrhagic biopsy cavity. The remaining cut surface displays 90% focally\u000adense white fibrous tissue, and 10% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the\u000aclip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
