VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOWER INNER:\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications.\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aUPPER OUTER:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present (best seen in block 4, level 1).\u000aThe ADH is not associated with calcifications.\u000aCalcifications are associated with lobules.\u000aThere is an area of adenosis which is confirmed by the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells (immunoperoxidase studies for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and smooth muscle\u000aalpha actin).\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated by excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 64 year old female with focal calcifications in RLIQ and RUOQ,\u000aincreased since prior studies.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic\u000aOperative findings: Calcifications in specimen\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Possible DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right lower inner breast tissue (3 cassettes - 1 white\u000acassette - tissue with no calcifications - off target, 2 orange cassettes - "A"\u000awith calcifications and "B" without calcifications at site of calcification)\u000a2) Right upper outer tissue (2 yellow cassettes - "A" with calcifications and\u000a"B" remainder of tissue)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one labeled "#1. right LIQ", and consists of three (3) cassettes. The\u000afirst unlabeled white cassette contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of\u000ayellow/tan fibrofatty cores. The second orange cassette is labeled "A" with\u000acalcifications and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow/red/tan\u000afibrofatty soft tissue cores (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The third\u000aorange cassette is labeled "B" and contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of\u000ayellow/tan/red focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissue cores.\u000aMicro 1: white unlabeled cassette, mult frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right UOQ", and consists of two (2) yellow cassettes.\u000aOne cassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.7 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 4: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: DENISON, CHRISTINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
