VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aDense stroma.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCysts.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Dense stroma may sometimes be associated with the radiographic finding of\u000aa mass lesion. However, radiographic/histologic correlation is\u000anecessary to assure this biopsy represents sampling of the underlying\u000alesion. Because of preoperative clinical or radiologic concern\u000aregarding the possibility of tumor, the margins of this specimen were\u000ainked, sampled, and examined microscopically.\u000aPortions of the accompanying requisition state "LEFT BREAST" as the site\u000aof the biopsy, while the specimen is labeled "RIGHT". Following\u000adiscussion with Dr. Rhei on REMOVED_DATE  and cross-checking with the\u000apre-operative ultrasound report and operating room schedule, the\u000aspecimen is confirmed as a RIGHT breast biopsy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 44 year old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammograms supplemented\u000aby U/S demonstrate a 4 cm fat containing oval mass with negative U/S.\u000aPatient wishes excision.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue (short/superior; long/lateral;\u000awhip stitch on deep margin)\u000a(Please note the discrepancies in designation of laterality on the submitted\u000arequisition and see the "NOTE" at the end of the FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS.)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Density in specimen. Millstone/Sedgwick.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan adipose breast tissue. The specimen is received with two orienting\u000asutures. A double long suture indicates lateral and a double short suture\u000aindicates superior. The specimen is received with a wire in place. The\u000aspecimen is received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a white/tan soft\u000aslightly nodular fibrous area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is adjacent to\u000athe superior and posterior margins and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin. This corresponds to the area designated on the specimen\u000aradiograph. The remainder of the breast tissue is comprised of unremarkable\u000aadipose tissue. The fibrous area is submitted in its entirety along with its\u000aclosest margins. Representative distant margins are also submitted.\u000aApproximately 40% of the total tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass in its entirety, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 9: distant medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 10: distant anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000arp\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
