00afocal, degenerative changes (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). These degenerative changes\u000aappear to grossly correspond to the area of calcifications, noted on the\u000aspecimen radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area grossly corresponding to calcifications seen on specimen\u000aradiograph, 14 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous nodule, multiple frags, RSS. Approximately\u000a60%\u000aof the fibrous tissue and of the entire specimen is submitted.\u000ajoc/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Joseph Woodward Carlson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/10/2005\u000a[report_end]
