nferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral to reveal approximately 90% unremarkable\u000ayellow lobulated fatty tissue and 10% firm white fibrous tissue with\u000ahemorrhage. The lesion localized by the wire and clip measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in total. The lesion is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin,\u000a3.1 cm to the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin. The clip is\u000aidentified in a small hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and the tissue\u000awith the clip is located in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. All of the lesion and fibrous tissue\u000ais submitted for histology. In total approximately 25% of the specimen is\u000asubmitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 perpendicular fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial aspect of lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Previous biopsy cavity with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral end of lesion, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White fibrous tissue at anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of hemorrhage near inferior margin, 1 frag per cassette,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000apva/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelat