VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aPrior excision/biopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aApocrine metaplasia and cysts.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aNo residual DCIS.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old woman with multiple breast biopsy in past. History of ADH.\u000aExcision wire loc. REMOVED_DATE  showed DCIS in lateral sample with close middle and\u000alateral margins. Second site biopsied same dated showed atypical hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision partial mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral", and consists of a 21 g lumpectomy specimen (3.1 cm medial to lateral,\u000a5.1 cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen\u000ais received oriented with short stitch designating superior aspect and long\u000astitch lateral aspect, and inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is an attached skin\u000aellipse on the lateral surface (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with no gross lesions. There is\u000aan excision cavity (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is present REMOVED_DATE cm to superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral and anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. Surrounding the\u000aexcision cavity, there is firm fibrous tissue and focal fat necrosis extending\u000aover an area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, focally present at the anterior, inferior,\u000aposterior and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000amedial margin. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Excision cavity and closest margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLDO/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 03, 2008 at 11:20:56AM\u000a[report_end]
