uperior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000aanterior to posterior, exhibiting a white/pink, rubbery, encapsulated,\u000alobulated mass (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which extends to the superior, lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin and medial margins. The remaining tissue\u000aconsists of tan/white fibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, (sequentially from anterior to posterior), multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDFI/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/3/2007\u000a[report_end]
