ck. At the anterior margin\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm poorly-defined area of hemorrhage, yellow\u000adiscoloration, and possible cystic change, with cystic spaces measuring up to\u000a0.4 cm in maximum dimension. All of the grossly abnormal tissue is submitted.\u000aThere are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. The remainder of\u000athe breast parenchyma is unremarkable. All margins are taken perpendicular.\u000aApproximately 40% of the specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro #1 : lateral margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #2 : medial margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #3 : superior margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #4 : inferior margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #5-6 : posterior margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #7 : anterior margin, RSS.\u000aMicro #8-10: additional anteroinferior margin, RSS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
