VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: AYODALE S ODULATE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Joanna A Gibson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a1.0 CM MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in\u000athis limited specimen.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade), is present.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes are present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 60-year-old woman with multiple fibroadenomas biopsied in both\u000abreasts and right upper outer quadrant mass on US. Suspect fibroadenoma.\u000aPlease rule out malignancy.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 10 mm, Nonpalpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound - Green cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast green", and consists of multiple white-yellow focally\u000ahemorrhagic irregular fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich are received in a green cassette. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: The carcinoma in situ is also positive for ER and PR but shows stronger\u000apositivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
