is and prior\u000aspecimens)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 year old woman, S/P R breast WL/SNB on REMOVED_DATE  revealing Grade\u000aII/III IL with ductal and lobular features, intermediate nuclear Grade DCIS.\u000a1/1 positive SNB (close medial margin on IL) -1, close medial/positive positive\u000amargin DCIS. Previous surgeries: REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000a11/26/01 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; and,\u000a4/11/08 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: R breast re-excision - ALND.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right axillary content - level one and two, and scar.\u000aB/2) posterior shave margin, whip stitch chest wall margin and scar.\u000aC/3) medial shave margin, whip stitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in three parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Level 1 and 2 right axillary contents and scar", and consists of\u000afibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Multiple lymph nodes were\u000aidentified in the fat, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is an\u000aadditional ellipse of skin, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with tan/brown skin surface.\u000aThe entire lymph nodes and the skin tissue are submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 possible lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Posterior shave margin whipstitch chest wall margin and scar",\u000aconsists of fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The new margin is\u000amarked by stitch and the opposite surface shows tan/yellow to brown relatively\u000afirm granulation tissue/fibrosis. The new margin is inked black and the\u000asurface containing the fibrotic area is inked blue. There is an additional\u000airregular fragment of skin tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The tissue is\u000aserially sectioned from side to the other perpendicular to the old and new\u000amargins to reveal fatty tissue with scattered tan/white punctate areas. The\u000atissue is totally submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrofatty tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Medial shave margin whipstitch new margin", consists of fibrofatty\u000atissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and consists of fibrofatty tissue with\u000astitch marking the new margin on one side. The other side consists of\u000arelatively firm tan/white to brown granulation tissue/fibrosis. The new margin\u000ais inked black, the firm fibrotic side is inked blue. The tissue is serially\u000asectioned to reveal fibrofatty tissue with areas of firm tissue with rubbery\u000aconsistency that probably represents fibrosis. Totally submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aJBE/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
