ION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "right breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (22.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a tan/white teardrop shaped skin (10.0 x\u000a4.0 cm) with a REMOVED_DATE cm slightly everted nipple and surrounding areola. There is\u000aan undesignated suture, arbitrarily designated 12 o'clock, inked red by the\u000aprosector. The specimen is sectioned from 3 o'clock to 9 o'clock and the deep\u000amargin is inked black. The breast consists of approximately REMOVED_DATE % tan/white\u000adense fibrous tissue admixed with REMOVED_DATE % adipose tissue. There are scattered\u000amultiple serosanguineous fluid-filled cysts (ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe breast parenchyma is otherwise unremarkable. The deep margin consists of\u000asmooth fascial plane. Representative sections of breast tissue and skin are\u000asubmitted to the tissue bank.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 12 o'clock to 3 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 o'clock to 6 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6 o'clock to 9 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 9 o'clock to 12 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast", consists of an 1120 gram simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (27.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a teardrop shaped skin (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aincluding an eccentrically located nipple (1.7 cm in greatest dimension) and\u000asurrounding areola. There is an undesignated suture, arbitrarily designated 12\u000ao'clock by the prosector. There are scattered serosanguineous fluid-filled\u000acysts (ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm), located mostly in the central breast.\u000aThe remainder breast tissue consists of approximately 10% fibrous tissue. The\u000adeep margin consists of a smooth fascial plane and scattered skeletal muscle.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 12 o'clock to 3 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 o'clock to 6 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6 o'clock to 9 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 9 o'clock to 12 o'clock, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "additional breast tissue", consists of skin and subcutaneous\u000aadipose tissue (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross lesions\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, labeled "additional left breast tissue", consists of two fragments of\u000askin and subcutaneous tissue (12.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm; REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aELC/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
