ds to an area of fibrous tissue but no areas of firmness,\u000amasses or granularity are identified. The specimen consists of approximately\u000a70% fibrous tissue and 40% fatty tissue. The area coinciding with\u000amicrocalcifications is entirely submitted with its closest margins which are\u000aposterior, superior, lateral and medial in the posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Representative sections are obtained from the remaining tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area corresponding to area of microcalcifications, 12 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: inferior border, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 7: anterior border, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: lateral and medial borders in inferior portion of specimen, 4\u000afrags, RSS\u000amir\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
