VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RETRO-AREOLAR, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aIntraductal papilloma with extensive squamous metaplasia associated with\u000areactive stroma with atypical stromal cells (see note).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies reveal that the majority of the stromal cells are\u000anot immunoreactive for cytokeratins (PANK and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2; blocks 1 and 2).\u000aHowever, occasional spindled stromal cells associated with the squamous\u000ametaplasia are keratin positive.\u000aNote: The findings are suspicious for possible early invasion by a\u000aspindle cell component of a squamous cell carcinoma. However, the\u000amajority of the squamoid areas are confined within a basement membrane and\u000adefinitive invasion is not demonstrated. A re-excision is recommended for\u000acomplete removal of this lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left retro-areolar mass.\u000aOperation: Excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ? intraductal papilloma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DINH,QUINN QUEYEN-BAO,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast mass", consists of an unoriented fragment of tan-brown\u000asoft tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There was no skin or wire localization. The\u000aspecimen is inked entirely black. Cross sectioning reveals well-circumscribed\u000apink firm white cut surface with less than 10% yellow adipose tissue. The\u000aentire specimen was submitted.\u000aMicro 1: left breast mass, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aqqd\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
