VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/B. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES\u000a(TWO SPECIMENS):\u000aResidual INVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm, present adjacent to prior\u000abiopsy site, see NOTE.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aExtensive LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread is present (see note).\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; see note).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000amultiple levels examined) and >0.3 cm from all other margins.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with focal atypia.\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aThree (3) sentinel lymph nodes with no carcinoma seen on H&E levels or keratin\u000aimmunohistochemistry.\u000aNOTE: Blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aLCIS is estrogen receptor positive, progesterone receptor positive, Her2/neu\u000anegative and E-cadherin negative. The focus of ADH is estrogen receptor\u000apositive, progesterone receptor positive, Her2/neu negative and E-cadherin\u000apositive.\u000aThe biopsy site is close to the yellow-inked lateral margin in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, but\u000aappears to have been entirely excised. In conjunction with the prior core\u000aneedle biopsy, showing a REMOVED_DATE cm focus of invasive tubular carcinoma, this\u000acarcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 year old premenopausal woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  L breast core bx\u000arevealing well-differentiated invasive tubular Ca, no LVI, ADH -\u000aOperation: L breast MRI-guided WL lumpectomy with 2 wires, SNM, SLNB -\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast Ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) sentinel nodes - L axilla (hot + blue REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aB/2) L breast tissue (short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on margin),\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #2: Please submit entire specimen for histology.\u000aMRI-guided loc specimen; clip, 2 wires, dense tissue between the 2 wires, and\u000aincidental calcifications are seen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - SENTINEL LYMPH NODES - L AXILLA (HOT + BLUE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node - negative for tumor.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Two lymph nodes - negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: ELIZABETH MORGAN, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "sentinel node - left axilla (hot and blue x3)". The specimen consists\u000aof three yellow/red lymph nodes marked with blue-dye. Lymph node #1 (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) is bisected and submitted entirety for frozen section review and\u000adesignated as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Lymph nodes #2 (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, inked black) and #3\u000a(1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) were both bisected and submitted in their entirety and\u000adesignated as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Please note that there is a small amount of fat (0.1 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) that was trimmed away from the smaller lymph node and not frozen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fat, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast tissue (short superior, long lateral, whipstitch on\u000amargin)". The specimen consists of one wire-localized excision (6.0 cm medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) that is\u000aoriented per surgeon (short suture superior, long stitch lateral). The\u000aspecimen was six-inked prior according to the inks protocol: Red/superior,\u000agreen/inferior, yellow/lateral, orange/medial, blue/anterior, black/posterior.\u000aThe accompanying radiograph shows calcification and clip. The specimen is\u000asectioned medial to lateral to reveal a clip is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margin,\u000a1.5 cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, 1 frag each, ESS. Please note, clip\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aKG/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
