VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Adam Rosendorff, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY\u000aFOR CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 y/o female with h/o right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNew left breast calcifications.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excision biopsy.\u000aPrevious surgery: Yes\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short suture - superior,\u000along suture - lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Positive calcs in specimen. - Dr. Yeh.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to\u000atan/pink fibroadipose tissue (2.5 SI x REMOVED_DATE ML x REMOVED_DATE AP cm) which is oriented\u000aper surgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThere is one needle localization wire in place entering the medial aspect of\u000athe specimen and exiting the inferolateral aspect of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen was previously radiographed confirming the presence of calcifications\u000awithin the specimen adjacent to the wire tip in the lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit\u000aapproximately 15% pink/white fibrous stroma (predominantly posterior/lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen) and 85% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified. The needle localization wire\u000atraverses fibrous stroma containing area of probable calcification, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The specimen is\u000aentirely sequentially submitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note, area of probable calcification in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/28/2007\u000a[report_end]
