VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aCalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46-year-old female with HVMA mammogram showing calcs at 12 o?clock (L)\u000abreast not amenable to core biopsy.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal (L) mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. (L) breast tissue ? short suture superior, long suture lateral, whipstitch\u000aat deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications are within the specimen. Intact hookwire is seen.\u000aE. Gombos, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.2\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting sutures ("short suture superior, long\u000asuture lateral, with stitch at the margin"), and a hook wire attached to a thin\u000astrand of soft tissue at the anterior/inferior aspect. The specimen is inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/ orange. The specimen is accompanied by radiograph, within which an\u000aarea of probable calcifications are identified approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ahook wire tip. A definitive margin associated with the calcification cannot\u000agrossly be assessed due to the loosely adherent wire. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from superior to inferior, exhibiting approximately 95% tan/white\u000adense stroma admixed with 5% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No gross lesions\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aLPI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
