VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBreast tissue with columnar cell change with focal micropapillary hyperplasia\u000awith atypia, and with calcifications associated with benign epithelium and\u000acysts, and biopsy site changes.\u000aNo in situ or invasive carcinoma.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for final diagnosis.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST - MEDIAL MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue with columnar cell change with atypia, and with calcifications\u000aassociated with benign epithelium.\u000aNo in situ or invasive carcinoma.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: Dr. J. Brock, Breast Pathology Service, also reviewed the case and\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55 yo female with right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia s/p image\u000aguide core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. RT breast wire localized excisional bx (short stitch - superior; long stitch\u000a- lateral)\u000aB. Rt breast - medial margin\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aTargeted clip is NOT in specimen ? if it was suctioned out. A few calcs are\u000aseen in specimen. Are biopsy site changes present ??? J. Ritner.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "right breast, wire-localized excisional biopsy, short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of wire-localized breast excision (4.4 cm superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short\u000astitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localization wire\u000aentering the superolateral aspect of the specimen and exiting the medial aspect\u000aof the specimen with few calcifications scattered in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior in nine slices to\u000areveal a red/brown hemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with associated firm\u000afibrous tissue in slices #1 through #3 and is located less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, grossly abuts the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, grossly abuts the superior margin, and\u000a2.0 cm from the inferior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular, 13 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen from superior-inferior, multi frags, ESS (micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000acorrespond to one slice transected in half.)\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "right breast, medial margin", consists of two soft tissue fragments\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) that are previously inked blue on one aspect\u000aand black on the other aspect of the specimen per surgeon.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aDP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 10, 2009 at 06:11:55PM\u000a[report_end]
