VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aHealing biopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast, DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 Left breast tissue, long stitch-lateral; short stitch-\u000asuperior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HEDVAT,CYRUS V.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast tissue" is a breast re-exicison specimen (6.5 x 5 x 4 cm\u000aoverall) with attached skin ellipse (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a well-healed surgical\u000ascar along its entire length. The specimen is oriented with two sutures, a\u000ashort indicating superior, and a long indicating lateral. The superior margin\u000ais inked in green, the medial in red, the lateral in orange, the posterior in\u000ablack, and the inferior in blue. There is a biopsy cavity with hemorrhage and\u000afat necrosis (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, 2 cm\u000afrom the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. There are no areas\u000agrossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. Approximately 90% of the tissue is\u000asubmitted including all fibrous areas.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity and superior margin, 2 frags, 2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Medial margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, 2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity with respect to inferior margin, perpendicular,\u000a2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: Posterior margin, perpendicular, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior margin, 3 frags, 3 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior/posterior margin, 3 frags, 2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior/inferior margin, 2 frags, 2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Lateral margin, 4 frags, 2 cassettes, RSS.\u000aMicro 22: Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 23: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
