VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aBenign changes including epithelial hyperplasia, columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy or atypia seen upon microscopic examination of\u000athe specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx of left breast CA (DCIS) 1998, 51 y o premenopausal female with\u000a(R) mammogram, calcs UIQ and UOQ. UOQ core bx = benign. UIQ calcs not\u000aamenable to core bx.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aOperation: R breast wire-loc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right breast mammography.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue (short stitch - sup, long - lateral; whip stitch on\u000adeep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: No cluster of Ca++ on specimen/ multiple scattered punctate Ca++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue (short superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep\u000amargin)", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue,\u000aoriented by sutures designating superior (short suture), lateral (long suture),\u000aand deep margin (whipstitch). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing\u000awire enters the anterior surface and exits posteriorly. Specimen is received\u000awith a radiograph demonstrating localizing wire in place within the specimen.\u000aThere is no obvious focus of calcifications, however, there are scattered\u000acalcifications throughout the entire specimen. Please note: There is a large\u000aanterior to posterior near full-thickness defect (4.2 cm in length x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adepth) in the lateral aspect of the specimen (approximated edges of tissue have\u000abeen sutured together by the surgeon; the two halves of the specimen are only\u000aloosely adherent once the suture material is removed). Cut surfaces\u000ademonstrate predominantly soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (at least\u000a90%), with occasional unremarkable-appearing tan/white fiber-dense tissue.\u000aThere are no palpable masses, lesions or other areas of gross abnormalities.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from anterior to posterior, with\u000aperpendicular anterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular posterior margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPlease note: Tissue will be held for further fixation prior to processing.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
