VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kyle L. Viani, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy cavity, sclerosing adenosis cysts and\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.4 cm).\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no residual phyllodes tumor seen upon microscopic examination\u000aof the specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old female S/P REMOVED_DATE  excision of a right breast mass\u000ademonstrating a low grade phyllodes tumor and <0.1 cm from all margins.\u000aOperation: R breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue - whip stitch on deep margin, long/lateral,\u000ashort/superior, scar/anterior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, long/lateral, short/superior, whip-stitch on deep\u000amargin, scar anterior", and consists of an irregular portion of yellow\u000alobulated fibrofatty tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and short suture designating superior, and a whip suture\u000adesignating deep margin. There is a tan irregular loosely adherent irregular\u000afragment of skin (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), on the anterior surface. The specimen is\u000areceived previously inked per pathology protocol as anterior/blue,\u000aposterior/black, superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, and\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a well-healed\u000abiopsy cavity (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cavity comes to REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The cavity is surrounded by focal\u000adense white fibrous tissue and yellow chalky adipose tissue, with no discrete\u000amasses or lesions identified. Please note that 98% of the cavity is submitted,\u000aand 95% of the fibrous tissue is submitted. Approximately 90% of the specimen\u000ais submitted.\u000aRepresentative sections are sequentially submitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, radially, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of fibrous tissue to additional superior\u000aand lateral margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential representative cross sections of cavity to closest\u000amargin, with the overlying smoothly adherent skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional cavity to surrounding fibrous tissue and closest\u000amargin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 entire cross section of cavity to margins, serially sectioned,\u000a1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of one cross section, to include the\u000awhite fibrous tissue and closest margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, to include the cavity, surrounding\u000afibrous tissue and closest margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, to include the cavity, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section of brain between REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Friday August 28, 2009 at 12:20:45PM\u000a[report_end]
