VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, DUCT EXCISION":\u000aDuct ectasia, hemosiderin deposition and chronic inflammation.\u000aNo papilloma seen.\u000aFibrocystic change including cysts, apocrine metaplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNo evidence of malignancy.\u000aCase reviewed with Dr. Susan Lester, breast pathology.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "DUCT BEHIND NIPPLE":\u000aBreast parenchyma with dense fibrous stroma and mild chronic inflammation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43 year old female on estrogen replacement therapy with a\u000a3 year history of right nipple discharge. Status post\u000aleft breast core biopsy showing dense fibrous tissue and a hyalinized\u000afibroadenoma. Right breast ductogram suggestive of lobulated filling defect.\u000aOperation: Right breast duct excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right nipple discharge.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short suture = superior\u000along suture lateral, bow tie on divided ducts.\u000a2. Duct immediately behind nipple.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GINEVAN,KIM MICHELE,M.D.\u000aThe specimens are received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number. Part one, "right breast tissue", and consists of an\u000aoriented yellow/tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring 4 x 5 x 2 cm in\u000aoverall dimensions. Short suture designates "superior" a long suture\u000adesignates "lateral" and a bow tie suture designates "divided ducts". The\u000aanterior aspect is inked blue, the medial aspect is inked green, the superior\u000aaspect is inked orange, the inferior margin is inked red, the lateral margin\u000ais inked yellow, the deep aspect is inked black. Cut section reveals fibrous\u000atissue in the area of the bow tie grossly consistent with dilated ducts the\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma consists of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000awithout other lesions noted.\u000aCassette 1, medial perpendicular margin, 2 f, RSS.\u000aCassette 2, lateral perpendicular margin, mult frags, RSS.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  remainder of breast parenchyma, mult frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "duct behind nipple", and consists of a single fragment of pink/tan\u000afibrous tissue measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimension.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted in for histologic analysis.\u000aCassette 14, duct behind nipple, 1 f, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
