VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, (focal)\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, (focal)\u000aOther findings:\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts, calcifications and atypia including atypical\u000amicropapillae.\u000aFibroademomatoid change and fibroadenoma(s) (up to REMOVED_DATE cm) with associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: Numerous clusters of calcifications are present predominantly associated\u000awith columnar cell change. The focus of ADH shows a solid pattern of\u000aintermediate grade nuclei, involves a single duct (seen only on REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000ais associated with calcifications. The focus of ADH is > REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amargins. ALH is seen only on one level (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aB. LEFT AXILLARY SKIN LESION, EXCISION:\u000aVerrucoid keratosis (see Note).\u000aNote: This diagnosis was rendered by Dr. Mei-Yu Hsu (Dermatopathology Service).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53-year-old postmenopausal woman with L breast mammo REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing grouped punctate and amorphous Ca++ - wire WL excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast skin mass, pending path.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast needle localization; short stitch - superior; long stitch -\u000alateral; whip stitch - chest wall margin.\u000aB/2) L axillary skin mass.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Intact wire and targeted calcifications are within the specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Lt breast needle localization ", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.2 cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented with sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture), lateral (long suture), and chest wall (whipstitch)\u000amargins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the\u000asuperior aspect of the specimen and exits the inferior aspect. Specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating localizing wire in place within an\u000aill-defined central area of scattered calcifications. Note: Calcifications\u000aappear to extend to at least one edge of the specimen. Sectioning demonstrates\u000a30-40% tan/white lobulated fibrous tissue without obvious masses, lesions or\u000aother abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is sequentially submitted from\u000asuperior to inferior following further fixation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multi frags, ESS (perpendicular superior margin\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular inferior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. L axillary skin mass", consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm shaved\u000averrucous lesion with a REMOVED_DATE cm base. Base is inked, specimen is sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane 