VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA: LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A FILLING DEFECT:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aSmall duct papillomas (e.g. blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: There is no carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, TISSUE BEHIND NIPPLE, BIOPSY:\u000aBenign beast tissue with nipple ducts.\u000aNote: There is no carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 yo female with L nipple discharge - REMOVED_DATE  - consult slides - Cape\u000aCod Hosp. - left nipple punch biopsy "fragments of normal nipple skin" -\u000a1/26/06 - consult slides - Cape Cod Hosp. - "no malignant cells"; REMOVED_DATE  -\u000aDuctogram - nipple discharge from single duct 3:30 on nipple surface - apex\u000amidway between enter and edge of nipple ... 2 mm filling defect within terminal\u000aramification with mid-lower breast ductal system on cannulation of duct\u000aorifice. REMOVED_DATE  - BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE  BC 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long lateral whip stitch on\u000adeep margin. Blue bowtie and divided duct\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue behind nipple\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aLocalization of a filling defect after galactogram. Wire and tissue\u000apresent ? wire within an oval small mass by US. Dr. Robyn Birdwell.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior margin. There is a short\u000asuture designated as superior, long suture designated as lateral, whip stitch\u000adesignated as deep and a blue bowtie designated as the divided duct. The\u000aspecimen was inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a wire entering through the lateral\u000ainferior margin. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a vague dense area\u000acircled by the radiologist. No definitive mass lesion is seen.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior (blue tie) to posterior\u000a(perpendicular to the blue tie) to reveal 10% fibrous tissue and 90% adipose\u000atissue. No mass is grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, superior and anterior margins, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, superior and anterior margins, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected anterior, medial, superior and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected superior, inferior, anterior and posterior margins,2\u000afrags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Wire tip, bisected to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, posterior and inferior margins, 1\u000afrag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, superior, posterior and lateral margins, 1\u000afrags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Wire tip, bisected to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, lateral and inferior margins\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, superior, posterior and lateral margins\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, inferior and superior margins, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue behind nipple", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast tissue behind nipple, 1 frag, ESS\u000aECH/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Eric C Huang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/27/2006\u000a[report_end]
