VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Douglas I. Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts and focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSkin and nipple with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (HOT & BLUE):\u000aFour (4) lymph nodes negative for carcinoma (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aC. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (HOT NOT BLUE):\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for carcinoma (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aD. RIGHT BREAST SKIN:\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue negative for carcinoma.\u000aE. LEFT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change, cysts, scattered calcifications\u000aand focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy sites x 2 (located at 6:00 and in LIQ at 7:00).\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSkin and nipple with no significant pathologic change.\u000aF. LEFT BREAST SKIN:\u000aSkin, subcutaneous tissue and breast tissue, negative for carcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 year old female with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID mutation, whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram\u000ademonstrates atypical left breast calcifications, REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy of 2 site\u000awith one demonstrating atypical ductal hyperplasia and one without atypia. The\u000apatient prefers prophylactic mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Bilateral prophylactic simple mastectomy L sentinel lymph node\u000amapping and biopsy with possible level I x II dissection. Bilateral tissue\u000aexpands.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left atypical ductal hyperplasia BRCA x 2 mutation.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast (short stitch superior, long stitch lateral).\u000aB/2. Left sentinel node hot/blue.\u000aC/3. Left sentinel node hot/not blue.\u000aD/4. Mastectomy skin right breast.\u000aE/5. Left breast short superior, long lateral.\u000aF/6. Mastectomy skin left breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast", consists of a simple mastectomy (187 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture\u000adesignating superior. There is an overlying tan-pink skin ellipse (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), with a nipple areolar complex (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and an everted nipple (1.3\u000acm in diameter). The posterior margin is inked black and the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal 60% dense nodular diffusely cystic fibrous tissue,\u000aand 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant dense white fibrous tissue, with posterior\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue lower outer quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, with\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left sentinel node hot/blue", consists of three tan-yellow\u000airregular rubbery tissue fragments, consistent with lymph nodes (ranging from\u000a0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph nodes display fragments\u000aof yellow adipose tissue, and are sectioned to reveal tan-white cut surfaces\u000awith focal areas of blue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye. The specimens\u000aare submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left sentinel node, hot not blue", consists of a tan-yellow\u000airregular rubbery tissue, consistent with a lymph node (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Mastectomy skin R breast", consists of a tan wrinkled irregular\u000aunremarkable fragment of skin (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE (depth) cm). A discrete mass\u000aor lesion is not identified. The specimen is sectioned, and representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Left breast short superior, long lateral", consists of a simple\u000amastectomy (198 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating\u000alateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is a tan-pink to\u000ayellow (6.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a nipple areolar complex (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and an\u000aeverted nipple (1.2 cm in diameter). The skin and surrounding tissue is\u000afocally stained in blue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye. The posterior\u000amargin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a well\u000ahealed biopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest black-inked\u000aposterior margin. This cavity contains a surgical clip, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aposterior/inferior to the nipple, at the 6 o'clock position. A second\u000awell-healed biopsy cavity is identified (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000athe first-described well-healed biopsy cavity. This second biopsy cavity does\u000anot contain a surgical clip, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm posterior/medial to the\u000anipple at the 7 o'clock position (within the lower inner quadrant). The\u000aremaining cut surface displays 60% dense white, nodular, diffusely cystic\u000afibrous tissue with focal areas of blue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye,\u000aand 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no additional discrete masses or\u000alesions identified. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections\u000aare submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity #1, with the surgical clip, sequential cross\u000asection, with the posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second biopsy cavity, without the surgical clip, sequential cross\u000asections, with the posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening tissue between biopsy cavity #1 and biopsy cavity #2,\u000a1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, with\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart F, "skin mastectomy left breast", consists of a tan wrinkled unremarkable\u000airregular fragment of skin (17.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE (depth) cm). A discrete mass or\u000alesion is not identified. The specimen is sectioned, and representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 03:16:20PM\u000a[report_end]
