VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINE S. GIESS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aSOLID MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in\u000athis limited specimen (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE (rare cells positive, <1%)\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) EQUIVOCAL (2+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors. FISH analysis for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID will be performed; results\u000awill be reported as an addendum.\u000aImmunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence of myoepithelium in\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aMorphology would be compatible with primary carcinoma of breast in an\u000aappropriate clinical setting.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 54 year-old with new solid mass LI 30 axis\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound Left breast - Pink cassette 9:50 am time in formalin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number and "left breast", consists of a pink cassette which contains\u000amultiple irregular tan-pink fibrofatty tissue cores (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate) which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues received in pink cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: 4548.\u000aLMC/ajb\u000aInterpretation:\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in < 30%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aFebruary 05, 2010 at 01:52:14PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (2/10/10)\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = 1\u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: 2\u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Amy Ly M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday February 11,\u000a2010 at 10:08:39AM\u000a[report_end]
