VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, LATERAL WIRE LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aApocrine cysts and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelial and stromal breast tissue.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL WIRE LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000ainvolving large ducts, present in five of sixteen (5:16).\u000ablocks (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 7).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, present in two of sixteen (2:16)\u000ablocks, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest (lateral) margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 14);\u000alevels have been examined.\u000aMultiple intraductal papillomata (0.2-0.3 cm) (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 7, 9, 15).\u000aDilated ducts, periductal fibrosis, and intraluminal debris\u000awith associated microcalcifications, consistent with\u000aduct ectasia.\u000aHyalinized fibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe radiologic mass most likely corresponds to the ectatic ducts with\u000aperiductal fibrosis.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE BEHIND NIPPLE":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread involving\u000aa large duct.\u000aNOTE:\u000aDr. Susan Lester has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 73-year-old female with left bloody nipple discharge with ductogram\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  revealing dilated duct with solid component and few calcifications\u000ain [ILLEGIBLE] peri-areolar region of lest breast "suspicious abnormality".\u000aOperation: Left breast WL terminal duct excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left lateral breast tissue - short stitch = superior, long stitch =\u000alateral, whipstitch = deep.\u000aB/2. Left medial breast tissue - - short stitch = superior, long stitch =\u000alateral, whipstitch = deep. Blue bowtie on divided ducts.\u000aC/3. Tissue behind nipple left breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1) LEFT LATERAL BREAST TISSUE:\u000aCalcifications and wire are within the specimen.\u000aSignature: Dr. Gombos.\u000a2) LEFT MEDIAL BREAST TISSUE:\u000aDensity (sonographic mass) and wire are within the specimen.\u000aCalcifications are also seen. Signature: Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left lateral breast tissue", and consists of a portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting sutures ("short\u000astitch equals superior; long stitch equals lateral; whipstitch equals deep")\u000aand a hookwire in place (entering at the anterior aspect and exiting\u000amedial/inferiorly. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is accompanied by\u000aa radiograph, which exhibits a hookwire, adjacent to an area of probable\u000acalcifications. The calcifications grossly comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000aand medial margins, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin. The remaining breast tissue,\u000aconsists of approximately equal portions of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and\u000atan/white dense stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially from inferior to superior\u000a(calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left medial breast tissue, short superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch - deep blue, bowtie on divided ducts", and consists of a portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with four orienting sutures ("short -\u000asuperior, long - lateral, whipstitch - deep margin, blue bowtie - divided\u000aducts") and a hookwire loosely in place (entering at the superior aspect and\u000aexiting posteriorly. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph, within which three foci of calcifications, two\u000adensities ("mass") and an intact hookwire are identified. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from anterior to posterior. There is a white/rubbery,\u000afairly well-circumscribed mass (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) (mass #1) which extends to\u000athe superior/lateral margin, comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial/anterior\u000amargin, and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. Approximately REMOVED_DATE \u000acm inferior and anterior to the aforementioned mass, is an ill-defined, firm,\u000acalcified area (approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), deep to the blue bowtie,\u000awhich grossly comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE of\u000athe superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. Adjacent to the area\u000aof calcification (area #1) are multiple prominent dilated ducts. Approximately\u000a1.5 cm superior to the aforementioned area of calcification is a second smaller\u000afocus of calcification and an ill-defined area of dense fibrous tissue\u000a(approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 06 cm), which is traversed by the hookwire (marked\u000aas mass on radiograph), grossly extends to the superior margin, comes within\u000a0.3 cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000ainferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. The remaining tissue\u000aconsists of approximately equal proportions of yellow lobulated adipose tissue\u000aand tan/white fibrous stroma. The specimen is sequentially submitted from\u000aanterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from anterior to posterior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #1.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Calcifications - area #1.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area marked by bowtie.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #2 and calcifications - area #2.\u000aPart C, "#3. Tissue behind nipple, left breast", and consists of a pink/tan,\u000acauterized, delicate fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is inked black and submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adfi/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
