VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aHealing biopsy cavity.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, multifocal.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aNo residual DCIS is present, including evaluation of surgical margins.\u000aB/2. LEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR/LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal calcifications.\u000aBiopsy site changes, including traumatic neuroma.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50-year-old premenopausal female s/p low-nuclear grade DCIS, ADH on\u000aL breast exc REMOVED_DATE  pathology accession numbers REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000a11/1/04, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: L breast WL re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None provided.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short suture superior, long - lateral, whipstitch on\u000achest wall margin, and color marking - FS room, mammo.\u000aB/2. Left superior/lateral shave margin - whipstitch - new margin - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a#1. A cluster of calcifications and 2 intact hookwires are within the specimen.\u000aDr. Gambos.\u000a#2. Scattered calcifications are within the specimen. Dr. Gambos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whipstitch on\u000achest wall", consists of one wire localized breast excision specimen (6.0 cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior), with only two orienting sutures (short equals superior/long equals\u000alateral, no whipstitch), accompanied by a specimen radiograph, which shows a\u000asmall punctate density between two wires. The specimen is inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThere are two wires within the specimen: One enters and exits medially (95% of\u000athe wire is outside of the specimen), and the other enters inferiorly and exits\u000ainferomedially (90% of the wire is outside of the specimen). The medial aspect\u000aof the specimen is firm. The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral and\u000athere are no discrete masses, but there is fibrous tissue present focally at\u000athe superior, inferior, medial, anterior, and posterior margins, and in\u000aapproximately 70% of the specimen overall. The remainder of the specimen is\u000acomposed of yellow lobulated adipose tissue. There is focal hemorrhage at one\u000aof the wire tracts. The specimen is entirely submitted, and the region of\u000atissue seen on the radiograph as the bracketed area (at the medial aspect) is\u000alocated in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicular, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin cross section, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section (medial, superior, inferior), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional medial fragments, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, M, I), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (M, S, I, A, P), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, A, P), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, A, P), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, A, P), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, A, P, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, A, P, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected, (S, I, A, P, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, L, P), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section bisected (S, I, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicular with portion of inferior, 11 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left superior/lateral shave margin whipstitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of one very disrupted fragment of yellow/brown fibroadipose tissue\u000a(4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm deep) with a whipstitch on one face (inked black by\u000aprosector). The face of the new margin measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The opposing\u000asurface is inked blue. Disruptions in the specimen make it likely that ink\u000awill run into non-margin surfaces. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph, which shows three punctate calcifications (this region is submitted\u000ain cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and contains a request to entirely submit the specimen.\u000aThe specimen contains about 40% fibrous tissue, and there are no masses but the\u000aspecimen is partially surfaced by a firm fibrous tissue (? Scar) on portions of\u000athe old margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aSAS/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
