VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION FOR NIPPLE\u000aDISCHARGE":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aFragments of papilloma.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe entire specimen is examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions\u000aand calcifications.\u000aPrevious biopsy site changes.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe entire specimen is examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe reason for the biopsy is not provided. Clinical correlation is needed.\u000aThe entire specimen is examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Nipple d/c, Lt - bloody - filling defect on outside ductogram, not\u000arepeated today, atypia and LCIS, right.\u000aOperation: Loc/excis\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue.\u000aC/3. Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1 --> intraductal solid material - US of specimen. OR called.\u000aClip in specimen. OR called.\u000aDr. Twohig\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast", consists of an unoriented, irregular, tan/yellow to\u000awhite lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000aloosely attached needle-localization wire in place. The accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates the wire but no soft tissue density. The specimen is\u000ainked and serially sectioned to reveal focal areas of dense white fibrous\u000atissue constituting approximately 80% of the breast parenchyma. The remainder\u000aof the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with no lesions or areas\u000aof disruption identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPlease note that radiograph are received with the specimen.\u000aPart B, "Right breast tissue", consists of an irregular tan/yellow to tan/white\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (6.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral) with a portion of overlying\u000atan/white wrinkled skin (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a needle-localization wire in\u000aplace entering through the anterior aspect of the specimen. The accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph demonstrates the wire and a clip, but no residual\u000acalcifications at the clip. The specimen has been previously inked per\u000apathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial\u000aorange, posterior black, and anterior is designated by skin). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior. There is an irregular red/brown\u000ahemorrhagic area of disruption (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with previous\u000abiopsy site located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. There are focal\u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 25% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. The remainder of the parenchyma is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with no lesions or areas of disruption identified. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections superior to inferior, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000apossible previous biopsy site with metallic clip,\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "Left breast tissue", consists of an unoriented irregular tan/yellow to\u000atan/white lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is inked, and serially sectioned to reveal focal areas of dense white\u000afibrous tissue constituting approximately 85% of the specimen. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags, ESS; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/29/2006\u000a[report_end]
