VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, SKIN-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (PART A):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with Pagetoid spread, involving nipple,\u000alactiferous sinuses, and central upper breast.\u000aSclerosing papilloma.\u000aCalcification in association with benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SKIN-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, & RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES\u000a(INCLUDING PARTS B, C, and D, AND FSA AND FSB):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, TWO FOCI\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aMultifocal - Yes (see NOTE)\u000aLesion #1 in upper central breast:\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aHistologic type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aLesion #2 in lower inner quadrant:\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aHistologic type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive and in situ)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:2\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of nodes w/micrometastases- 1 (see NOTE)\u000aNumber of nodes w/isolated tumor cells- 1 (see NOTE)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with lesion #2\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site (x2)\u000aCalcifications in normal epithelium and columnar cell change.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmi two foci\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma.\u000aLESION #1 IN UPPER CENTRAL BREAST (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE-LOW (1%-2%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aLESION #2 IN LOWER INNER QUADRANT (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE (100%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: The two tumors are morphologically and immunophenotypically distinct.\u000aTumor #1 has a higher nuclear grade than Tumor #2. Both tumors have mixed\u000aductal and lobular features and both show membranous staining for E-cadherin.\u000aThe morphology of the tumor in lymph nodes is clearly glandular/ductal.\u000aSentinel lymph node #1 shows tumor cells present on 1 of 3 permanent H&E levels\u000a(<0.015 cm, approximately 150 cells), best classified as isolated tumor cells.\u000aSentinel lymph node #2 contains two clusters of tumor cells (up to REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000a0.03 cm each) present on 3 of 3 permanent H&E levels, best classified as a\u000amicrometastasis. On review of the frozen slides of both lymph nodes, in\u000aretrospect, isolated tumor cells are seen in lymph node #1 and tumor cells are\u000anot seen on the slide of lymph node #2.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 66 year old female with right breast multicentric breast cancer - two\u000adifferent tumors.\u000aOperation: Left breast simple mastectomy, right axilla sentinel node biopsy,\u000aright breast.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast high risk of cancer and right breast\u000amulticentric cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing) - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aB/2) R axilla lymph node #1 (fs @ 11:20).\u000aC/3) right axillary sentinel lymph node #2 (fs @11:58).\u000aD/4) right breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing) - short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - R AXILLA LYMPH NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3 - RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2" (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing)", which\u000aconsists of a simple mastectomy specimen (1005 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a short suture designating superior surface and a long suture designating\u000athe lateral surface. The specimen includes a tan/white skin ellipse (14.5 x\u000a4.0 cm), which includes an unremarkable flattened nipple (1.5 cm in greatest\u000adimension). The deep aspect of the specimen is inked black and it is serially\u000asectioned to reveal predominantly yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue (65%)\u000aand intervening areas of white fibrous tissue (35%). No gross lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is radiographed to reveal no mammographic lesions,\u000acalcifications or clips within the specimen. No lymph nodes are identified in\u000athe upper outer quadrant. Representative sections are submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central upper region, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central lower region, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central aspect, to include deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections of nipple, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right axilla lymph node #1", consists of a single fragment\u000aof tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which includes\u000aa single candidate lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The candidate\u000alymph node is bisected and entirely submitted for intraoperative consultation\u000aas FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Right axilla sentinel lymph node #2", consists of a single\u000aportion of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which includes\u000aa single lymph node (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph node is bisected and\u000aentirely submitted for intraoperative consultation as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right breast simple mastectomy, skin sparing, short suture\u000asuperior, long lateral", consists of a simple mastectomy specimen (1066 grams;\u000a21.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and includes a short suture designating the superior\u000asurface and a long suture designating the lateral surface. The specimen\u000aincludes a tan/white skin ellipse (14.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is focally involved by\u000ablue dye in the periareolar region, and contains a single unremarkable\u000aflattened nipple (1.0 cm in greatest dimension). A radiograph of the specimen\u000ademonstrates two localization clips within the specimen located right\u000aupper/central aspect of the specimen (lesion #1) and a second clip in the right\u000alower inner aspect of the specimen (lesion #2).\u000aThe intact deep margin is inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal\u000awithin the upper central breast REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, an ill-defined\u000aarea of nodularity (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is associated with a clip and\u000adesignated lesion #1. Within the lower inner quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin and 10 cm from lesion #1, is a second biopsy site (lesion #2; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) associated with central hemorrhage and a metal clip.\u000aThe remaining breast parenchyma is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly\u000atan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue (approximately 75%) without additional\u000agross lesions present. Lesion #1 is entirely submitted for analysis and 90% of\u000athe tissue around lesion #2 are submitted for analysis. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified in the upper outer quadrant.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion #1, to include deep margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aClip associated with tissue in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue between lesion #1 and lesion #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion #2, multi frags, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aClip associated with tissue in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin associated with lesion #2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fatty tissue in the upper outer quadrant (for potential lymph\u000anodes), multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in the upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aSRK/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009 at 10:25:13AM\u000a[report_end]
