VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A PALPABLE MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, intermediate grade, approximately 2 cm in size\u000a(see note).\u000aThe stroma is focally highly cellular, but is less cellular at the\u000aperiphery.\u000aThere is moderate nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMitoses average 2 per 10 HPF's (50 HPF's counted).\u000aMinimal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aThe tumor is focally present at the anterior margin (over a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aarea; block 4), REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin (slide 1), REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The tumor\u000ais not seen close the lateral or inferior margins.\u000aBiopsy site changes are associated with the tumor.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread is present (best seen in\u000ablocks 1 and 9).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aNote: The tumor has a diffusely invasive pattern into the adjacent breast\u000atissue and the extent of the tumor was difficult to determine grossly.\u000aThe most likely size is 2 cm.\u000aAll fibrous tissue was examined microscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/p (L) breast bx showing phyllodes tumor at Faulkner Hospital,\u000areviewed at BWH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast biopsy - specimen inked per protocol.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KATZ,SAMUEL G,M.D.,PH.D.,M.S.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast bx, specimen inked", and consists of a breast biopsy specimen\u000a(61 gm, REMOVED_DATE (m-l) x REMOVED_DATE (s-i) x REMOVED_DATE (a-p) cm) which has been previously inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal two\u000aapparently separate masses. The first mass (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is white/tan, firm, lobulated,\u000aand homogenous (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and bulges from the cut surface. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, and approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000a0.1 cm superior/posterior to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, there is a focal cystic area (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm) composed of multiple smooth walled unilocular cysts filled with clear\u000afluid.\u000aThe second mass (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is tan/pink, firm, ill-defined (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000aand is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm medial to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. REMOVED_DATE cm superior/anterior to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000athere is a firm area of red/brown hemorrhage (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) grossly\u000aconsistent with prior core biopsy site. The remainder of the specimen is\u000acomposed predominately of yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with a moderate\u000aamount of interdigitating bands of tan/white fibrous stroma. There are\u000amultiple focal areas of red/brown hemorrhagic, firm stroma, and multiple\u000afocally cystic areas both medial and lateral to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Representative\u000asections are submitted as follows, including all fibrous tissue:\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in entirety, with closest superior and posterior margins, and\u000aadjacent cystic area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Anterior margin closest to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and additional superior margin close\u000ato REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Additional posterior margin close to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and inferior margin closest\u000ato REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: Additional anterior and inferior margins close to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in entirety, with closest posterior and superior margins, and\u000aadjacent hemorrhagic area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: Additional superior and posterior margins, close to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Medial and anterior margins, closest to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: Inferior margin closest to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice to include intervening tissue between REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 4 frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: Cystic area towards medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: Cystic area approaching posterior and superior margins lateral to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Dense hemorrhagic stroma lateral to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of fibrous stroma, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPlease note approximately 80% of the specimen was submitted.\u000almb\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
