rely composed of tan/white\u000afibrous tissue. A biopsy site is identified and consists of hemorrhagic\u000atissue. The clip is identified in this hemorrhagic focus. No foci are\u000agrossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma, however, the entire specimen is\u000asubmitted for microscopic examination. The biopsy site is submitted in\u000acassettes #3&4 with the area of the clip in cassette #4.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 20 frags, ESS.\u000aeab\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
