VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (seven of twelve blocks).\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, present in five of twelve blocks (blocks 2,\u000a3, 5, 6, and 9; multiple levels examined; see note).\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aCalcifications present predominantly in benign epithelium and cysts.\u000aPrior biopsy site consistent with prior needle biopsy (slide 8).\u000aNote: The ADH is present in small foci (each less than REMOVED_DATE cm). Although\u000asome foci approach a diagnosis of low grade DCIS, the size of the foci and\u000athe distribution favor a diagnosis of ADH. The calcifications do not\u000aappear to be specifically associated with the ADH. Two of these foci are\u000a< REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, one is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, one is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and one REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 51-year-old premenopausal female, not taking estrogens, with\u000amammogram (10/16/98) demonstrating a new cluster of microcalcifications. A core\u000abiopsy (11/6/98) revealed a large duct with mild epithelial hyperplasia of\u000ausual type, periductal stromal fibrous with multinucleated giant cell\u000areaction, chronic inflammation, and numerous stromal calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast microcalcifications\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue (short/superior; long/lateral)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (gross only):\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: The calcifications are in the specimen. D. Smith, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DEBNATH,JAYANTA,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue", and consists of an oriented segment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a needle localization wire\u000ain place, and the specimen is oriented with two sutures - short designates\u000asuperior and long designates lateral. The specimen is inked in six colors as\u000afollows: red/anterior, green/superior, black/inferior, yellow/medial,\u000ablue/lateral, and orange/posterior. Sectioning reveals no evidence of any\u000agritty or stellate fibrous areas. There is a tan/pink organized biopsy cavity\u000a(0.3 cm diameter) with a rim of fibrosis (0.2-0.4 cm thickness). The specimen\u000aconsists of seventy to eighty per cent tan/white fibrous tissue. The entire\u000aspecimen is examined histologically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Breast, fibrous tissue, multi frag, ESS.\u000ajd\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
