IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - ER and PR performed previously; HER-2\u000apending\u000aSUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN (specimen C):\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar hyperplasia, and\u000aapocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aINFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN (specimen D):\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar hyperplasia, and\u000aapocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 61 year old with hx of R breast ADH '99, now with L breast ca,\u000a12/27/05 L breast core needle bxs - IDL mod diff II/III - no def LVI, no def\u000aIS, ER/PR positive, Her2/neu positive\u000aOperation: None given\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1/A Left sentinel lymph nodes (fs)\u000a2/B Left breast primary tumor site\u000a3/C Superior shaved margin, suture superior\u000a4/D Inferior shaved margin\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. LEFT SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aOR Consultation by: DAVID MICHAEL DORFMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: PATRICIA A. R. BRUNKER, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 left sentinel lymph nodes," consists of two fragments of red-yellow\u000asoft tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The smaller fragment\u000acontains a single lymph node candidate, which is bisected and frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLarger fragment contains two additional lymph node candidates (each REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension). Each candidate is bisected, one is frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the\u000aother is entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: non frozen tissue, multiple frags, ESS\u000aPart B, "#2 left breast primary tumor site," consists of an excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture), lateral (long suture), and deep (whip stitch) margins\u000a(confirmed per surgeon's operative report). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is an\u000aattached light tan skin ellipse (5.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) on the anterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. A localizing wire enters the specimen superolaterally and is embedded\u000awithin an ill-defined firm tan-white mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with associated\u000afocal hemorrhage and fat necrosis consistent with prior biopsy. The mass is\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000asuperior margin, and is remote (>2 cm) from the medial, lateral, anterior, and\u000aposterior margins. The remaining specimen demonstrates occasional tan-white\u000afibro-dense bands (40%) with associated tan-yellow soft, lobulated adipose\u000atissue. There are no additional lesion or abnormalities grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass and closest inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass and closest superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest medial margin, additional (uninvolved) fibrous tissue, 3\u000afrags, RSS\u000aPart C, "#3 superior shaved margin, suture superior," consists of an excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a suture designating superior.\u000aThe superior surface has been previously inked blue by surgeon; the opposing\u000asurface is inked black by prosector. Sectioning demonstrates predominantly\u000aunremarkable soft yellow lobulated adipose tissue with occasional dense\u000atan-white fibrous tissue (<10%). There are no masses.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: representative sections (1 per cm in greatest dimension, to\u000ainclude majority of fibrous tissue), 7 frags, ESS\u000aPart D, "#4 inferior shaved margin, suture superior," consists of an excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (5.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a suture designating superior.\u000aThe superior surface has been inked black by prosector; the opposing surface\u000a(inferior) has been previously inked blue by surgeon. Sectioning demonstrates\u000apredominantly unremarkable tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue (70%) with dense\u000atan-white fibrous tissue (30%). The fibrous tissue is focally cystic but\u000aotherwise unremarkable. There are no masses.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, RSS\u000aDB/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/3/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study was performed with the following result for invasive\u000acarcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu WEAK AND FOCAL (1+)\u000aNote: Studies on the patient's prior core needle biopsy revealed that the\u000acarcinoma was positive for estrogen and progesterone receptors (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aIn this prior specimen, the study for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu was reported to be 2+ and FISH\u000ashowed the lowest limit considered amplification (a ratio of REMOVED_DATE ). In this\u000aspecimen, there is only focal and weak immunoreactivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
