VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MRI-GUIDED WIRE-LOCALIZATION:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aBreast parenchyma with apocrine metaplasia, calcifications associated with\u000abenign epithelium, and focal fat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was examined histologically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal MRI ? right breast. Family history of breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal breast MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight breast MRI localized biopsy ? short stitch superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aNo definitive visible lesion in specimen. MRI-guided localization.\u000aSigned: C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Right breast MRI localized biopsy - short stitch superior, long\u000alateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty excision, oriented by\u000asutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins.\u000aThe specimen is inked by prosector per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localizing wire enters the specimen superiorly\u000aand exits posterolaterally. The specimen is received with an accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place and no discrete mass.\u000aPosterior and inferior surfaces of the specimen are disrupted; definitive\u000asurgical margin cannot be accurately assessed in these areas due to disrupted\u000anature of specimen. Sectioning demonstrates only focal fibrous tissue\u000a(maximally REMOVED_DATE cm) in the area of the localizing wire tip (there are not\u000adiscrete lesions grossly). The remaining specimen is soft, lobulated adipose\u000atissue with occasional focal hemorrhage (localizing wire tracked) and no\u000adiscrete abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from\u000alateral to medial with tissue surrounding localizing wire tip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral, posterior, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral, anterior, posterior, superior;\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, posterior, superior, inferior, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior, anterior, posterior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, posterior, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, anterior,\u000aposterior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, anterior, posterior, medial; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial, superior,\u000aposterior.\u000aDB/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/19/2005\u000a[report_end]
