titch lateral,\u000ashort stitch superior. Specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen radiograph shows a\u000avague density at the tip of the wire and a separate denser area at the edge of\u000athe specimen.\u000aA single localization wire is noted entering the anterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral into seven\u000aslices. There is an area of firm fibrous tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) along the\u000ainferior aspect of slices 3 through 5, and no other lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of breast, sequential, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aEAS/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/15/2006\u000a[report_end]
