VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KEMI BABAGBEMI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 1:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR\u000aMASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in\u000athis limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Irregular solid mass in Lt brst 1 o'clock; prior borderline DCIS in\u000aRt brst.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: irregular.\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Solid mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Solid mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aL breast PINK CASSETTE\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", is a one (1) pink cassette, labeled "Left", which\u000acontains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.7 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags, ESS.\u000almb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated there