0aB/#2 Sentinel nodes.\u000aC/#3 Adjacent nodes.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass is in the specimen. KB/PT.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast needle-loc biopsy", is received with a radiograph\u000aand localizing wire in place and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, ovoid\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The margins have been inked,\u000aby the surgeon, per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aPosterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The localizing wire enters laterally and exits at the mid\u000aposterior aspect. Sectioning in the area of the wire demonstrates a central,\u000aill-defined, white, fibrous lesion (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior,\u000a0.4 cm from lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior and remote\u000a(greater than REMOVED_DATE cm) from closest superior and medial margins. There is an\u000aadjacent REMOVED_DATE cm area of hemorrhage consistent with biopsy site. The remaining\u000atissue is predominantly adipose (greater than 90%) with occasional, tan/white,\u000aunremarkable, fibrous tissue. The mass and surrounding tissue are submitted.\u000aThere are no additional abnormalities.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and surrounding tissue, full-thickness cross-sections,\u000asequentially from medial to lateral (lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amultiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000a30% of tissue is submitted.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Sentinel node", consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm tan/brown, lymph node,\u000abisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "3. Adjacent node", consists of an aggregate of fatty tissue (3\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing three (3) lymph nodes (0.3 to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 single whole lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
