VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aColumnar cell alterations with microcalcification.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNote: No residual atypical ductal hyperplasia is seen after microscopic\u000aexamination of the specimen, including the entire biopsy site and margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old with abnormal mammo at Leonard Morse/Natick, focal\u000aclusters of calcs superolateral aspect R breast 11 cm from nipple (core #4\u000asuspicious for malignancy). REMOVED_DATE  - consult slides - MetroWest Medical\u000aCenter - "ADH" - ER+, PR+.\u000aOperation: R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right breast mass - short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Clip in specimen. E.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name and unit number\u000aonly, and consists of a fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior.\u000aThe specimen is inked per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a short suture designated as superior, long suture\u000adesignated as lateral (note the lateral long suture is located at the\u000ainferior/lateral inked margin), and whip stitch on deep margin by the surgeon.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a clip and the localization wire. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from superior to inferior and reveals white foamy beads\u000athat are REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, indicating the prior biopsy site, and\u000ais located adjacent to the wire tip. The clip is identified REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. The clip is surrounded by fibrous tissue. There is another\u000aill-defined firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm abutting the inferior margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The red ink has smeared through the\u000aspecimen, which may not represent the true margin. The specimen consists of\u000a85% adipose tissue and 15% fibrous tissue. The entire fibrous tissue close to\u000athe clip and prior biopsy site are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: white foamy bead and superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area close to the wire, superior and lateral margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: foamy bead, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area adjacent to the wire tip, superior and lateral margin,\u000abisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area around the clip, superior, posterior and lateral\u000amargin, trisected, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area adjacent to the clip, superior, posterior and lateral\u000amargin, trisected, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: ill-defined lesion and inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aECH/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Eric C Huang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/28/2005\u000a[report_end]
