VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael A. Seidman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH).\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aInterlobular and intralobular fibrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND BIOPSY SITE:\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 year old premenopausal female who had REMOVED_DATE  OSH L LOQ\u000astereotactic core biopsy of calcifications demonstrating ADH for which excision\u000ais recommended. REMOVED_DATE  BWH R mammogram demonstrates upper lateral\u000acalcifications near the chest wall, not amenable to core biopsy for which wire\u000aloc and excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Bilateral wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue short superior/long lateral whip stitch on chest wall\u000amargin 1440 mammo.\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue short superior/long lateral whip stitch on chest wall\u000amargin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast tissue short superior long lateral whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE \u000a(anterior to posterior) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) cm breast biopsy with a\u000aneedle localization wire in place and a short suture marking superior, a long\u000asuture marking lateral, and a whip stitch marking the chest wall. The needle\u000awire enters the anterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aSpecimen radiograph is reviewed on Centricity. Sectioning reveals 99% tan/pink\u000afibrous tissue and 1% fatty tissue with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. There is minimal area of hemorrhage consistent with placement of\u000aneedle localization wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body submitted from lateral to medial, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aPlease note hemorrhage consistent with placement of needle localization wire is\u000alocated in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue short superior long lateral whip stitch\u000aon chest wall margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to\u000aposterior) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) cm breast biopsy with a localization\u000awire in place and a short suture designating superior, a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a whip stitch designating the chest wall margin. The\u000aneedle localization wire enters the superior aspect and exits the inferior\u000aaspect. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Specimen radiograph is reviewed\u000aon Centricity. Specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal 99%\u000afibrous and 1% fatty tissue with no discrete masses or lesions identified.\u000aThere is minimal area of hemorrhage consistent with placement of a needle\u000alocalization wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, perpendicular sections, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body submitted from medial to lateral, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note paired sections are REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000almc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 27, 2009 at 02:06:30PM\u000a[report_end]
