VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibrocystic breast tissue with dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia involving one duct is present (block 4).\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000amicrocalcifications are present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenoma (1.0 cm).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle loc breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right needle loc breast mass (short/superior;\u000along/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Two wires and density in specimen. E.P. Frost,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CULPEPPER,KELIEGH S.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right needle loc breast mass, short sup, long lateral",\u000aand consists of one oblong piece of fibroadipose tissue with a short and a long\u000asuture in place. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior. Two wires are present,\u000aone inserts at the lateral edge of the specimen, and the other inserts at the\u000aposteromedial portion of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. One of\u000athe wires inserts in a radial density that corresponds to the medial\u000aone-quarter of the specimen. The second wire inserts such that it terminates\u000ain the middle half of the specimen. The segment of breast corresponding with\u000athe medial wire is diffusely fibrous, particularly at the inferior edge of the\u000aspecimen. No definitive hard lesions are palpated. The second wire terminates\u000aapproximately 1 cm away from the first mass. It is separated by adipose tissue\u000awith focal hemorrhage. This hemorrhage extends along a tract longitudinally\u000athrough the remainder of the specimen going from medial to lateral. Sections\u000acorresponding to the central mass are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: slice of breast tissue separating the medial mass from the central\u000amass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial mass, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections corresponding to middle mass, 5 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections extending laterally, 6 frags, RSS\u000aksc\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
