VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell change,\u000asclerosing adenosis, and calcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy cavity.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB) SKIN WITH SCAR, EXCISION:\u000aSkin with scar and foreign body giant cell reaction; no tumor\u000apresent.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 year old woman with left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia on both\u000acore and wire-localized excision, with core biopsy changes at the medial\u000aexcision margin.\u000aOperation: Left breast excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast excision of medial margin, short/superior, long/lateral,\u000asingle long stitch/medial.\u000aB/2. Left breast scar.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast excision of medial margin, short/superior,\u000along/lateral, single long stitch/medial", consists of a pink/tan fragment of\u000a60% fibrous, and 40% adipose tissue (4.2 cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) oriented by three sutures (double\u000ashort equals superior, double long equals lateral, single long equals medial);\u000aThere are also two suture stumps on the inferior aspect. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe anterior, inferior and medial aspects show possible previous biopsy\u000achanges. A possible previous biopsy cavity (1.0 cm x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is located\u000a0.8 cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE from lateral, REMOVED_DATE from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE from superior, and REMOVED_DATE from the inferior margins. No masses are\u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted entirely for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicular sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral (possible biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast scar", consists of an unoriented skin ellipse (6.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm deep) with a REMOVED_DATE cm well healed scar, tan skin and no masses.\u000aLateral margins are inked black. The specimen is submitted entirely for\u000amicroscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen serially sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000adh/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
