VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications and small focus of columnar\u000acell hyperplasia with ATYPIA present adjacent to biopsy site changes (block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBiopsy site changes are present at the superior, deep and lateral margins\u000a(blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was submitted for histologic review. Multiple levels\u000aexamined.\u000aB) LEFT BREAST, "TISSUE LATERAL TO SPECIMEN #1", EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts and columnar cell\u000achange.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: The specimen was entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aC) LEFT BREAST, "TISSUE MEDIAL TO SPECIMEN #1", EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBreast tissue with microcysts, fibroadenomatoid changes, epithelial hyperplasia\u000aand biopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: The specimen was entirely submitted for histologic review. Multiple\u000alevels examined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy of microcalcifications -> atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSurgical resection recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized resection. Upper inner quadrant.\u000aOperative Findings: No masses or changes at the core site.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aPostop: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue = stitch = long medial, short inferior [mammo].\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue lateral to specimen #1 [mammo].\u000aC/3. Left breast tissue medial to specimen #1 [mammo].\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast tissue stitch = long medial, short inferior",\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast excision specimen. Two stitches\u000aindicate reorientation, long stitch, the medial edge, short stitch the inferior\u000aedge. The specimen is fixed in per path protocol. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aWire transverses the specimen from the superior to the lateral margin. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned sequentially from superior to inferior into five\u000asections. The superior margin is designated section 1, the inferior margin is\u000adesignated section 5. Upon examination of the specimen, a localization wire is\u000avisible. Adjacent to the wire, in slice 2, is a firm area palpable measuring\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The parenchyma is of brown/red color.\u000aEntirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, perpendicular sections, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue lateral to specimen #1 unmarked",\u000aconsists of two fragments of tan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.7 cm in aggregate. The specimen was received unoriented. Per radiograph\u000areport, the specimen contains calcifications. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal one area firmness in which two separate nodules can be\u000apalpated, each measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodules, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining tissue, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "left breast tissues medial to specimen #1", consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibroadipose tissue. Per radiograph report, this specimen\u000acontains the clip. The specimen is serially sectioned and the clip recovered.\u000aThere is one area of firmness spread over two tissue fragments measuring about\u000a1 cm each. The specimen is submitted entirely for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of the clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of firmness, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aNote: Tissue specimen has been received unoriented.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMDH:jjk\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
