VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aSCHNITT, STUART, J., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by SCHNITT,STUART J.,M.D.\u000a"RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aSeverely atypical papillary and cribriform ductal hyperplasia with\u000aapocrine features, bordering on low grade DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, 4 mm\u000ain diameter, extending to within 9 mm of inferior margin (block 11),\u000a(See Note).\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (block 11).\u000aMicroscopic cysts.\u000aCalcifications present in association with atypical ductal lesion, florid\u000ahyperplasia, lobules and stroma.\u000aNOTE: A detached fragment of similar histologic appearance is also seen\u000ain block 14.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcs, rt brst.\u000aOperation: Needle localized right breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal calcifications, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: ca++ in specimen. D. Smith, MD/rl\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph and a pink sheet stating\u000a"calcium in specimen". The specimen is received in one part, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number and "#1 right breast tissue". It consists of a\u000amass of fibroadipose tissue (4.0 cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior x REMOVED_DATE cm laterally). Two sutures have been placed in the specimen\u000aby the surgeon denoting the orientation of the specimen. A wire is present in\u000athe specimen. In addition the specimen has been inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe anterior portion of the specimen consists predominantly of fatty tissue.\u000aThe posterior portion of the specimen consists of white fibrous tissue (up to\u000a2.5 cm in greatest dimension). No lesions grossly suspicious for malignancy\u000aare present. The specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000adl\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
