ecimen is composed primarily of tan/white rubbery\u000afibrous tissue with areas of yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete\u000alesions are identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety from\u000aposterior to anterior. The area associated with microcalcifications is likely\u000apresent in micros #1 through #5.\u000aMicro #1-14: Right breast excision (bisected slices in micros REMOVED_DATE ), 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000ajfs/\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
