VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: Entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination and multiple\u000alevels were examined. However, a mass lesion was not identified. Clinical and\u000aradiologic correlation is needed to ensure that the specimen is representative\u000aof the underlying lesion.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, focal.\u000aCalcifications associated with usual epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "FINAL LATERAL MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with scant benign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 71-year-old female with history of left breast LCIS in 2000.\u000aRecent mammogram with left breast calcifications and mass. Right breast\u000amammogram with calcifications.\u000aOperation: First, left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy. Second, right\u000abreast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: First, left breast calcifications and mass.\u000aSecond, right breast calcifications. Postop: First, left breast\u000acalcifications and mass. Second, right breast calcifications.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior, long\u000asuture lateral - FS.\u000aB/2. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral - FS.\u000aC/3. Final lateral margin, suture on margin - FSR.\u000aD/4. Final superior margin, suture on margin - FSR\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aMass and calc in left specimen #1. OR called 11:45. L. Twohig.\u000aNo definite group of ca++ in specimen #2. C. Denison\u000aSingle ca++ in specimen #3 lateral margin; and\u000amo visible ca++ in specimen #4 superior margin. C. Denison.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received in four parts each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A. "#1. Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P)\u000abreast biopsy specimen with a localization of wire in place and a short suture\u000amarking the superior margin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. The\u000awire enters the specimen at the lateral margin and does not exit. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates a mass and calcification in the left\u000abreast specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned into eight slices (slice\u000a#1 designated as the lateral margin and slice #8 designated as the medial\u000amargin). The tip of the wire was located in slices #7 and marginally #8. The\u000aspecimen is examined to reveal a firm area of circular shape REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter\u000awhich is located in slice #7 and #8. This area is less than REMOVED_DATE cm distant\u000afrom the anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and about REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin. Grossly, the margins do not appear to be involved.\u000aThe remainder of the breast specimen consists of unremarkable adipose tissue.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, perpendicular sections of the lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, perpendicular sections, 2 and 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P)\u000acm breast biopsy with localization wire in placed and a short suture marking to\u000asuperior margin and a long suture marking to lateral margin. A localization\u000awire enters the specimen at the lateral margin and accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph shows no definite group of calcifications in the specimen (diagnosis\u000aof radiologist). The specimen is sectioned into eight slices (slice #1\u000adesignates the lateral margin, slice #8 of the medial margin). The wire\u000adislocated during sectioning and it cannot be determined where it was located.\u000aThe specimen is carefully examined grossly, the specimen consists of homogenous\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through the lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through the medial margin, 3 and 4 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Final lateral margin, suture on margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm shave margin with concave surface, which is marked by a stitch\u000adesignating the true margin per surgeon (inked black). On the opposite side,\u000athere is a convex margin, which is inked blue.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Final lateral margin, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Final superior margin, suture on margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm shave margin with concave surface designated with a stitch per surgeon\u000aas the true margin (inked black) as well as a convex margin on the opposite\u000asides inked blue. The specimen is submitted entirely for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Final superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000amdh/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/24/2006\u000a[report_end]
