VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE DIRECTED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal, with associated calcifications (block\u000a2, multiple levels examined).\u000aColumnar hyperplasia and cysts with calcifications.\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE: The entire case was reviewed with Dr. Stuart Schnitt at Beth Israel\u000aDeaconness Medical Center who concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43-year-old female with a prior history of ADH and bilateral\u000amammographic calcifications, whose REMOVED_DATE  mammograms demonstrate\u000aincreased right UOQ calcifications for which biopsy is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/\u000alateral, whip stitch/chest wall.\u000aCalcifications are in specimen Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, right breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral and\u000awhip stitch/chest wall", and consists of a single breast lumpectomy specimen\u000a(4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which includes two (2) sutures placed by the surgeon\u000adesignating the lateral and superior orientation of the specimen. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. A needle localization wire is present within the specimen,\u000aand an accompanying radiograph shows the needle localization wire adjacent to\u000aan area of microcalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals a tan to white,\u000afibrous cut surface with a minimal amount of admixed adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is approximately 80% fibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. No\u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial slices of specimen from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 9: inferior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.lrl\u000alrl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
