VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with microcalcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis and apocrine cysts with microcalcifications.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, including margins.\u000aNOTE: This case has been reviewed by Dr. Dillon, Breast Service, who\u000aconcurs. The specimen has been entirely submitted and reviewed\u000ahistologically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia and columnar cell\u000ahyperplasia with atypia on core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcification with atypia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen contains wire and clip. OR called/SR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aPart A, the specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, short/superior,\u000along/lateral", and consists one firm, yellow/tan breast biopsy (3.9 cm medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with\u000ascant-attached adipose tissue. The specimen contains two surgical sutures\u000aplaced by the surgeon for orientation (long = lateral, short = superior), which\u000aare marked with surgical clips (two clips = long, one clip = short) for\u000aradiologic orientation of the specimen. The specimen also contains a needle\u000alocalization wire that enters at the anterior aspect of the inferior-medial\u000amargin and exits at the lateral aspect of the anterior-superior margin. A\u000asmall, multiloculated cyst (0.2 cm) is centrally located in the anterior region\u000aof the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph and radiograph report that states that the specimen contains a wire\u000aand clip. No clip is identified grossly. The specimen is sectioned parallel\u000ato the localization wire (roughly anterior to posterior) and sequentially\u000asubmitted. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #1 and #2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #3 and #4 (cyst and possible area of clip), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 (wire), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #6 through #10, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #11 and #12, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aoob/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/16/2006\u000a[report_end]
