VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN AREA OF ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (blocks 4, 8 [levels examined]\u000aand blocks 3, 5).\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia approaches to within less than\u000a0.1 cm of the inked medial and lateral surgical margins of resection.\u000aApocrine cysts and adenosis are present.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aSee note.\u000aNote: The ADH is difficult to evaluate. After examination of\u000aadditional levels and review at the Staff Pathology Conference,\u000ait is agreed that diagnostic criteria for DCIS are not met.\u000aHowever, it is difficult to exclude the possibility there is\u000aeither a small focus of DCIS with an unusual appearance, or LCIS\u000ais present involving areas of hyperplasia. Re-excision is\u000arecommended to exclude the presence of more extensive areas of DCIS.\u000aDr. Susan Lester of the Breast Pathology Service has examined\u000athis case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old premenopausal female with mammo REMOVED_DATE  showing a\u000a6 mm area of architectural distortion in LUOQ mid depth.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L wire localized breast bx, mammo at 1205.\u000aRADIOLOGY; Architectural distortion present in specimen. EP Frost, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by IAFRATE,ANTHONY JOHN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 left wire localized breast biopsy". It consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). It is\u000areceived with a single localization wire in place. It is inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The cut surface reveals approximately 80% firm white fibrous tissue\u000aand 20% unremarkable yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand entirely submitted.\u000aThe specimen radiograph is examined and reveals a vague density and the\u000alocalization wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
