VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, MASS":\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion/radial scar, with florid hyperplasia, and with\u000afocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign lobular epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a(Case reviewed at Staff Conference.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 49 year old post menopausal female on hormone replacement therapy,\u000awhose REMOVED_DATE  right mammogram supplemented by U/S demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm area of\u000aarchitectural distortion for which excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast wire localization excision\u000aRADIOLOGY: Spiculated mass in specimen. DN Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast mass", and consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring 7 cm from medial to lateral, 4 cm from superior\u000ato inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen contains a wire with an accompanying radiograph\u000athat shows a wire in relation to a mass. The specimen is approximately 70%\u000afibrous tissue and 20% fat. There are no clearly identifiable masses. The\u000aarea corresponding to the lesion in the radiograph is an area of fibrous\u000atissue. This area is ill-defined and is approximately 2 cm from the lateral\u000amargin, 3 cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, 1 cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, and is adjacent to the anterior and posterior\u000amargins. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, mult frags, ESS (#1-6 contain area corresponding\u000ato the lesion in the radiograph with closest margins, #11 and 12\u000acontain the lateral and medial margins).\u000amir\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
