VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A NON PALPABLE MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "SUPERIOR BIOPSY CAVITY, EXCISION":\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: Radiologic correlation is advised to ensure the biopsy is representative\u000aof the radiologic lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided\u000aOperation: Not provided\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Main specimen, L breast mass\u000aB/2. Superior biopsy cavity\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a#1. Main L Breast Mass Specimen:\u000aCalcifications in tissue consistent with area localized. No visible clip, but\u000alikely removed during vacuuming of hematoma per Dr. Lesnikoski.\u000aC. Denison, MD\u000a#2. Superior Biopsy Cavity:\u000aNo radiographic findings.\u000a(no signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Main L breast mass specimen", consists of a portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a single undesignated suture.\u000aThe specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The undesignated suture is present on the\u000ared-inked surface which, according to the pathology inking protocol, would\u000adesignate superior margin. A hook wire is not present within the specimen or\u000aspecimen container. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, exhibiting\u000aprobable calcification and a separately received hook wire which does not enter\u000athe specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior,\u000aexhibiting a hemorrhagic cavity (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which communicates with\u000athe superior, posterior, and medial margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin,\u000a0.3 cm of the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin. The remaining\u000abreast tissue is composed of approximately 80% focally necrotic/hemorrhagic\u000aadipose tissue and 20% unremarkable fibrous stroma. No additional gross\u000alesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from anterior to posterior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hemorrhagic cavity.\u000aPart B, "#2. Superior biopsy cavity", consists of an unoriented portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is received previously inked red\u000aalong one surface. The surface opposite to the red ink is diffusely\u000ahemorrhagic and ragged (consistent with a previous biopsy site) and is\u000asubsequently inked black by the prosector. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aexhibiting approximately 90% hemorrhagic adipose tissue and 10% hemorrhagic\u000astroma, focally extending to the red inked margin. No additional gross lesions\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/1/2008\u000a[report_end]
