VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aNo residual DCIS is present.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is identified.\u000aFibrocystic changes with apocrine metaplasia, and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications are noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia and sclerosing\u000aadenosis.\u000aCalcifications are noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a3) RIGHT BREAST SKIN:\u000aSkin with scarring.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45-year-old female status post REMOVED_DATE  excisional biopsy for right\u000abreast UOQ calcifications, with pathology revealing DCIS. Post excision\u000amammogram with residual calcification. (Close margin REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast simple mastectomy, short suture/superior, long suture/axillary\u000atail.\u000a2. Left breast simple mastectomy, short suture/superior, long suture/axillary\u000atail.\u000a3. Skin, right breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast", is a 264 gram simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(15.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin ellipse (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm). The deep surface of the specimen is covered by a smooth fascial plane\u000awithout skeletal muscle present. The deep fascia is inked in black and the\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal dense fibrous breast tissue throughout\u000athe breast. There is a stellate area of brown discoloration likely\u000arepresenting a scar (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which lies approximately REMOVED_DATE cm\u000alateral to the nipple and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to the nipple. This scar/mass lies\u000agreater than 2 cm from the freely movable deep plane. This entire area, all\u000aquadrants of the breast and the nipple are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  stellate mass like lesion, 1 frag each cass., RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin just overlying mass, 1 frag each cass., RSS.\u000aMicro 7: representative section from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: representative section from lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: representative section from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: representative section from lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: representative sections of nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: representative section of skin near mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast" is a 304 gram simple mastectomy specimen (15 x\u000a14.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin (8.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and nipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is lined by smooth fascial plane on the deep surface. There is no\u000askeletal muscle. The deep surface is inked in black and the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a dense breast tissue. There are numerous cysts\u000apresent, these are mostly in the outer quadrants. There is no evidence of mass\u000alesion. Representative sections of all lesions of the breast are submitted\u000afor histologic evaluations.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag each\u000acass., RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag each\u000acass., RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from the lower inner quadrant, 1 frag\u000aeach cass., RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag\u000aeach cass., RSS.\u000aMicro 21: representative sections from the nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, skin right breast", is an unoriented skin ellipse (2.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin surface contains a small well-healed REMOVED_DATE cm scar.\u000aThe deep surface of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is submitted\u000ain its entirety for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 22: tips of specimen, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 23: remainder of specimen, 5 frags, RSS.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
