rior. It measures REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral. Sectioning reveals the specimen contains 95% tan/yellow adipose\u000asoft tissue. The biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrotic tissue (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm) is REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin. There is no gross evidence for\u000ainvasive carcinoma. The entire specimen is submitted. The enclosed radiograph\u000ashows microcalcifications in the specimen as documented by the radiologist.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior and lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mid portion of the specimen with inferior, anterior and posterior\u000amargins, biopsy cavity in Micro 11, 12 & 13, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial portion of the specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
