VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCysts, apocrine metaplasia, and microcalcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aClip and core biopsy site identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 42 year old female with history of core for calcifications at BWH\u000athat showed atypical hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue - LUOQ (short suture/superior; long\u000asuture/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcifications in specimen. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. left breast mass", and consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a localization wire in place, and\u000asutures have been placed by the surgeon for orientation including a long suture\u000ato designate lateral and a short suture to designated superior. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen arrives accompanied by a specimen radiograph\u000awhich indicates a clip and focal small calcifications centrally located within\u000athe specimen, and adjacent to the tip of the localization wire. Sectioning\u000areveals the specimen to be composed of approximately 60% dense tan/white\u000afibrous tissue, predominantly in the inferolateral aspect of the specimen, with\u000afocal hemorrhage consistent with prior biopsy procedure in slices six through\u000anine. The localization clip is identified in slice 8, and the cluster of\u000acalcifications is identified radiographically in slice 6. No grossly evident\u000amass lesions are identified. The specimen is sliced from inferior to superior,\u000aand the specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 1 (inferior), sliced perpendicularly, 10 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 2, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 3, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 4, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 6 (calcifications in cassette 11), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 8 (clip in micro 15), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 9, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 10, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 11, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 12, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 25: slice 13, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 26: slice 14 (superior), sliced perpendicularly, 8 frags, ESS\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
