VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Soft tissue biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Benjamin J-C Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, "PORTIONS OF PRESUMED INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA", EXCISION:\u000aFragments of an intraductal papilloma with florid epithelial hyperplasia and\u000aapocrine metaplasia, at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A BIOPSY SITE AND A CLIP:\u000aIntraductal papilloma with florid epithelial hyperplasia and apocrine\u000ametaplasia, is present associated with the prior core needle biopsy site. The\u000apapilloma is present at the margin.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNote: The patient underwent a core needle biopsy for a palpable\u000airregular mass which revealed fragments of an intraductal papilloma\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Portions of a large papilloma are present within this specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aIntraductal papilloma with epithelial hyperplasia and apocrine metaplasia, is\u000apresent and extends to the margin with cautery on the papilloma.\u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of ALH in 2007. Intraductal papilloma - MRI -abnormal,\u000aright.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op notes.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: As above.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Specimen contains intact wire and clip.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Portions of presumed intraductal papilloma.\u000aB/2. Right breast primary specimen - short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral.\u000aC/3. Superior shave margin of papilloma cavity - stitch superior (right\u000abreast).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Portion of presumed intraductal papilloma", consists of\u000amultiple pink/tan soft tissue fragments (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aare submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. R breast primary specimen stitch long lateral short\u000asuperior", consists of a portion of yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue (2.5 x\u000a2.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture\u000adesignating superior. The specimen is received previously inked per pathology\u000aprotocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green,\u000alateral yellow and medial orange. There is an inserted needle localization\u000awire, as displayed on the radiograph in centricity, which enters at the\u000aanterior margin, and exits at the posterior-inferior margin. The specimen\u000aradiograph shows an ill-defined density and a clip in the center of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a partially healed\u000abiopsy cavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains a surgical clip, as\u000adisplayed on the radiograph in centricity. This cavity is less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The remaining cut surface\u000adisplays 98% white fibrous tissue, and 2% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with\u000ano additional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from posterior to anterior, with the\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the surgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Superior shave margin of papilloma cavity stitch superior\u000aR breast", consists of a focally cauterized yellow fibrofatty tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), with a suture along one aspect designating superior. This aspect is\u000areceived previously inked red. The opposite aspect is inked black by the\u000aprosector. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 95% dense white\u000afibrous tissue, and 5% yellow adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or\u000alesions identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 29, 2009 at 06:46:20PM\u000a[report_end]
