VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR AN AREA OF DISTORTION AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (1.5 cm) with ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA\u000a(blocks 3, 4, and 5; levels examined). Calcifications are present within\u000athe lesion.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aIntraductal papillomas.\u000aNote: The ADH is difficult to evaluate due to the complex architecture of\u000athe complex sclerosing lesion. Areas diagnostic of DCIS are not seen.\u000aThe entire specimen is examined histologically, including margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson who concurred with a\u000adiagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Rt needle loc. breast bx. Suture short superior, long\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass/distortion & calcifications present in specimen. C.Denison,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast needle loc, short superior, long lateral".\u000aThe specimen radiograph is reviewed and reveals a vague irregular mass and\u000acalcifications in the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is a fragment (5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) of fibroadipose tissue with two\u000aattached sutures and two wires. The inferior one-half of the specimen is firm\u000aand fibrotic. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aat 3 mm intervals from superior to inferior. On cut section 80% of the tissue\u000ais comprised of firm, tan/white fibrosis which is concentrated in the\u000ainferior/lateral portion of the specimen that appears to involve all inked\u000amargins. There are cystic areas ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in toto for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aeab\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
