VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, NEEDLE DIRECTED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and microcyst formation.\u000aCore biopsy site present.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "BREAST TISSUE LATERAL TO SPECIMEN #1":\u000aBenign fibroadipose tissue.\u000aNo breast epithelium identified.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "BREAST TISSUE MEDIAL TO SPECIMEN #1":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy (Faulkner) reveals atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aMore complete sampling recommended. Biopsy also reveals\u000apseudo-angiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH).\u000aOperation: Left needle-directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left needle directed breast biopsy.\u000a2. Breast tissue lateral to specimen #1.\u000a3. Breast tissue medial to specimen #1.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WOLGAMOT,GREGORY M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labelled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "left needle-directed breast biopsy", consists of a single mass of\u000aunoriented fibroadipose tissue (5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A wire protrudes through the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is composed of approximately 60% yellow adipose\u000atissue, and 40% white fibrous tissue that extends to the margins. A\u000ahemorrhagic and yellow focus of (0.5 cm diameter) is consistent with fat\u000anecrosis. No stellate masses are identified. Also received is a radiograph\u000athat reveals a diffuse mass adjacent to the penetrating wire. The surgical\u000amargin is inked in black and the specimen is entirely submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast, mult frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "breast tissue lateral to specimen #1", consists of a single\u000aunoriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No firm\u000amasses are identified. The specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted\u000afor histologic examination.\u000aMicro 5: breast, 1 f, ESS.\u000aPart three, "breast tissue medial to specimen #1", consists of a single\u000afragment of unoriented yellow adipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No masses\u000aare grossly identified. The surgical margin is inked in black and the specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 6: breast, 1 f, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
