VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin bx cyst, tag, or debridement\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KARL H BREUING M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WOUND DEBRIDMENT AND CLOSURE:\u000aSkin, subcutaneous tissue and breast tissue with granulation tissue, chronic\u000ainflammation, fat necrosis and foreign body giant cell reaction to polarizable\u000amaterial.\u000aNon-necrotizing histiocytic aggregates, consistent with poorly formed\u000agranulomata, are present.\u000aA single acid fast bacillus is identified on AFB stain.\u000aGram and MSS stains are negative for organisms.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a(Clinical History: Microbiological cultures of a breast capsule performed at\u000aBWH on REMOVED_DATE  grew Mycobacterium fortuitum.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Status post left breast reconstruction for breast cancer (CIS),\u000aatypical tuberculosis.\u000aOperation: Vacuum removal of left breast, wound closure.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Status post breast cancer, followed by reconstruction and\u000aleft breast wound infection.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Atypical tuberculosis, left breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Atypical tuberculosis", and consists of two tan skin fragments (5.0 x\u000a2.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). The larger fragment exhibits a\u000a1.5 cm indurated, nodular area of subcutaneous tissue, with an overlying\u000apossible REMOVED_DATE cm superficial defect. The fragments are inked blue (true\u000asurgical margin cannot be assessed due to fragmented nature of specimen) and\u000asectioned. Representative sections are submitted, to include majority of\u000asubcutaneous nodular area.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional skin, multi frags, RSS.\u000adb\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a1/9/2007\u000a[report_end]
