VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast implant\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: STEPHANIE H. CATERSON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST IMPLANT":\u000aGross examination only.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST IMPLANT":\u000aGross examination only.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST SKIN":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with acute and chronic inflammation and\u000ascar.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST CAPSULE":\u000aFibrous tissue with mild chronic inflammation and foreign body giant\u000acell reaction.\u000aE. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST SKIN":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with scar.\u000aF. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST CAPSULE":\u000aFibrous tissue with mild chronic inflammation and foreign body giant\u000acell reaction.\u000aCOMMENT: There is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Bilateral Diep flap breast reconstruction.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast implant.\u000aB/2) left breast implant.\u000aC/3) right breast skin.\u000aD/4) right breast capsule.\u000aE/5) left breast skin.\u000aF/6) left breast capsule.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThis case has six parts; each is in formalin, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "right breast implant". It consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, 500 mL\u000afluid-filled tissue expander bearing the words "McGhan Style 133FV, lot\u000aREMOVED_CASE_ID". The external surface is lightly blood-stained. It is composed of\u000afinely granular synthetic membranous material. Gross diagnosis: Medical\u000adevice consistent with breast implant. No sections.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast implant". It consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm, 600 mL tissue\u000aexpander bearing the words "McGhan Style 133FV, lot REMOVED_CASE_ID". The external\u000asurface is lightly blood-stained. It is composed of finely granular, intact\u000asynthetic membrane and filled with clear watery fluid. Gross diagnosis:\u000aMedical device consistent with breast implant. No sections.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast skin". It consists of two strips of soft tan\u000aunremarkable skin (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). They are excised to an\u000aaverage depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. Subjacent tissue is composed of soft yellow lobulated\u000afat and a central layer of dense fibrous tissue suggestive of scar.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right breast capsule". It consists of a dense rubbery fibrous\u000amembrane. It is irregularly shaped (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and averages REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000athickness. One surface is smooth and glistening. The opposite side is almost\u000aentirely covered by adherent, soft, rubbery fibrous tissue and fat.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Membrane, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Left breast skin". It consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm strip of tan skin,\u000aranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in width. It is excised to a greatest depth of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The subjacent tissue is composed of soft yellow fat and dense fibrous\u000atissue as seen in the scar.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart F, "#6. Left breast capsule". It consists of a dense rubbery\u000afibromembranous segment of tissue with an intact, saccular shaped (13.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm x REMOVED_DATE cm in average thickness). One surface is smooth, pink and glistening.\u000aThe opposite side is uniformly covered by a thin layer of shaggy fibrous tissue\u000aand fat.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Membranous tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adf/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/20/2008\u000a[report_end]
