VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (ADH), multifocal, associated with columnar\u000acell change, calcifications, and focally with mucin.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes are present.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with focal sclerosis.\u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a(Multiple levels examined on select slides.)\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology\u000aService), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Atypical Ductal Hyperplasia, S/P core bx for microcalcs.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized wide local excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Normal breast tissue, clip in specimen.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical Ductal Hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue with wire (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip in specimen. Jay.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. right breast tissue with wire", and consists of\u000aa wire localized breast excision specimen (4.5 lateral to medial x REMOVED_DATE superior\u000ato inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a wire entering the specimen\u000aat the lateral side and exiting the specimen at the inferior side. The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol: superior=red,\u000ainferior=green, anterior=blue, posterior=black, medial=orange, lateral=yellow.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph shows a metal clip in the middle of the lateral half\u000aof the specimen that is traversed by the wire. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral into 10 slices (medial margin slice #1 and\u000alateral margin slice #10). A metal clip is recovered in slice #7 with\u000asurrounding fat necrosis (0.1 cm), consistent with core-biopsy site. An\u000aill-defined tan/white fibrous area (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present around the\u000acore biopsy/clip site, abutting the anterior, lateral, superior, inferior and\u000aposterior margins and REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest medial resection margin. The\u000aspecimen is composed of >90% tan/yellow adipose tissue and <10% of tan/white\u000afibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The medial margin, slice #1, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 6 frags, 1 frag in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 2 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 6 frags, 1 frag in each block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 5 frags, 2 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 1 frag in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 2 frags, 1 frag in each block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, the lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aQY/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/16/2008\u000a[report_end]
