VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF PREVIOUSLY\u000aEXCISED CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications, adjacent to the prior\u000abiopsy site (see NOTE).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm).\u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for histologic examination, including\u000amargins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE cm focus of severely atypical reactive hyperplasia in block 3\u000a(levels examined). An immunoperoxidase study reveals the absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in papillary areas. Although this focus could represent a\u000aminute focus of papillary DCIS, based on the small size of the lesion, it is\u000abest classified as ADH. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aCase reviewed with Dr. S. Lester.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammograms demonstrate\u000aincreased calcifications in the L breast. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy at South Shore\u000aHospital revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia and atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L abnormal mammogram atypical hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast mass to mammo. Long lateral, short, superior,\u000awhip stitch - deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fixed, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast mass", and consists of a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm breast mass with\u000aorienting sutures indicating superior, lateral and deep. No wire is localized\u000ain the specimen. The specimen has been previously inked. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Serial sectioning revealed a core biopsy cavity in the superior half\u000aof the specimen. No area grossly suspicious for carcinoma is identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, serially submitted superior to inferior, 14 frags,\u000aESS.\u000absc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
