VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL MARGIN, RE-EXCISION:\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aBenign cysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, INFERIOR-MEDIAL MARGIN, RE-EXCISION:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aBenign cysts.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female s/p left breast core biopsy for calcifications\u000aat SSH with pathology revealing ADH and ALH. REMOVED_DATE  left breast\u000awire localization biopsy reveals ADH with a focus of severely atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia vs DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast severely atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Medial shaved margin with stitch on new margin and scar\u000a#2) Inferior medial shaved margin with stitch on new margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. medial shaved margin with stitch on new margin and\u000ascar", consists of a single, yellow/tan, fibrofatty fragment of breast tissue\u000a(4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a black whip stitch on one aspect of the specimen to\u000adesignate new margin. A portion of biopsy cavity is present measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.4 cm, which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the new deep margin. The new deep margin is inked\u000ain black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm white fibrous\u000atissue at the deep margin, with focal areas of fat necrosis surrounding the\u000abiopsy cavity. No lesions suspicious for malignancy are grossly identified.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast medial margin re-excision, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. inferior medial shaved margin with stitch on new\u000amargin", consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan, fibrofatty breast tissue\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains a whip stitch on one aspect to designate\u000athe new margin. This area is inked in black, and the specimen is serially\u000asection to reveal predominantly white, firm fibrous tissue and focal areas of\u000afat necrosis with a biopsy cavity. No lesions concerning for malignancy are\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  shave re-excision of inferior medial margin, 2 or 3 frags each,\u000aESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
