VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vijay K Vanguri, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU,\u000aassociated with calcifications, multiple foci in 3 of 12 blocks (blocks, 7, 8,\u000aand 9).\u000aThe severely atypical lesion is within REMOVED_DATE cm of superior-medial and\u000asuperior-lateral margins and posterior margin.\u000aExtensive sclerosing adenosis, columnar hyperplasia with flat epithelial\u000aatypia, and addition areas of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications are also associated with sclerosing adenosis.\u000aNOTE: A re-excision of superior (medial and lateral) and deep margins is\u000arecommended to rule out a more diagnostic area of in situ carcinoma.\u000aHELD FOR: LEVELS\u000aPRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCalcifications are present. Levels are pending to better evaluate a focus of\u000aatypical glands close to the medial margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 y.o. premenopausal female whose mammogram REMOVED_DATE  showed new\u000acalcifications in right UOQ, not amenable to core biopsy, wire loc excision\u000arecommended. Prior history left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia, s/p\u000aexcision and re-excision 1991; and s/p REMOVED_MONTH 2003 L core needle breast biopsy of\u000a9 mm mass with associated calcifications demonstrating sclerosing adenosis with\u000acalcifications of cyst wall.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch chest wall, to\u000amammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast mass", and consists of a wire-localized, previously inked\u000aexcision of breast tissue (3.2 cm S-I, REMOVED_DATE cm A-P, and REMOVED_DATE cm M-L) with an\u000aembedded localization wire and two orienting sutures (short=superior,\u000along=lateral. A whipstitch is one the posterior aspect. An accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates an embedded localization wire in the specimen with\u000acalcifications identified. The specimen is serially sectioned revealing dense,\u000awhite, fibrous tissue encompassing the entire specimen with no discrete\u000alesions; wire is localized to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS\u000aVIV/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Russell K Dorer M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/21/2005\u000a[report_end]
