VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aSCHNITT, STUART, J., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by SCHNITT,STUART J.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UOQ, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present associated with\u000acalcifications.\u000aCysts with associated microcalcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: Atypical ductal hyperplasia is best evaluated on surgical excision.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UOQ, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSpecimen #1 was of a loose cluster of pleomorphic calcifications. This is the\u000afirst biopsy in the original report and has ADH.\u000aSpecimen #2 was of a cluster of calcifications associated with a nodule. This\u000ais the second biopsy in the original report and has ALH. Specific histologic\u000afeatures of a mass forming lesion are not seen. Radiologic correlation is\u000asuggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46-year-old female with calcifications in UOQ of left breast on\u000abaseline mammogram; biopsy of two (2) separate clusters revealed:\u000a#1: loose cluster of pleomorphism\u000a#2: assocated with nodule\u000aOperation: 11G stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 11 gauge core biopsy specimens from two (2) separate clusters\u000aof calcifications:\u000a1) "A"=with calcifications; "B"=w/o calcifications\u000a2) "B"=with calcifications; "B"=w/o calcifications\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHAH,RAJSHRI N.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, "left breast #1 ca++", and consists of two (2) orange cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A, ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow\u000ato white tissue cores (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette\u000ais labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "left breast #2", and consists of two (2) white cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A, ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, pink to\u000awhite tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette is\u000alabeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 3: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000atr\u000adf\u000aReports to: GOUGOUTAS, CHRISTINA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
