 REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. Remainder of the breast parenchyma\u000ais tan/yellow and homogenous with no additional lesions or areas of disruption\u000agrossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral block (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude lesion block, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID adjacent to clip as seen on mammogram), 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note block #15 does not have intact inked margins.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/9/2007\u000a[report_end]
