VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.2 cm)\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenomas (up to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aPrior biopsy site(s) associated with a cicatrix in the lateral portion of\u000athe breast.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48-year-old premenopausal female, not on hormones, past medical\u000ahistory of thyroid cancer. Status post right breast biopsy for evaluation of 2\u000amasses on mammogram with pathology demonstrating atypical ductal hyperplasia in\u000aaddition to 2 fibroadenomas. The biopsies were performed through the same skin\u000aincision and are adjacent to each other.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, short-superior, long-lateral.\u000a2. Right breast, short-superior, long-lateral, scar marks ADH.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast", and consists of a 500 gram simple\u000amastectomy specimen (18 cm superior to inferior x 21 cm medial to lateral x\u000a2.4 cm superior to deep). Two (2) sutures have been placed in the specimen by\u000athe surgeon marking the lateral and superior aspects of the specimen. A skin\u000aellipse is present on the specimen (16.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (3.5 cm in\u000adiameter), and nipple (1.4 cm in diameter). No lesions are present in the\u000asectioned breast, which is approximately 60% fibrous tissue, 40% fat.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: nipple, mult frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: additional fragments of breast tissue from middle of left breast\u000awith potential cysts (0.5 cm).\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast", consists of a 475 gram simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (19.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperficial to deep) with skin ellipse (17.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (4.0 cm in\u000adiameter) and nipple (1.5 cm in diameter). A curvilinear scar is present\u000alateral to the nipple (2.2 cm in length). This scar marks the site of two\u000aprevious biopsies showing ADH per the surgeon. Deep to the scar, there is a\u000acyst (0.8 cm in greatest dimension). The area of the scar and the fibrous\u000atissue deep to it are entirely submitted. Representative sections of the\u000aremainder of the breast are also submitted. No lesions are grossly present\u000awithin the breast specimen, which consists of 50% fat and 50% fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro 7: nipple, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  scar and underlying fibrous tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional fibrous tissue near previous biopsy site, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional fibrous tissue adjacent to biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000adl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
