/orange.\u000aThe localizing wire enters laterally and traverses the specimen medially. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing REMOVED_DATE %\u000atan/white focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue, which is grossly unremarkable\u000awith the exception of a REMOVED_DATE cm palpably firm tan/white nodule (? Cyst), REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin and\u000a1.5 cm from the closest posterior margin and greater than 2 cm from the closest\u000amedial margin. There are no additional abnormalities. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted, sequentially from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral\u000a(wire tip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; nodule in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multiple frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
