VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aFibroadipose tissue with fat necrosis and foreign body giant cell\u000areaction.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aThere is no evidence of in-situ or invasive carcinoma.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aThere is no evidence of in-situ or invasive carcinoma, including evaluation of\u000asurgical margins of the specimen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 52 year postmenopausal female on HRT with right UOQ 1 cm cluster of\u000acalcifications on REMOVED_DATE  mammogram. S/P REMOVED_DATE  excision revealing\u000aseverely atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on DCIS present <0.1 cm\u000afrom posterior margin.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH bordering on DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue (posterior shave margin; whip stitch\u000achest wall)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. right breast tissue, posterior shave margin, whip stitch chest wall",\u000aand consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais a whip stitch on one surface which is inked in black, the opposite side is\u000ainked in blue, serially sectioned and entirely submitted. A skin ellipse (2.2\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth) that contains a REMOVED_DATE cm centrally located well-healed\u000asurgical scar is present in the same container as second specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, mult frags each, ESS\u000aMicro 8: skin ellipse, 7 frags, ESS\u000ageb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
