VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aBreast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, columnar alteration of lobules\u000awith prominent snouts and secretions, apocrine metaplasia, and cysts.\u000aCalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium, but\u000anot in association with LCIS.\u000aThere is no evidence of invasive carcinoma or DCIS, in the specimen\u000aincluding the margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Scatered calcifications, abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast tissue (short - superior, long - lateral).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMammo: Calcifications are seen in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue", and consists of a wire localized breast excision (4.5\u000acm from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral) with a short suture denoting superior and a long suture\u000adenoting lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is bisected\u000afrom anterior to posterior. Inferior to superior sectioning reveals 85% of the\u000atissue is fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted. An accompanying\u000aradiograph shows calcifications in the specimen, as documented by the\u000aradiologist.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior half, inferior to superior sections, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Anterior half, breast tissue, inferior to superior sections,\u000amutliple frags, ESS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
