VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jian Shen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, MID UPPER, 11G STEREOTACTIC GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving almost all lobular units within\u000athe biopsy, as well as an intraductal papilloma (see note). Immunoperoxidase\u000astudies are performed with the following results for LCIS:\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PRESENT IN MYOEPITHELIAL CELLS\u000aAn intraductal papilloma with focal atypia is associated with\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aNote: The extent of LCIS in this biopsy is unusual. The immunoperoxidase\u000astudies show the typical pattern for LCIS and this is likely an incidental\u000afinding.\u000aThe papilloma shows focal areas of cribriforming and would be evaluated best\u000awith excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42-year-old female with 3 mm group of amorphous calcifications, left\u000amid upper breast.\u000aOperation: 11 G Stereotactic.\u000aOperative Findings: Calcification in specimen.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Probable FC change or stromal calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aLeft breast tissue in two orange cassettes: A - tissue with calcifications, B -\u000aremainder of tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left\u000abreast", are two (2) orange cassettes. One cassette is labeled "A Ca++" and\u000acontains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (2.0 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate). The other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar\u000atissue fragments (2.0 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/9/2006\u000a[report_end]
