VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (block #11).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia and columnar hyperplasia with flat atypia\u000aadjacent to core biopsy site (block #11)\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions, sclerosing adenosis, and\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aMargins examined microscopically.\u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy at BWH REMOVED_DATE  showed cysts with calcs (1 cm area\u000aof cales) focal atypia for which excision was recommended: clip left.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aLMP REMOVED_DATE desires pregnancy menopausal.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue upper outer quadrant, short=superior,\u000along=lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip, calcifications, and wire are within the specimen.\u000aSigned: Illegible.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short = superior, long = lateral", and consists of\u000aa yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with a short\u000astitch marking the superior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral\u000asurface. In place, is a wire which enters the specimen at the lateral surface\u000adirected medialposteriorally to exit the specimen at the posterior surface.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A specimen radiogram accompanies the specimen demonstrating\u000athe wire, clip, and calcifications within the specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral demonstrating a white/yellow firm\u000aarea with irregular borders (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) extending to the posterior,\u000ainferior, and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior surface, less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the medial surface, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral surface. A clip\u000ais identified within the fibrous area in slice #5. The remainder of the\u000abreast tissue is comprised of REMOVED_DATE % adipose tissue and grossly unremarkable.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #1, medial most, perpendicular, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #3, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #4, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #5 with clip contained in micro 11, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #6, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #7, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #8, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #9, lateral most, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
