VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.; Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE\u000aBIOPSY SITE:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present adjacent to biopsy site changes.\u000aNote: There is no evidence of malignancy after complete pathologic\u000aexamination of the specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 63 yo female with right breast calcifications and core biopsy\u000arevealing atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior, long\u000asuture lateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aThe clip and region of prior bx site are within the specimen.\u000aCalled OR - Dr. Yeh spoke with Dr. Golshan. /EY.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, SSS, LSL", consists of\u000aa portion of fibrofatty tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral (displaying two surgical clips), and a short suture\u000adesignating superior (displaying one surgical clip). The specimen radiograph\u000ashows a clip adjacent to the wire. There is an inserted needle-localization\u000awire, as designated on the accompanying radiograph, which enters along the\u000amedial aspect, and does not exit the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior\u000agreen, medial orange, and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal a cavity, consistent with a biopsy cavity (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000acontaining a surgical clip. The cavity is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin. The remaining cut surface displays 95% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, and 5% white fibrous tissue, with no additional discrete masses\u000aor lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, with the biopsy cavity, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections with the biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000acontaining the surgical clips, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/24/2007\u000a[report_end]
