ins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from anterior to posterior, exhibiting approximately 60% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue and 40% tan/white focally dense fibrous stroma. A\u000aclip is identified within focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue adjacent to the\u000aneedle localization wire, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin. No other gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. Please note area of clip and\u000aadjacent calcifications are present in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000asts/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
