nd closest medial margin is 3 cm. Remaining tissue is predominantly\u000aadipose (85%), without additional lesions or other abnormalities noted grossly.\u000aRepresentative tissue to include all fibrous tissue, submitted as follows:\u000amicro 1: slice one, 1 frag, ESS.\u000amicro REMOVED_DATE  slice two, 2 frags, ESS.\u000amicro REMOVED_DATE  slice three, 3 frags, ESS.\u000amicro REMOVED_DATE  slice four, 3 frags, ESS.\u000amicro REMOVED_DATE  slice five, 3 frags, ESS.\u000amicro 13: slice six, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000amicro 14: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aApproximately 50% of the tissue (including all fibrous tissue) is submitted.\u000aLesion in micros REMOVED_DATE with surgical clip removed from slice four, micros REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
