VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSIES (INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION):\u000aTwo lymph nodes with no tumor seen (4 HE levels examined).\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aEXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform, papillary, and solid types\u000a(intermediate nuclear grade) associated with calcifications and focal necrosis,\u000ais present throughout a 9 cm area of the breast, predominantly in the upper\u000aouter quadrant (present in 21 of 30 blocks) (see note).\u000aNo stromal invasion is seen. Immunoperoxidase studies for p63 and cytokeratin\u000aare performed on three blocks (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Although the myoepithelial\u000alayer is attenuated in some areas, no definitive stromal invasion can be\u000ademonstrated.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aThe deep margin is free of carcinoma. The skin is free of carcinoma.\u000aOne intramammary lymph node is present and is free of carcinoma.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aAdditional immunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results\u000afor DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu WEAKLY POSITIVE (2+)\u000aNote: The patient presented with bloody nipple discharge. Mammography\u000arevealed clusters of calcifications below the nipple and MRI revealed a 9 cm\u000aarea of rapid enhancement in the upper outer quadrant. A prior excision showed\u000aDCIS and extensive atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aIn the mastectomy, there is a 9 cm grossly evident mass in the upper outer\u000aquadrant that has been extensively sectioned and sampled. Ducts involved by\u000aDCIS contain hemorrhagic debris, consistent with the history of nipple\u000adischarge. No stromal invasion can be demonstrated.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present involving all four quadrants and\u000alactiferous sinuses of the nipple (in 17 of 22 blocks).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade), without\u000anecrosis or calcifications, is present in one block (0.3 cm focus; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for LCIS\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin 7 POSITIVE\u000aNote: The breast parenchyma is very dense. No gross lesions were evident.\u000aThe mastectomy was thinly sliced and sampled extensively. No stromal invasion\u000ais seen. No lymph nodes were present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS left breast.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left sentinel node.\u000aB/2) left breast tissue, stitch - long/lateral, short/superior.\u000aC/3) right breast tissue, stitch - long/lateral, short/superior.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - LEFT SENTINEL NODES" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: DEREK MARSEE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left sentinel node (fs)", consists of one fragment of\u000ablack/red soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing two lymph nodes (3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The first lymph node is submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(bisected), and the second lymph node is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000alarger lymph node (3.0 cm) was inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: non-frozen tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - left breast tissue", consists of a simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (716 grams, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a circular skin ellipse (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and two orienting sutures (short=superior, long=lateral). The skin is\u000asmooth with no visible scars, and the grossly unremarkable nipple measures REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The posterior aspect of the specimen consists of a smooth\u000afascial plane, which is inked black. The specimen contains a large firm\u000aheterogeneous mass with multiple small cysts (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which spans\u000afrom the upper/outer quadrant to the middle of the specimen underneath the skin\u000aellipse. The mass comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep resection margin, and\u000agrossly abuts the skin. A biopsy site cavity is not identified. The mass\u000aconsists of some firm, white, partially cystic areas, as well as one\u000ahemorrhagic, solid area and upper/outer quadrant (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and a gritty\u000afirm area (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area is located next to the blue dye from\u000athe sentinel node biopsy and is immediately deep to the skin. Representative\u000asections of the mass, including all the aforementioned areas, are submitted\u000afrom medial to lateral in sequential order. Additionally received are two\u000afragments of breast tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), as well\u000aas nine fragments of unremarkable skin (1.5-7.0 cm in greatest dimension). One\u000alymph node is identified within the lateral breast tissue.\u000aAfter examination of the initial slides, the breast is re-examined grossly by\u000aDr. Susan Lester and additional sections of all of the firmest areas are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one of mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: continuous sections of firm, gritty area on slice two, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: cystic area on slice two, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: gritty area on slice three, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: cystic area on slice three, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: cystic area on slice four, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: hemorrhagic area on slice four, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: hemorrhagic area on slice five, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous area on slice five, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous area on slice six, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: deep margin near firmest area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional fragments of skin and breast tissue, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections of the mass, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - right breast tissue", consists of a 728 gram simple\u000amastectomy specimen (18.5 cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a circular skin ellipse (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aand two intact orienting sutures (short=superior, long=lateral). There are no\u000ascars present on the skin, and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aposterior surface of the specimen is covered with a smooth fascial plane, which\u000ais inked black. The specimen contains firm fibrous tissue (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which extends from the center of the specimen to the lower/outer quadrant.\u000aThere are areas of cystic change but no gritty tissue. The dense fibrous area\u000ais 2 cm from the deep fascial margin, and is directly underneath the nipple.\u000aRepresentative sections of the fibrous area are submitted from medial to\u000alateral, and no biopsy site or areas of hemorrhage are identified. No lymph\u000anodes are identified within the lateral breast tissue. Additionally received\u000aare two pink/tan skin ellipses (4.0 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension,\u000arespectively).\u000aAfter examination of the initial slides, the specimen is examined a second time\u000aby Dr. Susan Lester. No gross lesions are identified. Additional tissue\u000asections are submitted to include tissue from all four quadrants and throughout\u000athe area of fibrous breast tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: sequential fragments of fibrous area from medial to lateral,\u000a5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior resection margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: skin fragments, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional sections of fibrous tissue to include all four\u000aquadrants, mult frags, RSS.\u000aAF/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/12/2006\u000a[report_end]
