VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Briana Gleason, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, INFERIOR, LOWER OUTER, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS NEAR A PRIOR SURGICAL SITE:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Although some areas involved by LCIS have calcifications, they do not\u000aappear to be specifically associated with LCIS.\u000aThe LCIS focally has higher nuclear grade than is typical for LCIS. However,\u000athe architectural pattern is typical of LCIS and this is the best\u000aclassification for this lesion.\u000aThe patient had a prior excision in this region on REMOVED_DATE  that showed LCIS and\u000aADH.\u000aB. SUPERIOR LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Although some areas involved by LCIS have calcifications, they do not\u000aappear to be specifically associated with LCIS.\u000aAs in the first specimen, the LCIS focally has nuclei of higher grade than is\u000atypical for LCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/O diffuse, severe ADH (L) lower inner quadrant. Wire #1 marks\u000aresidual Ca++ at surgery site LOQ. Wire #2 marks separate cluster of micro\u000aca++.\u000aOperation: Left needle-directed breast biopsies x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Hx of ADH with residual microcalcifications, left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(1) Wire #1 inferior left breast --> mammo inks per path.\u000a(2) Wire #2 superior left breast --> mammo inks per path.\u000aRADIATION REPORT:\u000a#1 Ca++ present consistent with more anterior aspect of area localized.\u000a#2 Ca++ + density present consistent with more posterior area localized.\u000a- C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "1. Wire #1, inferior left breast", consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire in place. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the wire and microcalcifications.\u000aThe specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. No discrete lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen appears to be composed of approximately 90% adipose\u000aand 10% fibrous tissue. The specimen is been entirely submitted from anterior\u000ato posterior, with the area of the wire head in Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central portion of specimen, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Wire #2, superior left breast", consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire in place. The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by radiograph that demonstrates the wire and\u000amicrocalcifications. The specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. No\u000amasses are grossly identified. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm area of focal hemorrhage in\u000athe area of the wire head. The specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to\u000amedial with the area of the wire head in Micros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Center of specimen, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 8 frags, ESS.\u000abgl/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/16/2005\u000a[report_end]
