VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell changes.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aFibroadenomatous changes.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelioma.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast ADH on core needle biopsy of calcifications, clip\u000aslightly superior to residual calcs.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: No gross disease; clip and calcs in specimen.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH on core biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire-localized excision (mammo), short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and residual Ca++ in specimen. E.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast wire localized excision, short\u000astitch = superior, long stitch = lateral". It consists of a right breast wire\u000alocalized excision specimen (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There are two orienting\u000asutures (long = lateral; short = superior). The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph which shows micro calcifications and a clip in the specimen. A\u000alocalization wire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits the\u000ainferomedial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. On the specimen\u000aradiograph, the area of the clip is potentially abutting the anterior margin of\u000athe specimen and the area of residual calcification is potentially abutting the\u000aposterior margin of the specimen. The specimen is bisected along the\u000alocalization wire. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan firm area of possible\u000aprior biopsy site. The firm area abuts the anterior margin, and is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from medial to lateral (full\u000acalcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; possible core biopsy site in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, ESS.\u000aSK/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/18/2007\u000a[report_end]
