VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCysts.\u000aFibrosis, granulation tissue, and pigment-laden macrophages consistent\u000awith prior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47-year-old female status post REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy for evaluation of\u000amammographic calcifications left mid-upper inner breast revealing\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue with short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral, whip stitch on deep margin.\u000aCA++ in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast tissue with short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral,\u000awhip stitch on deep margin", and consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to\u000amedial x REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. A metal localization wire is\u000aembedded in the specimen. The long stitch has been placed by the surgeon to\u000aindicate lateral margin; a short stitch has been placed by the surgeon to\u000aindicate the superior margin; a whip stitch has been placed by the surgeon to\u000aindicate the deep margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cut section reveals a\u000alarge cavity (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with adjacent areas of hemorrhage measuring\u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom superior to inferior and entirely submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast mass from superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates calcifications within the specimen and\u000aa single localizing wire.\u000adk\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
