VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 11:3O, 14 G ULTRASOUND CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED/SOLID MASS:\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 10:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED/SOLID MASS:\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma with cellular stroma.\u000aNOTE: It would be difficult to distinguish a cellular fibroadenoma from\u000aa reccurence of a phyllodes tumor based on the limited sampling of a core\u000aneedle biopsy. Radiologic correlation is suggested to determine if this\u000alesion is near the patient's prior phyllodes tumor excision site.\u000a(Clinical history: 36 year old woman with a history of a right breast\u000aintermediate grade phyllodes tumor excised in 2002.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 1. Isoechoic left breast mass at 11:30.\u000a2. Isoechoic right breast mass at 10:00.\u000aHistory of prior phyllodes. Bilateral solid masses.\u000aOperation: 14 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative findings: Right breast masses.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Circumscribed/lobulated.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast masses, fibroadenoma vs. phyllodes.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Orange cassette contains left breast tissue.\u000a2. Brown cassette contains right breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Left breast", consists of a single orange cassette consisting of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Right breast", consists of a single brown unmarked cassette\u000aconsisting of multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.3 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: TORRES-BERASTAIN, IDELISA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
