VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFragments of benign fibroadenoma (0.7 cm) and fibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block #11, levels examined; see NOTE).\u000aFoci of columnar cell hyperplasia, cysts, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThere are three foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia in block #11, each with\u000aa different appearance: low grade cribriform, micropapillary, and clinging ina\u000aduct. The small size of each focus, and the variable appearance, favors\u000aclassification as atypical ductal hyperplasia. Case reviewed by Dr. S. Lester.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 36 yo female with h/o right breast sarcoma - now has a second (R)\u000abreast mass - fibroadenoma with atypical features (see previous\u000aneedle bx (R) breast mass).\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass, r/o cystosarcoma phyllodes.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right needle localized breast mass.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARLSON,JOSEPH WOODWARD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. right needle-localized breast biopsy", and consists of two (2)\u000afragments of fibrofatty tissue (#1: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and #2: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen radiograph reveals a localization wire marking a\u000acircumscribed density. A firm, white, rubbery mass (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is\u000apresent. The fragments are inked black and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fragment #1, 9 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fragment #2, 8 frag, ESS.\u000ajoc\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
