VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, involving a complex sclerosing lesion\u000a(0.9 cm; block 3; levels examined). Some of the glands have a\u000apseudo-infiltrative pattern around nerves. Immunoperoxidase studies for\u000amyoepithelial cells (p63, SMA, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) clearly show myoepithelial cells\u000athroughout the lesion, including the glands surrounding nerves. The area\u000ais also associated with fibrosis and hemosiderin deposits, consistent with\u000athe prior core needle biopsy site.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: No invasive carcinoma or ductal carcinoma in situ is seen after\u000acomplete microscopic examination of the specimen including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. Jack Meyer, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 left breast tissue", and consists of a single unoriented fragment of\u000ayellow/pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a metal\u000alocalizing wire embedded within the specimen. The specimen is inked black and\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a dense white/pink nodule (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation in four cassettes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aTwo accompanying radiograms show the presence of a mass within the specimen.\u000adk\u000aReports to: PILSON, KARL, D. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
