with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast and axillary contents, stitch on axillary tail", consists\u000aof a left modified radical mastectomy (1770 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is\u000aa suture designating the axillary tail (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an\u000aoverlying tan/pink skin ellipse (27.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a pink-white well healed\u000airregular scar (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The scar is REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the\u000anipple-areolar complex (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), located at the 3 o'clock position.\u000aThere is an unremarkable everted nipple (1.3 cm in diameter). The posterior\u000amargin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a\u000awhite-yellow, focally hemorrhagic ill-defined irregular mass (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest black-inked deep margin. The mass is located\u000abetween the upper inner and upper outer quadrants, and is REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000athe nipple, at the 12 o'clock position. The remaining cut surface displays 30%\u000afocally dense white fibrous tissue, and 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue,\u000awith no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. Multiple lymph nodes\u000aare identified within the axillary tail region, ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm, to REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension. The lymph nodes are selectively bisected, to reveal\u000atan-pink cut surfaces. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple and well-healed scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White-yellow focally hemorrhagic mass at the 12 o'clock position,\u000asequentially from medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Corresponding black-inked posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from the upper outer quadrant, to\u000ainclude the posterior margin at REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Whole lymph nodes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/15/2008\u000a[report_end]
