terior margin, to the\u000aposterior margin, to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and\u000ato the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. There is a second\u000awhite/tan firm illdefined area (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located at the lateral\u000amargin, at the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, at the inferior margin, and at the superior margin. The\u000aremainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 40% fibrous tissue and\u000athe rest is adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior, inferior margins, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Area adjacent to first lesion with posterior, anterior, superior\u000amargin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: Area adjacent to cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior,\u000ainferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: Area adjacent to cystic lesion with anterior, posterior, superior, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: Fibrous tissue nearest to cystic lesion with medial, anterior,\u000aposterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion lesion with superior, anterior,\u000aposterior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion with posterior, medial margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: Medial, anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: Second lesion with lateral, superior, posterior margins, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 11: Second lesion with posterior, lateral, inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: Second lesion with inferior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: Second lesion with lateral, superior, posterior, anterior margins, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: Fibrous tissue adjacent to second lesion with inferior, posterior,\u000alateral margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: Anterior, posterior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: Anterior, posterior, superior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: Superior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: Inferior, posterior, lateral margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
