VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Thomas Brenn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical lobular hyperplasia, columnar alteration of\u000aLobules with prominent snouts and secretions, cysts and apocrine\u000achanges.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 49 y/o premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrates two\u000aright breast UIQ 6mm solid lesions at the 1:00 axis, 3 cm from the nipple for\u000awhich US-guided wire localization excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization excision\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue - short stitch superior, long lateral, whip stitch on\u000achest wall margin -> mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aWire target in specimen (mammo US). OR called.\u000a--SR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long lateral, whip stitch\u000aon chest wall margin", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose breast tissue\u000a(4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle-localization wire in place (entering\u000alateroposteriorly and exiting medially), three orienting sutures (short\u000astitch=superior, long=lateral, whip stitch=chest wall margin) and accompanying\u000aradiograph. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral\u000ato medial, revealing a white/tan, focally cystic, ill-defined fibrous area (3.2\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which extends to the inferior, posterior, anterior, medial,\u000aand lateral margins and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin. The\u000aneedle-localization wire traverses this area and coincides with the\u000aaccompanying radiograph and confirmation per radiology. The remaining breast\u000atissue consists of yellow/tan, lobulated fat. No other gross lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from lateral to\u000amedial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple\u000afrags, ESS\u000aDFI/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Thomas Brenn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/28/2005\u000a[report_end]
