orange cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "5 o'clock left breast", consists of a yellow cassette containing\u000amultiple tan/white to tan/yellow fragments of fibrofatty cores soft tissue (2.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of yellow cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/29/2006\u000a[report_end]
