VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST LOWER OUTER 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with columnar cell change with cysts (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amicropapillary hyperplasia and flat epithelial atypia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), see NOTE.\u000aE-cadherin confirms absent membranous staining in the LCIS which focally\u000ainvolves areas of columnar cell change with calcifications.\u000aOther findings:\u000aLactational change.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: The micropapillary hyperplasia shows architectural atypia, and along with\u000athe flat epithelial atypia present, would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 41 year old female with new right lower/outer coarse heterogeneous\u000acalcifications posteriorly in possibly a segmental distribution.\u000aFormalin time - 11:20 am.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Non-palpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: lower/outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core biopsy in two green cassettes - A/with calcs and B/no\u000acalcs.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast", and consists of two labeled green\u000acassettes. The first green cassette, labeled "A/Calcification", contains two\u000atan/pink to yellow irregular fibrofatty tissues (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate), which are submitted in toto. The second green cassette, labeled\u000a"B", contains multiple irregular tan/pink to yellow fibrofatty tissues (2.5 x\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues in cassette, labeled "A/Calcification", 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues in cassette, labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000almc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25, 2009 at 01:04:28PM\u000a[report_end]
