VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, one focus (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSclerosing adenosis and calcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aImmunostains demonstrate absence of e-cadherin in LCIS. Sclerosing\u000aadenosis is positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and shows myoepithelial cells as\u000ahighlighted by p63 (double stain).\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 yo F with h/o atypical ductal and lobular hyperplasia; new right\u000abreast calcification\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy (short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aSpecimen radiograph demonstrates the intact wire (examined visually) and\u000acluster of calcs that approximately an edge/margin -> called into Dr. Golshan.\u000aDr. Wang\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast wire localized excisional biopsy", consists of\u000aan irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.6 cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm M-L x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aA-P) with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating\u000alateral per surgeon. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The accompanying\u000aradiograph denotes a needle localization wire within the specimen, which enters\u000athrough the anterosuperior aspect of the specimen and exits through the\u000aanteroinferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior to exhibit a dense white fibrous area/? nodule (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) abutting the inferior, posterior, anterior, medial, and lateral\u000amargins, and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The remaining breast\u000aparenchyma consists of 100% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, which readily\u000afragments upon sectioning. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior to include\u000aill-defined firm area (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and area of interest (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 2 frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajc/pab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday August 27, 2009 at 11:30:35AM\u000a[report_end]
