VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (INCLUDING REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aB/2. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2 (INCLUDING FSB):\u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aC/3. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #3 (INCLUDING FSC):\u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aD/4. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (686 GM):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE\u000aLYMPH NODES.\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - Two foci - REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMultifocal - Yes\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - I (Well) (3 to 5 points)\u000aTubules - > 75% (1 point)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep margin\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Comedo, solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep margin\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes ? Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Columnar cell changes\u000aADH\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb sREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Mx with two foci of invasion.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (on REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE: Double stain performed (p63, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates\u000aloss of myoepithelial cells in the invasive component.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 62 year old woman with DCIS documented in 2 quadrants by stereotactic\u000acore biopsy for microcalcifications. Clips placed in L UIQ + L UOQ.\u000aOperation: Left SLN biopsy, left simple mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) SLN L.\u000aB/2) SLN #2.\u000aC/3) SLN #3.\u000aD/4) L breast, suture on tail of Spence.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - SLN" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - SLN #2" (FSB):\u000aLymph node negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3 - SENTINEL NODE #3" (FSC):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: ANNA LAURY, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel lymph node #1", consists of one fragment of soft tissue\u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Sentinel node #2", consists of one fragment of red/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was bisected and\u000aentirely submitted as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Sentinel node #3", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted as FSC.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSC remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Left breast", consists of a 686-g simple mastectomy specimen with\u000astitch designating the tail (22.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached skin ellipse\u000a(4.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). One clip (#1) is found in the upper inner quadrant with an\u000aill-defined fibrotic area (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin\u000a(inked in black) is a smooth fascial plane with no skeletal muscle attached. A\u000asecond clip was found in the outer upper quadrant an ill-defined fibrotic area\u000a(3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin. An ill\u000adefined tan/white firm area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the lower outer quadrant is\u000a3 cm from the closest deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the clip #1, 3 cm from\u000athe clip #2. No additional lesion is identified. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is predominantly white and yellow fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip #1 site, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip #2 site, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area in the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest deep margin to clip #1 site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest deep margin to clip #2 site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibrotic firm area in lower outer quadrant, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest deep margin to lower outer quadrant firm area, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aLC/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block d12):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
