VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, intermediate grade, at least REMOVED_DATE cm. SEE NOTE.\u000aTumor is extensively present at the inferior margin and focally at the\u000aanterior margin.\u000aA second fibroadenoma is present (1.0 cm).\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: The phyllodes tumor arises from a hyalinized fibroadneoma. There are\u000afocal areas of moderate hypercellularity with some nuclear atypia and a low\u000amitotic rate (up to 4 per 10 HPF). There is stromal overgrowth in areas, but\u000ano necrosis, hemorrhage or heterologenous differentiation. The borders of the\u000alesions are circumscribed. Overall, the features are consistent with an\u000aintermediate grade phyllodes tumor.\u000aDr. Andrea Richardson concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast wire localized biopsy, short stitch/\u000asuperior, long stitch/lateral, black silk is marking\u000astitch.\u000aMass is accompanied by a radiograph that demonstrates a mass within the breast\u000aspecimen that has been circled by the radiologist. There is a wire protruding\u000athrough the mass. This wire contains a hub. There is a 2nd area of the breast\u000awhere a short portion of wire is noted (no circle denotes any mass). The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a pink sheet that indicates the mass is in the\u000aspecimen (CD).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KWAAN,MARY R.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left wire localized breast biopsy, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, black silk marking stitch", and is a portion of breast tissue (5.8 x\u000a4.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimension) with two (2) black silk marking sutures. The\u000awire with the hub is through the breast specimen at the lateral marking suture.\u000aThe other portion of the wire is very loosely within tissue at the inferior and\u000amedial portion of the breast. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is 90%\u000afibrous tissue. There is a possible mass at the posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area is not surrounded by adipose\u000atissue, rather it is surrounded by fibrous tissue. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin and abuts the posterior margin. There is a second mass in\u000athe area of the wire with hub that is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, abuts the anterior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm of fibrous tissue separated this mass from the 1st mass\u000adescribed. All tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: 2nd mass (1.2 cm), lateral margin, wire with hub, 3 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  connected and adjacent to micro 1, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent to 2 and 3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent and are medial to 4 and 5, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent to 6 and 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent and medial to 8 and 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: adjacent to 10 and 11, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1st mass (1.7 cm), REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of 2nd wire, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000amrk\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
