, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Left breast #1 inferior wide", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial\u000ato lateral) REMOVED_DATE cm (inferior to superior) REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm\u000abreast biopsy with a localization wire in place. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates calcification and wire within the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen consists of approximately 50%\u000ayellow adipose tissue and approximately 50% white fibrous tissue without gross\u000alesions. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. Left breast #2 superior wide", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial\u000ato lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm\u000abreast biopsy with a localization wire in place. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates calcifications and a localization wire. The specimen\u000ais inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a firm white area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm at the\u000amedial aspect of the specimen. The remainder of the specimen is unremarkable\u000aadipose tissue. The firm white area abuts the medial, superior, inferior,\u000aposterior, and anterior margins and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, mult frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Right breast tissue with wire", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial\u000ato lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm\u000abreast biopsy with a localization wire in the specimen container. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates calcifications and wire in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The parenchyma consists of\u000aapproximately 80% adipose tissue and 20% white fibrous tissue without gross\u000alesions. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 8 frags, ESS.\u000amah\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
