ification. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen was sectioned from lateral to medial and consists primarily of\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue with minimal fibrous tissue. The wire is\u000alocalized to sections 3 and 4. The specimen has been entirely submitted from\u000alateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral (perpendicular), 8 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS (wire localized in sections REMOVED_DATE )\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial (perpendicular), REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fragments of fatty tissue, 4 frags, ESS\u000aDM/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
