VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE WITH WIRE";\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia, pseudoangiomatous\u000astromal hyperplasia, biopsy site changes, and calcifications\u000aassociated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female with core biopsy --> atypical hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L needle localized breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast atypical hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue with wire.\u000aB/2) additional left breast tissue, yellow ink on new true margin, black on\u000aprevious resection.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aA/1) Y-shaped clip in specimen (medial to old bx site). OR called. LBT.\u000aB/2) S-shaped clip in specimen (lateral to bx site). OR called. LBT.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left breast tissue with wire", and consists of a\u000alumpectomy specimen, which is inked by the surgeon according to the pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange, and measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral. There is one wire in the specimen in the lateral/superior portion.\u000aThe superior portion of the specimen is almost entirely fibrous tissue, whereas\u000athe remaining 60% of the specimen is a mix of roughly 60% adipose and 40%\u000afibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior portion of specimen with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: anterior, posterior and medial margins with fibrous tissue,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: inferior margin, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000a(NOTE: approximately 50% of the specimen and 75% of the fibrous tissue is\u000asubmitted.)\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - additional left breast tissue" and consists of one\u000afragment of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Half of the surface is\u000ainked in black, and the other half is inked in yellow by the surgeon. A biopsy\u000asite with gel-foam is identified in the central portion of the specimen\u000aabutting the black-inked margin. The gel-foam comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000ayellow-inked margin. The remainder of the cut surface consists entirely of\u000ayellow adipose tissue. The biopsy site cavity is submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional left breast tissue, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000a(NOTE: approximately 60% of the specimen and 100% of the fibrous tissue have\u000abeen submitted.)\u000aESN/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/16/2006\u000a[report_end]
