lateral/anterior corner and exits the specimen at the\u000amiddle medial/posterior border. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a\u000aclip within an ill-defined density. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000asectioned parallel to the wire (approximately inferior to superior) into eleven\u000asections. No discrete masses are identified. No clip is identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation serially from the\u000ainferior to the superior margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior most tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site and clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, wire in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOOB/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher P Crum M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/20/2006\u000a[report_end]
