VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.; Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST LOWER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A\u000aMASS:\u000aIntraductal papilloma(s) with florid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications, cysts and florid\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked an evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST UPPER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN AREA OF\u000aARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, present associated with a complex sclerosing\u000alesion (2.2 cm) and as small scattered foci associated with columnar cell\u000achange and intraductal papillomas (see NOTE).\u000aExtensive sclerosing adenosis with associated calcifications.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications, cysts and florid\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double immunohistochemical stains confirm the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells around sclerotic ducts within the complex sclerosing lesion\u000aand in areas of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: The foci of ADH are small and have varied morphology including a\u000acribriform pattern, a micropapillary pattern and apocrine pattern. Dr. Susan\u000aLester has reviewed selected slides and agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: history of abnormal (+)mammogram with atypical core bx in RUOQ\u000asclerosing adenosis with small radial sclerosing lesion.\u000aOperative findings Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnl R mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R lower - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral (mammo).\u000aB/2) R upper - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Called to OR. Specimen with Ca++, mass and wire.\u000aSpecimen #2: Architectural distortion and wire in specimen/OR called. DGS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "right lower", consists of a fragment of yellow-pink lobulated\u000afibrofatty soft tissue (6.5 cm M - L x REMOVED_DATE cm A - P x REMOVED_DATE cm S - I) with a\u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral per\u000asurgeon. The specimen was received inked per pathology protocol. The specimen\u000ais inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. Please note: The specimen was received from radiology with the\u000aneedle-localization wire detached. An accompanying radiograph was received\u000awhich demonstrates a wire, calcifications and a mass in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit an ill-defined\u000aslightly hemorrhagic area with minimal fat necrosis (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior and inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of 98%\u000ayellow lobulated unremarkable adipose tissue to 2% wispy white delicate fibrous\u000atissues. No discrete masses or lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of fat necrosis and focal hemorrhage sequentially submitted\u000afrom medial to lateral, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening minimal fibrous stroma, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPlease note: Approximately 35% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aPart B, "right upper", consists of an irregular fragment of fibrofatty soft\u000atissue (9.0 S - I x REMOVED_DATE cm M - L x REMOVED_DATE cm A - P) with a short suture\u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is\u000areceived with a needle-localization wire entering the specimen at the\u000aintersection of the lateral, superior and anterior borders. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph which demonstrates a wire and an area of\u000aarchitectural distortion present. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral to exhibit a tan-white, stellate mass (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and posterior margins, and\u000a2.5 cm from the medial margin. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of 75%\u000ayellow lobulated unremarkable adipose tissue to 25% focally dense white fibrous\u000atissue. The specimen is sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and stellate\u000amass, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and\u000astellate mass more towards medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and\u000astellate mass lateral to Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and\u000astellate mass lateral to Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and\u000astellate mass lateral to Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional intervening fibrous stroma between medial margin and\u000astellate mass lateral to Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and medially adjacent to stellate mass\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPlease note: Approximately 85% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000ajc/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
