VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: left breast tissue, re-excision\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-04-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident\u000aPETER M. SADOW, M.D., PH.D.\u000aPathologist\u000aLucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, RE-EXCISION:\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent apical snouts and\u000asecretions.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aBiopsy site changes with fibrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction,\u000aand hemosiderin-laden macrophages.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 70 year old female, S/P REMOVED_DATE (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) L breast wire localized\u000aexcision of mammographic calcifications showing atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000a11/04 mammogram demonstrates L breast calcifications for which wire\u000alocalization and excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mammographic calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whipped stitch/chest\u000awall margin (to mammo).\u000aRadiograph report: Ca++ are seen on specimen. E. Gombos, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number, and further designated as "#1 - left breast tissue, to\u000amammo first, short/superior, long/lateral, whipped stitch/chest wall margin",\u000aand consists of fibrofatty breast tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000areceived inked according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is also designated with sutures by\u000athe surgeon, with a short stitch placed in the red-inked section (superior), a\u000along stitch in the yellow-inked area (lateral), and a whip-stitch affixed to\u000athe deep area (inked black). There is a wire placed by radiology.\u000aAccompanying the specimen is a radiograph from radiology, localizing\u000acalcifications to the area beside the wire in the deep lateral portion of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal white, fibrous tissue\u000acontained within fibrofatty breast tissue, though the majority is indeed\u000afibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast excision specimen, 2 and 1 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue associated with wire, 2, 2, 4, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: remainder of excision specimen, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000apes/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
