VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST LUMPECTOMY":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, with associated calcifcations.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, microscopic\u000afibroadenoma, and calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "FINAL LEFT BREAST INFERIOR/DEEP MARGIN":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and microcalcifications\u000aassociated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast core.\u000aOperation: Left breast needle loc.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Interdeterminate calcs/ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast lumpectomy, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000a#2 - final left breast inferior/deep margin, suture on new margin\u000aside.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aFirst part, sublabeled "#1 - left breast needle localized mass", consists of a\u000aneedle localized breast lumpectomy specimen (6.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which includes\u000atwo sutures placed by the surgeon to indicate the superior and lateral margins.\u000aA radiograph accompanies the specimen, which shows a needle localization wire\u000aadjacent to a density and microcalcifications. The specimen is inked as\u000afollows: lateral = red, superior = yellow, posterior = black, anterior = blue,\u000ainferior = green, and medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000ainferior to superior to reveal an ill-defined, stellate fibrous area (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which is adjacent to a white/yellow, firmer area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is circular and grossly abuts the inferior margin. This firmer area\u000ais located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral (inked red) margin, and\u000a2.1 cm from the superior (inked yellow) margin. A spherical, firm area (2.2 x\u000a2.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present at the inferior margin, comprising the majority of the\u000ainferior margin, and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The specimen is approximately\u000a65% fatty tissue and 35% fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted\u000afrom inferior to superior for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1-4: Firm area and inferior margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5-15: Sections through body of specimen, including medial, posterior,\u000aanterior, and lateral margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #16-17: Superior margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, sublabeled "#2 - final left breast inferior/deep margin", consists of\u000aa breast shave margin specimen (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a stitch placed by the\u000asurgeon to indicate the "new" inferior margin. The old margin is inked in\u000ablue, and the new margin is inked in black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal a golden yellow to tan/pink heterogeneous cut surface. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #18-19: New left breast inferior margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
