VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving sclerosing adenosis.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia involving a papilloma (block 3; levels\u000aexamined; see NOTE).\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aCysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aBiopsy site changes present.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe atypical ductal hyperplasia approaches a diagnosis of papillary DCIS. The\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest (anterior) margin.\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. S. Lester who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aOperation: Excision of wire localized breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue, stitch long/lateral, short/superior.\u000aRadiology Report:\u000aClip and wire confined in specimen.\u000a(signature illegible)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast tissue", and consists of a right breast wire\u000alocalized excision (7.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior), with two orienting sutures and a wire in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating a wire and\u000aa clip in the ill-defined density in the center of the specimen. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Sectioning reveals a biopsy cavity in the middle of the\u000aspecimen (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, 1 cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. There is an area of firmness (1.1 cm x 1 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the medial\u000aportion of the breast, associated with a small area of hemorrhage. A second\u000aarea of firmness (0.3 cm in diameter) is noted abutting the inferior margin.\u000aThe tissue is approximately 90% adipose tissue. Ninety (90%) percent of the\u000atissue is submitted, and all of the fibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro #1-6: Biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue in margin, including\u000ainferior, lateral, posterior and anterior margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #7+8: Superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #9-11: Medial margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #12: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
