VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (specimens #1 and #2 of 2\u000aspecimens):\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, clinging\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block) - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 3:26 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, anterior, posterior, superior,\u000ainferior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - lateral\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:2\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aForeign body giant cell reaction with acute inflammation (s/p excision)\u000aBenign cysts with apocrine metaplasia\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - See note\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously by report\u000aNOTE:\u000aBy report, the patient has invasive carcinoma; however, those specimens have\u000anot been evaluated at BWH and so are not included in the pathologic staging.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer of left breast - for re-excision.\u000aOperation: Left needle loc/wide excision left breast and sentinel node\u000abiopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left sentinel nodes - fs\u000a#2) Left breast mass (long lateral; short superior)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Wires and calcifications in specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S) LT" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARLSON,JOSEPH WOODWARD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left sentinel nodes biopsy", consists of two pink/tan lymph\u000anodes (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The first node is bisected and\u000aentirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The second node is bisected and entirely submitted\u000aas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast mass", consists of a left breast excision\u000aspecimen (2.3 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior). The anterior edge of the specimen has a skin ellipse\u000a(5.2 cm in length x REMOVED_DATE cm in width) with a scar (3.4 cm in length) running\u000adown its superior aspect. There are two sutures in the skin ellipse which have\u000abeen designated by the surgeon (short superior, long lateral). Additionally\u000atwo needle localization wires enter the specimen. The first enters in the\u000acenter of the skin ellipse and exits on the medial edge of the specimen. The\u000asecond enters at the inferior/anterior/lateral edge of the specimen and does\u000anot exit. A specimen radiograph accompanies the tissue which indicate wires\u000aand calcifications in the spcimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibroadipose tissue, 100% of fibrous tissue submitted, 30 frags,\u000aRSS\u000ajoc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
