rgins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is one needle localization wire in place, which enters\u000athe inferior aspect of the specimen and exits the superoanterior aspect of the\u000aSpecimen. The specimen was previously radiographed and also a fat area of\u000acalcifications ????? by the ??????. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral to exhibit approximately 60% dense focally hemorrhagic\u000awhite/tan fibrous stroma and 40% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified. The needle localization wire\u000atraverses the dense fibrous stroma through the central specimen. The specimen\u000ais entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: specimen sequentially submitted from medial to lateral with\u000aprobable calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/25/2006\u000a[report_end]
