uptured breast\u000aprosthesis (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an abundant amount of yellow, sticky\u000amaterial and multiple chalky, calcified fragments. The specimen is consistent\u000awith a silicone implant and is for gross examination only.\u000aNote: Gross photographs are taken.\u000aPart C, "Left breast silicone implant", consists of a ruptured breast\u000aprosthesis (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an abundant amount of pale yellow,\u000asticky material and multiple minute, calcified fragments. The specimen is\u000aconsistent with a silicone implant and is for gross examination only.\u000aNote: Gross photographs are taken.\u000aPart D, "Left breast capsule", consists of a collapsed pink, discoid, cystic,\u000arubbery tissue (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The external surface is pale pink with a\u000asmall amount of attached fat. The inside lining is pink, roughened, with\u000amoderate calcification. Further examination shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm attached\u000afragment of dense white tissue. Representative sections are submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aThe specimen is fixed and decalcified prior to processing.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Capsule, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Capsule with adjacent breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aWP/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
