VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aNo residual atypical ductal hyperplasia identified.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN, EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast and fibroadipose tissue with focal chronic inflammation\u000aand fat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle loc excision of right breast mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast microcalcification.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue with wire (mammo).\u000aB/2. Additional deep margin (blue ink adjacent to prior specimen; black ink\u000aadjacent to chest wall - mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpoke with Dr. Lesnikoski - intact wire and calcifications are in first\u000aspecimen; no clip seen. No calcifications in second specimen.\u000a- Rachna Madan.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled, "#1. Right breast tissue with wire", consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by inks per surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The localizing wire enters the specimen posterolaterally and\u000atraverses the superficial posterior surface, exiting medially. Specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within\u000athe specimen, adjacent to a small cluster of microcalcification. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates 60% to 70% tan/white cystic-appearing fibrous tissue without\u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is submitted,\u000asequentially from superior to inferior, with area of interest per localizing\u000awire/radiograph in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled, "#2. Additional deep margin - blue ink adjacent to prior\u000aspecimen, black adjacent to chest wall", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(maximum thickness) excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented with inks by the\u000asurgeon as follows: Blue - adjacent to prior specimen, black - adjacent to\u000achest wall. The specimen is anteriorly sectioned revealing predominantly\u000atan/yellow soft, lobulated adipose tissue without masses, lesions, or other\u000aabnormalities grossly. The specimen is sequentially submitted as follows:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multiple frags, ESS. Please note: Specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph. There are no calcifications in the radiograph\u000aspecimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/4/2007\u000a[report_end]
