VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROBERT T OSTEEN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Samuel G Katz, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT BREAST, STITCH @ THE AXILLARY TAIL" (168g):\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrous tissue, sclerosing adenosis,\u000afat necrosis, acute and chronic inflammation, foreign body giant cell reaction,\u000aand fibrosis (s/p excision).\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT BREAST, STITCH @ THE AXILLARY TAIL" (161g):\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibroadenoma.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt. breast CA\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 Left breast - stitch @ the axillary tail.\u000a#2 Right breast - Stitch @ the axillary tail.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "1. Left breast - stitch @ the axillary tail", consists of a\u000a168-gm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, left simple mastectomy specimen to include\u000atan/pink skin ellipse (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), everted nipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000atan/brown areola (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and a single stitch at the "axillary tail". A\u000adefinitive axillary tail is not grossly identified. There is a tan,\u000awell-healed, curvilinear scar (2.0 cm in length), extending from the superior\u000aaspect of the areola to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest skin margin. The deep\u000amargin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral, revealing a white/tan, ill-defined, focally necrotic, fibrous lesion\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), deep to the aforementioned scar, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin, between the upper/outer and lower/outer quadrants, consistent with\u000aprevious biopsy site. The second tan/white fibrous focally necrotic lesion\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present, REMOVED_DATE cm superior/medial to the aforementioned\u000acavity, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, between the upper/inner and upper/outer\u000aquadrants. There is an area of white/focally pink, focally cystic, firm,\u000adense, fibrous tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), extending from the lateral to\u000acentral aspect of the breast, predominantly involving the upper and lower outer\u000aquadrants and extending to the deep margin. The remaining breast consists of\u000aapproximately 60%, yellow, lobulated fat and 40% tan/white, dense, fibrous\u000astroma; no lymph nodes are identified within the lateral aspect of the breast.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, probable biopsy cavity in relationship to skin scar,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, probable biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: More medial, probable second, biopsy cavity in relation to deep\u000amargin, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous tissue between the lateral and more medial biopsy\u000acavities, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous lesion (upper/outer quadrant), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous lesion (lower/outer quadrant), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Right breast stitch at axillary tail", consists of a\u000aright, simple mastectomy specimen (161-gm, 14 x 13 x 2 cm), to include tan/pink\u000askin ellipse (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), tan/brown areola (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm), tan/pink everted\u000anipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and a single stitch at "the axillary tail". The\u000adeep margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral, revealing an area of white/tan, dense, fibrous tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 cm) within the central breast, focally extending to the lateral aspect and\u000aextending to the deep margin. No lesions consistent with invasive carcinoma\u000aare identified. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately equal\u000aproportions of yellow/tan, lobulated fat and tan/white, fibrous stroma. No\u000alymph nodes are identified at the lateral aspect of the breast.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant (including dense fibrous area), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant (including dense fibrous area), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional, dense, fibrous lesion (central breast), 1 frag, RSS.\u000adfi/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Samuel G Katz M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
