ing breast parenchyma is unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule and hemorrhagic cavity to anterior, lateral, medial and\u000aposterior\u000amargins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hemorrhagic cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining margins and uninvolved breast parenchyma, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000apal/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Thomas Brenn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/11/2005\u000a[report_end]
