 margin"), and a needle localization\u000awire in place (entering anteriorly and exiting at the superoposterior aspect).\u000aSpecimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial, exhibiting a\u000apredominantly white/tan, focally cystic fibrous stroma admixed with scant\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue. The accompanying radiograph and radiology\u000aconfirm "sample image demonstrates a cluster of heterogeneous calcifications at\u000athe distal tip of the intact hook wire". No other gross lesions are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue (sequentially from lateral to medial), multi frags,\u000aESS. Please note: Probable calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/25/2007\u000a[report_end]
