VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.; Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, with cribriform and micropapillary patterns\u000aarising in columnar cell change (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts, calcifications and flat epithelial atypia.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change with calcifications.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts and flat epithelial atypia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 34 year old female with history of L ADH after biopsy 2005. Had\u000aincreasing calcifications on mammographic LUOQ examination REMOVED_DATE  with severe\u000aADH bordering on DCIS - re-excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, with\u000astitch on chest wall margin plus scar.\u000aB/2) left medial shave margin - whipstitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral, whipstitch on chest wall margin with scar", consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (5.0 grams; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000ashort stitch placed per surgeon to designate the superior position and a long\u000astitch placed per surgeon to designate the lateral position. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe cut surface reveals an 80% fibrous parenchyma with a dense focus of fat\u000anecrosis consistent with prior excision site (located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin). The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section with prior excision site including medial, lateral, anterior\u000aand posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Successive sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 5 frags, perpendicularly sectioned, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left medial shave margin, whipstitch new margin", consists\u000aof one yellow/tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais suture placed per surgeon to designate the new margin. The corresponding\u000asurface is inked black. The old margin is inked red. The sectioned surface is\u000apredominantly fibrous in composition. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000amicroscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New left medial shave margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aSWY/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 02:40:40PM\u000a[report_end]
