VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Javad Beheshti, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread into ducts.\u000aColumnar cell change with flat epithelial atypia and associated calcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis associated with calcifications.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of invasive malignancy upon microscopic examination\u000aof the specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 36-year-old female with core biopsy x2 revealing LCIS, calcifications,\u000aand columnar cell change with flat atypia.\u000aOperation: Not provided\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast LCIS and calcifications x 2 areas.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast double wire localized excisional biopsy, short stitch\u000asuperior, long lateral ? mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a2 clips + many Ca++ in specimen. EP Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in one part, labeled with the patient's name, medical\u000arecord number, and "right breast double wire loc excision", along with a\u000aspecimen radiograph showing two localization wires and two clips marking\u000acalcifications within the breast tissue. The specimen consists of a segmental\u000abreast resection measuring REMOVED_DATE (medial - lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior - inferior) x\u000a2.5 (anterior - posterior). Short and long sutures mark superior and lateral\u000asurgical resection margins respectively. The specimen is inked as follows:\u000aanterior blue, posterior black, medial orange, lateral yellow, superior red,\u000ainferior green. Two localization wires are entering the specimen at superior\u000amargin. The tissue is sectioned along the localization wires to reveal two\u000aclips. The medial clip is inserted in the middle of a round tan solid firm\u000aarea consistent with biopsy site measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. This area\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior surgical\u000aresection margins. The lateral clip is placed in another area consistent with\u000abiopsy site measuring, which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and is REMOVED_DATE cm lateral\u000ato the first nodule. This nodule measures REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial, REMOVED_DATE from the anterior, and\u000a1.0 cm from posterior surgical resection margins respectively. Ill-defined,\u000amoderately rubbery, tan, fibrous tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, extends\u000afrom the lateral nodule to the posterior and lateral surgical resection\u000amargins. The tissue is totally submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial nodule, 1 frag in each cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial surgical resection margin, sectioned perpendicular to\u000athe margin, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The lateral nodule and corresponding margins, 1 frag in each\u000acassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag in each cassette, tissue between the nodules and\u000acorresponding margins, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral extension of fibrous tissue from the lateral nodule to\u000alateral surgical resection margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior surgical resection margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aJBE/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a8/7/2007\u000a[report_end]
