VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS\u000aAND A CLIP":\u000aMicroscopic focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia with associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCyst formation.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 31 year old female with a breast atypical ductal hyperplasia, s/p\u000aimage guided core biopsy.\u000aOperation: #1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right wire localized excisional biopsy - short stitch sup, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Targeted clip and calcification in specimen. Called to OR at\u000a12:15pm. J. Ritner.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. R breast wide localized excisional biopsy short stitch superior long\u000alateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue,\u000aoriented by sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long\u000asuture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). The\u000aspecimen is received along with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire\u000ain place in the area of a metallic surgical clip and a cluster of\u000acalcifications at one edge of the central portion of the specimen (? inferior).\u000aSectioning demonstrates 40% tan/white granular fibrous tissue without palpable\u000aor visible masses, lesions, or other abnormalities. The entire specimen is\u000asequentially submitted from medial to lateral, with perpendicular medial margin\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest per radiograph,\u000awire, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 01:08:51PM\u000a[report_end]
