rts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "blue top white bottom right breast site #1", consists of\u000amultiple tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate). The breast tissue cores are received in two individual\u000acassettes, each with a blue top. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette blue top, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette blue top, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "right breast site #2 green top white bottom", consists of\u000amultiple tan/white to tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores\u000a(6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The breast tissue cores are received in\u000afive individual cassettes, each with a green top. The specimen is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Individual white cassette, green top, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Individual white cassette, green top, multi frags each, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 04, 2009 at 02:23:34PM\u000a[report_end]
