ial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest lateral margin. The remaining tissue is an admixture of\u000afibrous tissue with cysts and lobulated adipose tissue (80%). The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted from lateral to medial with a spiculated lesion in Micros\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen to include anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior and inferior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000almb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/5/2005\u000a[report_end]
