VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Lymph node biopsy (non-heme)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, LEFT AXILLA (including FSA):\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP, AND\u000aSENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (including Part A and Part B):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - I (Well) (3 to 5 points)\u000aTubules - > 75% (1 point)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - All margins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - PRESENT\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 4:19 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - All margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:1\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aColumnar cell change\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDsn MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously at BWH\u000aNOTE:\u000aKeratin immunostain is negative in the sentinel lymph node. Levels examined.\u000aDr. Tan Ince, Breast Pathology Service, concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized excision; sentinel lymph node bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Sentinel lymph nodes left axilla (FS)\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (L) AXILLA" (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Vania Nose, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "sentinel lymph node left axilla", is received in the frozen\u000alab for intraoperative consultation and consists of a blue-tinged lymph node\u000awith attached fat (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked, bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted for frozen section as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x\u000a3.2 (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm irregular\u000afibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place entering the anterior\u000aaspect and exiting the posterior inferior aspect. The specimen is received\u000ainked per the surgeon per pathology protocol. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aAn accompanying specimen radiograph displays a silver metallic clip adjacent to\u000athe needle localization wire. The specimen is sliced from lateral to medial\u000ainto twelve slices to reveal a silver metallic clip in slice 7. The clip is\u000alocated within a firm poorly circumscribed tan-white mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000alocated abutting the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The mass is located in slices 5\u000athrough 9. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, lateral margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7 (with clip), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 12, medial margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMC/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 09, 2009 at 06:32:30PM\u000a[report_end]
