u000aof the breast parenchyma. A specimen radiograph is received with the specimen\u000adesignating a localized area of calcification adjacent to the needle\u000alocalization wire and a secondary additional group of calcification. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and the specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include possible\u000asecondary mammographic area of calcification, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include targeted\u000aarea of calcification, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast tissue, multiple frags each, ESS.\u000aSEK/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
