VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present associated with calcifications (best\u000aseen on slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; see note).\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia and cysts with calcifications.\u000aRadial sclerosing lesion (0.3 cm).\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aMargins inked and evaluated.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Atypical cells, right breast.\u000aOperation: Localization/excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical cells, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Primary tumor site, right breast - short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aHookwire, clip and calcifications in specimen.\u000aCalled to OR HP, 12:15.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe case is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aSpecimen A, "#1. Primary tumor site, right breast, short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral - mammo", and consists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in medial to lateral direction, REMOVED_DATE cm in the anterior to\u000aposterior direction, and REMOVED_DATE cm in the superior to inferior direction. The\u000aspecimen is received inked per the Inks protocol. A localization wire enters\u000aat the junction of the lateral and inferior margins. Sectioning the specimen,\u000ain a medial to lateral direction, into eleven slices reveals that the specimen\u000ais 90% adipose tissue. The clip is seen in slice #6. A white/tan lesion is\u000aseen slices #4 and #5, and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The closest extension\u000aof the mass to a margin is REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior green - inked margin). The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 (medial margin), 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11 (lateral margin), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000achd/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 02:42:11PM\u000a[report_end]
