VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrosis, chronic inflammation, and foreign\u000abody giant cell reaction to polarizable material consistent with prior excision\u000asite.\u000aNo residual carcinoma present, including deep margin.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SKIN:\u000aSkin and scant subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS of right breast, extensive. Deformed breast, S/P 2 resections.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, TRAM flap reconstruction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right breast, short suture/superior, long suture/lateral.\u000aB/2 - right breast skin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe case is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - right breast, short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral", consists of a 697-gram mastectomy specimen that measures 17 x\u000a16 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a short suture and a long suture designating the\u000asuperior and lateral aspect of the specimen, respectively. There is an\u000airregularly shaped, approximately stellate-shaped skin ellipse that measures\u000a12.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple is REMOVED_DATE cm and the areola is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is\u000aa scar that measures REMOVED_DATE cm in length at the superior aspect of the skin\u000asurface (0.5 cm from the superior edge) and lying REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple. The\u000aposterior surface consists of a smooth fascial plane with no skeletal muscle\u000afragments. There is an area of retraction and fibrosis, which lies REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior edge of the specimen. This area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and reveals an irregular white fibrotic lesion\u000athat measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In one of the slices this lesion is adjacent\u000ato the black-inked posterior margin corresponding to the area of retraction.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of\u000aapproximately 90% yellow adipose tissue with 10% being interlacing white\u000afibrous bands.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: white fibrous mass lesion adjacent to posterior margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional representations of the mass, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: skin scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional representation of white fibrous mass with\u000arespect\u000ato deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - right breast skin", consists of two fragments of skin\u000a(3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There are no visible scars or\u000alesions present on the skin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: representative sections of right breast skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aROH/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/16/2005\u000a[report_end]
