VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST, ANTERIOR SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aB) LEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aCysts and usual ductal hyperplasia, (see note).\u000aC) LEFT BREAST MEDIAL SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aCysts and usual ductal hyperplasia.\u000aD) LEFT BREAST, INFERIOR SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aCysts and usual ductal hyperplasia.\u000aE) LEFT BREAST LATERAL SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aCysts and usual ductal hyperplasia, (see note).\u000aF) LEFT BREAST, POSTERIOR SURGICAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aResidual papilloma with marked cautery artifact.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: Extensive cautery artifact in all of the specimens limits the histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Status-post L breast excision biopsy outside hospital. Consult slides\u000asent and reviewed. Third review at BI. Left breast DCIS, S/P lumpectomy,\u000apositive unoriented margins.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision lumpectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - final anterior margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aB/2 - final superior margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aC/3 - final medial margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aD/4 - final inferior margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aE/5 - final lateral margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aF/6 - final posterior margin L breast - suture on new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - final anterior margin lt breast, suture on new margin",\u000aconsists of a tan/white, wrinkled skin fragment (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached\u000adense white/pink fibrous tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per surgeon, there is a\u000asuture on the epithelial surface (new anterior margin). The fibrous tissue is\u000ainked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the skin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - final superior margin lt breast, suture on new margin",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibrofatty tissue (2.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with a suture designating the\u000anew true margin (inked black). The opposite surface (not true margin) is inked\u000ablue. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit a firm yellow/tan cut\u000asurface with a focus of dense yellow/tan, gritty fibrous tissue (0.7 cm in\u000agreatest dimension) adjacent to the blue-inked surface. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - final medial margin left breast, suture on new margin",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of firm yellow/tan to tan/pink fibrofatty tissue\u000a(2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with a suture designating\u000athe new true medial margin (inked black). The opposite surface is inked blue\u000a(not true margin). The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit approximately\u000a40% dense pink/white fibrous tissue extending to both the blue and black inked\u000asurfaces and approximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted sequentially.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4 - final inferior margin L breast, stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of firm yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.1 cm), which is oriented per surgeon with a suture designating the new true\u000ainferior margin (inked black). The opposite surface (not true margin) is inked\u000ablue. The specimen is sectioned to exhibit greater than 95% focally\u000ahemorrhagic, yellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue with less than 5% delicate\u000afibrous tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted sequentially.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aPart E, labeled "#5 - final lateral margin lt breast, suture on new margin",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of firm yellow/tan to pink/tan fibrofatty tissue\u000a(2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with a suture designating\u000athe new true lateral margin (inked black). The opposite surface is composed of\u000atrabecular pink/tan, hyperemic fibrous tissue (presumed biopsy cavity, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.9 cm), and this surface (not true margin) is inked blue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to exhibit approximately 30% dense pink/white, gritty\u000afibrous tissue extending to both the blue and black inked surfaces, and\u000aapproximately 70% yellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart F, labeled "#6 - final posterior margin L breast, suture on new margin",\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of firm yellow/tan to pink/tan fibrofatty tissue\u000a(4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with one suture designating\u000athe new true posterior margin (inked black). The opposite surface (not true\u000amargin) exhibits trabecular pink/tan, focally hyperemic fibrous tissue (grossly\u000aconsistent with biopsy cavity, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked blue. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned to exhibit approximately 70% dense, gritty pink/white\u000afibrous tissue extending to both the blue and black inked surfaces and\u000aapproximately 30% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, ESS.\u000almb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Travis J Hollmann M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/7/2005\u000a[report_end]
