VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA M DURFEE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth M. Manion, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 12:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types, (low to intermediate\u000anuclear grade) is present.\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 42 year old with history of ADH in left breast presents today for core\u000abiopsy of cluster of calcifications in right breast at 12:00. Time in formalin\u000a9:50 am.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 5 mm, non-palpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper/inner (12:00 approximately).\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core biopsy (8 cores submitted) in two pink cassettes -\u000aA/with Ca++ and B/no Ca++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast", and consists of two labeled pink\u000acassettes. The first cassette, labeled "A calcifications", contains multiple\u000airregular tan/pink fibrofatty tissues (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which\u000aare submitted in toto. The second cassette, labeled "B" contains multiple\u000airregular fibrofatty tissues (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues in cassette labeled "A calcifications", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues in cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000almc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 05, 2009 at 01:02:59PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID was also performed which higlights\u000athe presence of myoepithelial cells lining ducts of DCIS and confirms that\u000athere is no evidence of an invasive component.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in < 30%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday August 07, 2009 at 03:11:36PM\u000a[report_end]
