VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (3 SPECIMENS)\u000a(INCLUDING FSA):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Present\u000aTypes Solid and cribriform\u000aNuclear grade Low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS: Present\u000aNecrosis in DCIS: Present\u000aMicroinvasion: Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS:\u000aEstimated overall size Approximately 1 cm measured on slide\u000aNumber of blocks/total REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS):\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with columnar cell change.\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) Mx\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Performed previously at BWH\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old female with a history of core biopsy dx L ADH REMOVED_DATE  On\u000a7/29/09 mammograms demonstrate R calcifications - REMOVED_DATE  stereotactic core\u000abiopsy revealed DCIS. ER/PR/Her2Mei(+).\u000aOperation: R simple mastectomy, sentinel node mapping, biopsy and possible\u000aaxillary dissection and reconstruction.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right sentinel node - hot + blue (fs).\u000aB/2) sentinel node R - hot + blue.\u000aC/3) right breast - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - RIGHT SENTINEL NODE - HOT + BLUE" (FSA):\u000aLymph node; negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D.\u000aResident: Elizabeth Morgan, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A is received in the frozen lab for intraoperative consultation and\u000alabeled, "right sentinel node hot and blue", consists of a fragment of\u000ayellow/tan firm soft tissue with attached fat consistent with a lymph node (1.7\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm overall). The lymph node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000alymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "right sentinel node hot and blue", consists of a tan/yellow irregular\u000afibrofatty tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which exhibits a tan/pink lymph node\u000a(2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "right breast", consists of a 378-g right simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(19.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (12.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aexhibits a tan areola (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and an everted nipple (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a tan/pink well-healed scar (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000anipple. The deep margin is intact and no skeletal muscle is identified; REMOVED_DATE cm\u000adeep to the scar is an ill-defined hemorrhagic area with focal areas of fat\u000anecrosis (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located 12 o'clock, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aThere is a silver metallic clip identified within the area. The remainder of\u000athe breast parenchyma is predominantly white and firm fibrous tissue (80%) and\u000ayellow fatty tissue (20%). The most lateral tissue is palpated; however, no\u000alymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hemorrhagic area to scar, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of hemorrhagic area to include area to deep margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000almc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 05:40:10PM\u000a[report_end]
