ic, white/tan fibrous\u000astroma admixed with approximately 95% yellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and dense/cystic fibrous stroma, multiple frags in each, RSS.\u000aFollowing initial histologic evaluation, the remaining fibrous tissue\u000are-examined and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibrous tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 R breast tissue (525 grams)", consists of multiple fragments of\u000afocally hemorrhagic, yellow/tan to tan/pink fibrofatty tissue admixed with\u000amultiple fragments of tan/white, wrinkled skin (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). The fragments are sectioned to exhibit approximately 5% focally\u000adense/cystic, white/tan fibrous stroma admixed with approximately 95%\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and focally dense/cystic fibrous stroma, multiple frags in\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aFollowing initial histologic evaluation, the remaining fibrous tissue\u000are-examined and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibrous tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
