VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: AYODALE S ODULATE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST LOWER INNER 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical papillary proliferation with associated calcifications (see NOTE).\u000aNOTE: This lesion is best evaluated after excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 69 y. o. female with group of punctate and amorphous Ca++ in right\u000alower inner breast. Please rule out malignancy.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: lower inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic. vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic, vacuum-assisted; A = specimen with Ca++; b = specimen\u000awithout Ca++ - Pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast, pink", and consists of multiple irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aA portion of the breast tissue cores received in a pink cassette marked with\u000a"A. Ca+2" and the remainder of the breast tissue cores are received in a pink\u000acassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if