tions). The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial showing dense, white fibrous tissue and fat\u000awith a 50:50 ratio and no obvious lesion. The specimen is submitted from\u000alateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: right breast tissue with presumed calcification in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000amulti frag, ESS.\u000aWP/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/23/2006\u000a[report_end]
