VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marian H Harris, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aColumnar cell change with atypia.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aMultiple cysts with associated dense stroma, cyst rupture, chronic\u000ainflammation.\u000aNumerous calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of all\u000afibrous tissue, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Status post biopsy at BWH on REMOVED_DATE  showing lobular carcinoma in\u000asitu. Surgical excision recommended for complete evaluation of lesion.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aLeft breast tissue at 1:00 - short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOGRAPH:\u000aSpecimen shows wire, clip and calcifications. OR called. Signed: S.R.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a6.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm ovoid fragment of fibrofatty tissue with two orienting sutures -\u000ashort stitch = superior, long stitch = lateral. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a needle-localization wire in-situ, which enters at the superior end\u000aand is embedded firmly in the parenchyma. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph with a circled area of a vague density with calcifications and a\u000aclip. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, respectively,\u000ashowing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm multicystic area in the mid portion of the\u000aspecimen, which contains gel pledgets and the metal clip. This cystic area is\u000a0.5 cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The rest\u000aof the cut surface shows dense, white fibrous tissue, comprising approximately\u000a20% of the parenchyma, most of which is located along the posterior aspect. A\u000amass lesion is not seen. All fibrous tissue is submitted from medial to\u000alateral, respectively, including the cystic area and all surrounding margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial to lateral sections with surrounding margins, multiple\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: All remaining fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS.\u000aWP/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/2/2006\u000a[report_end]
