VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE @ 12 O'CLOCK, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), with pagetoid\u000aspread.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis, cysts, intraductal papilloma, microscopic fibroadenoma\u000a(0.2 cm), calcifications in benign breast epithelium, columnar cell changes,\u000aepithelial hyperplasia, pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH).\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service), who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx of right breast mass @ 12 o'clock, core bx @HVMA REMOVED_DATE  showed\u000acyst, inflammation, calcs, excisional bx recommended by radiologist as imaging\u000anot felt to be concordant with path, mass no longer palpable after core bx,\u000apost bx u/s @BWH REMOVED_DATE  showed persistent REMOVED_DATE  cm mass @ 12 o'clock BWH\u000aradiology also recommended repeat bx\u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight breast tissue @ 12 o'clock, short=superior, long=lateral\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aTarget wire in specimen. OR called.\u000a---SR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 R needle directed bx", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(6.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two orienting sutures (short=superior, long=lateral)\u000aand a needle localization wire in place (entering at the lateral aspect). The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000arevealing a focus of white-pale yellow, cystic, focally necrotic, focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrous tissue (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly extends to the\u000aposterior, medial, and superior margins and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000anearest lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin. A hemorrhagic\u000apurulent cavity (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present within this fibrous area,\u000acontains green-tan purulent exudate, and is adjacent to the needle localization\u000awire. This is consistent with a previous biopsy site, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and\u000a3.5 cm from the lateral margin. There are two accompanying radiographs that\u000ademonstrate a wire localized within an area of increased density. The remaining\u000abreast tissue consists predominantly of yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The\u000afibrous tissue is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: cystic fibrous area, sequentially from medial to lateral,\u000amultiple frags, ESS (Note: probable previous biopsy site in Micros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.)\u000aDFI/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/4/2006\u000a[report_end]
