VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.; Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, BIOPSY":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, small foci (see NOTE).\u000aPrior core biopsy site changes.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Only three minute foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia are present, each\u000ainvolving only a single duct profile. Two of these are adjacent to the biopsy\u000asite (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, seen only on original slide and not on deeper levels, and on\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and are not near any margin. The third is away from the biopsy\u000asite and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, seen only on the\u000aoriginal slide and not on deeper levels).\u000aDr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed the case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast Bx; short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass, biopsy clip, and intact hookwire are seen in the specimen. Dr. Iglehart\u000awas notified of these findings at 3:30 p.m. by Dr. I. Khan and Dr. C. Denison.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "R breast; short superior, long lateral", and consists of a tan yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (6.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture\u000adesignating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral\u000amargin. There is a needle localization wire in place, entering through the\u000alateral anterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial orange, anterior\u000ablue, and posterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aThere is an irregular hemorrhagic lesion with surrounding dense white fibrous\u000atissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. There is a metallic clip located within the hemorrhagic lesion\u000acorrelating with the radiograph received with the specimen. Remainder of the\u000abreast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with no additional lesions or\u000aareas of disruption identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire biopsy cavity and surrounding breast parenchyma, blocks\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include slice with the metallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Uninvolved breast parenchyma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 4890.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
