VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Douglas I. Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aSmall residual focus of an atypical epithelial proliferation (0.2 cm in size),\u000aadjacent to prior biopsy site, see NOTE.\u000aExtensive calcifications associated with normal lobules, columnar cell change\u000awith small cysts and lactational change.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNote: An area of ducts and lobules (0.2 cm in diameter, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is present\u000ainvolved by the same atypical proliferation seen in the core biopsy\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reviewed). In contrast to the core biopsy where a lobule (< REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain diameter) is completely involved by a clonal appearing population of\u000aatypical cells associated with calcifications, the residual ducts seen in this\u000aexcision are partially involved and not associated with calcifications.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH - right breast; microca++\u000aOperation: Not specified.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: As above.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast biopsy after needle loc. - long suture = lateral, short\u000asuture = superior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number, and "#1. Right breast biopsy after needle localization, long\u000asuture lateral, short suture superior", and consists of an 18-gram wire\u000alocalized excisional breast biopsy specimen (4.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior). The specimen is oriented\u000awith a long stitch designating lateral, and a short stitch designating superior\u000aas per surgeon. The specimen is inked as follows: superior-red,\u000ainferior-green, anterior-blue, posterior-black, medial-orange and\u000alateral-yellow. The specimen contains a localization wire entering the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the inferior lateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reviewed in centricity shows a wire, clip and\u000acalcifications in the specimen. The specimen contains a tan/white/red\u000ahemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with a previous biopsy site,\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. A clip is identified in the\u000acentral portion of this lesion, in the posterior aspect of the specimen. The\u000aremainder of the specimen is composed of 20% fibrous tissue and 80% adipose\u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted to include perpendicular sections\u000aof all margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast biopsy entirely submitted medially to laterally, with the\u000aarea containing the clip in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aDIL/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 10, 2009 at 03:43:18PM\u000a[report_end]
