s\u000awithin the specimen. There are associated calcifications more towards the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned in\u000athirteen slices going medial to lateral. The clip is identified in slice #6\u000aand is located from margins as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm superior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm lateral. Associated\u000awith the clip are biopsy site changes (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located from margins\u000aas follows: REMOVED_DATE cm superior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm lateral. No distinct mass is associated\u000awith the clip other than the biopsy site changes. The specimen is\u000aapproximately 20% fibrous and 80% adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, medial margin perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, anterior aspect, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, posterior portion with clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, anterior portion with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, anterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, anterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, anterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, anterior aspect, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, posterior aspect, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #13 with lateral perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aGL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Sunday February 22, 2009 at 01:04:05PM\u000a[report_end]
