le yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Anterior right breast", contains two yellow cassettes. The first\u000ayellow cassette, labeled "A. Ca++", contains multiple tan/yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue cores (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second yellow cassette\u000alabeled "B" contains multiple yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue cores (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/18/2006\u000a[report_end]
