VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL, WIRE LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR CLIPS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47-year-old female with three sites of calcifications and atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia bordering on DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID wires.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast lateral wire localized excisional biopsy; short\u000astitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast medial wire x2, localized excisional biopsy; short\u000asuture/superior, long suture/lateral (mammography).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and wire in specimen. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aTwo specimens were received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aSpecimen 1, "#1. Right breast lateral wire", consists of a wire localized\u000abreast excision (4.6 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior), with a short suture marking\u000athe superior margin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. The\u000alocalization wire enters the specimen at the lateral side. An accompanying\u000aspecimen radiography demonstrates the localization wire next to a clip and a\u000asmall cluster of punctate calcifications within an irregular radiodense area.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned into twelve slices from lateral to\u000amedial. The specimens contains a white fibrous area in slices #6 to #9 (1.6 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin,\u000a0.5 cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000amedial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin. This fibrous area contains a\u000abiopsy site with a clip in slice #7. Additional diffuse white fibrous areas\u000aare present in slice #5, #10, and #11. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, fibrous area with biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, superior, inferior, and posterior margins, 3 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, fibrous area (containing clips), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 with fibrous area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 with fibrous area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 and slice #5, fibrous area, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aSpecimen 2, "#2. Right breast medial wire x2, localized excisional biopsy,\u000ashort suture/superior, long suture/lateral", consists a wire localized breast\u000aexcision (7.6 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, and\u000a3.8 cm superior to inferior), with a short suture marking the superior and a\u000along suture marking lateral. The specimen contains two localization wires; one\u000aentering the specimen at the medial/posterior side, the second one entering the\u000aspecimen at the inferior side. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates two localization wires, both adjacent to a clip. The second wire\u000ais placed adjacent to a radiodense area with a possible punctate calcification.\u000aThe specimen is inked per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned into eighteen slices. A clip is\u000apresent in slice #3 within an area of yellow fat necrosis (0.2 cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin. A specimen radiograph is taken to locate the second clip.\u000aThe radiograph shows the second clip in slice #9. It is located within an area\u000aof gray/white fibrous tissue, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. No distinct\u000amasses are present. The specimen is composed of yellow, lobulated adipose\u000atissue (90%), and diffuse area of fibrosis (10%), focally with small cysts. All\u000aof the fibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 (with clip), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous areas, slices #10 to #12, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous areas, slice #12, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous areas, slices #13 and #15, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aSTS/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-3750.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a1/31/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM\u000aA AND B. RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL, WIRE LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR CLIPS:\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThe diagnoses are unchanged.\u000aAddendum #1 by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2007\u000a[report_end]
