s received to pathology freely floating within the specimen container.\u000aSectioning demonstrates focal hemorrhage and possible fat necrosis in the area\u000asurrounding the embedded metallic clip (hemorrhagic area is REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension and abuts the superior and medial margins). There are no obvious\u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities, grossly. The remaining specimen\u000aexhibits REMOVED_DATE % tan/white fibrodense tissue, without additional discrete\u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities. The entire specimen is submitted,\u000asequentially from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire specimen (area of interest in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 9079.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a3/8/2007\u000a[report_end]
