y cystic white to tan fibrous tissue, with the remainder composed\u000aof yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are\u000aidentified. There are multiple punctate areas of hemorrhage (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension) surrounding the needle localization wire. The specimen is\u000aentirely sequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially submitted, with perpendicular undesignated\u000amargins in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000almb/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
