uals orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior into nine slices\u000a(anterior margin as slice #1 and posterior margin as slice #9), revealing\u000amultifocally hemorrhagic breast tissue with an ill-defined tan/pink/white\u000afibrotic area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) at the posterior/medial margin and abuts the\u000asuperior, inferior, and posterior margins grossly. The metal clip is\u000aidentified grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, anterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 and #3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 and #5, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 and #7, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, the posterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, ESS.\u000aQY/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
