 specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast pink top, white bottom 11:50 a.m.", consists of\u000amultiple yellow-white focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with pink tops. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 02, 2009 at\u000a12:58:07PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 03:28:14PM\u000a[report_end]
