VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin bx cyst, tag, or debridement\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINA ZABICKI CALVILLO M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST SCAR":\u000aSkin with scarring.\u000aFibroadipose tissue with scarring and foreign body giant cell reaction to\u000apolarizable material consistent with suture.\u000aResidual breast tissue is present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #1" (including FSA):\u000aOne (1) Lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aThree (3) H&E levels examined.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST":\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aRadial scar with epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000asclerosing adenosis associated with microcalcifications.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSkin and nipple with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: The microcalcifications identified on imaging (by report) likely\u000acorrelate to the extensive adenosis identified in this specimen. A "negative"\u000abiopsy of this area was reportedly performed, but no biopsy site changes are\u000aidentified. Clinical correlation is suggested.\u000aThis portion of the case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology\u000aService, who concurs.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2" (including FSB):\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aThree (3) H&E levels examined.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST SKIN TISSUE":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 y o female with history of left breast CA presenting today for\u000aprophylactic right breast mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, sentinel node biopsy, bilateral pedicle\u000aTram breast reconstruction.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast scar.\u000aB/2) Right axillary sentinel lymph node #1 --> FS.\u000aC/3) Right breast - stitch - long - lateral, short - superior.\u000aD/4) Right axillary sentinel lymph node #2 --> FS.\u000aE/5) Right breast skin tissue.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #1" (FSA);\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aArrival time: 4:33 PM\u000aReport time: 4:50 PM\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "4. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2" (FSB):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aArrival time: 17:16\u000aReport time: 5:36 PM\u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D.\u000aEDMUND SAULIUS CIBAS, M.D.\u000aResident: STEPHANIE SCHULTE, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A is received in two containers, both of which are labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aOne of the containers is labeled "#1. Left breast scar" and contains four\u000airregular portions of skin and underlying soft tissue (ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm, to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimens are sectioned to reveal an\u000aunremarkable cut surface.\u000aThe second container is labeled "#1. Left breast scar cont B" and consists of\u000atwo irregular unremarkable fragments of skin and underlying adipose tissue\u000a(measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The larger portion of\u000askin displays a surgical staple. The specimen are serially sectioned to reveal\u000aunderlying yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and underlying adipose tissue from container labeled "#1.\u000aLeft breast scar", 3 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and underlying adipose tissue from container labeled "#1. Left\u000abreast scar cont B", 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #1", consists of an\u000airregular portion of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), in\u000awhich a thin rubbery lymph node is identified (2.0 cm). The lymph node is\u000abisected, and is submitted in its entirety for frozen section as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Right breast stitch, long lateral, short superior",\u000aconsists of a right mastectomy (1334 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long\u000asuture designating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is\u000aan overlying, unremarkable nipple-areolar complex (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with an\u000aeverted nipple (1.4 cm in diameter). The posterior margin is inked black and\u000athe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a pink, chalky yellow stellate\u000aarea (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), within the lower inner quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to\u000athe nipple at the 6 o'clock position and REMOVED_DATE cm from the black inked posterior\u000amargin. The remaining cut surface displays 50% dense white, focally nodular\u000aand cystic fibrous tissue, and 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, with the\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the stellate area in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, mult frags RSS\u000a(stellate area, ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #2", consists of an\u000airregular portion of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), in\u000awhich a pink/tan rubbery lymph node is identified (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000ais bisected and submitted in its entirety for frozen section as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Rt breast skin tissue", consists of multiple irregular\u000aportions of tan/pink unremarkable skin fragments with underlying fibrofatty\u000atissue (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimens are serially sectioned\u000ato reveal underlying yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses\u000aor lesions identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/17/2007\u000a[report_end]
