VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Javad Beheshti, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA with associated calcifications (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSclerosing adenosis and fibrocytic changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications seen associated with benign epithelium.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFEROLATERAL SHAVED MARGIN":\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present.\u000aSclerosing adenosis and fibrocystic changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications seen associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE:\u000aDr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, also reviewed the slides and concurs\u000awith the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67-year-old woman with L breast mammogram on REMOVED_DATE  revealing cluster\u000aof microcalcifications in deep central L breast, not amenable to core.\u000aOperation: L breast WL box.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Lt breast tissue; short suture - superior; long suture - lateral; whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin (mammo)\u000aB/2) Inferolateral shaved margin; whip stitch, new margin (mammo)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen with wire - no suspicious lesion. Specimen without wire\u000a1/2 linear calcifications may be part of cluster in question. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. LT breast tissue, short suture superior, long suture lateral,\u000awhipstitch on chest wall margin", consists of an ovoid tan/yellow breast\u000aexcision (4.2 S-I x REMOVED_DATE M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm) which is oriented per surgeon as\u000afollows, short equals superior, long equals lateral, whipstitch equals chest\u000awall margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. A needle-localization wire is not present\u000awithin the specimen or the specimen container. The specimen was previously\u000aradiograph, confirming the presence of calcification in the periphery of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit\u000aapproximately 90% yellow/tan adipose tissue and 10% delicate pink/tan fibrous\u000astroma. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly suctioned, multi frags in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from lateral to medial (probable area of\u000acalcification in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Inferolateral shaved margin, whip stitch new margin", consists of\u000aan irregular multifocally disrupted fragment of yellow/tan breast tissue (3.8 x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per surgeon, one surface of the specimen exhibits a whipstitch,\u000adesignating the new true margin (inked black per prosector). The opposite\u000anon-sutured surface is inked blue (blue does not equal true margin). A\u000aneedle-localization wire is received separately free-floating within the\u000aspecimen container. The specimen was previously radiographed, with no masses\u000aor calcifications identified. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit\u000agreater than 90% yellow/tan adipose tissue and less than 10% pink/tan fibrous\u000astroma which extends to the black inked new true margin. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are grossly identified. Also received in the specimen container are\u000atwo irregular fragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate) with unremarkable cut surfaces.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Shave margin, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Separate tissue fragment, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
