VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR RESIDUAL CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications and multifocal cyst rupture.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aPapilloma.\u000aExcision site changes.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67 year old woman, S/P L breast excision REMOVED_DATE  revealing ADH - and\u000aS/P inferolateral shave margin revealing ADH - mammo REMOVED_DATE  revealed residual\u000aclustered calcifications in LIQ with excision recommended. Previous surgery:\u000a5/30/08 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: L breast WK exc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Same.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short = superior, long = lateral, whipstitch = chest\u000awall margin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCa++ in specimen. Hookwire present. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whipstitch/chest wall\u000amargin", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (4.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating\u000asuperior margin, a long suture designating margin, and a whip stitch\u000adesignating the posterior margin. There is a needle localization wire in place\u000awhich enters through the inferior aspect of the specimen and exits through the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000a(superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue,\u000aand posterior/black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. There\u000ais a focal ill-defined dense white fibrous area (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aabuts the anterior, posterior, and inferior margins, comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. The remainder of the cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous with no\u000adiscrete lesions grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include focal dense\u000awhite fibrous areas corresponding to areas of calcification on the specimen\u000aradiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/02/08):\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy including examination of margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
