VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, PROPHYLACTIC TOTAL MASTECTOMY" (1480g):\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, apocrine cysts,\u000aand giant cell reaction with hemosiderin-laden macrophages\u000aconsistent with a ruptured cyst.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, BIOPSY":\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT MASTECTOMY SCAR, EXCISION":\u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT MASTECTOMY SKIN, EXCISION":\u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor.\u000aE. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT MASTECTOMY SKIN, EXCISION":\u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of contralateral breast cancer - elevated risk L breast\u000acancer.\u000aOperation: L prophylactic total mastectomy, bilat breast reconstruction, DIEP\u000aFlaps.\u000aOperative Findings: Normal-appearing breast - 2 nodes in tail of breast.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: History of right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast - short/superior, long/lateral (1485).\u000aB/2) non-sentinel nodes (tail of breast).\u000aC/3) rt mastectomy scar.\u000aD/4) left mastectomy skin.\u000aE/5) right mastectomy skin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast short superior, long lateral, 1480", consists of a\u000aleft simple mastectomy (1480 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is an\u000aoverlying tan-pink irregular skin (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm), displaying focal areas of\u000ablue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye. There is an unremarkable nipple\u000aareolar complex (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a slightly inverted nipple (1.2 cm in\u000adiameter). The posterior margin is inked black and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal 60% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 40% focally dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. A\u000atan-pink possible rubbery lymph node is identified within the upper outer\u000aquadrant (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant dense white fibrous tissue, with the\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include\u000athe black-inked posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, to include\u000athe posterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tan-pink lymph node from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Nonsentinel node", consists of two tan-pink rubber lymph nodes\u000a(0.5 cm, and REMOVED_DATE cm), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. RT mastectomy scar", consists of a tan-pink unremarkable wrinkled\u000airregular skin (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A discrete mass or lesion is not\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Left mastectomy skin", consists of two tan-pink irregular wrinkled\u000aportions of skin (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000asecond described portion of skin displays a pink vesicle (0.4 cm). No\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions are identified. Representative sections\u000aare submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Unremarkable tan-pink irregular skin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tan-pink skin with vesicle (inked blue), 2 frags, RSS (vesicle ESS).\u000aPart E, "#5. Right mastectomy skin", consists of an unremarkable irregular\u000atan-pink skin (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE (depth) cm). A discrete mass or lesion is not\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/20/2008\u000a[report_end]
