cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast posterior", consists of multiple yellow/white focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are\u000areceived in two brown cassettes labeled "A. Ca2+" and "B". The specimens are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast anterior", consists of multiple yellow/white focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are\u000areceived in two yellow cassettes labeled "A. Ca2+" and "B". The specimens are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca2+", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/25/2008\u000a[report_end]
