VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP":\u000aSevere atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on DCIS, very close\u000a(<0.1 cm) to the posterior margin in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; see NOTE.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is associated with calcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site changes extending to posterior and inferior\u000amargins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aNOTE:\u000aA re-excision is recommended for further evaluation and to rule out a more\u000asevere lesion. The case was reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, Breast\u000aPathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 39 year old female with left breast core biopsy revealing atypia, on\u000aoutside called DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized lobectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast wire localized lumpectomy, short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcs/intact wire/clip (displaced from site of bx'd calcs). Called to Dr.\u000aGolshan by Dr. Ritner @ 11:50 on REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Left breast wire localized lumpectomy, short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral", and consists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 cm\u000asuperior inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior posterior).\u000aThere are two orienting sutures with short designating superior and long\u000adesignating lateral per surgeon. A radiograph accompanies the specimen showing\u000aa wire entering the lateral aspect of the specimen marking a clip and a\u000aseparate area of calcification. The clip is towards the lateral and inferior\u000aaspect of the specimen while the area of calcification is towards the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen according to the radiograph. The specimen is sectioned\u000ain 12 slices going lateral to medial and a clip is identified in slice #4\u000alocated from margins as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm superior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm posterior. Associated with\u000athe clip is a white area (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is possible Gelfoam\u000amaterial and located from margins as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm superior, abutting\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm posterior.\u000aThe white area is in slices #3, #4, and #5. Area of calcification is in slices\u000a#8-#11. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 lateral margin perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 with whitish area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 with clip and whitish area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 with whitish area, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12 with medial margin perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aGL/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/13/2008\u000a[report_end]
