ter of calcifications. REMOVED_DATE \u000astereotactic core biopsy revealed solid and cribriform, ER/PR (+) her 2/Neu(-)\u000aDCIS (LCIS was in LLOQ).\u000aOperation: L simple mastectomy, sentinel lymph node biopsy with possible Level\u000aI & II dissections; R prophylactic mastectomy.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast - Stitch, short - superior; long - lateral.\u000aB/2) Left sentinal lymph node (hot ^ not blue) - FS.\u000aC/3) Left sentinel lymph node (hot & blue) - F.S.\u000aD/4) Left breast - stitch, short - superior; long - lateral.\u000aE/5) Old scar, right breast.\u000aF/6) Additional skin margin, left breast site.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSA):\u000aThree lymph nodes, negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Alessandra F. Nascimento, M.D.\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast - stitch short superior - long lateral", consists of\u000aa 360 gram simple mastectomy specimen (17.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior), areolar complex (7.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), and an inverted nipple (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep resection margin is lined\u000aby fascia, which is focally disrupted and inked black. The specimen consists\u000aof 50% breast tissue and 50% adipose tissue. An irregular area of fibrosis is\u000alocated behind the nipple (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and extends to the deep\u000aresection margin. No gross lesions are identified. Representative sections\u000aare submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Areas of fibrosis behind nipple, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left sentinel lymph node (hot blue) FS", consists of three\u000atan/pink lymph nodes and adipose tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Lymph node #2 is inked black. The two largest lymph\u000anodes are bisected and three lymph nodes are entirely submitted as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left sentinel lymph node (hot and blue) - FS", consists of one\u000atan/pink lymph node (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and attached adipose tissue. The\u000alymph node is bisected and entirely submitted as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Left breast - stitch shot superior, long lateral", consists of 498\u000agrams simple mastectomy specimen (18.3 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial\u000ato lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior), with areolar complex (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), and everted nipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep resection margin is bound by\u000afascia, which is focally disrupted and inked black. Upon sectioning, the\u000aspecimen contains 60% breast parenchyma and 40% adipose tissue with extensive\u000afibrosis. A clip is identified at 6 o'clock at REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep resection\u000amargin. A second clip is identified at 2 o'clock in the upper outer quadrant\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep resection margin. Both clips are surrounded by areas of\u000afibrosis. Representative sections are submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip at 2 o'clock, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant fibrosis adjacent to the 2 o'clock clip, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip at 6 o'clock, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrosis adjacent to clip at 6 o'clock, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma upper lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma inner outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2:00 tissue, 4 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6:00 tissue, 4 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Additional scar right breast", consists of fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with firm fibrosed surface on one\u000aside and adipose tissue on the opposite side. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned and submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast tissue, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart F, "#6. Additional skin margin - left breast side", consists of two skin\u000afragments (#1 REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm; and #2 REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The fragments\u000aare sectioned and entirely submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fragment #1, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fragment #2, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aKST/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 08, 2009 at 11:49:09AM\u000a[report_end]
