\u000ainked and representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "right breast tissue expander", consists of an intact tan/white\u000adiscoid device consistent with a tissue expander (11.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000ais filled with a clear liquid to gel-like material. The device displays the\u000ainscription Allergan, Style 133 MV, REMOVED_DATE cm - 300 cc lot REMOVED_CASE_ID. There is no\u000aattached soft tissue. No sections are submitted. The specimen is for gross\u000aidentification only.\u000aPart D, labeled "left breast tissue expander", consists of an intact tan/pink\u000adiscoid medical device consistent with a tissue expander (11.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is filled with a clear liquid to gel-like material. The device\u000adisplays the inscription Allergan, Style 133 MV, REMOVED_DATE cm - 300 cc lot REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aThere is no attached soft tissue. No sections are submitted. The specimen is\u000afor gross identification only.\u000aPart E, labeled "left breast core biopsy site", consists of an unoriented\u000airregular tan/white skin (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aexhibits an irregular tan/pink scar (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aclosest margin. The specimen is inked, bisected, and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000almc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrew M. Bellizzi M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 10, 2009 at 05:10:22PM\u000a[report_end]
