 aspect of the specimen. The wire tip is associated\u000awith a clip and core biopsy site (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a white/yellow\u000afirm fibrosis/lesion surrounding the biopsy cavity (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000adistance to the margin as follows: posterior REMOVED_DATE cm, superior REMOVED_DATE cm, inferior\u000a1.0 cm, anterior REMOVED_DATE cm, lateral REMOVED_DATE cm, and medial REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of\u000athe specimen consists of 80% unremarkable white/tan fibrous tissue and 20%\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to\u000amedial and entirely submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from lateral to medial, 2 blocks per slice\u000a(biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aDH/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 10:51:26AM\u000a[report_end]
