1 is located predominantly at the inferior margin, while\u000aneedle localization wire #2 is located predominantly at the superior margin.\u000aThe specimen is inked by the prosector per pathology protocol as the\u000aanterior/blue, posterior/black, superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow\u000aand medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000ato reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a clip\u000a(as displayed on the accompanying radiograph). This cavity is located towards\u000aneedle localization wire #2, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. The remaining cut surface consists of 90% yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue and 10% white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from medial to lateral, with the cavity\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with a clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the area of calcifications on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009 at 05:12:05PM\u000a[report_end]
