esignating lateral, a short\u000asuture designating superior, and whip suture designating chest wall margin\u000a(posterior). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol by the prosector as\u000aanterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow,\u000aand medial orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a densely\u000awhite/pink cut surface extending to all inked margins. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aCP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday May 15, 2009 at 03:36:43PM\u000a[report_end]
