m size (site #1). This\u000arepresents MRI bx of 7 mm focal area of enhancement L mid upper breast (site\u000a#2). Solid 7 mm hypoechoic mass left subareolar breast at 9:00 region (site\u000a#3).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 8 mm, non-palpable, focal and non-mass forming on MRI (site #1).\u000a2. Left: 7 mm, non-palpable, focal and non-mass forming on MRI (site #2).\u000a3. Left: 7 mm, non-palpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass on ultrasound\u000a(site #3).\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper/inner (site #1).\u000a2. Left: 12:00 (site #2).\u000a3. Left: 9:00 region (site #3).\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8G MRI and vacuum-assisted (site #1).\u000a2. 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted (site #2).\u000a3. 14G Ultrasound (site #3).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core biopsy in three cassettes with white bottoms/blue tops\u000ain formalin @ 9:40 am (site #1)\u000aB/2) Left breast core biopsy in three cassettes with white bottoms/green tops\u000a(site #2)\u000aC/3) Left breast core biopsy in 4 samples in a white cassette (site #3).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in three parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "blue top, white bottom right breast site 2 formalin 9:35\u000aa.m.", consists of multiple white-yellow fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with blue top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "green top, white bottom left breast site #1 formalin 9:45\u000aa.m.", consists of multiple white-yellow fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with green top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "left breast white", consists of multiple yellow-white\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000awhite cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009\u000aat 04:33:53PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 15, 2009 at 03:01:56PM\u000a[report_end]
