VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 11:32 CLINICAL DATA: Calcifications in left breast. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH CALCIFICATIONS (SEE TABLE 1). DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, HIGH NUCLEAR GRADE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. CALCIFICATIONS INVOLVING BENIGN BREAST EPITHELIUM. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA The tumor is predominantly in-situ with a small invasive component. Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Focally present (slide A). Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin of the specimen in one focus. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within the region of the mass. Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: 3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin of the specimen in one focus. Stains for receptors: Requested. Diagnosis by: JOSEPH T. RABBAN, M.D., M.P.H. Signed On: 02 MAY 04 at 11:12 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block B): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Rosemary Tambouret,MD Signed On: 06 MAY 04 at 17:36 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block B): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Rosemary Tambouret,MD Signed On: 06 MAY 04 at 17:36 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast biopsy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular tan-yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect. The superior aspect is inked blue, the inferior-black, the medial-green and lateral-yellow. The specimen is sequentially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a tan-yellow to pink lobulated unremarkable cut surface. The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted from anterior to posterior in cassettes A-E with the anterior margin in cassette A and the posterior margin in cassette E and the area denoted by the localization wire in cassettes B-C. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: ANDRAS SCHAFFER, MD,PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART : BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
