haracteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 29 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13:07 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node axilla level 1" are 2 tan-pink lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm, with minimal attached tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue. Both nodes are bisected and submitted entirely as A and B, respectively. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast lumpectomy, short superior, long lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with 2 stitches designating the superior and lateral margins. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior blue, the medial yellow, and the lateral orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm indurated gray-white stellate mass, which comes to REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margins. The remaining cut surface is 5% gray-white fibrous and 95% tan-yellow lobular fibroadipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: C: Superior margin, radially sectioned. D-F: Tumor submitted entirely from superior to inferior. G: Inferior margin, radially sectioned. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final margin inferior-lateral half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments with no orientation. The 