VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON: 30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11:10 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast lobular carcinoma, in-situ. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, FOCAL. LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA AND ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYERPLASIA, FOCAL. NOTE: The resection margins are free of tumor. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS, APROCRINE METAPLASIA, AND MICROCYST FORMATION. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: G. Richard Dickersin, M.D. Signed On: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13:12 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, with the patient's name and unit number, labelled "right breast" is a simple mastectomy with a 16 x 5 cm skin ellipse, excised to a depth of 5 cm. A biopsy scar on the right breast is designated as being in the right superior lateral position relative to the nipple. 2 cm posterior to the biopsy site which is 3 cm right lateral/superior to the nipple is a biopsy site of containing firm, tan, focally hemorrhagic tissue. This biopsy cavity and firm tissue is approximately 3 x 2 x 3 cm. The parenchyma medial to the biopsy site is white, firm admixed with yellow adipose tissue. SECTION CODE: A-D: lateral, superior, medial and inferior margins, respectively. E-J: parenchyma near and around biopsy site. K-M: additional representative parenchyma, right breast. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, labeled "Left breast", is a simple mastectomy with a 16 x 8 mm skin ellipse excised to a depth of 4 to 5 cm. The nipple is 1 cm in average dimension and is grossly unremarkable as is the skin. The parenchyma is white and firm interlaced with fat. The white firm parenchyma contains multiple small cysts, varying in size up to 2 mm. The cysts contain light pink, otherwise clear fluid. Ten representative sections of the parenchyma are submitted. SECTION CODE: N-W: representative parenchyma, left breast X-AA: lateral, superior, medial, inferior margins, respectively BB: nipple, left breast CC: scar, right breast DD: nipple, right breast Resident: Rex Neal Smith, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Edwin Lee Carter, M.D. John D Mitchell, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT) PART B: BREAST (LEFT)\u000a[report_end]
