VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10:46 CLINICAL DATA: Strong family history of breast cancer. Patient has breast reduction in REMOVED_MONTH 2003. At that time, lobular carcinoma in situ was diagnosed. CA-125 was 73. Please rule out fat necrosis on left breast lump. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA), MICROSCOPIC FOCUS, PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED MARGIN. 2. FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 4. FAT NECROSIS. ADNEXA (RIGHT), EXCISION: OVARY: EPITHELIAL INCLUSION GLANDS. CORPORA ALBICANTIA. FALLOPIAN TUBE: CYSTIC WALTHARD REST. ADNEXA (LEFT), EXCISION: OVARY: EPITHELIAL INCLUSION GLANDS WITH FOCAL MILD CYTOLOGIC ATYPIA. CORPORA ALBICANTIA. FALLOPIAN TUBE: WALTHARD RESTS. UTERUS, HYSTERECTOMY: CERVIX: FOLLICULAR CERVICITIS. PARAKERATOSIS WITH REACTIVE CHANGES AND IMMATURE SQUAMOUS METAPLASIA. TUNNEL CLUSTERS. ENDOMETRIUM: INACTIVE ENDOMETRIUM. MYOMETRIUM: LEIOMYOMA. ADENOMYOSIS. SEROSA: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. Note: The breast specimen was diagnosed by Drs. Joseph Rabban and Frederick Koerner. Diagnosis by: Debra Ann Bell, M.D. Signed On: 28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 18:08 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast biopsy", are two portions of unoriented firm fibroadipose tissue, measuring 4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Both specimens are inked entirely in black. The smaller specimen is sectioned to reveal predominantly adipose tissue, with a focal area of increased firmness and fibrous tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, that abuts the inked margin. Representative sections of this area are submitted in A-C, with further sections of the smaller piece as D and E. Sectioning of the larger piece reveals predominantly adipose tissue, with a focal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of tan-white fibrosis. Representative sections of the fibrotic areas are submitted in F and G, with additional representative sections in H-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right adnexa", is a right adnexa specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow cerebriform ovary, and a REMOVED_DATE cm in length x REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter fimbriated fallopian tube. Sectioning of the ovary reveals a yellow-white heterogeneous cut surface, without nodules or masses. The ovary is submitted entirely in K-M. Sectioning of the fallopian tube reveals a closed, unremarkable lumen. The fallopian tube is submitted entirely in N. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left adnexa", is a left adnexa consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow cerebriform ovary, and a REMOVED_DATE cm length of fimbriated fallopian tube with a diameter of REMOVED_DATE cm. Sectioning of the ovary reveals a tan-yellow to tan-white heterogeneous cut surface containing several corpora albicantia. The ovary is submitted entirely in O-Q. Sectioning of the fallopian tube reveals a closed unremarkable lumen. The fallopian tube is submitted entirely in R. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "uterus and cervix", is a REMOVED_DATE gram, 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm uterus. The exocervix measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, and contains a REMOVED_DATE cm slit shaped os. The uterus is opened at 9 o'clock and 3 o'clock to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm endocervical canal with a tan-white herringbone cut surface, with adherent tan-yellow mucoid material. The uterus measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and contains a triangular endometrial cavity measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Sectioning of the uterus and cervix reveals a maximal endometrial thickness of REMOVED_DATE cm, and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white, well circumscribed nodule located within the submucosal region of the posterior myometrium. The remainder of the myometrium is tan-pink and rubbery, without nodules or abnormalities. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows: S: Anterior cervix. T: Posterior cervix. U: Anterior uterus. V: Posterior uterus with myometrial nodule. Resident: ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Linda Anne Duska, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: ADNEXA(RIGHT),EXCISION PART C: ADNEXA(LEFT),EXCISION PART D: UTERUS, HYSTERECTOMY
