VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15:29 CLINICAL DATA: Left core biopsy showed invasive carcinoma. Now also with medial calcifications in the lumpectomy specimen. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. SEE TABLE 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU WITH NECROSIS. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: Multiple independent foci of invasive tumor are present, ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm in the lateral breast (site of localization wires) , REMOVED_DATE cm in the medial breast (site of additional localization wires), to several smaller independent foci scattered between these largest areas of invasion. Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Present. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: The dominant area of invasive tumor in the lateral portion of the specimen is focally positive at the inferior margin and extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus. Another focus of invasive tumor in the medial portion of the specimen focally approaches within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin. An additional microfocus of invasive tumor in the medial specimen is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within and beyond the region of the mass. Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: 3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Stains for receptors: Requested on block E. LYMPH NODE (LEFT, "PRIMARY" AXILLA SENTINEL), BIOPSY: METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES. SEE NOTE NOTE: The metastatic deposit (1 cm) replaces the node and extends into the extranodal adipose extensively. LYMPH NODE (LEFT, "SECONDARY" AXILLA SENTINEL), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE. LYMPH NODE (LEFT, "TERTIARY", AXILLA SENTINEL), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE. Diagnosis by: JOSEPH T. RABBAN, M.D., M.P.H. Signed On: 31 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16:36 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block E): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15:17 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast lumpectomy", is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x 9 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibrofatty breast parenchyma with four needle localization wires, two in the medial portion of the specimen and two in the lateral portion of the specimen. A bow-tie designates the cephalad margin, a short suture denotes the inferior margin, and a long suture denotes the lateral margin. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, and inferior - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white, stellate, and firm region in the lateral portion of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. This area is in the region of two of the needle localization wires. Also noted in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm region denoted by two needle localization wires in the medial portion of the specimen which show a focally calcified and fibrotic region. Also within this region, there are focal small, round, tan-yellow areas which appear to represent caseous necrosis. There is no distinct mass identified. The intervening breast parenchyma is tan-white, focally fibrous, and predominant fibrofatty. Photographs of the specimen have been taken. Representative sections are submitted as per section code. Section Code: A-D: REMOVED_DATE cm nodule in lateral breast. E-G: Intervening unremarkable appearing-breast parenchyma. H-P: Calcifications denoted by medial localization wires. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "primary sentinel node #150", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm node. In addition, a smaller firm region of possibly hemorrhagic fat is noted in the specimen. The largest lymph node is bisected to reveal a tan-white and focally fatty cut surface with scattered punctate red foci. This largest bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette Q, the remainder fibrofatty tissue and smaller nodular region are submitted into cassette R. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "secondary sentinel node #80", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggegrate of yellow fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node. The lymph node and attached fibrofatty tissue are entirely submitted into cassette S. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "tertiary sentinel node #79", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm lymph node with a fibrofatty and focally tan-pink cut surface. The bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette T and U and the remainder of the fibrofatty tissue is entirely submitted into cassette V. Resident: PAUL MICHAELS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE(LEFT PRIMARY AXILLA,SENTINEL),EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODE(LEFT SECONDARY AXILLA,SENTINEL),EXCISIO PART D: LYMPH NODE(LEFT TERTIARY AXILLA,SENTINEL),EXCISION
