VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14:59 CLINICAL DATA: Abnormal mammogram. Needle localization x 2. Additional left breast tissue from lesion #2 of 2. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR, "#2"), BIOPSY": -- LOBULAR CARCINOMA-IN-SITU, ARISING IN A FIBROADENOMA VARIANT AND INVOLVING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITHIN THE FIBROADENOMA (SEE NOTE). -- SCLEROSING ADENOSIS, DIFFUSE, WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS. NOTE: Cautery artifact precludes optimal assessment of the lobular carcinoma. Furthermore, the distortion by sclerosing adenosis makes the assessment of invasion difficult. However, no definite invasion is seen. BREAST (LEFT BREAST LESION #2, INFERIOR; ADDITIONAL TISSUE): LOBULAR CARCINOMA-IN-SITU ARISING IN A FIBROADENOMA VARIANT. BREAST (LEFT, SUPERIOR, "#1"), BIOPSY: -- FIBROADENOMA VARIANT WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS. -- SCLEROSING ADENOSIS, DIFFUSE, WITH FOCAL APOCRINE ATYPIA, AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18:38 Consulting Pathologist(s): Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, are two specimens. Labeled "#1", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast tissue fragment, inked and sectioned to reveal a fibroadipose cut surface with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan, slightly bosselated, firm nodule that has a tiny irregular cavity in the center. The nodule is at one end of the specimen, abutting the inked margin. A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX#1. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes A through F, with F representing FX#1. Labeled "#2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast tissue fragment, inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, white-tan, bosselated, firm nodule located at one end of the specimen, abutting the inked margins. This specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes G through K. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left breast lesion 2, inferior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white, firm tissue fragment, bisected and submitted entirely in cassette L. Resident: DARRYL E. PALMER-TOY, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: (BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR), BIOPSY: NODULE WITH FOCAL FEATURES OF FIBROADENOMA. NO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS SEEN. GROSS DIAGNOSIS : (BREAST LEFT INFERIOR): MULTIPLE SMALL NODULES, SIMILAR TO THOSE IN THE FIRST SPECIMEN; FAVOR BENIGN. O.R. Resident: FANG FANG, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Wiley W Souba Jr., M.D. PART A: SUPERIOR LEFT BREAST PART B: INFERIOR LEFT BREAST PART C: ADDITIONAL TISSUE FROM LESION\u000a[report_end]
