VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12:28 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast cancer. Right needle localization. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), LUMPECTOMY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. (SEE TABLE #1). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified Blood vessel invasion: Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin of the specimen along a broad front and less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin of the specimen in one focus Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within and beyond the region of the mass Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: REMOVED_DATE Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Ductal in-situ extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins of the specimen in two foci Stains for receptors: Not indicated LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: RARE (<10) KERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ARE PRESENT IN THE SUBCAPSULAR SINSUS IN ONE LYMPH NODE. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: The tumor cells are not seen on hematoxylin and eosin stained sections. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL ANTERIOR), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH HEALING BIOPSY SITE CHANGES; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SUPERIOR), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SUPERIOR), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT FINAL LATERAL), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MEDIAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL DEEP SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT "FINAL I"), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 20 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 07:53 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow and tan fibrofatty soft tissue fragment penetrated by a localization needle. There is a long stitch marking the inferior aspect of the tissue. There is a short stitch marking the deep aspect of the tissue. The external surface shows no gross abnormalities. The specimen is inked according to protocol: superior - blue, inferior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan-white, ill-defined area with a hemorrhagic component which may represent the tract of the needle. The lesion abuts the lateral and inferior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and 1 cm from the superior margin. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A-J with the lesion in cassettes E-I with closest margins. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right axillary sentinel", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node with scant attached fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K-N. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast final anterior", are four unoriented, fibrofatty, tan-yellow, soft tissue fragments ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and aggregating to 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes O-R. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final superior", are two yellow-tan fibrofatty soft tissue fragments, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The black suture marking the new margin on each fragment. The new margin is inked black and the specimens are serially sectioned. One fragment is submitted entirely in cassettes S and T. The other fragment is submitted entirely in cassette U. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow, fibrofatty, soft tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassette V. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast shaved margin, final medial", is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty, yellow-tan, unremarkable soft tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassette W-X. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm, yellow-tan, unremarkable fibrofatty tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassettes Y-Z. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final I", is a 5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm, unremarkable, yellow-tan, fibrofatty tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassettes AA-DD. Resident: MINDY J. HULL, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE(RIGHT AXILLA,SENTINEL),EXCISION PART C: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL ANTERIOR),EXCISION PART D: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL SUPERIOR),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL LATERAL),EXCISION PART F: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL MEDIAL SHAVED MARGIN),EXCISION PART G: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL DEEP SHAVED MARGIN),EXCISION PART H: BREAST (RIGHT, "FINAL I"), EXCISION
