VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10:46 CLINICAL DATA: Incision made into specimen. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: LYMPHOCYTIC MASTITIS. NOTE: An atypical epithelial proliferation is not identified. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11:46 Consulting Pathologist(s): Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS, PARAFFIN SECTIONS: With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is no staining. With antibody to B-lineage antigen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), there is staining of most cells in a perivascular pattern, and associated with breast lobular ducts. The B cells are positive for antibody to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. With antibody to T-lineage associated antigens (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), there is staining of rare small cells scattered within the tissue. With antibody to cytokeratin, (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,3 cam REMOVED_DATE ), there is staining of epithelial cells. No lymphoepithelial lesions are identified. Together with the morphologic features on routine sections, these results are suspicious for a low-grade B-cell lymphoma or B-cell chronic lymphocytic leukemia. Additional studies that might help to provide a definite diagnosis include rebiopsy to obtain fresh frozen tissue for more optimal immunohistologic analysis, if clinically indicated. In addition, review of the peripheral blood with flow cytometric analysis for any evidence of monoclonal lymphoid population is also suggested. Added by: Phuong Nguyen, MD Signed On: 20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09:15 Consulting Pathologist(s): Nancy Lee Harris, M.D. Proofread by: Nancy Lee Harris, M.D. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number and "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm rubbery white-tan tissue. Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable white-tan breast tissue with multiple small, tan, well-circumscribed areas each of one less than REMOVED_DATE cm. No frozen done. Everything submitted from A-E. Resident: ESTHER OLIVA, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS: NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE; AWAIT PERMANENTS. O.R. Resident: Robin E. Kirby, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michael Ned Margolies, M.D. PART : BREAST MASS (RIGHT)\u000a[report_end]
