ng the deep margin. F: Representative section of more firm breast tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary contents" is a 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue, dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to 2 cm in greatest dimension, admixed with more fibrous tissue. Representative sections of the lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H through L. Resident: SAHA SADEGHI, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. Alphonse Taghian, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
