VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14:59 CLINICAL DATA: 60-year-old woman with infiltrating lobular carcinoma in left upper mid-line less than REMOVED_DATE cm from several inked margins and a granular cell tumor involving skeletal muscle in the tail of the left breast with positive inked margins on REMOVED_DATE  lumpectomy. Now for left modified radical mastectomy with en bloc specimen; stitch (long silk) on edge of tail of breast biopsy cavity, where it abutted serratus anterior muscle. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: 1. METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN FOUR OF EIGHTEEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. 2. ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, FOCAL; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN EXAMINED BREAST TISSUE. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL GRANULAR CELL TUMOR. 4. BIOPSY SITE WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION, FAT NECROSIS AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION. Diagnosis by: Leonard Atkins, M.D. Signed On: 28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09:13 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left breast and axillary contents" is a modified radical mastectomy specimen, designated left, 410 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. On the surface is a skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm containing a nipple areolar complex at the medial margin REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. On the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE cm curvilinear incision which goes to the edge of the skin. The remaining skin surface is unremarkable. Attached to the specimen is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm axillary tail containing multiple lymph nodes. On the posterior aspect of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity which is open and extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior lateral resection margin and to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral resection margin. There is a fragment of unremarkable skeletal muscle on the lateral, deep aspect of this area; a suture designates the area involved previously by granular cell tumor. The biopsy cavity extends medially under the skin surface and into the breast tissue to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is scant, fibrous, white-pink septa running through unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. Section Code: A: nipple and areolar complex. B-E: representative radial sections of biopsy cavity with superior margin and skeletal muscle (area near long silk suture). F,G: representative radial sections of biopsy cavity with lateral margin. H-K: representative biopsy cavity. L-O: representative breast tissue. P-T: axillary lymph nodes. Resident: Mark vanGorder, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. Simon Kaspar Ashiku, M.D. PART : BREAST (LEFT)\u000a[report_end]
