VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON: 15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10:40 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, GRADE 2, REMOVED_DATE CM, EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN ONE SMALL FOCUS. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13:13 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST (RIGHT): THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN. THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN. SEE NOTE. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17:19 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Right breast lesion" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white stellate firm nodule abutting the inked margin. A representative section of the tumor and margin is frozen as frozen section #1, and resubmitted in cassette H. The lesion is submitted entirely in cassettes A - C. Representative sections of the remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes D - G. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC Resident: ERIN OCHOA, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1, RIGHT BREAST LESION: INVASIVE CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: Suzanne B. Keel, M.D. O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Charles Mason Ferguson, M.D. PART : BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
