riented, tan-yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable reddish brown portion of attached skeletal muscle. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable predominantly fibrotic cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes K-N. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "additional superior tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unoriented, tan-yellow to pink portion of fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable, predominantly fibrotic cut surface with no discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes O-V. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(LEFT,MEDIAL),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(LEFT,SUPERIOR),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
