VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 04 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 04 MAY 95 at 12:38 CLINICAL DATA: New breast calcifications and right chest lesion. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT "A"), BIOPSY: 1. ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. 2. ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. 3. SIMPLE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. 4. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA, SCLEROSING ADENOSIS, AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. BREAST (LEFT "B"), BIOPSY: 1. ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED (SEE NOTE). 2. ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. 3. SIMPLE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. 4. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. NOTE: The atypical lobular hyperplasia is focally present at an inked resection margin. BREAST (LEFT), BIOPSY #3: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. 2. DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. SKIN (RIGHT CHEST), EXCISION: TRICHOBLASTOMA (SEE NOTE). NOTE: This is a benign adnexal tumor of pilar origin. Drs. Elizabeth Bailey and Lyn Duncan have reviewed the slide and agree with the diagnosis. Diagnosis by: G. Richard Dickersin, M.D. Signed On: 12 MAY 95 at 14:55 Consulting Pathologist(s): Dennis Sgroi, M.D. =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, are two parts. Labeled "Left breast, A" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibroadipose tissue, with accompanying wire and x-ray. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal no grossly suspicious lesion. The specimen is submitted entirely in A through F. Labeled "Left breast, B" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibroadipose tissue, with accompanying wire and x-ray. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm soft, red, well-circumscribed nodule adjacent to one inked margin. Sectioning through the nodule reveals a homogeneous yellow cut surface. The specimen is submitted entirely in G through J. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, are two additional parts. Labeled "Left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragmented and cauterized piece of fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm fibrous, slightly firm, gritty nodule with ill-defined borders, which focally abuts an inked resection margin. The specimen is submitted entirely in K and L. Labeled "Right chest lesion" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white, smooth, lobulated nodule elevated REMOVED_DATE cm above a base measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nodule is sectioned to reveal a lobulated, solid, homogeneous, well-circumscribed mass that extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked base; ends in M, nodule in N. Resident: EDWIN S. MONUKI, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS: LEFT BREAST: NO AREA GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED. DEFER TO PERMANENTS. GROSS DIAGNOSIS: LEFT BREAST: NO AREA GOSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS PRESENT. DEFER TO PERMANENTS. O.R. Resident: Robin E. Kirby, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Ashby Carter Moncure, M.D. Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: LEFT BREAST #1 PART B: LEFT BREAST #B PART C: SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION: PART D: SKIN (RIGHT CHEST), EXCISION:\u000a[report_end]
