VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16:11 CLINICAL DATA: New left breast lump. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. RADIAL SCAR. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The neoplastic cells do not stain for E-cadherin. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 13:53 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains (kappa and lambda) results are uninterpretable due to high background. With antibodies to B-lineage antigen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) there is staining of many cells in an architecturally appropriate follicular pattern. The B-cells are negative for antibody to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and cyclin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. With antibodies to T-lineage associated antigens (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) there is staining of many small cells in the interfollicular region. With antibody to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID there is staining of follicular dendritic cells. BCL-2 is negative within germinal centers, which are positive for BCL-6. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is non-contributory. Together with the morphologic features on routine sections, these results confirm the diagnosis of a reactive lymph node with prominent primary follicles. There is no evidence of lymphoma. See note. NOTE: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: ROBERT P. HASSERJIAN, M.D. Signed On: 12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18:20 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "right axillary lymph node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-pink lymph node entirely frozen as FX#1, now resubmitted in cassettes A-B. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unoriented tan-yellow to pink irregular lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly dense rubbery white fibrotic cut surface with no discrete masses or lesions grossly appreciated. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes C-F. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: STEWART M. KNOEPP, MD., Ph.D. *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: SHABIN NANJI, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: GREGORY LAUWERS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Janey Sue Pratt, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY), EXCISION PART B: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
