 Labeled "additional superior margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white-yellow fibrofatty and fibrous portion of breast; it is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as F-H. Labeled "additional deep margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow fatty tissue; it is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as I-L. Labeled "additional medial margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white-yellow fibrofatty portion of breast, sectioned to reveal an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white gritty nodule. The specimen is submitted entirely as M-R with M and N containing the nodule. Resident: SOHEIL DADRAS, MD, PHD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Sarah P Thayer, M.D. Matthew Thomas Menard, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT MAIN), RE-EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISIO PART C: BREAST (RIGHT ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (RIGHT ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
