VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON: 21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15:17 CLINICAL DATA: Abnormal right mammogram, stellate density, left nipple discharge. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), BIOPSY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI. RADIAL SCAR. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. BREAST (NIPPLE DUCT, LEFT), BIOPSY: UNREMARKABLE LACTIFEROUS DUCT. BREAST (NIPPLE DUCT, LEFT), BIOPSY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI. FAT NECROSIS WITH CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOREIGN BODY CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS AND MICROCYST FORMATION. SEE NOTE. NOTE: THE CAUSE OF THE PATIENT'S LEFT NIPPLE MAY NOT BE REPRESENTED IN THIS SPECIMEN. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13:27 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Right breast" is a 9 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm breast biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and accompanying x-ray demonstrating a vague, white nodular density. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal white, semifirm fibrous tissue and soft yellow adipose tissue with numerous cysts measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension and a firm nodule up to REMOVED_DATE cm in dimension. An area with the firm nodule is frozen as frozen section #1. The area corresponding to the x-ray lesion is submitted in cassettes A through G, representative sections of remaining breast tissue are submitted in cassettes H through M, and the frozen is submitted in cassette N. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, are two parts. Labeled "Nipple duct, A" are two pink-tan, rubbery nodules of tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm; submitted entirely in cassette O. Labeled "Nipple duct, B" is a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue with duct and a long stitch designating distal and short designating superficial. Specimen is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The duct has length REMOVED_DATE cm and diameter REMOVED_DATE cm. The external surface is inked black and the superficial aspect is inked yellow on black and the distal margin of the nipple duct is submitted in cassette P. Representative sections of the duct are submitted in cassette Q, and representative sections of the breast material are submitted in cassette R through Y. Resident: Mark vanGorder, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: (RIGHT BREAST MASS): FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. O.R. Resident: Douglas B. Flieder, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B: NIPPLE DUCT (LEFT) PART C: NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
