nts are not oriented. They consist of fatty tissue admixed with firm white areas. They are totally submitted in cassettes O-T. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "additional axillary tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0.4 cm fragment of fatty tissue entirely submitted as U. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left axillary contents" are several fragments of fatty tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Candidate lymph nodes are submitted entirely as follows: V-W: one trisected node X-Y: one bisected node Z-BB:one bisected node in each cassette CC-FF: two bisected candidates nodes in each cassette GG-HH: entire candidate nodes Resident: LAURENCE DE LEVAL, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Simon Powell, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLARY), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), FINAL SHAVE MARGIN PART D: LYMPH NODES (ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
