VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14:49 CLINICAL DATA: 69 year old female wtih breast cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** LYMPH NODES (SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 LYMPH NODES. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed. BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: HEALING BIOPSY SITE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. DUCT ECTASIA. RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: FOCAL SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. Diagnosis by: MELINDA J. LERWILL, M.D. Signed On: 29 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 17:29 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node", are multiple nodules surrounded by adipose tissue. The nodules are removed (3 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) and frozen as FX#1 and FX#2. The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassette C. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast lumpectomy tissue" is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lumpectomy specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm blue discolored tan skin ellipse and abundant fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is oriented with a short stitch denoting the superior margin and a long stitch denoting the lateral margin. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green, and inferior-yellow. The biopsy cavity is exposed on the superior, posterior and lateral portions of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial towards lateral. The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is lined by a tan-white, dull, and focally hemorrhagic tissue. Surrounding the biopsy cavity there are scattered golden yellow areas of fat necrosis and brown-red regions of hemorrhage. The biopsy cavity extends to at the posterior, superior, and lateral margins and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. In addition, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well-defined, soft, and yellow region in the medial inferior portion of the specimen. There are also scattered areas of tan-white fibrosis within the blue-green discolored predominantly fatty parenchyma. Representative sections are submitted as per section code. Section Code: D-G: Biopsy cavity with surrounding margins. H: REMOVED_DATE cm yellow medial inferior nodule. I-J: Fatty breast parenchyma with fibrous streaks. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved superior margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassettes K-Q. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved inferior margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow fibrofatty breast parenchyma. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassettes R-W. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved lateral margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassettes X-Y. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved medial margin" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow fibrofatty fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassettes Z-EE. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved deep margin" are 2 unoriented fragments of yellow fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate which are serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassettes FF-II. Resident: PAUL MICHAELS, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1-2: LYMPH NODES (SENTINEL): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: MASSIMO D'APUZZO, MD,PhD O.R. Diagnosis by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-OUTPATIENT (OFF.P/CLINIC) REPORTS TO: Janey Sue Pratt, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODES (SENTINEL), EXCISION PART B: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SHAVED SUPERIOR MARGIN),EXCISION PART D: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SHAVED INFERIOR MARGIN),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SHAVED LATERAL MARGIN),EXCISION PART F: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SHAVED MEDIAL MARGIN),EXCISION PART G: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SHAVED DEEP MARGIN),EXCISION
