ance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15:09 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue with attached fibrous tissue along one aspect. This margin is marked with blue ink, the remaining undesignated margins are marked with black ink. On sectioning, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm, mottled yellow-white ill defined lesion which extends to the adherent deep margin. The remainder of the tissue consists predominantly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of intervening soft white fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted as: A-D: Lesion. E-F: Sections away from lesion. The remaining tissue is submitted entirely from G-R. Gross Description by: TIM J. ROBINSON Resident: MASSIMO D'APUZZO, MD,PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Charles Mason Ferguson, M.D. PART : BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
