 fragments of tissue, one with skin attached, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension; two pieces of grossly unremarkable adipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension; a skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with minimal subcutaneous tissue attached. Two representative samples of the largest piece of breast tissue are in M and N. Single sections from each of the two smaller pieces of fibroadipose tissue are in O and P. Representative sections of the free skin segment are in Q. Labeled "right axillary lymph node, level I" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of adipose tissue. The fatty tissue contains linear areas of tan, which could represent a lymph node. The specimen is submitted entirely in R-X. Resident: STUART HOUSER, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. James Warren May Jr., M.D. PART A: LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: RIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C: RIGHT BREAST, ADDITIONAL TISSUE PART D: RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
