E x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined, firm, gritty lesion with hemorrhagic cut surface and fat necrosis consistent with previous biopsy site. This lesion is located from the following margins: deep-0.1 cm, superior-0.1 cm, anterior-0.2 cm, inferior-2.0 cm, medial-0.6 cm, and lateral REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the parenchyma is composed of 80% adipose and 20% fibrous tissue with no other lesions identified. Representative sections are submitted. B: medial margin C: lateral margin D: lesion to inferior-posterior margin E: lesion to posterior-superior margin F: lesion to posterior, lateral G: lesion, deep-medial H: uninvolved parenchyma, lateral I: uninvolved parenchyma, medial Labeled "final shaved margin, inferior half cavity" are multiple fragments of unoriented fibrofatty soft tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, serially sectioned to reveal a cut surface composed of 90% adipose and 10% fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions, representative sections are submitted as J-N. Labeled "final shave, superior half of cavity" are multiple fragments of unoriented fibrofatty soft tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with no discrete lesions identified. The entire specimen is submitted as O-S. Resident: SOHEIL DADRAS, MD, PHD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL, HOT&BLUE #1195),E PART B: BREAST(LEFT),RE-EXCISION PART C: BREAST(LEFT,INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED PART D: BREAST(LEFT,SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED
