VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11:47 CLINICAL DATA: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, calcifications. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, "MEDIAL, FINAL SHAVED MARGINS"), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, "LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGINS"), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13:20 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow to white fibrofatty breast tissue with a localizing wire in place. There is a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior-black, anterior-blue, lateral-green. Sectioning reveals multiple cysts within dense white fibrous tissue, the largest (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is hemorrhagic and comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin. The remaining parenchyma is yellow lobulated fatty tissue. A designating metal clip is identified. The specimen is submitted sequentially from superior to inferior in cassettes A-H, with the designated metal clip area in D and the hemorrhagic cyst in F-G. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final shave margins medial aspect" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-yellow to white fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating furthest from biopsy, medial aspect. The medial aspect is inked black and the opposing aspect is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan-yellow to white fibrofatty tissue, with minimal cystic change. The specimen is submitted in its entirely in cassettes I-M. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final shaved margins-lateral aspect" are 2 tan-yellow to white, irregular fibrofatty tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, each with a suture designating the lateral aspect. The lateral aspect of each is inked black and the opposing aspect is inked blue. Each portion is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-yellow to white fibrofatty tissue. The specimens are submitted in their entirety as N-S, with the smaller portion in N-P and the larger in Q-S. Gross Description by: BRAD MOSBURG Resident: JOHN BISSONNETTE, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (RIGHT MEDIAL), FINAL SHAVED MARGINS PART C: BREAST (RIGHT LATERAL), FINAL SHAVED MARGINS
