ecimen is provided. With the skin ellipse in the 12 o'clock position, the short stitch in the 6 o'clock position, and the long stitch in the 9 o'clock position (short stitch indicating deep margin and long stitch lateral). The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of fibrosis with cysts ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. This fibrotic area is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior resection margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial resection margin. Representative sections are submitted as follows: F: Lesion and anterior resection margin. G: Lesion and lateral resection margin. H: Lesion and medial resection margin. I: Representative section of lesion (ink is anterolateral). J: Representative section of overlying skin ellipse. Labeled "additional deep margin Phylloid's" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma, submitted entirely in K through M. Resident: RHONDA YANTISS, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS: LEFT BREAST MAMMOGRAPHIC LESION: DISCRETE NODULE. AWAIT PERMANENTS. O.R. Resident: STEPHEN LAU, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT), REEXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
