 lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, entirely frozen as FX#1 and 2, now F and G. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "non sentinel nodes" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fatty tissue, dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The smaller lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassette H, with largest lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette I. Resident: SAHA SADEGHI, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1-2: LYMPH NODES (SENTINEL): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: SELIM NASSER, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODES (SENTINEL), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODES (NON SENTINEL), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), LUMPECTOMY\u000a[report_end]
