 margin B-K: Cross sections of specimen superior to inferior. L: Inferior margin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of yellow adipose tissue containing two possible lymph nodes. Entirely submitted in cassete M. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast, final shave" are multiple fragments of tan-pink tissue, in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Entirely submitted in cassettes N and O. Resident: STACEY L. MIKESELL, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Simon Powell, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT "FINAL SHAVE MARGIN"), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
