ted in cassette C. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast, re-excision, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue. A short stitch marks the superior margin and a long stitch marks the lateral margin. The specimen is inked black overall with additional colors as follows: blue, anterior; yellow, medial; and green, lateral. Serial sections show predominantly white fibrous tissue with no discrete mass. Entirely submitted. D : Superior margin E-S: Cross sections of specimen superior to inferior T: Inferior margin Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast, additional margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue. The suture placed by the surgeon marks the aspect furthest from the tumor. This aspect is inked black. Serial sections show white fibro-glandular tissue admixed with smaller amounts of yellow adipose tissue with no grossly suspicious areas. Entirely submitted in cassettes U-W. Resident: STACEY L. MIKESELL, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** Frozen section diagnoses #1,2 (Sentinel lymph nodes, right axilla): There is no evidence of malignancy. O.R. Resident: GARY LETTS, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA PART B: NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA PART C: RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION PART D: RIGHT BREAST, ADDITIONAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
