tive sections are submitted as follows: A: first nodule in its entirety B: closest posterior margin to first nodule and representative section of fibrous parenchyma. C: second firm nodular area to posterior margin D-J: representative sections of parenchyma from medial to lateral with posterior margin in G and anterior margin in H. Within the small portion of axillary fat rare lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, and they are submitted in their entirety in K, along with a representative portion of skin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of axillary fat. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse with a eccentric REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable nipple. There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the axillary sampling. The skin is notable for a REMOVED_DATE cm linear well healed scar in the lateral, inferior portion. This overlies a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrotic area within the parenchyma that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior deep margin. The remainder of the parenchyma is moderately fibrous but contains no discrete masses. The entire fibrous area beneath the scar is submitted in L-P with posterior margin in L-O and anterior margin in P. Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma are submitted from lateral to medial in Q-W with posterior ink in Q-R and anterior ink in S. Within the small segment of axillary fat several lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. Whole nodes are in X-Y, representative sections of nodes are in Z. Resident: MELINDA J. FAN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (LEFT): NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS SEEN. O.R. Resident: TAN A. INCE, 