EMOVED_DATE cm skin which includes the nipple and shows a linear healed REMOVED_DATE cm in length scar in the lower outer quadrant. The skin and nipple are grossly unremarkable. The specimen is inked as follows: deep in black, anterior superior in green and anterior-inferior in blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a focal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm and fibrotic area beneath the scar and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The remaining breast tissue is grossly unremarkable. The attached portion of axillary tail is serially sectioned and a few lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: Section code: M-N: sclerotic area and closest deep margin. O-S: sections from the firm area and adjacent tissue. T: superior anterior margin and scar. U: nipple and inferior/anterior margin. V: one lymph node bisected. W: one lymph node. Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fatty tissue including a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node which is bisected to reveal yellow tan homogeneous cut surface. It is entirely submitted as X. Resident: SOUHAD YOUNES, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: DANIELLE ELLIOTT, M.D. O.R. Diagnosis by: Gunnlaugur P. Nielsen, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT),SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL),EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
