VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11:59 CLINICAL DATA: Left breast cancer (lobular carcinoma in situ and ductal carcinoma in situ). Two lumpectomies done previously, with ductal carcinoma in-situ at the margin of one of them. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU), EXTENSIVE, WITH INVOLVEMENT OF SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND DUCTS. 2. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SEVERAL SMALL FOCI OUTSIDE OF THE "2 O'CLOCK" HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS, WITH A RADIAL SCAR, FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA, AND EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. 4. COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS, MINOR FOCI. 5. TWO HEALING BIOPSY SITES (12 O'CLOCK AND 2 O'CLOCK). 6. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU. 7. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE NODE). Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15:09 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left simple mastectomy specimen with no stitches for orientation. The overlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple areola complex which is unremarkable. There are 2 linear well healed scars superior (designated 12 o'clock), and lateral (2 o'clock) to the nipple. The 12 o'clock scar measures REMOVED_DATE cm; the 2 o'clock scar REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-white of firm breast parenchyma with 2 retracted areas directly beneath the linear scars. Directly beneath the 12 o'clock scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm stellate retracted firm area with focal grittiness and tan-white cut surface, coming within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior deep margin. Directly beneath the 2 o'clock scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm stellate retracted firm area with focal grittiness and tan-white cut surface, coming within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior deep margin. The remainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable. The dissection of the axillary portion of the specimen reveals no obvious lymph nodes. Representative sections are submitted as follows: Section Code: A-F: Representative sections of the firm area beneath the 12 o'clock scar, submitted from medial to lateral, with lesion to deep posterior margin in cassettes D-E. G-L: Firm area beneath the 2 o'clock scar, submitted entirely from medial to lateral, with lesion to posterior deep margin in cassette K. M: A representative section of the unremarkable breast parenchyma from the medial aspect. N: A representative section of the unremarkable breast parenchyma from the lateral portion of the specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary lymph node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan-yellow soft tissue fragment, bisected and entirely submitted as O. Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY)
