y grossly identified masses. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A-E. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "B-additional lateral breast left breast margins" are two oriented fragments of fibrofatty tissue each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a suture on each denoting the surface furthest from the biopsy cavity. This surface is black-inked and the specimens are serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassette F. Resident: PAUL MICHAELS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT LATERAL), ADDITIONAL MARGIN
