e tissue. On sectioning the tissue consists predominantly of adipose tissue with a small amount of intervening white, fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as A-H from the superior margin to the inferior margin with the lesion in cassettes B-C. The separately received fragment of tissue is submitted as I. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast final shaved margin" are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm of several irregular portions of unoriented fibrofatty tissue. On sectioning there are no gross lesions. The tissue consists predominantly of adipose tissue except for a few foci of white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as J-K. Gross Description by: TIM J. ROBINSON Resident: ANDRAS SCHAFFER, MD,PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(LEFT, FINAL MARGIN),EXCISION
