VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 14:14 CLINICAL DATA: Locally advanced breast cancer, s/p preop chemotherapy. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM, EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS. NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), NODE DISSECTION: A FEW CARCINOMA CELLS PRESENT IN A LYMPHATIC VESSEL. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 EXAMINED LYMPH NODES. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA, "ADDITIONAL TISSUE"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 EXAMINED LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: MELINDA J. FAN, MD Signed On: 15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17:46 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, in two parts: Labeled "left breast" is a 20 x 15 x REMOVED_DATE cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm attached axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple. There is a long stitch designating the lateral and a short stitch designating the superior margins. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan fibrotic area in the mid-portion of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior skin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from all other resection margins. The remaining parenchyma is yellow and fatty with no discernable masses or nodules. Representative sections of the fibrotic area are submitted in cassette A-F and M-Q (A-B with deep margin). Sectioning through the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. Half of the large lymph nodes and the entire smaller ones are submitted in cassettes G-J. Labeled "additional axillary tissue" are multiple fibroadipose tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Sectioning reveals 4 lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The large lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette K. The three smaller lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassette L. Resident: QUN DONG, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
