VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 08 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON: 08 AUG 01 at 14:55 CLINICAL DATA: Two areas of calcification left breast, DCIS on core biopsy. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, GRADE 1, ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF EXTENSIVE SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. SEE TABLE #1 AND NOTE. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU). MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU Tumor size: Involving 2 of 15 blocks. Spanning at least REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 1 Calcifications: In the carcinoma in-situ, atypical ductal hyperplasia and in benign changes. Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin of the specimen in one focus. NOTE: Atypical ductal hyperplasia is focally present at the deep margin, and is <0.1 cm from the deep and lateral margins in several foci. The ductal carcinoma in situ is found in the more central portion of the specimen closer to the clip, whereas the second area of calcification represents severely atypical ductal hyperplasia. BREAST (LEFT, "SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"). EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: MELINDA J. FAN, MD Signed On: 15 AUG 01 at 15:37 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast wide excision" is a 6 x 4 x 3 cm portion of breast tissue with two needle-localization wires attached. The specimen is oriented with the short stitch denotating the superior margin and a long stitch denoting the lateral margin. The specimen is inked as follows: medial-black, lateral-blue, anterior-red, posterior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two nodules. The first nodule measures 1 x 1 x 1 cm and is white, firm and abuts one needle localization wire and is located <0.1 cm from the medial resection margin. The second nodule is also white and firm and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and abuts the second needle localization wire (designating the clip) and is located <0.1 cm from the medial resection margin. Multiple soft white fibrous areas are also encountered measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension throughout the breast parenchyma. No gross calcifications are identified. Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes A-M with the previously described nodules in B and M. Additional representative sections from the inferior half are submitted in AA-BB. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shave margin-superior" is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes N-P. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margin-inferior" is a 4 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes Q-R. Resident: CHRISTINE GARCIA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT SUPERIOR), FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART C: BREAST (LEFT INFERIOR), FINAL SHAVED MARGIN
