e lobular process. Stains for calponin and smooth muscle myosin highlight an intact myoepithelial cell layer throughout the LCIS. No areas diagnostic of invasive carcinoma are identified, although the stromal changes suggest that an adjacent area of invasion cannot be excluded. Excision is recommended. Final Diagnosis by: Anthony R. Mattia, M.D. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 1448 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 1453 PAT.GILD DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: (Continued) REMOVED_DATE  - 1541 MD.MATANCODES: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Right breast, N-Lobular carcino REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Left breast, NO-Fibroadenoma, N BREANBX - -BREANBX Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0821 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1440 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 1441 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 1536 MD.MATANMARKERS: Breast Disease Related, Tumor case Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0821 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1441 PAT.GILDPROCEDURES: IMMUNOCYTO (08/08/07-1448 PAT.GILD) REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (08/08/07-1448 PAT.GILD) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0821 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1440 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 1448 PAT.GILDTISSUES: A. Breast, needle biopsy - right 9 o'clock B. Breast, needle biopsy - left 3 o'clock Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0821 PAT.DORDFinal: ROSS,MICHAEL J. M.D. * REMOVED_DATE  <08/08/07-1556> by MD.ROSMJ MATTIA,ANTHONY R.MD * REMOVED_DATE  <08/08/07-1610> by MD.MATAN --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
