VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, excision:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with microcalcifications, focally\u000apresent adjacent to area of fibroplasia and chronic inflammation\u000aconsistent with prior needle biopsy site.\u000aFibrocystic changes with multiple microcalcifications in unremarkable\u000aacini.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aB. Left breast, additional inferior tissue, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with multiple microcalcifications in unremarkable\u000aacini.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: A few ducts with atypical ductal hyperplasia are seen adjacent to the\u000aarea consistent with the prior needle biopsy site; the inked margin is\u000afree of atypical ductal hyperplasia. The report of the outside left\u000abreast needle biopsy (Massachusetts General Hospital, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is\u000anoted.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast calcifications, atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - additional inferior\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast biopsy" consists of two portions of\u000afibroadipose tissue, one with two sutures and a localizing wire, measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm., and a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of tissue. The\u000afirst has a suture at one end which is long and is oriented as lateral and on\u000aan adjacent surface is a short suture oriented as superior of the left breast.\u000aThe wire enters the lateral end of the specimen and the tip of the wire extends\u000aout the deep superior aspect of the specimen. The margins of this piece\u000athroughout are inked black. The deep surface is double-inked red and the\u000asuperior surface is inked blue. It is cross sectioned and serially submitted\u000afrom the long suture towards the short suture revealing a central area of\u000arubbery, white-tan fibrous tissue surrounding an area of fat necrosis. It is\u000aentirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The separate portion is inked black throughout\u000aand is cross sectioned and serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 14 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "additional breast tissue" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue. The outer surfaces are inked black throughout.\u000aIt is serially sectioned revealing areas of rubbery white-tan fibrous tissue\u000aand is serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 12 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
